], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09088425887258429, "compression_ratio": 1.381578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671203925869069e-12}, {"id": 16, "seek": 5930, "start": 70.8, "end": 71.8, "text": " I love that analogy.", "tokens": [50940, 286, 959, 300, 21663, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09088425887258429, "compression_ratio": 1.381578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671203925869069e-12}, {"id": 17, "seek": 7180, "start": 71.8, "end": 81.22, "text": " And every single day, you have to wake up, find that note, and creatively reinterpret what it means based on exactly how you were feeling right at that second.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 633, 2167, 786, 11, 291, 362, 281, 6634, 493, 11, 915, 300, 3637, 11, 293, 43750, 319, 41935, 437, 309, 1355, 2361, 322, 2293, 577, 291, 645, 2633, 558, 412, 300, 1150, 13, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0770189642906189, "compression_ratio": 1.618421052631579, "no_speech_prob": 1.74148206705943e-12}, {"id": 18, "seek": 7180, "start": 81.42, "end": 84.6, "text": " That framing gets right to the heart of the debate we're unpacking today.", "tokens": [50846, 663, 28971, 2170, 558, 281, 264, 1917, 295, 264, 7958, 321, 434, 26699, 278, 965, 13, 51005], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0770189642906189, "compression_ratio": 1.618421052631579, "no_speech_prob": 1.74148206705943e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 7180, "start": 84.86, "end": 93.34, "text": " The idea of the cryptic note perfectly captures the foundation of this really fascinating public conversation that recently took place.", "tokens": [51018, 440, 1558, 295, 264, 9844, 299, 3637, 6239, 27986, 264, 7030, 295, 341, 534, 10343, 1908, 3761, 300, 3938, 1890, 1081, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0770189642906189, "compression_ratio": 1.618421052631579, "no_speech_prob": 1.74148206705943e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 9334, "start": 93.34, "end": 97.46000000000001, "text": " Yeah, the one between Michael Levin, the biologist, and Katrina Schleisman, the AI researcher.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 11, 264, 472, 1296, 5116, 1456, 4796, 11, 264, 3228, 9201, 11, 293, 42550, 2065, 306, 1434, 282, 11, 264, 7318, 21751, 13, 50571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13177976608276368, "compression_ratio": 1.4701754385964911, "no_speech_prob": 1.5791239843521154e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 9334, "start": 97.62, "end": 98.10000000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50579, 7587, 13, 50603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13177976608276368, "compression_ratio": 1.4701754385964911, "no_speech_prob": 1.5791239843521154e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 9334, "start": 98.42, "end": 102.24000000000001, "text": " And we have a brilliant synthesis of their dialogue to guide us today.", "tokens": [50619, 400, 321, 362, 257, 10248, 30252, 295, 641, 10221, 281, 5934, 505, 965, 13, 50810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13177976608276368, "compression_ratio": 1.4701754385964911, "no_speech_prob": 1.5791239843521154e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 9334, "start": 102.48, "end": 106.92, "text": " It's a July 2026 essay by a researcher known as Flixian.", "tokens": [50822, 467, 311, 257, 7370, 945, 10880, 16238, 538, 257, 21751, 2570, 382, 3235, 970, 952, 13, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13177976608276368, "compression_ratio": 1.4701754385964911, "no_speech_prob": 1.5791239843521154e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 9334, "start": 107.12, "end": 112.02000000000001, "text": " Titled, Histories Become Operators, Biological Notes on Retained Admissibility.", "tokens": [51054, 14489, 1493, 11, 9038, 2083, 44308, 12480, 3391, 11, 13007, 4383, 41360, 322, 11495, 3563, 46292, 891, 2841, 13, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13177976608276368, "compression_ratio": 1.4701754385964911, "no_speech_prob": 1.5791239843521154e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 9334, "start": 113.32000000000001, "end": 116.84, "text": " Which, I mean, that title alone sounds like it requires a PhD to decode.", "tokens": [51364, 3013, 11, 286, 914, 11, 300, 4876, 3312, 3263, 411, 309, 7029, 257, 14476, 281, 979, 1429, 13, 51540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13177976608276368, "compression_ratio": 1.4701754385964911, "no_speech_prob": 1.5791239843521154e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 9334, "start": 116.88, "end": 117.98, "text": " She had a bit of a mouthful, yeah.", "tokens": [51542, 1240, 632, 257, 857, 295, 257, 4525, 906, 11, 1338, 13, 51597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13177976608276368, "compression_ratio": 1.4701754385964911, "no_speech_prob": 1.5791239843521154e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 11798, "start": 117.98, "end": 118.98, "text": " Okay, let's unpack this.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 26699, 341, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09576581736079982, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 1.085723524973936e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 11798, "start": 119.16000000000001, "end": 124.96000000000001, "text": " The core premise Flixian pulls from Levin and Schleisman completely rewires how we should think about our own agency.", "tokens": [50424, 440, 4965, 22045, 3235, 970, 952, 16982, 490, 1456, 4796, 293, 2065, 306, 1434, 282, 2584, 319, 86, 3145, 577, 321, 820, 519, 466, 527, 1065, 7934, 13, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09576581736079982, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 1.085723524973936e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 11798, "start": 125.7, "end": 128.4, "text": " Biological memory is not a hard drive storing the past.", "tokens": [50751, 13007, 4383, 4675, 307, 406, 257, 1152, 3332, 26085, 264, 1791, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09576581736079982, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 1.085723524973936e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 11798, "start": 128.84, "end": 131.56, "text": " It is a living, breathing constraint on the future.", "tokens": [50908, 467, 307, 257, 2647, 11, 9570, 25534, 322, 264, 2027, 13, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09576581736079982, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 1.085723524973936e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 11798, "start": 131.86, "end": 132.12, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51059, 1779, 13, 51072], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09576581736079982, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 1.085723524973936e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 11798, "start": 132.36, "end": 137.92000000000002, "text": " It's moving from memory as a record of what happened to memory as a rulebook for what can happen next.", "tokens": [51084, 467, 311, 2684, 490, 4675, 382, 257, 2136, 295, 437, 2011, 281, 4675, 382, 257, 4978, 2939, 337, 437, 393, 1051, 958, 13, 51362], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09576581736079982, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 1.085723524973936e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 11798, "start": 137.92000000000002, "end": 143.68, "text": " And to really grasp that pivot, we first have to dismantle the engineering habit we all carry around, right?", "tokens": [51362, 400, 281, 534, 21743, 300, 14538, 11, 321, 700, 362, 281, 30506, 306, 264, 7043, 7164, 321, 439, 3985, 926, 11, 558, 30, 51650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09576581736079982, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 1.085723524973936e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 14368, "start": 143.68, "end": 149.58, "text": " We do, because in computer science, memory is entirely treated as a fidelity problem.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 360, 11, 570, 294, 3820, 3497, 11, 4675, 307, 7696, 8668, 382, 257, 46404, 1154, 13, 50660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14851222073074674, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.472443803170187e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 14368, "start": 149.82, "end": 150.68, "text": " Fidelity, meaning accuracy.", "tokens": [50672, 479, 33343, 11, 3620, 14170, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14851222073074674, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.472443803170187e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 14368, "start": 151.34, "end": 151.52, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50748, 865, 13, 50757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14851222073074674, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.472443803170187e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 14368, "start": 151.92000000000002, "end": 154.64000000000001, "text": " You write a bit of data, like a one or a zero.", "tokens": [50777, 509, 2464, 257, 857, 295, 1412, 11, 411, 257, 472, 420, 257, 4018, 13, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14851222073074674, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.472443803170187e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 14368, "start": 155.20000000000002, "end": 162.58, "text": " And the entire architecture of the system is dedicated to ensuring that when you go back to read it ten years later, you get the exact same one or zero.", "tokens": [50941, 400, 264, 2302, 9482, 295, 264, 1185, 307, 8374, 281, 16882, 300, 562, 291, 352, 646, 281, 1401, 309, 2064, 924, 1780, 11, 291, 483, 264, 1900, 912, 472, 420, 4018, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14851222073074674, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.472443803170187e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 14368, "start": 162.76000000000002, "end": 164.02, "text": " So you build in redundancy.", "tokens": [51319, 407, 291, 1322, 294, 27830, 6717, 13, 51382], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14851222073074674, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.472443803170187e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 14368, "start": 164.62, "end": 166.12, "text": " You use error correction codes.", "tokens": [51412, 509, 764, 6713, 19984, 14211, 13, 51487], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14851222073074674, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.472443803170187e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 14368, "start": 166.22, "end": 166.42000000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51492, 1779, 13, 51502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14851222073074674, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.472443803170187e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 14368, "start": 166.54000000000002, "end": 168.64000000000001, "text": " You shield the physical drive from magnets.", "tokens": [51508, 509, 10257, 264, 4001, 3332, 490, 33022, 13, 51613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14851222073074674, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.472443803170187e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 14368, "start": 168.86, "end": 171.20000000000002, "text": " Because the hard drive doesn't care what the data means.", "tokens": [51624, 1436, 264, 1152, 3332, 1177, 380, 1127, 437, 264, 1412, 1355, 13, 51741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14851222073074674, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.472443803170187e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 14368, "start": 171.4, "end": 173.48000000000002, "text": " The meaning lives outside the drive.", "tokens": [51751, 440, 3620, 2909, 2380, 264, 3332, 13, 51855], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14851222073074674, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.472443803170187e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 17348, "start": 173.48, "end": 176.39999999999998, "text": " In the human observer or the software program using it.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 264, 1952, 27878, 420, 264, 4722, 1461, 1228, 309, 13, 50511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1481750940872451, "compression_ratio": 1.6085526315789473, "no_speech_prob": 1.2545421515866573e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 17348, "start": 176.45999999999998, "end": 176.79999999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50514, 7587, 13, 50531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1481750940872451, "compression_ratio": 1.6085526315789473, "no_speech_prob": 1.2545421515866573e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 17348, "start": 177.35999999999999, "end": 180.76, "text": " The drive's only job is to hold the data perfectly still in a vacuum.", "tokens": [50559, 440, 3332, 311, 787, 1691, 307, 281, 1797, 264, 1412, 6239, 920, 294, 257, 14224, 13, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1481750940872451, "compression_ratio": 1.6085526315789473, "no_speech_prob": 1.2545421515866573e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 17348, "start": 181.29999999999998, "end": 185.14, "text": " But biological systems operate on the exact opposite premise.", "tokens": [50756, 583, 13910, 3652, 9651, 322, 264, 1900, 6182, 22045, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1481750940872451, "compression_ratio": 1.6085526315789473, "no_speech_prob": 1.2545421515866573e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 17348, "start": 185.26, "end": 186.42, "text": " Right, because brains are messy.", "tokens": [50954, 1779, 11, 570, 15442, 366, 16191, 13, 51012], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1481750940872451, "compression_ratio": 1.6085526315789473, "no_speech_prob": 1.2545421515866573e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 17348, "start": 186.56, "end": 187.07999999999998, "text": " Very messy.", "tokens": [51019, 4372, 16191, 13, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1481750940872451, "compression_ratio": 1.6085526315789473, "no_speech_prob": 1.2545421515866573e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 17348, "start": 187.23999999999998, "end": 190.82, "text": " Fliction roots this in a theoretical framework called the ecology of distinctions.", "tokens": [51053, 3235, 4105, 10669, 341, 294, 257, 20864, 8388, 1219, 264, 39683, 295, 1483, 49798, 13, 51232], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1481750940872451, "compression_ratio": 1.6085526315789473, "no_speech_prob": 1.2545421515866573e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 17348, "start": 191.42, "end": 197.33999999999997, "text": " It basically argues that wet, squishy biology couldn't achieve perfect fidelity even if it wanted to.", "tokens": [51262, 467, 1936, 38218, 300, 6630, 11, 45402, 14956, 2809, 380, 4584, 2176, 46404, 754, 498, 309, 1415, 281, 13, 51558], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1481750940872451, "compression_ratio": 1.6085526315789473, "no_speech_prob": 1.2545421515866573e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 17348, "start": 197.66, "end": 201.66, "text": " Because cells turn over, proteins degrade, synapses are noisy.", "tokens": [51574, 1436, 5438, 1261, 670, 11, 15577, 368, 8692, 11, 5451, 2382, 279, 366, 24518, 13, 51774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1481750940872451, "compression_ratio": 1.6085526315789473, "no_speech_prob": 1.2545421515866573e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 20166, "start": 201.66, "end": 202.14, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2585326268122746, "compression_ratio": 1.5207100591715976, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689054431294093e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 20166, "start": 202.14, "end": 208.34, "text": " Evolution would be fighting a totally losing battle, trying to make a brain act like a silicon disk.", "tokens": [50389, 40800, 576, 312, 5237, 257, 3879, 7027, 4635, 11, 1382, 281, 652, 257, 3567, 605, 411, 257, 22848, 12355, 13, 50699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2585326268122746, "compression_ratio": 1.5207100591715976, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689054431294093e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 20166, "start": 208.98, "end": 212.8, "text": " So biological memory isn't defined by perfect storage.", "tokens": [50731, 407, 13910, 4675, 1943, 380, 7642, 538, 2176, 6725, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2585326268122746, "compression_ratio": 1.5207100591715976, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689054431294093e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 20166, "start": 213.01999999999998, "end": 217.04, "text": " It's defined by what Fliction calls preserved recoverability.", "tokens": [50933, 467, 311, 7642, 538, 437, 3235, 4105, 5498, 22242, 8114, 2310, 13, 51134], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2585326268122746, "compression_ratio": 1.5207100591715976, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689054431294093e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 20166, "start": 217.54, "end": 219.01999999999998, "text": " Preserved recoverability.", "tokens": [51159, 2718, 6913, 8114, 2310, 13, 51233], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2585326268122746, "compression_ratio": 1.5207100591715976, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689054431294093e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 20166, "start": 219.26, "end": 219.51999999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51245, 1779, 13, 51258], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2585326268122746, "compression_ratio": 1.5207100591715976, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689054431294093e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 21952, "start": 219.52, "end": 221.0, "text": " Let me make sure I'm picturing this correctly.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 385, 652, 988, 286, 478, 2317, 1345, 341, 8944, 13, 50439], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14935762156610904, "compression_ratio": 1.569811320754717, "no_speech_prob": 2.108831121880317e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 21952, "start": 221.52, "end": 226.62, "text": " This implies the system isn't keeping a perfect high-definition copy of the past, right?", "tokens": [50465, 639, 18779, 264, 1185, 1943, 380, 5145, 257, 2176, 1090, 12, 1479, 5194, 849, 5055, 295, 264, 1791, 11, 558, 30, 50720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14935762156610904, "compression_ratio": 1.569811320754717, "no_speech_prob": 2.108831121880317e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 21952, "start": 226.70000000000002, "end": 226.84, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50724, 865, 13, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14935762156610904, "compression_ratio": 1.569811320754717, "no_speech_prob": 2.108831121880317e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 21952, "start": 226.94, "end": 228.74, "text": " It's just keeping a skeletal footprint.", "tokens": [50736, 467, 311, 445, 5145, 257, 32321, 304, 24222, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14935762156610904, "compression_ratio": 1.569811320754717, "no_speech_prob": 2.108831121880317e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 21952, "start": 229.06, "end": 229.76000000000002, "text": " Yeah, exactly.", "tokens": [50842, 865, 11, 2293, 13, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14935762156610904, "compression_ratio": 1.569811320754717, "no_speech_prob": 2.108831121880317e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 21952, "start": 229.88, "end": 235.0, "text": " Just enough of a trace so that the past can be reconstructed on the fly when the organism needs it.", "tokens": [50883, 1449, 1547, 295, 257, 13508, 370, 300, 264, 1791, 393, 312, 31499, 292, 322, 264, 3603, 562, 264, 24128, 2203, 309, 13, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14935762156610904, "compression_ratio": 1.569811320754717, "no_speech_prob": 2.108831121880317e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 21952, "start": 235.16000000000003, "end": 235.48000000000002, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51147, 1079, 13, 51163], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14935762156610904, "compression_ratio": 1.569811320754717, "no_speech_prob": 2.108831121880317e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 21952, "start": 235.72, "end": 237.54000000000002, "text": " Consider Michael Levin's argument here.", "tokens": [51175, 17416, 5116, 1456, 4796, 311, 6770, 510, 13, 51266], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14935762156610904, "compression_ratio": 1.569811320754717, "no_speech_prob": 2.108831121880317e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 21952, "start": 238.02, "end": 242.62, "text": " He asserts that a living system never actually has access to its own past.", "tokens": [51290, 634, 19810, 82, 300, 257, 2647, 1185, 1128, 767, 575, 2105, 281, 1080, 1065, 1791, 13, 51520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14935762156610904, "compression_ratio": 1.569811320754717, "no_speech_prob": 2.108831121880317e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 24262, "start": 242.62, "end": 246.66, "text": " Which sounds completely paradoxical because we feel like we remember things all the time.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 3263, 2584, 26221, 804, 570, 321, 841, 411, 321, 1604, 721, 439, 264, 565, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14679847979078106, "compression_ratio": 1.683127572016461, "no_speech_prob": 1.890632832582395e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 24262, "start": 246.86, "end": 246.94, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50577, 1779, 13, 50581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14679847979078106, "compression_ratio": 1.683127572016461, "no_speech_prob": 1.890632832582395e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 24262, "start": 247.0, "end": 249.20000000000002, "text": " But his point is that you don't have the past itself.", "tokens": [50584, 583, 702, 935, 307, 300, 291, 500, 380, 362, 264, 1791, 2564, 13, 50694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14679847979078106, "compression_ratio": 1.683127572016461, "no_speech_prob": 1.890632832582395e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 24262, "start": 249.3, "end": 250.14000000000001, "text": " You only have traces.", "tokens": [50699, 509, 787, 362, 26076, 13, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14679847979078106, "compression_ratio": 1.683127572016461, "no_speech_prob": 1.890632832582395e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 24262, "start": 250.4, "end": 253.3, "text": " You have basically messages from your past self.", "tokens": [50754, 509, 362, 1936, 7897, 490, 428, 1791, 2698, 13, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14679847979078106, "compression_ratio": 1.683127572016461, "no_speech_prob": 1.890632832582395e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 24262, "start": 253.4, "end": 253.86, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [50904, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14679847979078106, "compression_ratio": 1.683127572016461, "no_speech_prob": 1.890632832582395e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 24262, "start": 254.36, "end": 262.12, "text": " And because the brain is constantly rewiring itself, the you that is reading the message today is physically different from the you that wrote the message yesterday.", "tokens": [50952, 400, 570, 264, 3567, 307, 6460, 319, 86, 5057, 2564, 11, 264, 291, 300, 307, 3760, 264, 3636, 965, 307, 9762, 819, 490, 264, 291, 300, 4114, 264, 3636, 5186, 13, 51340], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14679847979078106, "compression_ratio": 1.683127572016461, "no_speech_prob": 1.890632832582395e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 24262, "start": 262.64, "end": 263.08, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51366, 48746, 736, 13, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14679847979078106, "compression_ratio": 1.683127572016461, "no_speech_prob": 1.890632832582395e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 26308, "start": 263.08, "end": 270.71999999999997, "text": " So rather than optimizing for the perfect storage of the trace, evolution optimized for the creativity of the reading.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 2831, 813, 40425, 337, 264, 2176, 6725, 295, 264, 13508, 11, 9303, 26941, 337, 264, 12915, 295, 264, 3760, 13, 50747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853686226738824, "compression_ratio": 1.628, "no_speech_prob": 1.649044832977009e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 26308, "start": 271.09999999999997, "end": 274.52, "text": " Meaning biological memory preserves salience over fidelity.", "tokens": [50766, 19948, 13910, 4675, 1183, 9054, 1845, 1182, 670, 46404, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853686226738824, "compression_ratio": 1.628, "no_speech_prob": 1.649044832977009e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 26308, "start": 274.76, "end": 275.14, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50949, 7587, 13, 50968], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853686226738824, "compression_ratio": 1.628, "no_speech_prob": 1.649044832977009e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 26308, "start": 275.68, "end": 281.59999999999997, "text": " It cares deeply about what the trace implies for your survival right now in this current environment.", "tokens": [50995, 467, 12310, 8760, 466, 437, 264, 13508, 18779, 337, 428, 12559, 558, 586, 294, 341, 2190, 2823, 13, 51291], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853686226738824, "compression_ratio": 1.628, "no_speech_prob": 1.649044832977009e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 26308, "start": 281.91999999999996, "end": 286.24, "text": " It doesn't obsess over the exact pixel-perfect details of the original event.", "tokens": [51307, 467, 1177, 380, 35803, 670, 264, 1900, 19261, 12, 610, 1836, 4365, 295, 264, 3380, 2280, 13, 51523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853686226738824, "compression_ratio": 1.628, "no_speech_prob": 1.649044832977009e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 26308, "start": 286.32, "end": 288.06, "text": " So the organism is its own interpreter.", "tokens": [51527, 407, 264, 24128, 307, 1080, 1065, 34132, 13, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853686226738824, "compression_ratio": 1.628, "no_speech_prob": 1.649044832977009e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 28806, "start": 288.06, "end": 295.54, "text": " There's no external software reading the brain's hard drive because the brain is the hard drive, the software, and the user all at once.", "tokens": [50365, 821, 311, 572, 8320, 4722, 3760, 264, 3567, 311, 1152, 3332, 570, 264, 3567, 307, 264, 1152, 3332, 11, 264, 4722, 11, 293, 264, 4195, 439, 412, 1564, 13, 50739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1453903763382523, "compression_ratio": 1.7328767123287672, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250605040288077e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 28806, "start": 295.66, "end": 295.9, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50745, 1079, 13, 50757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1453903763382523, "compression_ratio": 1.7328767123287672, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250605040288077e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 28806, "start": 296.06, "end": 299.56, "text": " It has to look at its own internal traces and decide what they mean today.", "tokens": [50765, 467, 575, 281, 574, 412, 1080, 1065, 6920, 26076, 293, 4536, 437, 436, 914, 965, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1453903763382523, "compression_ratio": 1.7328767123287672, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250605040288077e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 28806, "start": 299.68, "end": 302.94, "text": " And the essay brings up an example of this that absolutely blew my mind.", "tokens": [50946, 400, 264, 16238, 5607, 493, 364, 1365, 295, 341, 300, 3122, 19075, 452, 1575, 13, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1453903763382523, "compression_ratio": 1.7328767123287672, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250605040288077e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 28806, "start": 303.38, "end": 308.32, "text": " When we think of a biological system reading a trace or a code, the ultimate example is DNA.", "tokens": [51131, 1133, 321, 519, 295, 257, 13910, 1185, 3760, 257, 13508, 420, 257, 3089, 11, 264, 9705, 1365, 307, 8272, 13, 51378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1453903763382523, "compression_ratio": 1.7328767123287672, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250605040288077e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 28806, "start": 308.58, "end": 308.76, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51391, 1779, 13, 51400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1453903763382523, "compression_ratio": 1.7328767123287672, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250605040288077e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 28806, "start": 308.76, "end": 308.94, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51400, 1779, 13, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1453903763382523, "compression_ratio": 1.7328767123287672, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250605040288077e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 28806, "start": 309.04, "end": 309.88, "text": " The classic blueprint.", "tokens": [51414, 440, 7230, 35868, 13, 51456], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1453903763382523, "compression_ratio": 1.7328767123287672, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250605040288077e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 28806, "start": 310.3, "end": 310.52, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51477, 865, 13, 51488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1453903763382523, "compression_ratio": 1.7328767123287672, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250605040288077e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 28806, "start": 310.62, "end": 313.64, "text": " We are all taught in high school biology that the genome is a blueprint.", "tokens": [51493, 492, 366, 439, 5928, 294, 1090, 1395, 14956, 300, 264, 21953, 307, 257, 35868, 13, 51644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1453903763382523, "compression_ratio": 1.7328767123287672, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250605040288077e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 28806, "start": 313.9, "end": 314.22, "text": " Uh-huh.", "tokens": [51657, 4019, 12, 18710, 13, 51673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1453903763382523, "compression_ratio": 1.7328767123287672, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250605040288077e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 31422, "start": 314.22, "end": 321.88000000000005, "text": " But, Fliction points out that this interpretation over fidelity principle exists right there at the foundational level of developmental biology.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 11, 3235, 4105, 2793, 484, 300, 341, 14174, 670, 46404, 8665, 8198, 558, 456, 412, 264, 32195, 1496, 295, 30160, 14956, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10163522683657132, "compression_ratio": 1.6338983050847458, "no_speech_prob": 1.912906898854372e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 31422, "start": 322.24, "end": 328.66, "text": " What's fascinating here is that the clearest evidence isn't even in something complex, like a caterpillar turning into a butterfly.", "tokens": [50766, 708, 311, 10343, 510, 307, 300, 264, 1233, 17363, 4467, 1943, 380, 754, 294, 746, 3997, 11, 411, 257, 44982, 30635, 6246, 666, 257, 22140, 13, 51087], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10163522683657132, "compression_ratio": 1.6338983050847458, "no_speech_prob": 1.912906898854372e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 31422, "start": 329.08000000000004, "end": 333.8, "text": " It's an ordinary embryogenesis compared to the formation of anthrobots.", "tokens": [51108, 467, 311, 364, 10547, 31588, 8799, 9374, 5347, 281, 264, 11723, 295, 25820, 16614, 1971, 13, 51344], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10163522683657132, "compression_ratio": 1.6338983050847458, "no_speech_prob": 1.912906898854372e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 31422, "start": 333.90000000000003, "end": 339.56, "text": " Okay, we have to break down anthrobots because this is where the blueprint metaphor just completely collapses for me.", "tokens": [51349, 1033, 11, 321, 362, 281, 1821, 760, 25820, 16614, 1971, 570, 341, 307, 689, 264, 35868, 19157, 445, 2584, 48765, 337, 385, 13, 51632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10163522683657132, "compression_ratio": 1.6338983050847458, "no_speech_prob": 1.912906898854372e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 31422, "start": 339.64000000000004, "end": 340.26000000000005, "text": " It really does.", "tokens": [51636, 467, 534, 775, 13, 51667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10163522683657132, "compression_ratio": 1.6338983050847458, "no_speech_prob": 1.912906898854372e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 34026, "start": 340.26, "end": 352.42, "text": " So, anthrobots are these novel self-assembling biological robots, and they are created entirely from ordinary human tracheal cells, windpipe cells.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 25820, 16614, 1971, 366, 613, 7613, 2698, 12, 29386, 1688, 13910, 14733, 11, 293, 436, 366, 2942, 7696, 490, 10547, 1952, 504, 6000, 304, 5438, 11, 2468, 50042, 5438, 13, 50973], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11601264136178153, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 1.769161748522985e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 34026, "start": 352.58, "end": 352.9, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50981, 1779, 13, 50997], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11601264136178153, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 1.769161748522985e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 34026, "start": 353.0, "end": 356.2, "text": " So, normally you have standard human embryogenesis.", "tokens": [51002, 407, 11, 5646, 291, 362, 3832, 1952, 31588, 8799, 9374, 13, 51162], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11601264136178153, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 1.769161748522985e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 34026, "start": 356.34, "end": 362.32, "text": " A cell divides, follows its pathway, and eventually forms a human being with skin, organs, a brain.", "tokens": [51169, 316, 2815, 41347, 11, 10002, 1080, 18590, 11, 293, 4728, 6422, 257, 1952, 885, 365, 3178, 11, 20659, 11, 257, 3567, 13, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11601264136178153, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 1.769161748522985e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 34026, "start": 362.38, "end": 363.12, "text": " And a windpipe, yeah.", "tokens": [51471, 400, 257, 2468, 50042, 11, 1338, 13, 51508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11601264136178153, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 1.769161748522985e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 34026, "start": 363.32, "end": 365.15999999999997, "text": " But on the other hand, you have these anthrobots.", "tokens": [51518, 583, 322, 264, 661, 1011, 11, 291, 362, 613, 25820, 16614, 1971, 13, 51610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11601264136178153, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 1.769161748522985e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 34026, "start": 365.3, "end": 368.32, "text": " They are multicellular structures that use cilia to move around.", "tokens": [51617, 814, 366, 2120, 573, 285, 1040, 9227, 300, 764, 269, 24169, 281, 1286, 926, 13, 51768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11601264136178153, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 1.769161748522985e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 34026, "start": 368.46, "end": 369.59999999999997, "text": " They can navigate mazes.", "tokens": [51775, 814, 393, 12350, 463, 12214, 13, 51832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11601264136178153, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 1.769161748522985e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 36960, "start": 369.6, "end": 370.12, "text": " Wait, really?", "tokens": [50365, 3802, 11, 534, 30, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15743547144944106, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733240649161266e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 36960, "start": 370.18, "end": 370.72, "text": " They run mazes?", "tokens": [50394, 814, 1190, 463, 12214, 30, 50421], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15743547144944106, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733240649161266e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 36960, "start": 370.94, "end": 371.32000000000005, "text": " They do.", "tokens": [50432, 814, 360, 13, 50451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15743547144944106, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733240649161266e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 36960, "start": 371.48, "end": 376.22, "text": " They behave in entirely novel ways, and they do not look or act anything like a human windpipe.", "tokens": [50459, 814, 15158, 294, 7696, 7613, 2098, 11, 293, 436, 360, 406, 574, 420, 605, 1340, 411, 257, 1952, 2468, 50042, 13, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15743547144944106, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733240649161266e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 36960, "start": 376.3, "end": 381.20000000000005, "text": " But, and this is the kicker, they start with materially identical genetic information.", "tokens": [50700, 583, 11, 293, 341, 307, 264, 4437, 260, 11, 436, 722, 365, 2389, 2270, 14800, 12462, 1589, 13, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15743547144944106, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733240649161266e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 36960, "start": 381.34000000000003, "end": 382.24, "text": " Exactly identical.", "tokens": [50952, 7587, 14800, 13, 50997], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15743547144944106, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733240649161266e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 36960, "start": 382.46000000000004, "end": 389.34000000000003, "text": " The anthrobot has the exact same genome, the exact same DNA sequence, as a normal human cell.", "tokens": [51008, 440, 25820, 16614, 310, 575, 264, 1900, 912, 21953, 11, 264, 1900, 912, 8272, 8310, 11, 382, 257, 2710, 1952, 2815, 13, 51352], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15743547144944106, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733240649161266e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 36960, "start": 390.18, "end": 391.68, "text": " The trace is identical.", "tokens": [51394, 440, 13508, 307, 14800, 13, 51469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15743547144944106, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733240649161266e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 36960, "start": 392.40000000000003, "end": 394.18, "text": " The message from the past is the same.", "tokens": [51505, 440, 3636, 490, 264, 1791, 307, 264, 912, 13, 51594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15743547144944106, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733240649161266e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 36960, "start": 394.40000000000003, "end": 397.16, "text": " Yet they diverge into completely different anatomies.", "tokens": [51605, 10890, 436, 18558, 432, 666, 2584, 819, 21618, 298, 530, 13, 51743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15743547144944106, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733240649161266e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 39716, "start": 397.16, "end": 402.12, "text": " Thousands of genes are expressed differently between the human embryo and the anthrobot.", "tokens": [50365, 40535, 295, 14424, 366, 12675, 7614, 1296, 264, 1952, 31588, 78, 293, 264, 25820, 16614, 310, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16011388802234036, "compression_ratio": 1.5260663507109005, "no_speech_prob": 1.714480662474982e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 39716, "start": 402.20000000000005, "end": 404.54, "text": " But nothing about the genome itself mutated, right?", "tokens": [50617, 583, 1825, 466, 264, 21953, 2564, 5839, 770, 11, 558, 30, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16011388802234036, "compression_ratio": 1.5260663507109005, "no_speech_prob": 1.714480662474982e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 39716, "start": 404.62, "end": 406.40000000000003, "text": " No, not a single letter scrambled.", "tokens": [50738, 883, 11, 406, 257, 2167, 5063, 49127, 13, 50827], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16011388802234036, "compression_ratio": 1.5260663507109005, "no_speech_prob": 1.714480662474982e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 39716, "start": 406.72, "end": 411.06, "text": " What changed was the interpretive context in which that trace was read.", "tokens": [50843, 708, 3105, 390, 264, 7302, 488, 4319, 294, 597, 300, 13508, 390, 1401, 13, 51060], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16011388802234036, "compression_ratio": 1.5260663507109005, "no_speech_prob": 1.714480662474982e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 39716, "start": 411.18, "end": 412.5, "text": " The environment changed.", "tokens": [51066, 440, 2823, 3105, 13, 51132], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16011388802234036, "compression_ratio": 1.5260663507109005, "no_speech_prob": 1.714480662474982e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 39716, "start": 412.94000000000005, "end": 414.64000000000004, "text": " The cell was placed in a different context.", "tokens": [51154, 440, 2815, 390, 7074, 294, 257, 819, 4319, 13, 51239], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16011388802234036, "compression_ratio": 1.5260663507109005, "no_speech_prob": 1.714480662474982e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 39716, "start": 414.94000000000005, "end": 415.08000000000004, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51254, 865, 13, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16011388802234036, "compression_ratio": 1.5260663507109005, "no_speech_prob": 1.714480662474982e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 41508, "start": 415.08, "end": 420.08, "text": " And it looked at the exact same genetic code and basically built a crawling robot instead", "tokens": [50365, 400, 309, 2956, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 12462, 3089, 293, 1936, 3094, 257, 32979, 7881, 2602, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13890354529671048, "compression_ratio": 1.5991189427312775, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722199154215687e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 41508, "start": 420.08, "end": 420.76, "text": " of a windpipe.", "tokens": [50615, 295, 257, 2468, 50042, 13, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13890354529671048, "compression_ratio": 1.5991189427312775, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722199154215687e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 41508, "start": 421.0, "end": 422.03999999999996, "text": " Yeah, exactly.", "tokens": [50661, 865, 11, 2293, 13, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13890354529671048, "compression_ratio": 1.5991189427312775, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722199154215687e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 41508, "start": 422.15999999999997, "end": 427.09999999999997, "text": " Which is wild, because if I hand a blueprint for a house to a construction crew, and they", "tokens": [50719, 3013, 307, 4868, 11, 570, 498, 286, 1011, 257, 35868, 337, 257, 1782, 281, 257, 6435, 7260, 11, 293, 436, 50966], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13890354529671048, "compression_ratio": 1.5991189427312775, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722199154215687e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 41508, "start": 427.09999999999997, "end": 430.06, "text": " use those exact instructions to build a submarine, they failed.", "tokens": [50966, 764, 729, 1900, 9415, 281, 1322, 257, 33995, 11, 436, 7612, 13, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13890354529671048, "compression_ratio": 1.5991189427312775, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722199154215687e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 41508, "start": 430.7, "end": 433.06, "text": " The blueprint is objectively wrong for a submarine.", "tokens": [51146, 440, 35868, 307, 46067, 2085, 337, 257, 33995, 13, 51264], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13890354529671048, "compression_ratio": 1.5991189427312775, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722199154215687e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 41508, "start": 433.2, "end": 433.36, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51271, 1779, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13890354529671048, "compression_ratio": 1.5991189427312775, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722199154215687e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 41508, "start": 433.41999999999996, "end": 434.65999999999997, "text": " The engineer would be furious.", "tokens": [51282, 440, 11403, 576, 312, 33470, 13, 51344], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13890354529671048, "compression_ratio": 1.5991189427312775, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722199154215687e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 43466, "start": 434.66, "end": 436.36, "text": " But biology doesn't fail here.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 14956, 1177, 380, 3061, 510, 13, 50450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12115569230986804, "compression_ratio": 1.6254295532646048, "no_speech_prob": 1.531075721934727e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 43466, "start": 436.54, "end": 437.22, "text": " It adapts.", "tokens": [50459, 467, 23169, 1373, 13, 50493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12115569230986804, "compression_ratio": 1.6254295532646048, "no_speech_prob": 1.531075721934727e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 43466, "start": 437.8, "end": 441.36, "text": " Fliction calls the genome a heavily underdetermined musical score.", "tokens": [50522, 3235, 4105, 5498, 264, 21953, 257, 10950, 833, 49136, 2001, 9165, 6175, 13, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12115569230986804, "compression_ratio": 1.6254295532646048, "no_speech_prob": 1.531075721934727e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 43466, "start": 441.48, "end": 443.12, "text": " I find that to be a stunning analogy.", "tokens": [50706, 286, 915, 300, 281, 312, 257, 18550, 21663, 13, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12115569230986804, "compression_ratio": 1.6254295532646048, "no_speech_prob": 1.531075721934727e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 43466, "start": 443.38000000000005, "end": 446.82000000000005, "text": " Think of a piece of sheet music composed by Bach in the 1700s.", "tokens": [50801, 6557, 295, 257, 2522, 295, 8193, 1318, 18204, 538, 30920, 294, 264, 43373, 82, 13, 50973], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12115569230986804, "compression_ratio": 1.6254295532646048, "no_speech_prob": 1.531075721934727e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 43466, "start": 446.92, "end": 448.92, "text": " The notes on the page represent the trace.", "tokens": [50978, 440, 5570, 322, 264, 3028, 2906, 264, 13508, 13, 51078], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12115569230986804, "compression_ratio": 1.6254295532646048, "no_speech_prob": 1.531075721934727e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 43466, "start": 449.34000000000003, "end": 454.6, "text": " But handing that score to a classical orchestra playing in a grand concert hall will result in", "tokens": [51099, 583, 34774, 300, 6175, 281, 257, 13735, 25280, 2433, 294, 257, 2697, 8543, 6500, 486, 1874, 294, 51362], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12115569230986804, "compression_ratio": 1.6254295532646048, "no_speech_prob": 1.531075721934727e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 43466, "start": 454.6, "end": 460.24, "text": " a radically different realization than handing that same score to a jazz quartet in a cramped", "tokens": [51362, 257, 35508, 819, 25138, 813, 34774, 300, 912, 6175, 281, 257, 15066, 20837, 302, 294, 257, 941, 36970, 51644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12115569230986804, "compression_ratio": 1.6254295532646048, "no_speech_prob": 1.531075721934727e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 43466, "start": 460.24, "end": 461.08000000000004, "text": " basement club.", "tokens": [51644, 16893, 6482, 13, 51686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12115569230986804, "compression_ratio": 1.6254295532646048, "no_speech_prob": 1.531075721934727e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 43466, "start": 461.22, "end": 461.96000000000004, "text": " Oh, I like that.", "tokens": [51693, 876, 11, 286, 411, 300, 13, 51730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12115569230986804, "compression_ratio": 1.6254295532646048, "no_speech_prob": 1.531075721934727e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 46196, "start": 461.96, "end": 467.23999999999995, "text": " The jazz musicians might swing the rhythm, alter the tempo, maybe improvise over the", "tokens": [50365, 440, 15066, 16916, 1062, 11173, 264, 11801, 11, 11337, 264, 8972, 11, 1310, 29424, 908, 670, 264, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15214274754034024, "compression_ratio": 1.654109589041096, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984644163857809e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 46196, "start": 467.23999999999995, "end": 467.88, "text": " chord structure.", "tokens": [50629, 14137, 3877, 13, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15214274754034024, "compression_ratio": 1.654109589041096, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984644163857809e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 46196, "start": 468.09999999999997, "end": 470.62, "text": " And the classical musicians will play it with rigid precision.", "tokens": [50672, 400, 264, 13735, 16916, 486, 862, 309, 365, 22195, 18356, 13, 50798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15214274754034024, "compression_ratio": 1.654109589041096, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984644163857809e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 46196, "start": 470.84, "end": 475.97999999999996, "text": " They sound completely different, but both are entirely valid interpretations of the original", "tokens": [50809, 814, 1626, 2584, 819, 11, 457, 1293, 366, 7696, 7363, 37547, 295, 264, 3380, 51066], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15214274754034024, "compression_ratio": 1.654109589041096, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984644163857809e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 46196, "start": 475.97999999999996, "end": 476.41999999999996, "text": " trace.", "tokens": [51066, 13508, 13, 51088], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15214274754034024, "compression_ratio": 1.654109589041096, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984644163857809e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 46196, "start": 477.09999999999997, "end": 481.29999999999995, "text": " Neither performance is trivialized as the correct reading of the ink on the page.", "tokens": [51122, 23956, 3389, 307, 26703, 1602, 382, 264, 3006, 3760, 295, 264, 11276, 322, 264, 3028, 13, 51332], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15214274754034024, "compression_ratio": 1.654109589041096, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984644163857809e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 46196, "start": 481.44, "end": 481.96, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51339, 7587, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15214274754034024, "compression_ratio": 1.654109589041096, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984644163857809e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 46196, "start": 481.96, "end": 486.84, "text": " Because the musicians, much like the biological organism, are reacting to their instruments,", "tokens": [51365, 1436, 264, 16916, 11, 709, 411, 264, 13910, 24128, 11, 366, 25817, 281, 641, 12190, 11, 51609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15214274754034024, "compression_ratio": 1.654109589041096, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984644163857809e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 46196, "start": 487.17999999999995, "end": 488.62, "text": " their audience, their environment.", "tokens": [51626, 641, 4034, 11, 641, 2823, 13, 51698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15214274754034024, "compression_ratio": 1.654109589041096, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984644163857809e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 48862, "start": 488.62, "end": 494.48, "text": " The organism interprets its own traces based on the situation it finds itself in, which", "tokens": [50365, 440, 24128, 17489, 1373, 1080, 1065, 26076, 2361, 322, 264, 2590, 309, 10704, 2564, 294, 11, 597, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09234633737680864, "compression_ratio": 1.6164874551971327, "no_speech_prob": 1.655510255792192e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 48862, "start": 494.48, "end": 499.26, "text": " honestly is a monumental departure from how we conceptualize and build artificial machines", "tokens": [50658, 6095, 307, 257, 43105, 25866, 490, 577, 321, 24106, 1125, 293, 1322, 11677, 8379, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09234633737680864, "compression_ratio": 1.6164874551971327, "no_speech_prob": 1.655510255792192e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 48862, "start": 499.26, "end": 499.64, "text": " today.", "tokens": [50897, 965, 13, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09234633737680864, "compression_ratio": 1.6164874551971327, "no_speech_prob": 1.655510255792192e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 48862, "start": 499.82, "end": 501.18, "text": " It is a totally different paradigm.", "tokens": [50925, 467, 307, 257, 3879, 819, 24709, 13, 50993], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09234633737680864, "compression_ratio": 1.6164874551971327, "no_speech_prob": 1.655510255792192e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 48862, "start": 501.32, "end": 502.82, "text": " Which opens up a massive question.", "tokens": [51000, 3013, 9870, 493, 257, 5994, 1168, 13, 51075], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09234633737680864, "compression_ratio": 1.6164874551971327, "no_speech_prob": 1.655510255792192e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 48862, "start": 503.64, "end": 508.62, "text": " If biological intelligence is fundamentally defined by this creative, situational, highly", "tokens": [51116, 759, 13910, 7599, 307, 17879, 7642, 538, 341, 5880, 11, 2054, 1478, 11, 5405, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09234633737680864, "compression_ratio": 1.6164874551971327, "no_speech_prob": 1.655510255792192e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 48862, "start": 508.62, "end": 513.38, "text": " contextual interpretation of traces, how does that reflect on the AI systems we interact", "tokens": [51365, 35526, 14174, 295, 26076, 11, 577, 775, 300, 5031, 322, 264, 7318, 3652, 321, 4648, 51603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09234633737680864, "compression_ratio": 1.6164874551971327, "no_speech_prob": 1.655510255792192e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 48862, "start": 513.38, "end": 514.04, "text": " with every day?", "tokens": [51603, 365, 633, 786, 30, 51636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09234633737680864, "compression_ratio": 1.6164874551971327, "no_speech_prob": 1.655510255792192e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 51404, "start": 514.04, "end": 518.8, "text": " The systems that completely lack this biological squishiness.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3652, 300, 2584, 5011, 341, 13910, 31379, 1324, 13, 50603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1570351182921859, "compression_ratio": 1.6174496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754513137457906e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 51404, "start": 519.0, "end": 519.0999999999999, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50613, 865, 13, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1570351182921859, "compression_ratio": 1.6174496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754513137457906e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 51404, "start": 519.52, "end": 524.9599999999999, "text": " This is exactly where Flixion pulls in Katrina Schleisman's work on the stark contrast between", "tokens": [50639, 639, 307, 2293, 689, 3235, 970, 313, 16982, 294, 42550, 2065, 306, 1434, 282, 311, 589, 322, 264, 17417, 8712, 1296, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1570351182921859, "compression_ratio": 1.6174496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754513137457906e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 51404, "start": 524.9599999999999, "end": 529.4, "text": " biological memory and large language models, or LLMs.", "tokens": [50911, 13910, 4675, 293, 2416, 2856, 5245, 11, 420, 441, 43, 26386, 13, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1570351182921859, "compression_ratio": 1.6174496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754513137457906e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 51404, "start": 529.54, "end": 529.76, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51140, 1779, 13, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1570351182921859, "compression_ratio": 1.6174496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754513137457906e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 51404, "start": 529.9, "end": 534.76, "text": " And Schleisman draws a very sharp boundary here between semantic memory and episodic memory.", "tokens": [51158, 400, 2065, 306, 1434, 282, 20045, 257, 588, 8199, 12866, 510, 1296, 47982, 4675, 293, 39200, 299, 4675, 13, 51401], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1570351182921859, "compression_ratio": 1.6174496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754513137457906e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 51404, "start": 534.9399999999999, "end": 535.74, "text": " Let's define those.", "tokens": [51410, 961, 311, 6964, 729, 13, 51450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1570351182921859, "compression_ratio": 1.6174496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754513137457906e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 51404, "start": 535.98, "end": 536.0799999999999, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51462, 3153, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1570351182921859, "compression_ratio": 1.6174496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754513137457906e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 51404, "start": 536.0799999999999, "end": 538.0799999999999, "text": " Because that distinction is crucial for the listener.", "tokens": [51467, 1436, 300, 16844, 307, 11462, 337, 264, 31569, 13, 51567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1570351182921859, "compression_ratio": 1.6174496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754513137457906e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 51404, "start": 538.56, "end": 543.52, "text": " Semantic memory is your repository of general abstracted facts about the world, right?", "tokens": [51591, 14421, 7128, 4675, 307, 428, 25841, 295, 2674, 12649, 292, 9130, 466, 264, 1002, 11, 558, 30, 51839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1570351182921859, "compression_ratio": 1.6174496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754513137457906e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 54352, "start": 543.52, "end": 543.88, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11526042659108232, "compression_ratio": 1.6568627450980393, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396434549317053e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 54352, "start": 544.4, "end": 549.22, "text": " It's knowing that Paris is the capital of France, or that water boils at 100 degrees", "tokens": [50409, 467, 311, 5276, 300, 8380, 307, 264, 4238, 295, 6190, 11, 420, 300, 1281, 35049, 412, 2319, 5310, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11526042659108232, "compression_ratio": 1.6568627450980393, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396434549317053e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 54352, "start": 549.22, "end": 549.62, "text": " Celsius.", "tokens": [50650, 22658, 13, 50670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11526042659108232, "compression_ratio": 1.6568627450980393, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396434549317053e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 54352, "start": 549.98, "end": 554.02, "text": " And you probably don't remember the exact moment, the lighting in the classroom or what you were", "tokens": [50688, 400, 291, 1391, 500, 380, 1604, 264, 1900, 1623, 11, 264, 9577, 294, 264, 7419, 420, 437, 291, 645, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11526042659108232, "compression_ratio": 1.6568627450980393, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396434549317053e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 54352, "start": 554.02, "end": 555.78, "text": " wearing when you first learned about water boiling.", "tokens": [50890, 4769, 562, 291, 700, 3264, 466, 1281, 16208, 13, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11526042659108232, "compression_ratio": 1.6568627450980393, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396434549317053e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 54352, "start": 555.84, "end": 556.28, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50981, 7587, 13, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11526042659108232, "compression_ratio": 1.6568627450980393, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396434549317053e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 54352, "start": 556.4399999999999, "end": 559.9, "text": " The fact has been totally decontextualized from the experience of learning it.", "tokens": [51011, 440, 1186, 575, 668, 3879, 979, 896, 3828, 901, 1602, 490, 264, 1752, 295, 2539, 309, 13, 51184], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11526042659108232, "compression_ratio": 1.6568627450980393, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396434549317053e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 54352, "start": 560.26, "end": 562.04, "text": " It's just a raw fact now.", "tokens": [51202, 467, 311, 445, 257, 8936, 1186, 586, 13, 51291], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11526042659108232, "compression_ratio": 1.6568627450980393, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396434549317053e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 54352, "start": 562.36, "end": 567.34, "text": " But on the other hand, episodic memory is the cognitive process of storing and creatively", "tokens": [51307, 583, 322, 264, 661, 1011, 11, 39200, 299, 4675, 307, 264, 15605, 1399, 295, 26085, 293, 43750, 51556], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11526042659108232, "compression_ratio": 1.6568627450980393, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396434549317053e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 54352, "start": 567.34, "end": 571.12, "text": " constructing memories of specific situated experiences.", "tokens": [51556, 39969, 8495, 295, 2685, 30143, 5235, 13, 51745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11526042659108232, "compression_ratio": 1.6568627450980393, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396434549317053e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 57112, "start": 571.12, "end": 575.74, "text": " It's remembering your 10th birthday party, recalling the smell of the icing, the feeling", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 20719, 428, 1266, 392, 6154, 3595, 11, 9901, 278, 264, 4316, 295, 264, 30086, 11, 264, 2633, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12833988189697265, "compression_ratio": 1.517509727626459, "no_speech_prob": 1.661987604831272e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 57112, "start": 575.74, "end": 579.26, "text": " of the chair, the specific social dynamics of who was sitting next to you.", "tokens": [50596, 295, 264, 6090, 11, 264, 2685, 2093, 15679, 295, 567, 390, 3798, 958, 281, 291, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12833988189697265, "compression_ratio": 1.517509727626459, "no_speech_prob": 1.661987604831272e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 57112, "start": 579.6, "end": 582.24, "text": " It is intrinsically tied to a lived episode.", "tokens": [50789, 467, 307, 28621, 984, 9601, 281, 257, 5152, 3500, 13, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12833988189697265, "compression_ratio": 1.517509727626459, "no_speech_prob": 1.661987604831272e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 57112, "start": 582.72, "end": 587.82, "text": " And Schleisman points out that current large language models operate almost exclusively on", "tokens": [50945, 400, 2065, 306, 1434, 282, 2793, 484, 300, 2190, 2416, 2856, 5245, 9651, 1920, 20638, 322, 51200], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12833988189697265, "compression_ratio": 1.517509727626459, "no_speech_prob": 1.661987604831272e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 57112, "start": 587.82, "end": 588.7, "text": " semantic memory.", "tokens": [51200, 47982, 4675, 13, 51244], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12833988189697265, "compression_ratio": 1.517509727626459, "no_speech_prob": 1.661987604831272e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 57112, "start": 588.94, "end": 589.16, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51256, 1779, 13, 51267], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12833988189697265, "compression_ratio": 1.517509727626459, "no_speech_prob": 1.661987604831272e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 57112, "start": 589.5600000000001, "end": 593.16, "text": " Under the hood, an LLM relies on what's called an embedding space.", "tokens": [51287, 6974, 264, 13376, 11, 364, 441, 43, 44, 30910, 322, 437, 311, 1219, 364, 12240, 3584, 1901, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12833988189697265, "compression_ratio": 1.517509727626459, "no_speech_prob": 1.661987604831272e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 59316, "start": 593.16, "end": 600.1, "text": " And Schleisman describes this embedding space as a compressed, hyper-dense, and completely", "tokens": [50365, 400, 2065, 306, 1434, 282, 15626, 341, 12240, 3584, 1901, 382, 257, 30353, 11, 9848, 12, 67, 1288, 11, 293, 2584, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1149866749921183, "compression_ratio": 1.6384364820846906, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674077704155853e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 59316, "start": 600.1, "end": 603.0, "text": " decontextualized store of general knowledge.", "tokens": [50712, 979, 896, 3828, 901, 1602, 3531, 295, 2674, 3601, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1149866749921183, "compression_ratio": 1.6384364820846906, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674077704155853e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 59316, "start": 603.06, "end": 603.26, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50860, 865, 13, 50870], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1149866749921183, "compression_ratio": 1.6384364820846906, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674077704155853e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 59316, "start": 603.38, "end": 606.78, "text": " It basically maps how concepts relate to one another mathematically.", "tokens": [50876, 467, 1936, 11317, 577, 10392, 10961, 281, 472, 1071, 44003, 13, 51046], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1149866749921183, "compression_ratio": 1.6384364820846906, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674077704155853e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 59316, "start": 607.14, "end": 611.64, "text": " It knows that the vector for king relates to queen in the same way that man relates to", "tokens": [51064, 467, 3255, 300, 264, 8062, 337, 4867, 16155, 281, 12206, 294, 264, 912, 636, 300, 587, 16155, 281, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1149866749921183, "compression_ratio": 1.6384364820846906, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674077704155853e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 59316, "start": 611.64, "end": 611.88, "text": " woman.", "tokens": [51289, 3059, 13, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1149866749921183, "compression_ratio": 1.6384364820846906, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674077704155853e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 59316, "start": 611.88, "end": 617.0, "text": " But it has absolutely no record of what happened to it, when it happened, or under what specific", "tokens": [51301, 583, 309, 575, 3122, 572, 2136, 295, 437, 2011, 281, 309, 11, 562, 309, 2011, 11, 420, 833, 437, 2685, 51557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1149866749921183, "compression_ratio": 1.6384364820846906, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674077704155853e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 59316, "start": 617.0, "end": 618.66, "text": " conditions it absorbed that text.", "tokens": [51557, 4487, 309, 20799, 300, 2487, 13, 51640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1149866749921183, "compression_ratio": 1.6384364820846906, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674077704155853e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 59316, "start": 618.6999999999999, "end": 619.14, "text": " Not at all.", "tokens": [51642, 1726, 412, 439, 13, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1149866749921183, "compression_ratio": 1.6384364820846906, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674077704155853e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 59316, "start": 619.1999999999999, "end": 621.26, "text": " It doesn't remember the experience of its own training.", "tokens": [51667, 467, 1177, 380, 1604, 264, 1752, 295, 1080, 1065, 3097, 13, 51770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1149866749921183, "compression_ratio": 1.6384364820846906, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674077704155853e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 62126, "start": 621.26, "end": 623.14, "text": " It doesn't have an episodic layer.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1177, 380, 362, 364, 39200, 299, 4583, 13, 50459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14904870520104896, "compression_ratio": 1.578616352201258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736860599357971e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 62126, "start": 623.46, "end": 623.7, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50475, 1033, 13, 50487], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14904870520104896, "compression_ratio": 1.578616352201258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736860599357971e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 62126, "start": 624.04, "end": 625.56, "text": " I have to push back on this a little bit, though.", "tokens": [50504, 286, 362, 281, 2944, 646, 322, 341, 257, 707, 857, 11, 1673, 13, 50580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14904870520104896, "compression_ratio": 1.578616352201258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736860599357971e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 62126, "start": 625.6, "end": 626.1, "text": " Sure, go ahead.", "tokens": [50582, 4894, 11, 352, 2286, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14904870520104896, "compression_ratio": 1.578616352201258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736860599357971e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 62126, "start": 626.3199999999999, "end": 628.48, "text": " Because I use AI constantly for work.", "tokens": [50618, 1436, 286, 764, 7318, 6460, 337, 589, 13, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14904870520104896, "compression_ratio": 1.578616352201258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736860599357971e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 62126, "start": 628.92, "end": 635.1, "text": " If I take a massive 500-page chat history or a company manual and I dump it into the AI's", "tokens": [50748, 759, 286, 747, 257, 5994, 5923, 12, 15161, 5081, 2503, 420, 257, 2237, 9688, 293, 286, 11430, 309, 666, 264, 7318, 311, 51057], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14904870520104896, "compression_ratio": 1.578616352201258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736860599357971e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 62126, "start": 635.1, "end": 641.28, "text": " context window, or if I use a retrieval augmented generation system, a RAGI system, to let the", "tokens": [51057, 4319, 4910, 11, 420, 498, 286, 764, 257, 19817, 3337, 36155, 5125, 1185, 11, 257, 14626, 26252, 1185, 11, 281, 718, 264, 51366], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14904870520104896, "compression_ratio": 1.578616352201258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736860599357971e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 62126, "start": 641.28, "end": 646.0, "text": " AI search through my past documents, aren't I giving it episodic memory?", "tokens": [51366, 7318, 3164, 807, 452, 1791, 8512, 11, 3212, 380, 286, 2902, 309, 39200, 299, 4675, 30, 51602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14904870520104896, "compression_ratio": 1.578616352201258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736860599357971e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 62126, "start": 646.1, "end": 647.12, "text": " It feels like you are, right?", "tokens": [51607, 467, 3417, 411, 291, 366, 11, 558, 30, 51658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14904870520104896, "compression_ratio": 1.578616352201258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736860599357971e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 62126, "start": 647.42, "end": 647.64, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51673, 865, 13, 51684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14904870520104896, "compression_ratio": 1.578616352201258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736860599357971e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 62126, "start": 648.06, "end": 650.9399999999999, "text": " I'm literally handing it the history of our exact conversation.", "tokens": [51705, 286, 478, 3736, 34774, 309, 264, 2503, 295, 527, 1900, 3761, 13, 51849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14904870520104896, "compression_ratio": 1.578616352201258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736860599357971e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 65094, "start": 650.94, "end": 653.2, "text": " That is the intuitive counter-argument.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 264, 21769, 5682, 12, 33544, 2206, 13, 50478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1586814562479655, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352456076573538e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 65094, "start": 653.36, "end": 653.5600000000001, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50486, 865, 13, 50496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1586814562479655, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352456076573538e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 65094, "start": 653.7, "end": 658.4200000000001, "text": " And Fliction addresses it directly by pointing out that this approach treats the symptom rather", "tokens": [50503, 400, 3235, 4105, 16862, 309, 3838, 538, 12166, 484, 300, 341, 3109, 19566, 264, 29370, 2831, 50739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1586814562479655, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352456076573538e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 65094, "start": 658.4200000000001, "end": 659.2600000000001, "text": " than the structure.", "tokens": [50739, 813, 264, 3877, 13, 50781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1586814562479655, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352456076573538e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 65094, "start": 659.5600000000001, "end": 659.94, "text": " How so?", "tokens": [50796, 1012, 370, 30, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1586814562479655, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352456076573538e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 65094, "start": 660.3000000000001, "end": 665.98, "text": " When you dump a massive chat history into an LLM's context window, you are essentially", "tokens": [50833, 1133, 291, 11430, 257, 5994, 5081, 2503, 666, 364, 441, 43, 44, 311, 4319, 4910, 11, 291, 366, 4476, 51117], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1586814562479655, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352456076573538e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 65094, "start": 665.98, "end": 668.0400000000001, "text": " just pasting text onto a screen.", "tokens": [51117, 445, 1791, 278, 2487, 3911, 257, 2568, 13, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1586814562479655, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352456076573538e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 65094, "start": 668.5600000000001, "end": 674.6, "text": " You are attempting to inject storage-style fidelity into a system that is fundamentally missing", "tokens": [51246, 509, 366, 22001, 281, 10711, 6725, 12, 15014, 46404, 666, 257, 1185, 300, 307, 17879, 5361, 51548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1586814562479655, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352456076573538e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 65094, "start": 674.6, "end": 676.6800000000001, "text": " the architecture of biological memory.", "tokens": [51548, 264, 9482, 295, 13910, 4675, 13, 51652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1586814562479655, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352456076573538e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 65094, "start": 677.1400000000001, "end": 680.48, "text": " But wait, how is pasting the history not giving it a history?", "tokens": [51675, 583, 1699, 11, 577, 307, 1791, 278, 264, 2503, 406, 2902, 309, 257, 2503, 30, 51842], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1586814562479655, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352456076573538e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 68048, "start": 680.48, "end": 683.84, "text": " Because it lacks what Schleisman calls indexicality.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 309, 31132, 437, 2065, 306, 1434, 282, 5498, 8186, 804, 507, 13, 50533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12622155409592847, "compression_ratio": 1.7448275862068965, "no_speech_prob": 1.708052210953881e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 68048, "start": 684.12, "end": 684.84, "text": " Indexicality, okay.", "tokens": [50547, 33552, 804, 507, 11, 1392, 13, 50583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12622155409592847, "compression_ratio": 1.7448275862068965, "no_speech_prob": 1.708052210953881e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 68048, "start": 684.96, "end": 685.08, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50589, 865, 13, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12622155409592847, "compression_ratio": 1.7448275862068965, "no_speech_prob": 1.708052210953881e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 68048, "start": 685.34, "end": 690.6800000000001, "text": " Indexicality means the memory is intrinsically tied to a specific past occasion from the", "tokens": [50608, 33552, 804, 507, 1355, 264, 4675, 307, 28621, 984, 9601, 281, 257, 2685, 1791, 9674, 490, 264, 50875], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12622155409592847, "compression_ratio": 1.7448275862068965, "no_speech_prob": 1.708052210953881e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 68048, "start": 690.6800000000001, "end": 692.4200000000001, "text": " perspective of a continuous self.", "tokens": [50875, 4585, 295, 257, 10957, 2698, 13, 50962], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12622155409592847, "compression_ratio": 1.7448275862068965, "no_speech_prob": 1.708052210953881e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 68048, "start": 692.7, "end": 693.9200000000001, "text": " Ah, continuous self.", "tokens": [50976, 2438, 11, 10957, 2698, 13, 51037], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12622155409592847, "compression_ratio": 1.7448275862068965, "no_speech_prob": 1.708052210953881e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 68048, "start": 694.0, "end": 694.26, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51041, 1779, 13, 51054], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12622155409592847, "compression_ratio": 1.7448275862068965, "no_speech_prob": 1.708052210953881e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 68048, "start": 694.5, "end": 698.78, "text": " When you feed a chat history into an LLM, the model processes that history as just more", "tokens": [51066, 1133, 291, 3154, 257, 5081, 2503, 666, 364, 441, 43, 44, 11, 264, 2316, 7555, 300, 2503, 382, 445, 544, 51280], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12622155409592847, "compression_ratio": 1.7448275862068965, "no_speech_prob": 1.708052210953881e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 68048, "start": 698.78, "end": 701.64, "text": " general semantic data occurring in its present moment.", "tokens": [51280, 2674, 47982, 1412, 18386, 294, 1080, 1974, 1623, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12622155409592847, "compression_ratio": 1.7448275862068965, "no_speech_prob": 1.708052210953881e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 68048, "start": 702.04, "end": 705.0, "text": " It does not experience that history as its own lived past.", "tokens": [51443, 467, 775, 406, 1752, 300, 2503, 382, 1080, 1065, 5152, 1791, 13, 51591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12622155409592847, "compression_ratio": 1.7448275862068965, "no_speech_prob": 1.708052210953881e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 68048, "start": 705.16, "end": 708.44, "text": " So it doesn't creatively interpret that trace based on its own continuity.", "tokens": [51599, 407, 309, 1177, 380, 43750, 7302, 300, 13508, 2361, 322, 1080, 1065, 23807, 13, 51763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12622155409592847, "compression_ratio": 1.7448275862068965, "no_speech_prob": 1.708052210953881e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 70844, "start": 708.44, "end": 709.44, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263303406741641, "compression_ratio": 1.607773851590106, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683238550004644e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 70844, "start": 709.7600000000001, "end": 715.1600000000001, "text": " It's the difference between me remembering the house I grew up in versus me reading a", "tokens": [50431, 467, 311, 264, 2649, 1296, 385, 20719, 264, 1782, 286, 6109, 493, 294, 5717, 385, 3760, 257, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263303406741641, "compression_ratio": 1.607773851590106, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683238550004644e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 70844, "start": 715.1600000000001, "end": 717.0600000000001, "text": " Wikipedia article about a house I used to live in.", "tokens": [50701, 28999, 7222, 466, 257, 1782, 286, 1143, 281, 1621, 294, 13, 50796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263303406741641, "compression_ratio": 1.607773851590106, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683238550004644e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 70844, "start": 717.1600000000001, "end": 717.6600000000001, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [50801, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263303406741641, "compression_ratio": 1.607773851590106, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683238550004644e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 70844, "start": 718.36, "end": 719.1, "text": " That makes sense.", "tokens": [50861, 663, 1669, 2020, 13, 50898], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263303406741641, "compression_ratio": 1.607773851590106, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683238550004644e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 70844, "start": 719.98, "end": 724.6, "text": " One is an episode that physically shaped your neural structure over years, and the other", "tokens": [50942, 1485, 307, 364, 3500, 300, 9762, 13475, 428, 18161, 3877, 670, 924, 11, 293, 264, 661, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263303406741641, "compression_ratio": 1.607773851590106, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683238550004644e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 70844, "start": 724.6, "end": 727.7800000000001, "text": " is just raw data you're processing in the present tense.", "tokens": [51173, 307, 445, 8936, 1412, 291, 434, 9007, 294, 264, 1974, 18760, 13, 51332], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263303406741641, "compression_ratio": 1.607773851590106, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683238550004644e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 70844, "start": 727.9200000000001, "end": 729.74, "text": " That distinction is profound.", "tokens": [51339, 663, 16844, 307, 14382, 13, 51430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263303406741641, "compression_ratio": 1.607773851590106, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683238550004644e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 70844, "start": 730.7, "end": 737.2, "text": " Reading a transcript of an event does not fundamentally rewire your architecture in the way living through", "tokens": [51478, 29766, 257, 24444, 295, 364, 2280, 775, 406, 17879, 319, 42689, 428, 9482, 294, 264, 636, 2647, 807, 51803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263303406741641, "compression_ratio": 1.607773851590106, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683238550004644e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 73720, "start": 737.2, "end": 738.2, "text": " the event does.", "tokens": [50365, 264, 2280, 775, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15419735807053586, "compression_ratio": 1.5405405405405406, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903450853258175e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 73720, "start": 738.2, "end": 742.32, "text": " And that's why Schleisman and her colleague, Eric Davis, have been proposing new algorithmic", "tokens": [50415, 400, 300, 311, 983, 2065, 306, 1434, 282, 293, 720, 13532, 11, 9336, 15658, 11, 362, 668, 29939, 777, 9284, 299, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15419735807053586, "compression_ratio": 1.5405405405405406, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903450853258175e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 73720, "start": 742.32, "end": 747.58, "text": " architectures to integrate episodic and semantic memory directly into an artificial teammate.", "tokens": [50621, 6331, 1303, 281, 13365, 39200, 299, 293, 47982, 4675, 3838, 666, 364, 11677, 25467, 13, 50884], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15419735807053586, "compression_ratio": 1.5405405405405406, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903450853258175e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 73720, "start": 748.0200000000001, "end": 753.22, "text": " Because true episodic recall isn't just a USB drive of retrieved documents you plug into", "tokens": [50906, 1436, 2074, 39200, 299, 9901, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 10109, 3332, 295, 19817, 937, 8512, 291, 5452, 666, 51166], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15419735807053586, "compression_ratio": 1.5405405405405406, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903450853258175e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 73720, "start": 753.22, "end": 754.58, "text": " the side of a neural network.", "tokens": [51166, 264, 1252, 295, 257, 18161, 3209, 13, 51234], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15419735807053586, "compression_ratio": 1.5405405405405406, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903450853258175e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 73720, "start": 754.88, "end": 759.0, "text": " It must be built into how the system interprets its own continuing existence.", "tokens": [51249, 467, 1633, 312, 3094, 666, 577, 264, 1185, 17489, 1373, 1080, 1065, 9289, 9123, 13, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15419735807053586, "compression_ratio": 1.5405405405405406, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903450853258175e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 75900, "start": 759.0, "end": 764.6, "text": " Okay, so if true biological memory isn't about perfectly storing facts, and if it requires", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 498, 2074, 13910, 4675, 1943, 380, 466, 6239, 26085, 9130, 11, 293, 498, 309, 7029, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1109040301779042, "compression_ratio": 1.619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071349116629884e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 75900, "start": 764.6, "end": 770.74, "text": " this episodic indexicality, this sense of a localized, lived past, what is the memory", "tokens": [50645, 341, 39200, 299, 8186, 804, 507, 11, 341, 2020, 295, 257, 44574, 11, 5152, 1791, 11, 437, 307, 264, 4675, 50952], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1109040301779042, "compression_ratio": 1.619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071349116629884e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 75900, "start": 770.74, "end": 772.62, "text": " actually doing for the organism right now?", "tokens": [50952, 767, 884, 337, 264, 24128, 558, 586, 30, 51046], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1109040301779042, "compression_ratio": 1.619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071349116629884e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 75900, "start": 772.66, "end": 773.88, "text": " That's the million-dollar question.", "tokens": [51048, 663, 311, 264, 2459, 12, 40485, 1168, 13, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1109040301779042, "compression_ratio": 1.619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071349116629884e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 75900, "start": 774.04, "end": 778.28, "text": " Right, because if it's not a lookup table that says do X when Y happens, what is its function?", "tokens": [51117, 1779, 11, 570, 498, 309, 311, 406, 257, 574, 1010, 3199, 300, 1619, 360, 1783, 562, 398, 2314, 11, 437, 307, 1080, 2445, 30, 51329], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1109040301779042, "compression_ratio": 1.619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071349116629884e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 75900, "start": 778.44, "end": 782.38, "text": " This brings us to a really elegant concept from continuation geometry.", "tokens": [51337, 639, 5607, 505, 281, 257, 534, 21117, 3410, 490, 29357, 18426, 13, 51534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1109040301779042, "compression_ratio": 1.619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071349116629884e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 75900, "start": 782.9, "end": 786.14, "text": " The principle is that constraint is not determination.", "tokens": [51560, 440, 8665, 307, 300, 25534, 307, 406, 18432, 13, 51722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1109040301779042, "compression_ratio": 1.619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071349116629884e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 78614, "start": 786.14, "end": 788.16, "text": " Constraint is not determination.", "tokens": [50365, 8574, 424, 686, 307, 406, 18432, 13, 50466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17005065336065778, "compression_ratio": 1.7216117216117217, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040641680192038e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 78614, "start": 788.42, "end": 788.8, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50479, 7587, 13, 50498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17005065336065778, "compression_ratio": 1.7216117216117217, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040641680192038e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 78614, "start": 789.22, "end": 791.86, "text": " History does not function as a deterministic lookup table.", "tokens": [50519, 12486, 775, 406, 2445, 382, 257, 15957, 3142, 574, 1010, 3199, 13, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17005065336065778, "compression_ratio": 1.7216117216117217, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040641680192038e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 78614, "start": 792.4, "end": 798.08, "text": " Instead, history narrows the space of available continuations for a system without selecting", "tokens": [50678, 7156, 11, 2503, 6397, 1509, 264, 1901, 295, 2435, 2993, 763, 337, 257, 1185, 1553, 18182, 50962], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17005065336065778, "compression_ratio": 1.7216117216117217, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040641680192038e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 78614, "start": 798.08, "end": 799.24, "text": " uniquely among them.", "tokens": [50962, 31474, 3654, 552, 13, 51020], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17005065336065778, "compression_ratio": 1.7216117216117217, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040641680192038e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 78614, "start": 799.56, "end": 801.68, "text": " Narrows the space of available continuations.", "tokens": [51036, 45658, 1509, 264, 1901, 295, 2435, 2993, 763, 13, 51142], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17005065336065778, "compression_ratio": 1.7216117216117217, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040641680192038e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 78614, "start": 802.06, "end": 803.4, "text": " Let's ground this for the listener.", "tokens": [51161, 961, 311, 2727, 341, 337, 264, 31569, 13, 51228], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17005065336065778, "compression_ratio": 1.7216117216117217, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040641680192038e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 78614, "start": 803.88, "end": 808.66, "text": " Think about walking into your kitchen, opening the pantry, and finding you only have three ingredients", "tokens": [51252, 6557, 466, 4494, 666, 428, 6525, 11, 5193, 264, 40689, 11, 293, 5006, 291, 787, 362, 1045, 6952, 51491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17005065336065778, "compression_ratio": 1.7216117216117217, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040641680192038e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 78614, "start": 808.66, "end": 811.96, "text": " left, say eggs, sugar, and flour.", "tokens": [51491, 1411, 11, 584, 6466, 11, 5076, 11, 293, 7693, 13, 51656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17005065336065778, "compression_ratio": 1.7216117216117217, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040641680192038e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 78614, "start": 812.1, "end": 813.18, "text": " A very limited pantry.", "tokens": [51663, 316, 588, 5567, 40689, 13, 51717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17005065336065778, "compression_ratio": 1.7216117216117217, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040641680192038e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 78614, "start": 813.34, "end": 813.9399999999999, "text": " Very limited.", "tokens": [51725, 4372, 5567, 13, 51755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17005065336065778, "compression_ratio": 1.7216117216117217, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040641680192038e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 81394, "start": 813.94, "end": 819.7, "text": " That history, the sequence of grocery shopping choices that led to this exact pantry, acts", "tokens": [50365, 663, 2503, 11, 264, 8310, 295, 14410, 8688, 7994, 300, 4684, 281, 341, 1900, 40689, 11, 10672, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13543482773176585, "compression_ratio": 1.740484429065744, "no_speech_prob": 1.734952459475636e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 81394, "start": 819.7, "end": 821.72, "text": " as a strict constraint on what you can cook.", "tokens": [50653, 382, 257, 10910, 25534, 322, 437, 291, 393, 2543, 13, 50754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13543482773176585, "compression_ratio": 1.740484429065744, "no_speech_prob": 1.734952459475636e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 81394, "start": 821.86, "end": 821.98, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50761, 865, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13543482773176585, "compression_ratio": 1.740484429065744, "no_speech_prob": 1.734952459475636e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 81394, "start": 822.1, "end": 824.08, "text": " You absolutely cannot make a pepperoni pizza.", "tokens": [50773, 509, 3122, 2644, 652, 257, 8532, 17049, 8298, 13, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13543482773176585, "compression_ratio": 1.740484429065744, "no_speech_prob": 1.734952459475636e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 81394, "start": 824.22, "end": 824.5600000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50879, 1779, 13, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13543482773176585, "compression_ratio": 1.740484429065744, "no_speech_prob": 1.734952459475636e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 81394, "start": 824.6800000000001, "end": 828.46, "text": " The constraint of your history renders the pizza an inadmissible future.", "tokens": [50902, 440, 25534, 295, 428, 2503, 6125, 433, 264, 8298, 364, 42148, 76, 41073, 2027, 13, 51091], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13543482773176585, "compression_ratio": 1.740484429065744, "no_speech_prob": 1.734952459475636e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 81394, "start": 829.0600000000001, "end": 832.1800000000001, "text": " It creates a hard boundary around what is physically possible next.", "tokens": [51121, 467, 7829, 257, 1152, 12866, 926, 437, 307, 9762, 1944, 958, 13, 51277], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13543482773176585, "compression_ratio": 1.740484429065744, "no_speech_prob": 1.734952459475636e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 81394, "start": 832.34, "end": 832.5600000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51285, 1779, 13, 51296], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13543482773176585, "compression_ratio": 1.740484429065744, "no_speech_prob": 1.734952459475636e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 81394, "start": 832.72, "end": 838.2800000000001, "text": " But, and here is the vital distinction, that constraint doesn't determine that you must make a cake.", "tokens": [51304, 583, 11, 293, 510, 307, 264, 11707, 16844, 11, 300, 25534, 1177, 380, 6997, 300, 291, 1633, 652, 257, 5908, 13, 51582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13543482773176585, "compression_ratio": 1.740484429065744, "no_speech_prob": 1.734952459475636e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 81394, "start": 838.4200000000001, "end": 839.5600000000001, "text": " You could make cookies.", "tokens": [51589, 509, 727, 652, 13670, 13, 51646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13543482773176585, "compression_ratio": 1.740484429065744, "no_speech_prob": 1.734952459475636e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 81394, "start": 839.7600000000001, "end": 839.9200000000001, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51656, 865, 13, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13543482773176585, "compression_ratio": 1.740484429065744, "no_speech_prob": 1.734952459475636e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 81394, "start": 840.0, "end": 841.08, "text": " You could make a sweet crepe.", "tokens": [51668, 509, 727, 652, 257, 3844, 1197, 494, 13, 51722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13543482773176585, "compression_ratio": 1.740484429065744, "no_speech_prob": 1.734952459475636e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 84108, "start": 841.08, "end": 848.0400000000001, "text": " The history eliminates options, but it still forces you to actively decide and act among", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2503, 49893, 3956, 11, 457, 309, 920, 5874, 291, 281, 13022, 4536, 293, 605, 3654, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09614869952201843, "compression_ratio": 1.1139240506329113, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579938798780505e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 84804, "start": 848.04, "end": 849.62, "text": " the remaining admissible futures.", "tokens": [50365, 264, 8877, 5910, 41073, 26071, 13, 50444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19058571106348282, "compression_ratio": 1.6213592233009708, "no_speech_prob": 2.244353791355791e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 84804, "start": 849.8399999999999, "end": 855.9, "text": " Infliction takes this logic a step further, noting that two systems can inherit the exact", "tokens": [50455, 682, 3423, 4105, 2516, 341, 9952, 257, 1823, 3052, 11, 26801, 300, 732, 3652, 393, 21389, 264, 1900, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19058571106348282, "compression_ratio": 1.6213592233009708, "no_speech_prob": 2.244353791355791e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 84804, "start": 855.9, "end": 861.74, "text": " same history, the exact same pantry of ingredients, but experience completely different admissible", "tokens": [50758, 912, 2503, 11, 264, 1900, 912, 40689, 295, 6952, 11, 457, 1752, 2584, 819, 5910, 41073, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19058571106348282, "compression_ratio": 1.6213592233009708, "no_speech_prob": 2.244353791355791e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 84804, "start": 861.74, "end": 862.24, "text": " futures.", "tokens": [51050, 26071, 13, 51075], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19058571106348282, "compression_ratio": 1.6213592233009708, "no_speech_prob": 2.244353791355791e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 84804, "start": 862.66, "end": 864.0999999999999, "text": " Wait, how does that work?", "tokens": [51096, 3802, 11, 577, 775, 300, 589, 30, 51168], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19058571106348282, "compression_ratio": 1.6213592233009708, "no_speech_prob": 2.244353791355791e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 84804, "start": 864.5999999999999, "end": 868.88, "text": " If the constraint is the same, shouldn't the remaining options be identical?", "tokens": [51193, 759, 264, 25534, 307, 264, 912, 11, 4659, 380, 264, 8877, 3956, 312, 14800, 30, 51407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19058571106348282, "compression_ratio": 1.6213592233009708, "no_speech_prob": 2.244353791355791e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 86888, "start": 868.88, "end": 873.08, "text": " Because the act of reading the constraint is itself a further constraint.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 264, 605, 295, 3760, 264, 25534, 307, 2564, 257, 3052, 25534, 13, 50575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10554678463241429, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253337209783727e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 86888, "start": 873.42, "end": 876.02, "text": " The organism isn't just looking at the pantry objectively.", "tokens": [50592, 440, 24128, 1943, 380, 445, 1237, 412, 264, 40689, 46067, 13, 50722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10554678463241429, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253337209783727e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 86888, "start": 876.3, "end": 879.48, "text": " It brings its own internal state to the interpretation.", "tokens": [50736, 467, 5607, 1080, 1065, 6920, 1785, 281, 264, 14174, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10554678463241429, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253337209783727e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 86888, "start": 879.74, "end": 880.2, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [50908, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10554678463241429, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253337209783727e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 86888, "start": 880.32, "end": 885.5, "text": " So if I walk into that kitchen with my specific kind of limited culinary skills, and maybe I'm", "tokens": [50937, 407, 498, 286, 1792, 666, 300, 6525, 365, 452, 2685, 733, 295, 5567, 39273, 3942, 11, 293, 1310, 286, 478, 51196], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10554678463241429, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253337209783727e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 86888, "start": 885.5, "end": 887.56, "text": " feeling lazy, my admissible futures are pretty narrow.", "tokens": [51196, 2633, 14847, 11, 452, 5910, 41073, 26071, 366, 1238, 9432, 13, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10554678463241429, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253337209783727e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 86888, "start": 887.66, "end": 889.54, "text": " Maybe I just scramble the eggs and call it a day.", "tokens": [51304, 2704, 286, 445, 795, 48382, 264, 6466, 293, 818, 309, 257, 786, 13, 51398], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10554678463241429, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253337209783727e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 86888, "start": 889.68, "end": 889.98, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51405, 1779, 13, 51420], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10554678463241429, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253337209783727e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 88998, "start": 889.98, "end": 894.04, "text": " But if my friend, who's a professional pastry chef, walks into the exact same kitchen with", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 452, 1277, 11, 567, 311, 257, 4843, 29198, 10530, 11, 12896, 666, 264, 1900, 912, 6525, 365, 50568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1383033165564904, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213623767550532e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 88998, "start": 894.04, "end": 898.6, "text": " the exact same ingredients, their act of reading the constraint opens up futures I couldn't", "tokens": [50568, 264, 1900, 912, 6952, 11, 641, 605, 295, 3760, 264, 25534, 9870, 493, 26071, 286, 2809, 380, 50796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1383033165564904, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213623767550532e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 88998, "start": 898.6, "end": 899.24, "text": " even perceive.", "tokens": [50796, 754, 20281, 13, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1383033165564904, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213623767550532e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 88998, "start": 899.46, "end": 899.6, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50839, 865, 13, 50846], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1383033165564904, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213623767550532e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 88998, "start": 899.64, "end": 901.38, "text": " They might whip up some complex meringue.", "tokens": [50848, 814, 1062, 22377, 493, 512, 3997, 50044, 13, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1383033165564904, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213623767550532e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 88998, "start": 901.78, "end": 902.3000000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50955, 7587, 13, 50981], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1383033165564904, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213623767550532e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 88998, "start": 902.76, "end": 906.88, "text": " The way you interpret the available traces actively shapes what futures are possible for", "tokens": [51004, 440, 636, 291, 7302, 264, 2435, 26076, 13022, 10854, 437, 26071, 366, 1944, 337, 51210], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1383033165564904, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213623767550532e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 88998, "start": 906.88, "end": 907.08, "text": " you.", "tokens": [51210, 291, 13, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1383033165564904, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213623767550532e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 88998, "start": 907.84, "end": 912.58, "text": " And Michael Levin argues forcefully that this specific moment of interpretation is a locus", "tokens": [51258, 400, 5116, 1456, 4796, 38218, 3464, 2277, 300, 341, 2685, 1623, 295, 14174, 307, 257, 450, 1149, 51495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1383033165564904, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213623767550532e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 88998, "start": 912.58, "end": 913.2, "text": " of agency.", "tokens": [51495, 295, 7934, 13, 51526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1383033165564904, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213623767550532e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 88998, "start": 913.4200000000001, "end": 914.44, "text": " A locus of agency.", "tokens": [51537, 316, 450, 1149, 295, 7934, 13, 51588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1383033165564904, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213623767550532e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 91444, "start": 914.44, "end": 915.0400000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50395], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939676673666943, "compression_ratio": 1.6547619047619047, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612899428169014e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 91444, "start": 915.84, "end": 921.22, "text": " The continuing system, the organism, or the person is not just a passive object that history", "tokens": [50435, 440, 9289, 1185, 11, 264, 24128, 11, 420, 264, 954, 307, 406, 445, 257, 14975, 2657, 300, 2503, 50704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939676673666943, "compression_ratio": 1.6547619047619047, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612899428169014e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 91444, "start": 921.22, "end": 923.1600000000001, "text": " washes over, dictating its path.", "tokens": [50704, 48616, 670, 11, 12569, 990, 1080, 3100, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939676673666943, "compression_ratio": 1.6547619047619047, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612899428169014e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 91444, "start": 923.6800000000001, "end": 928.0, "text": " The continuer partly authors the admissibility in the very act of continuing.", "tokens": [50827, 440, 35660, 17031, 16552, 264, 5910, 891, 2841, 294, 264, 588, 605, 295, 9289, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939676673666943, "compression_ratio": 1.6547619047619047, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612899428169014e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 91444, "start": 928.32, "end": 933.22, "text": " So you are an active participant in deciding what your past constraints mean for your future.", "tokens": [51059, 407, 291, 366, 364, 4967, 24950, 294, 17990, 437, 428, 1791, 18491, 914, 337, 428, 2027, 13, 51304], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939676673666943, "compression_ratio": 1.6547619047619047, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612899428169014e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 91444, "start": 933.46, "end": 933.9200000000001, "text": " You are.", "tokens": [51316, 509, 366, 13, 51339], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939676673666943, "compression_ratio": 1.6547619047619047, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612899428169014e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 91444, "start": 934.0200000000001, "end": 936.9200000000001, "text": " That is an incredibly empowering view of biology.", "tokens": [51344, 663, 307, 364, 6252, 28261, 1910, 295, 14956, 13, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939676673666943, "compression_ratio": 1.6547619047619047, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612899428169014e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 91444, "start": 937.46, "end": 940.46, "text": " We aren't purely victims of our past traumas or traces.", "tokens": [51516, 492, 3212, 380, 17491, 11448, 295, 527, 1791, 16790, 296, 420, 26076, 13, 51666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939676673666943, "compression_ratio": 1.6547619047619047, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612899428169014e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 94046, "start": 940.46, "end": 946.7, "text": " We are the active authors creatively misinterpreting those traces to find new paths forward.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 366, 264, 4967, 16552, 43750, 3346, 5106, 3712, 783, 729, 26076, 281, 915, 777, 14518, 2128, 13, 50677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13849288698226686, "compression_ratio": 1.6755852842809364, "no_speech_prob": 1.950838145539646e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 94046, "start": 946.94, "end": 948.2, "text": " It's a very proactive stance.", "tokens": [50689, 467, 311, 257, 588, 28028, 21033, 13, 50752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13849288698226686, "compression_ratio": 1.6755852842809364, "no_speech_prob": 1.950838145539646e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 94046, "start": 948.38, "end": 951.88, "text": " But, I mean, that level of agency introduces a massive engineering problem.", "tokens": [50761, 583, 11, 286, 914, 11, 300, 1496, 295, 7934, 31472, 257, 5994, 7043, 1154, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13849288698226686, "compression_ratio": 1.6755852842809364, "no_speech_prob": 1.950838145539646e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 94046, "start": 952.32, "end": 957.0400000000001, "text": " If an organism is actively authoring its future based on subjective interpretations of", "tokens": [50958, 759, 364, 24128, 307, 13022, 3793, 278, 1080, 2027, 2361, 322, 25972, 37547, 295, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13849288698226686, "compression_ratio": 1.6755852842809364, "no_speech_prob": 1.950838145539646e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 94046, "start": 957.0400000000001, "end": 959.14, "text": " its constraints, how do you control it?", "tokens": [51194, 1080, 18491, 11, 577, 360, 291, 1969, 309, 30, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13849288698226686, "compression_ratio": 1.6755852842809364, "no_speech_prob": 1.950838145539646e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 94046, "start": 959.26, "end": 960.0400000000001, "text": " Well, you don't.", "tokens": [51305, 1042, 11, 291, 500, 380, 13, 51344], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13849288698226686, "compression_ratio": 1.6755852842809364, "no_speech_prob": 1.950838145539646e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 94046, "start": 960.26, "end": 963.1, "text": " Or rather, you can't control it with the precision an engineer demands.", "tokens": [51355, 1610, 2831, 11, 291, 393, 380, 1969, 309, 365, 264, 18356, 364, 11403, 15107, 13, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13849288698226686, "compression_ratio": 1.6755852842809364, "no_speech_prob": 1.950838145539646e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 94046, "start": 963.2, "end": 965.62, "text": " The price of agency is the loss of absolute control.", "tokens": [51502, 440, 3218, 295, 7934, 307, 264, 4470, 295, 8236, 1969, 13, 51623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13849288698226686, "compression_ratio": 1.6755852842809364, "no_speech_prob": 1.950838145539646e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 94046, "start": 965.98, "end": 966.32, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51641, 1079, 13, 51658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13849288698226686, "compression_ratio": 1.6755852842809364, "no_speech_prob": 1.950838145539646e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 94046, "start": 967.12, "end": 968.24, "text": " Levin makes this very clear.", "tokens": [51698, 1456, 4796, 1669, 341, 588, 1850, 13, 51754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13849288698226686, "compression_ratio": 1.6755852842809364, "no_speech_prob": 1.950838145539646e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 96824, "start": 968.24, "end": 974.08, "text": " When you shift to a system that interprets its own traces, the relationship shifts from", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 291, 5513, 281, 257, 1185, 300, 17489, 1373, 1080, 1065, 26076, 11, 264, 2480, 19201, 490, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10963957900301032, "compression_ratio": 1.6654676258992807, "no_speech_prob": 1.586025906961941e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 96824, "start": 974.08, "end": 979.7, "text": " a programmer and program dynamic to something closer to a negotiation between agents.", "tokens": [50657, 257, 32116, 293, 1461, 8546, 281, 746, 4966, 281, 257, 27573, 1296, 12554, 13, 50938], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10963957900301032, "compression_ratio": 1.6654676258992807, "no_speech_prob": 1.586025906961941e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 96824, "start": 980.38, "end": 983.98, "text": " So it's less like coding a machine and more like training an animal.", "tokens": [50972, 407, 309, 311, 1570, 411, 17720, 257, 3479, 293, 544, 411, 3097, 364, 5496, 13, 51152], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10963957900301032, "compression_ratio": 1.6654676258992807, "no_speech_prob": 1.586025906961941e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 96824, "start": 984.14, "end": 984.58, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51160, 7587, 13, 51182], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10963957900301032, "compression_ratio": 1.6654676258992807, "no_speech_prob": 1.586025906961941e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 96824, "start": 985.4, "end": 991.0, "text": " But what you gain in exchange for giving up that micromanagement is extraordinary robustness", "tokens": [51223, 583, 437, 291, 6052, 294, 7742, 337, 2902, 493, 300, 3123, 81, 4277, 11129, 307, 10581, 13956, 1287, 51503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10963957900301032, "compression_ratio": 1.6654676258992807, "no_speech_prob": 1.586025906961941e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 96824, "start": 991.0, "end": 992.44, "text": " and adaptive plasticity.", "tokens": [51503, 293, 27912, 5900, 507, 13, 51575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10963957900301032, "compression_ratio": 1.6654676258992807, "no_speech_prob": 1.586025906961941e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 96824, "start": 992.64, "end": 996.6, "text": " It's the difference between coding a factory robot and training a border collie.", "tokens": [51585, 467, 311, 264, 2649, 1296, 17720, 257, 9265, 7881, 293, 3097, 257, 7838, 1263, 414, 13, 51783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10963957900301032, "compression_ratio": 1.6654676258992807, "no_speech_prob": 1.586025906961941e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 96824, "start": 996.86, "end": 997.42, "text": " I like that.", "tokens": [51796, 286, 411, 300, 13, 51824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10963957900301032, "compression_ratio": 1.6654676258992807, "no_speech_prob": 1.586025906961941e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 99742, "start": 997.42, "end": 1003.0, "text": " I can write a script for a robot arm that says, move exactly 13 inches to the left, close", "tokens": [50365, 286, 393, 2464, 257, 5755, 337, 257, 7881, 3726, 300, 1619, 11, 1286, 2293, 3705, 8478, 281, 264, 1411, 11, 1998, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11669546763102213, "compression_ratio": 1.6641509433962265, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491468784850637e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 99742, "start": 1003.0, "end": 1005.06, "text": " the claw, move 14 inches to the right.", "tokens": [50644, 264, 32019, 11, 1286, 3499, 8478, 281, 264, 558, 13, 50747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11669546763102213, "compression_ratio": 1.6641509433962265, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491468784850637e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 99742, "start": 1005.2199999999999, "end": 1007.0799999999999, "text": " It will do it perfectly a million times.", "tokens": [50755, 467, 486, 360, 309, 6239, 257, 2459, 1413, 13, 50848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11669546763102213, "compression_ratio": 1.6641509433962265, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491468784850637e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 99742, "start": 1007.1999999999999, "end": 1010.02, "text": " But if a box falls in its path, it just crashes and breaks.", "tokens": [50854, 583, 498, 257, 2424, 8804, 294, 1080, 3100, 11, 309, 445, 28642, 293, 9857, 13, 50995], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11669546763102213, "compression_ratio": 1.6641509433962265, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491468784850637e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 99742, "start": 1010.12, "end": 1010.52, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51000, 7587, 13, 51020], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11669546763102213, "compression_ratio": 1.6641509433962265, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491468784850637e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 99742, "start": 1011.02, "end": 1016.04, "text": " But if I train a border collie to herd sheep, I establish constraints and reward behaviors.", "tokens": [51045, 583, 498, 286, 3847, 257, 7838, 1263, 414, 281, 29484, 14213, 11, 286, 8327, 18491, 293, 7782, 15501, 13, 51296], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11669546763102213, "compression_ratio": 1.6641509433962265, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491468784850637e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 99742, "start": 1016.5799999999999, "end": 1021.14, "text": " But I can't write a line of code for how the dog should react if a wolf suddenly appears", "tokens": [51323, 583, 286, 393, 380, 2464, 257, 1622, 295, 3089, 337, 577, 264, 3000, 820, 4515, 498, 257, 19216, 5800, 7038, 51551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11669546763102213, "compression_ratio": 1.6641509433962265, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491468784850637e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 99742, "start": 1021.14, "end": 1022.4, "text": " or if a fence breaks.", "tokens": [51551, 420, 498, 257, 15422, 9857, 13, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11669546763102213, "compression_ratio": 1.6641509433962265, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491468784850637e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 102240, "start": 1022.4, "end": 1022.84, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17381510170557166, "compression_ratio": 1.5173745173745175, "no_speech_prob": 1.65243242266494e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 102240, "start": 1022.92, "end": 1027.42, "text": " You have to trust the dog's internal agency to creatively interpret its constraints and", "tokens": [50391, 509, 362, 281, 3361, 264, 3000, 311, 6920, 7934, 281, 43750, 7302, 1080, 18491, 293, 50616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17381510170557166, "compression_ratio": 1.5173745173745175, "no_speech_prob": 1.65243242266494e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 102240, "start": 1027.42, "end": 1028.46, "text": " solve the novel problem.", "tokens": [50616, 5039, 264, 7613, 1154, 13, 50668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17381510170557166, "compression_ratio": 1.5173745173745175, "no_speech_prob": 1.65243242266494e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 102240, "start": 1028.82, "end": 1033.02, "text": " And biology overwhelmingly favors the border collie over the robot arm when it comes to", "tokens": [50686, 400, 14956, 42926, 40554, 264, 7838, 1263, 414, 670, 264, 7881, 3726, 562, 309, 1487, 281, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17381510170557166, "compression_ratio": 1.5173745173745175, "no_speech_prob": 1.65243242266494e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 102240, "start": 1033.02, "end": 1034.86, "text": " survival in unpredictable environments.", "tokens": [50896, 12559, 294, 31160, 12388, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17381510170557166, "compression_ratio": 1.5173745173745175, "no_speech_prob": 1.65243242266494e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 102240, "start": 1035.36, "end": 1036.46, "text": " It absolutely does.", "tokens": [51013, 467, 3122, 775, 13, 51068], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17381510170557166, "compression_ratio": 1.5173745173745175, "no_speech_prob": 1.65243242266494e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 102240, "start": 1036.58, "end": 1041.44, "text": " And to put quantitative weight behind this, Fliction introduces work from Federico Bagazzi.", "tokens": [51074, 400, 281, 829, 27778, 3364, 2261, 341, 11, 3235, 4105, 31472, 589, 490, 45545, 2789, 24377, 33910, 13, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17381510170557166, "compression_ratio": 1.5173745173745175, "no_speech_prob": 1.65243242266494e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 102240, "start": 1041.92, "end": 1043.54, "text": " He's a researcher in Levin's lab.", "tokens": [51341, 634, 311, 257, 21751, 294, 1456, 4796, 311, 2715, 13, 51422], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17381510170557166, "compression_ratio": 1.5173745173745175, "no_speech_prob": 1.65243242266494e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 104354, "start": 1043.54, "end": 1047.3799999999999, "text": " And he focuses on a metric called causal emergence.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 415, 16109, 322, 257, 20678, 1219, 38755, 36211, 13, 50557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12570612481299867, "compression_ratio": 1.5746606334841629, "no_speech_prob": 1.962116233378275e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 104354, "start": 1047.8, "end": 1048.56, "text": " Causal emergence.", "tokens": [50578, 7544, 11765, 36211, 13, 50616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12570612481299867, "compression_ratio": 1.5746606334841629, "no_speech_prob": 1.962116233378275e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 104354, "start": 1048.96, "end": 1050.8, "text": " Let's unpack that because it's a heavy term.", "tokens": [50636, 961, 311, 26699, 300, 570, 309, 311, 257, 4676, 1433, 13, 50728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12570612481299867, "compression_ratio": 1.5746606334841629, "no_speech_prob": 1.962116233378275e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 104354, "start": 1051.04, "end": 1056.6399999999999, "text": " At a high level, causal emergence measures how much of a system's behavior is driven by", "tokens": [50740, 1711, 257, 1090, 1496, 11, 38755, 36211, 8000, 577, 709, 295, 257, 1185, 311, 5223, 307, 9555, 538, 51020], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12570612481299867, "compression_ratio": 1.5746606334841629, "no_speech_prob": 1.962116233378275e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 104354, "start": 1056.6399999999999, "end": 1062.3, "text": " its macro level structure rather than just the sum of its micro level parts bumping into", "tokens": [51020, 1080, 18887, 1496, 3877, 2831, 813, 445, 264, 2408, 295, 1080, 4532, 1496, 3166, 9961, 278, 666, 51303], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12570612481299867, "compression_ratio": 1.5746606334841629, "no_speech_prob": 1.962116233378275e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 104354, "start": 1062.3, "end": 1062.76, "text": " each other.", "tokens": [51303, 1184, 661, 13, 51326], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12570612481299867, "compression_ratio": 1.5746606334841629, "no_speech_prob": 1.962116233378275e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 104354, "start": 1062.86, "end": 1062.98, "text": " OK.", "tokens": [51331, 2264, 13, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12570612481299867, "compression_ratio": 1.5746606334841629, "no_speech_prob": 1.962116233378275e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 104354, "start": 1063.08, "end": 1064.24, "text": " Think of a traffic jam.", "tokens": [51342, 6557, 295, 257, 6419, 7872, 13, 51400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12570612481299867, "compression_ratio": 1.5746606334841629, "no_speech_prob": 1.962116233378275e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 104354, "start": 1064.3799999999999, "end": 1065.08, "text": " Perfect example.", "tokens": [51407, 10246, 1365, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12570612481299867, "compression_ratio": 1.5746606334841629, "no_speech_prob": 1.962116233378275e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 106508, "start": 1065.08, "end": 1070.08, "text": " If you just look at the individual micro level parts, one car braking, another swerving,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 445, 574, 412, 264, 2609, 4532, 1496, 3166, 11, 472, 1032, 32140, 11, 1071, 262, 1554, 798, 11, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09878819830277387, "compression_ratio": 1.7556270096463023, "no_speech_prob": 2.036296478657995e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 106508, "start": 1070.1799999999998, "end": 1073.96, "text": " another speeding up, it's chaotic and really hard to model.", "tokens": [50620, 1071, 35593, 493, 11, 309, 311, 27013, 293, 534, 1152, 281, 2316, 13, 50809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09878819830277387, "compression_ratio": 1.7556270096463023, "no_speech_prob": 2.036296478657995e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 106508, "start": 1074.62, "end": 1079.4399999999998, "text": " But if you zoom out to the macro level structure, the traffic jam itself behaves almost like a", "tokens": [50842, 583, 498, 291, 8863, 484, 281, 264, 18887, 1496, 3877, 11, 264, 6419, 7872, 2564, 36896, 1920, 411, 257, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09878819830277387, "compression_ratio": 1.7556270096463023, "no_speech_prob": 2.036296478657995e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 106508, "start": 1079.4399999999998, "end": 1080.04, "text": " solid object.", "tokens": [51083, 5100, 2657, 13, 51113], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09878819830277387, "compression_ratio": 1.7556270096463023, "no_speech_prob": 2.036296478657995e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 106508, "start": 1080.1599999999999, "end": 1083.74, "text": " It moves backwards down the highway like a wave, even though all the individual cars are", "tokens": [51119, 467, 6067, 12204, 760, 264, 17205, 411, 257, 5772, 11, 754, 1673, 439, 264, 2609, 5163, 366, 51298], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09878819830277387, "compression_ratio": 1.7556270096463023, "no_speech_prob": 2.036296478657995e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 106508, "start": 1083.74, "end": 1084.28, "text": " moving forward.", "tokens": [51298, 2684, 2128, 13, 51325], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09878819830277387, "compression_ratio": 1.7556270096463023, "no_speech_prob": 2.036296478657995e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 106508, "start": 1084.36, "end": 1084.8, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51329, 7587, 13, 51351], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09878819830277387, "compression_ratio": 1.7556270096463023, "no_speech_prob": 2.036296478657995e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 106508, "start": 1085.0, "end": 1089.3999999999999, "text": " The macro structure of the jam dictates the behavior of the cars more than the individual", "tokens": [51361, 440, 18887, 3877, 295, 264, 7872, 12569, 1024, 264, 5223, 295, 264, 5163, 544, 813, 264, 2609, 51581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09878819830277387, "compression_ratio": 1.7556270096463023, "no_speech_prob": 2.036296478657995e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 106508, "start": 1089.3999999999999, "end": 1090.1799999999998, "text": " drivers do.", "tokens": [51581, 11590, 360, 13, 51620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09878819830277387, "compression_ratio": 1.7556270096463023, "no_speech_prob": 2.036296478657995e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 106508, "start": 1090.46, "end": 1092.04, "text": " So that's high causal emergence.", "tokens": [51634, 407, 300, 311, 1090, 38755, 36211, 13, 51713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09878819830277387, "compression_ratio": 1.7556270096463023, "no_speech_prob": 2.036296478657995e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 106508, "start": 1092.6, "end": 1094.3, "text": " The system operates as a unified whole.", "tokens": [51741, 440, 1185, 22577, 382, 257, 26787, 1379, 13, 51826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09878819830277387, "compression_ratio": 1.7556270096463023, "no_speech_prob": 2.036296478657995e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 109430, "start": 1094.3, "end": 1095.82, "text": " That's a great way to visualize it.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 311, 257, 869, 636, 281, 23273, 309, 13, 50441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1917007121633976, "compression_ratio": 1.63003663003663, "no_speech_prob": 1.604325396489803e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 109430, "start": 1096.5, "end": 1101.96, "text": " And Pagazzi's quantitative work demonstrates that biological and synthetic systems with", "tokens": [50475, 400, 430, 559, 33910, 311, 27778, 589, 31034, 300, 13910, 293, 23420, 3652, 365, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1917007121633976, "compression_ratio": 1.63003663003663, "no_speech_prob": 1.604325396489803e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 109430, "start": 1101.96, "end": 1106.04, "text": " high causal emergence are exceptionally good at learning.", "tokens": [50748, 1090, 38755, 36211, 366, 37807, 665, 412, 2539, 13, 50952], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1917007121633976, "compression_ratio": 1.63003663003663, "no_speech_prob": 1.604325396489803e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 109430, "start": 1106.6, "end": 1111.18, "text": " When you train these systems, their causal emergence actually increases.", "tokens": [50980, 1133, 291, 3847, 613, 3652, 11, 641, 38755, 36211, 767, 8637, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1917007121633976, "compression_ratio": 1.63003663003663, "no_speech_prob": 1.604325396489803e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 109430, "start": 1111.9199999999998, "end": 1117.06, "text": " Their macro level structure becomes more integrated and more capable of top down direction.", "tokens": [51246, 6710, 18887, 1496, 3877, 3643, 544, 10919, 293, 544, 8189, 295, 1192, 760, 3513, 13, 51503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1917007121633976, "compression_ratio": 1.63003663003663, "no_speech_prob": 1.604325396489803e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 109430, "start": 1117.5, "end": 1119.1, "text": " They basically become more agential.", "tokens": [51525, 814, 1936, 1813, 544, 623, 2549, 13, 51605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1917007121633976, "compression_ratio": 1.63003663003663, "no_speech_prob": 1.604325396489803e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 109430, "start": 1119.3999999999999, "end": 1121.76, "text": " And here's where it gets really interesting for the listener.", "tokens": [51620, 400, 510, 311, 689, 309, 2170, 534, 1880, 337, 264, 31569, 13, 51738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1917007121633976, "compression_ratio": 1.63003663003663, "no_speech_prob": 1.604325396489803e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 112176, "start": 1121.76, "end": 1126.0, "text": " This leads to the most mind-bending discovery in the entire essay.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 6689, 281, 264, 881, 1575, 12, 65, 2029, 12114, 294, 264, 2302, 16238, 13, 50577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1557621261448536, "compression_ratio": 1.6692607003891051, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832362989393832e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 112176, "start": 1126.68, "end": 1130.54, "text": " When Pagazzi's team trained these systems, the causal emergence went up.", "tokens": [50611, 1133, 430, 559, 33910, 311, 1469, 8895, 613, 3652, 11, 264, 38755, 36211, 1437, 493, 13, 50804], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1557621261448536, "compression_ratio": 1.6692607003891051, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832362989393832e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 112176, "start": 1130.74, "end": 1132.62, "text": " The system became structurally smarter.", "tokens": [50814, 440, 1185, 3062, 6594, 6512, 20294, 13, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1557621261448536, "compression_ratio": 1.6692607003891051, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832362989393832e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 112176, "start": 1132.8799999999999, "end": 1133.12, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50921, 1779, 13, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1557621261448536, "compression_ratio": 1.6692607003891051, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832362989393832e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 112176, "start": 1133.46, "end": 1138.06, "text": " But then they forced the system to forget the specific content it had learned.", "tokens": [50950, 583, 550, 436, 7579, 264, 1185, 281, 2870, 264, 2685, 2701, 309, 632, 3264, 13, 51180], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1557621261448536, "compression_ratio": 1.6692607003891051, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832362989393832e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 112176, "start": 1138.46, "end": 1141.36, "text": " They essentially wiped the specific data traces from the hard drive.", "tokens": [51200, 814, 4476, 26879, 264, 2685, 1412, 26076, 490, 264, 1152, 3332, 13, 51345], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1557621261448536, "compression_ratio": 1.6692607003891051, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832362989393832e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 112176, "start": 1141.5, "end": 1143.8, "text": " And the result totally defies engineering logic.", "tokens": [51352, 400, 264, 1874, 3879, 1060, 530, 7043, 9952, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1557621261448536, "compression_ratio": 1.6692607003891051, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832362989393832e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 112176, "start": 1143.96, "end": 1146.02, "text": " The gain in causal emergence did not reverse.", "tokens": [51475, 440, 6052, 294, 38755, 36211, 630, 406, 9943, 13, 51578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1557621261448536, "compression_ratio": 1.6692607003891051, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832362989393832e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 114602, "start": 1146.02, "end": 1151.2, "text": " The system completely lost the specific facts it was trained on, but it retained the structural", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1185, 2584, 2731, 264, 2685, 9130, 309, 390, 8895, 322, 11, 457, 309, 33438, 264, 15067, 50624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434346889627391, "compression_ratio": 1.6583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668280475139573e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 114602, "start": 1151.2, "end": 1151.7, "text": " upgrade.", "tokens": [50624, 11484, 13, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434346889627391, "compression_ratio": 1.6583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668280475139573e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 114602, "start": 1152.1399999999999, "end": 1154.16, "text": " Levin calls this an asymmetric ratchet.", "tokens": [50671, 1456, 4796, 5498, 341, 364, 37277, 17475, 45885, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434346889627391, "compression_ratio": 1.6583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668280475139573e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 114602, "start": 1154.6399999999999, "end": 1159.96, "text": " A ratchet that only turns one way, pointing upwards toward higher intelligence and agency.", "tokens": [50796, 316, 45885, 300, 787, 4523, 472, 636, 11, 12166, 22167, 7361, 2946, 7599, 293, 7934, 13, 51062], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434346889627391, "compression_ratio": 1.6583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668280475139573e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 114602, "start": 1160.22, "end": 1167.4, "text": " It suggests that what survives the act of forgetting is not the data itself, but a permanent structural", "tokens": [51075, 467, 13409, 300, 437, 46231, 264, 605, 295, 25428, 307, 406, 264, 1412, 2564, 11, 457, 257, 10996, 15067, 51434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434346889627391, "compression_ratio": 1.6583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668280475139573e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 114602, "start": 1167.4, "end": 1170.72, "text": " upgrade in the system's capacity to integrate information.", "tokens": [51434, 11484, 294, 264, 1185, 311, 6042, 281, 13365, 1589, 13, 51600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434346889627391, "compression_ratio": 1.6583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668280475139573e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 117072, "start": 1170.72, "end": 1174.5, "text": " It's kind of like spending 10 years mastering advanced mathematics.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 733, 295, 411, 6434, 1266, 924, 49382, 7339, 18666, 13, 50554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1884789222326034, "compression_ratio": 1.5048076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.9130957668728188e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 117072, "start": 1175.02, "end": 1176.78, "text": " You train your brain rigorously.", "tokens": [50580, 509, 3847, 428, 3567, 42191, 5098, 13, 50668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1884789222326034, "compression_ratio": 1.5048076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.9130957668728188e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 117072, "start": 1176.92, "end": 1177.1200000000001, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50675, 865, 13, 50685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1884789222326034, "compression_ratio": 1.5048076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.9130957668728188e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 117072, "start": 1177.3600000000001, "end": 1181.16, "text": " Then, hypothetically, you hit your head and develop amnesia for formulas.", "tokens": [50697, 1396, 11, 24371, 22652, 11, 291, 2045, 428, 1378, 293, 1499, 669, 4081, 654, 337, 30546, 13, 50887], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1884789222326034, "compression_ratio": 1.5048076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.9130957668728188e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 117072, "start": 1181.72, "end": 1184.1200000000001, "text": " You completely forget the quadratic equation.", "tokens": [50915, 509, 2584, 2870, 264, 37262, 5367, 13, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1884789222326034, "compression_ratio": 1.5048076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.9130957668728188e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 117072, "start": 1184.5, "end": 1186.5, "text": " You can't remember how to integrate a function.", "tokens": [51054, 509, 393, 380, 1604, 577, 281, 13365, 257, 2445, 13, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1884789222326034, "compression_ratio": 1.5048076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.9130957668728188e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 117072, "start": 1186.8600000000001, "end": 1189.0, "text": " The specific semantic traces are gone.", "tokens": [51172, 440, 2685, 47982, 26076, 366, 2780, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1884789222326034, "compression_ratio": 1.5048076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.9130957668728188e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 118900, "start": 1189.0, "end": 1194.56, "text": " But the way those 10 years of intense study physically rewired the macro structure of your", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 636, 729, 1266, 924, 295, 9447, 2979, 9762, 319, 86, 1824, 264, 18887, 3877, 295, 428, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15251536523142167, "compression_ratio": 1.5936507936507935, "no_speech_prob": 1.58588290069539e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 118900, "start": 1194.56, "end": 1200.78, "text": " brain, your enhanced logical reasoning, your ability to spot patterns, that structural upgrade", "tokens": [50643, 3567, 11, 428, 21191, 14978, 21577, 11, 428, 3485, 281, 4008, 8294, 11, 300, 15067, 11484, 50954], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15251536523142167, "compression_ratio": 1.5936507936507935, "no_speech_prob": 1.58588290069539e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 118900, "start": 1200.78, "end": 1202.04, "text": " survives the forgetting.", "tokens": [50954, 46231, 264, 25428, 13, 51017], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15251536523142167, "compression_ratio": 1.5936507936507935, "no_speech_prob": 1.58588290069539e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 118900, "start": 1202.28, "end": 1203.1, "text": " The ratchet turn.", "tokens": [51029, 440, 45885, 1261, 13, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15251536523142167, "compression_ratio": 1.5936507936507935, "no_speech_prob": 1.58588290069539e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 118900, "start": 1203.38, "end": 1205.92, "text": " And you can't unturn it just by deleting the files.", "tokens": [51084, 400, 291, 393, 380, 1701, 925, 309, 445, 538, 48946, 264, 7098, 13, 51211], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15251536523142167, "compression_ratio": 1.5936507936507935, "no_speech_prob": 1.58588290069539e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 118900, "start": 1206.26, "end": 1209.72, "text": " Which is a profound challenge to how we think about artificial neural networks today,", "tokens": [51228, 3013, 307, 257, 14382, 3430, 281, 577, 321, 519, 466, 11677, 18161, 9590, 965, 11, 51401], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15251536523142167, "compression_ratio": 1.5936507936507935, "no_speech_prob": 1.58588290069539e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 118900, "start": 1209.82, "end": 1210.08, "text": " isn't it?", "tokens": [51406, 1943, 380, 309, 30, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15251536523142167, "compression_ratio": 1.5936507936507935, "no_speech_prob": 1.58588290069539e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 118900, "start": 1210.12, "end": 1210.32, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51421, 865, 13, 51431], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15251536523142167, "compression_ratio": 1.5936507936507935, "no_speech_prob": 1.58588290069539e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 118900, "start": 1210.38, "end": 1214.46, "text": " Because they generally do not exhibit this kind of irreversible structural growth from single", "tokens": [51434, 1436, 436, 5101, 360, 406, 20487, 341, 733, 295, 16014, 840, 964, 15067, 4599, 490, 2167, 51638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15251536523142167, "compression_ratio": 1.5936507936507935, "no_speech_prob": 1.58588290069539e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 118900, "start": 1214.46, "end": 1214.82, "text": " episodes.", "tokens": [51638, 9313, 13, 51656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15251536523142167, "compression_ratio": 1.5936507936507935, "no_speech_prob": 1.58588290069539e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 118900, "start": 1214.94, "end": 1215.56, "text": " No, they don't.", "tokens": [51662, 883, 11, 436, 500, 380, 13, 51693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15251536523142167, "compression_ratio": 1.5936507936507935, "no_speech_prob": 1.58588290069539e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 121556, "start": 1215.56, "end": 1219.5, "text": " If you wipe the weights of an LLM, you are literally back to zero.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 14082, 264, 17443, 295, 364, 441, 43, 44, 11, 291, 366, 3736, 646, 281, 4018, 13, 50562], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1446758635500644, "compression_ratio": 1.5719844357976653, "no_speech_prob": 2.051935444474795e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 121556, "start": 1219.94, "end": 1225.0, "text": " So to understand the mechanics of how this ratchet actually works, and why AI fails to replicate", "tokens": [50584, 407, 281, 1223, 264, 12939, 295, 577, 341, 45885, 767, 1985, 11, 293, 983, 7318, 18199, 281, 25356, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1446758635500644, "compression_ratio": 1.5719844357976653, "no_speech_prob": 2.051935444474795e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 121556, "start": 1225.0, "end": 1230.8999999999999, "text": " it, Fliction dives into a formal architecture called the adaptation hierarchy.", "tokens": [50837, 309, 11, 3235, 4105, 274, 1539, 666, 257, 9860, 9482, 1219, 264, 21549, 22333, 13, 51132], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1446758635500644, "compression_ratio": 1.5719844357976653, "no_speech_prob": 2.051935444474795e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 121556, "start": 1231.1599999999999, "end": 1233.22, "text": " Let's translate this into something visual.", "tokens": [51145, 961, 311, 13799, 341, 666, 746, 5056, 13, 51248], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1446758635500644, "compression_ratio": 1.5719844357976653, "no_speech_prob": 2.051935444474795e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 121556, "start": 1233.82, "end": 1240.1799999999998, "text": " Because Fliction breaks down recursive continuation, systems that feed back into themselves into three", "tokens": [51278, 1436, 3235, 4105, 9857, 760, 20560, 488, 29357, 11, 3652, 300, 3154, 646, 666, 2969, 666, 1045, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1446758635500644, "compression_ratio": 1.5719844357976653, "no_speech_prob": 2.051935444474795e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 121556, "start": 1240.1799999999998, "end": 1241.2, "text": " nested levels.", "tokens": [51596, 15646, 292, 4358, 13, 51647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1446758635500644, "compression_ratio": 1.5719844357976653, "no_speech_prob": 2.051935444474795e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 124120, "start": 1241.2, "end": 1246.1200000000001, "text": " The math here is dense, but the concepts are intuitive once we ground them.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 5221, 510, 307, 18011, 11, 457, 264, 10392, 366, 21769, 1564, 321, 2727, 552, 13, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13553242847837252, "compression_ratio": 1.6245487364620939, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111205894386084e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 124120, "start": 1246.32, "end": 1246.5800000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50621, 1779, 13, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13553242847837252, "compression_ratio": 1.6245487364620939, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111205894386084e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 124120, "start": 1247.0800000000002, "end": 1250.76, "text": " Let's start with level one, which Fliction defines as the state update.", "tokens": [50659, 961, 311, 722, 365, 1496, 472, 11, 597, 3235, 4105, 23122, 382, 264, 1785, 5623, 13, 50843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13553242847837252, "compression_ratio": 1.6245487364620939, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111205894386084e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 124120, "start": 1251.3400000000001, "end": 1254.92, "text": " In mathematical notation, it's a fixed mechanism acting on a changing state.", "tokens": [50872, 682, 18894, 24657, 11, 309, 311, 257, 6806, 7513, 6577, 322, 257, 4473, 1785, 13, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13553242847837252, "compression_ratio": 1.6245487364620939, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111205894386084e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 124120, "start": 1255.2, "end": 1259.3600000000001, "text": " The rules of the system do not alter, only the output shifts based on the input.", "tokens": [51065, 440, 4474, 295, 264, 1185, 360, 406, 11337, 11, 787, 264, 5598, 19201, 2361, 322, 264, 4846, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13553242847837252, "compression_ratio": 1.6245487364620939, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111205894386084e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 124120, "start": 1259.6200000000001, "end": 1262.8600000000001, "text": " Okay, think of playing a video game, like a classic Mario platformer.", "tokens": [51286, 1033, 11, 519, 295, 2433, 257, 960, 1216, 11, 411, 257, 7230, 9343, 3663, 260, 13, 51448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13553242847837252, "compression_ratio": 1.6245487364620939, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111205894386084e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 124120, "start": 1263.0800000000002, "end": 1265.52, "text": " Level one is you just sitting on the couch playing the game.", "tokens": [51459, 16872, 472, 307, 291, 445, 3798, 322, 264, 16511, 2433, 264, 1216, 13, 51581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13553242847837252, "compression_ratio": 1.6245487364620939, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111205894386084e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 124120, "start": 1265.64, "end": 1265.94, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51587, 1779, 13, 51602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13553242847837252, "compression_ratio": 1.6245487364620939, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111205894386084e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 126594, "start": 1265.94, "end": 1268.94, "text": " The physics engine, the mechanism, is totally fixed.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 10649, 2848, 11, 264, 7513, 11, 307, 3879, 6806, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1339142716775729, "compression_ratio": 1.6896551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393522382281757e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 126594, "start": 1269.0800000000002, "end": 1271.42, "text": " Gravity always pulls Mario down at the same rate.", "tokens": [50522, 49478, 1009, 16982, 9343, 760, 412, 264, 912, 3314, 13, 50639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1339142716775729, "compression_ratio": 1.6896551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393522382281757e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 126594, "start": 1271.5, "end": 1274.04, "text": " He jumps exactly the same height every time you press the button.", "tokens": [50643, 634, 16704, 2293, 264, 912, 6681, 633, 565, 291, 1886, 264, 2960, 13, 50770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1339142716775729, "compression_ratio": 1.6896551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393522382281757e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 126594, "start": 1274.3, "end": 1275.28, "text": " But the state changes.", "tokens": [50783, 583, 264, 1785, 2962, 13, 50832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1339142716775729, "compression_ratio": 1.6896551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393522382281757e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 126594, "start": 1275.76, "end": 1279.6000000000001, "text": " Mario moves from the left side of the screen to the right side based on the inputs you give", "tokens": [50856, 9343, 6067, 490, 264, 1411, 1252, 295, 264, 2568, 281, 264, 558, 1252, 2361, 322, 264, 15743, 291, 976, 51048], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1339142716775729, "compression_ratio": 1.6896551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393522382281757e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 126594, "start": 1279.6000000000001, "end": 1280.14, "text": " the controller.", "tokens": [51048, 264, 10561, 13, 51075], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1339142716775729, "compression_ratio": 1.6896551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393522382281757e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 126594, "start": 1280.28, "end": 1280.64, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51082, 7587, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1339142716775729, "compression_ratio": 1.6896551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393522382281757e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 126594, "start": 1281.14, "end": 1282.96, "text": " Fixed rules, changing state.", "tokens": [51125, 25538, 292, 4474, 11, 4473, 1785, 13, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1339142716775729, "compression_ratio": 1.6896551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393522382281757e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 126594, "start": 1283.2, "end": 1283.48, "text": " Perfect.", "tokens": [51228, 10246, 13, 51242], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1339142716775729, "compression_ratio": 1.6896551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393522382281757e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 126594, "start": 1284.46, "end": 1287.42, "text": " Moving to level two, we have the parameter update.", "tokens": [51291, 14242, 281, 1496, 732, 11, 321, 362, 264, 13075, 5623, 13, 51439], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1339142716775729, "compression_ratio": 1.6896551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393522382281757e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 126594, "start": 1287.98, "end": 1293.18, "text": " Here, the core functional form is still fixed, but a parameter within it is allowed to vary.", "tokens": [51467, 1692, 11, 264, 4965, 11745, 1254, 307, 920, 6806, 11, 457, 257, 13075, 1951, 309, 307, 4350, 281, 10559, 13, 51727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1339142716775729, "compression_ratio": 1.6896551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393522382281757e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 129318, "start": 1293.74, "end": 1295.72, "text": " Okay, so the rules can tweak slightly.", "tokens": [50393, 1033, 11, 370, 264, 4474, 393, 29879, 4748, 13, 50492], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11101824304331905, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.2643849725893497e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 129318, "start": 1295.8600000000001, "end": 1296.0600000000002, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50499, 865, 13, 50509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11101824304331905, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.2643849725893497e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 129318, "start": 1296.38, "end": 1301.2, "text": " A standard example in machine learning is an ordinary neural network updating its synaptic", "tokens": [50525, 316, 3832, 1365, 294, 3479, 2539, 307, 364, 10547, 18161, 3209, 25113, 1080, 5451, 2796, 299, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11101824304331905, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.2643849725893497e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 129318, "start": 1301.2, "end": 1302.5, "text": " weights during a training run.", "tokens": [50766, 17443, 1830, 257, 3097, 1190, 13, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11101824304331905, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.2643849725893497e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 129318, "start": 1302.6200000000001, "end": 1303.72, "text": " Back to the Mario analogy.", "tokens": [50837, 5833, 281, 264, 9343, 21663, 13, 50892], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11101824304331905, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.2643849725893497e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 129318, "start": 1304.38, "end": 1309.0800000000002, "text": " Level two is like pausing the game, going into the settings menu, and changing the difficulty", "tokens": [50925, 16872, 732, 307, 411, 2502, 7981, 264, 1216, 11, 516, 666, 264, 6257, 6510, 11, 293, 4473, 264, 10360, 51160], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11101824304331905, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.2643849725893497e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 129318, "start": 1309.0800000000002, "end": 1309.5, "text": " sliders.", "tokens": [51160, 1061, 6936, 13, 51181], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11101824304331905, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.2643849725893497e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 129318, "start": 1309.5800000000002, "end": 1309.8, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51185, 1779, 13, 51196], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11101824304331905, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.2643849725893497e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 129318, "start": 1309.8, "end": 1314.16, "text": " You increase the enemy spawn rate, or you decrease how much health Mario has.", "tokens": [51196, 509, 3488, 264, 5945, 17088, 3314, 11, 420, 291, 11514, 577, 709, 1585, 9343, 575, 13, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11101824304331905, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.2643849725893497e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 129318, "start": 1314.3600000000001, "end": 1318.8400000000001, "text": " You haven't rewritten the game's core code, still the exact same physics engine, but you've", "tokens": [51424, 509, 2378, 380, 319, 26859, 264, 1216, 311, 4965, 3089, 11, 920, 264, 1900, 912, 10649, 2848, 11, 457, 291, 600, 51648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11101824304331905, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.2643849725893497e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 129318, "start": 1318.8400000000001, "end": 1322.3200000000002, "text": " adjusted the parameters that govern how those fixed rules apply to the player.", "tokens": [51648, 19871, 264, 9834, 300, 1980, 577, 729, 6806, 4474, 3079, 281, 264, 4256, 13, 51822], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11101824304331905, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.2643849725893497e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 132232, "start": 1322.32, "end": 1323.62, "text": " Exactly like that, yeah.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 411, 300, 11, 1338, 13, 50430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13404075588498796, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.847009524491572e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 132232, "start": 1324.2, "end": 1326.56, "text": " And finally, level three is the rule update.", "tokens": [50459, 400, 2721, 11, 1496, 1045, 307, 264, 4978, 5623, 13, 50577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13404075588498796, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.847009524491572e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 132232, "start": 1326.96, "end": 1329.26, "text": " This is the most radical form of adaptation.", "tokens": [50597, 639, 307, 264, 881, 12001, 1254, 295, 21549, 13, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13404075588498796, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.847009524491572e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 132232, "start": 1330.06, "end": 1331.6799999999998, "text": " The functional mapping itself changes.", "tokens": [50752, 440, 11745, 18350, 2564, 2962, 13, 50833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13404075588498796, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.847009524491572e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 132232, "start": 1332.0, "end": 1335.6, "text": " The actual mechanism is modified by a higher order process over time.", "tokens": [50849, 440, 3539, 7513, 307, 15873, 538, 257, 2946, 1668, 1399, 670, 565, 13, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13404075588498796, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.847009524491572e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 132232, "start": 1335.76, "end": 1340.1399999999999, "text": " In our video game, level three would be the game rewriting its own source code while you", "tokens": [51037, 682, 527, 960, 1216, 11, 1496, 1045, 576, 312, 264, 1216, 319, 19868, 1080, 1065, 4009, 3089, 1339, 291, 51256], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13404075588498796, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.847009524491572e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 132232, "start": 1340.1399999999999, "end": 1340.78, "text": " were playing it.", "tokens": [51256, 645, 2433, 309, 13, 51288], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13404075588498796, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.847009524491572e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 132232, "start": 1340.9199999999998, "end": 1342.98, "text": " Yeah, which is crazy to imagine.", "tokens": [51295, 865, 11, 597, 307, 3219, 281, 3811, 13, 51398], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13404075588498796, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.847009524491572e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 132232, "start": 1343.3799999999999, "end": 1347.9199999999998, "text": " You're jumping around as Mario, and the system realizes you actually prefer puzzle games,", "tokens": [51418, 509, 434, 11233, 926, 382, 9343, 11, 293, 264, 1185, 29316, 291, 767, 4382, 12805, 2813, 11, 51645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13404075588498796, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.847009524491572e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 134792, "start": 1347.92, "end": 1351.2, "text": " so the physics engine structurally alters itself on the fly.", "tokens": [50365, 370, 264, 10649, 2848, 6594, 6512, 419, 1559, 2564, 322, 264, 3603, 13, 50529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18981316577957338, "compression_ratio": 1.5043859649122806, "no_speech_prob": 1.668239765079127e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 134792, "start": 1351.8200000000002, "end": 1355.6200000000001, "text": " Gravity shifts, the blocks rearrange, and suddenly you are playing Tetris.", "tokens": [50560, 49478, 19201, 11, 264, 8474, 39568, 11, 293, 5800, 291, 366, 2433, 31580, 5714, 13, 50750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18981316577957338, "compression_ratio": 1.5043859649122806, "no_speech_prob": 1.668239765079127e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 134792, "start": 1355.8600000000001, "end": 1360.1000000000001, "text": " The fundamental rules of reality within the system have altered themselves.", "tokens": [50762, 440, 8088, 4474, 295, 4103, 1951, 264, 1185, 362, 28783, 2969, 13, 50974], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18981316577957338, "compression_ratio": 1.5043859649122806, "no_speech_prob": 1.668239765079127e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 134792, "start": 1360.5800000000002, "end": 1366.24, "text": " Now, the true analytical power of Fitchin's essay comes from mapping our real-world examples", "tokens": [50998, 823, 11, 264, 2074, 29579, 1347, 295, 479, 1549, 259, 311, 16238, 1487, 490, 18350, 527, 957, 12, 13217, 5110, 51281], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18981316577957338, "compression_ratio": 1.5043859649122806, "no_speech_prob": 1.668239765079127e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 134792, "start": 1366.24, "end": 1367.88, "text": " onto this three-level hierarchy.", "tokens": [51281, 3911, 341, 1045, 12, 12418, 22333, 13, 51363], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18981316577957338, "compression_ratio": 1.5043859649122806, "no_speech_prob": 1.668239765079127e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 134792, "start": 1368.22, "end": 1368.44, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51380, 1033, 13, 51391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18981316577957338, "compression_ratio": 1.5043859649122806, "no_speech_prob": 1.668239765079127e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 136844, "start": 1368.44, "end": 1371.3400000000001, "text": " Let's revisit the developmental biology case.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 32676, 264, 30160, 14956, 1389, 13, 50510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1369884119624585, "compression_ratio": 1.573943661971831, "no_speech_prob": 1.649207463302882e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 136844, "start": 1371.9, "end": 1375.92, "text": " The genome creating either a human embryo or an anthrobot.", "tokens": [50538, 440, 21953, 4084, 2139, 257, 1952, 31588, 78, 420, 364, 25820, 16614, 310, 13, 50739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1369884119624585, "compression_ratio": 1.573943661971831, "no_speech_prob": 1.649207463302882e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 136844, "start": 1376.28, "end": 1377.54, "text": " Where do you think that sits?", "tokens": [50757, 2305, 360, 291, 519, 300, 12696, 30, 50820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1369884119624585, "compression_ratio": 1.573943661971831, "no_speech_prob": 1.649207463302882e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 136844, "start": 1378.0, "end": 1383.64, "text": " Well, given how wildly different an antibody is from a human windpipe, and how complex biological", "tokens": [50843, 1042, 11, 2212, 577, 34731, 819, 364, 34507, 307, 490, 257, 1952, 2468, 50042, 11, 293, 577, 3997, 13910, 51125], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1369884119624585, "compression_ratio": 1.573943661971831, "no_speech_prob": 1.649207463302882e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 136844, "start": 1383.64, "end": 1386.8, "text": " adaptation seems, my instinct is to put it at level three.", "tokens": [51125, 21549, 2544, 11, 452, 16556, 307, 281, 829, 309, 412, 1496, 1045, 13, 51283], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1369884119624585, "compression_ratio": 1.573943661971831, "no_speech_prob": 1.649207463302882e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 136844, "start": 1387.16, "end": 1389.48, "text": " It feels like the rules of reality are changing.", "tokens": [51301, 467, 3417, 411, 264, 4474, 295, 4103, 366, 4473, 13, 51417], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1369884119624585, "compression_ratio": 1.573943661971831, "no_speech_prob": 1.649207463302882e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 136844, "start": 1389.68, "end": 1390.74, "text": " It's a very common assumption.", "tokens": [51427, 467, 311, 257, 588, 2689, 15302, 13, 51480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1369884119624585, "compression_ratio": 1.573943661971831, "no_speech_prob": 1.649207463302882e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 136844, "start": 1391.02, "end": 1395.0, "text": " But Fitchin argues that the genome case actually sits cleanly at level one.", "tokens": [51494, 583, 479, 1549, 259, 38218, 300, 264, 21953, 1389, 767, 12696, 2541, 356, 412, 1496, 472, 13, 51693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1369884119624585, "compression_ratio": 1.573943661971831, "no_speech_prob": 1.649207463302882e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 139500, "start": 1395.0, "end": 1399.44, "text": " Wait, level one, just a changing state with fixed rules, how is that possible?", "tokens": [50365, 3802, 11, 1496, 472, 11, 445, 257, 4473, 1785, 365, 6806, 4474, 11, 577, 307, 300, 1944, 30, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1255549069108634, "compression_ratio": 1.6476190476190475, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203957001001637e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 139500, "start": 1399.6, "end": 1400.56, "text": " Think about the mechanism.", "tokens": [50595, 6557, 466, 264, 7513, 13, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1255549069108634, "compression_ratio": 1.6476190476190475, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203957001001637e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 139500, "start": 1401.18, "end": 1405.36, "text": " The genome itself, the interpretive apparatus of the cellular machinery reading the DNA,", "tokens": [50674, 440, 21953, 2564, 11, 264, 7302, 488, 38573, 295, 264, 29267, 27302, 3760, 264, 8272, 11, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1255549069108634, "compression_ratio": 1.6476190476190475, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203957001001637e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 139500, "start": 1405.82, "end": 1410.68, "text": " doesn't change between standard embryogenesis and induced anthrobot formation.", "tokens": [50906, 1177, 380, 1319, 1296, 3832, 31588, 8799, 9374, 293, 33991, 25820, 16614, 310, 11723, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1255549069108634, "compression_ratio": 1.6476190476190475, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203957001001637e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 139500, "start": 1411.02, "end": 1414.06, "text": " What changes is the environment, the input state.", "tokens": [51166, 708, 2962, 307, 264, 2823, 11, 264, 4846, 1785, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1255549069108634, "compression_ratio": 1.6476190476190475, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203957001001637e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 139500, "start": 1414.58, "end": 1418.76, "text": " The resulting divergence in anatomy, building a robot instead of a windpipe,", "tokens": [51344, 440, 16505, 47387, 294, 31566, 11, 2390, 257, 7881, 2602, 295, 257, 2468, 50042, 11, 51553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1255549069108634, "compression_ratio": 1.6476190476190475, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203957001001637e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 139500, "start": 1418.76, "end": 1423.42, "text": " is exactly what a fixed mechanism predicts when it is forced to operate under radically", "tokens": [51553, 307, 2293, 437, 257, 6806, 7513, 6069, 82, 562, 309, 307, 7579, 281, 9651, 833, 35508, 51786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1255549069108634, "compression_ratio": 1.6476190476190475, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203957001001637e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 139500, "start": 1423.42, "end": 1424.8, "text": " different starting conditions.", "tokens": [51786, 819, 2891, 4487, 13, 51855], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1255549069108634, "compression_ratio": 1.6476190476190475, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203957001001637e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 142500, "start": 1425.0, "end": 1425.68, "text": " Ah, I see.", "tokens": [50365, 2438, 11, 286, 536, 13, 50399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18252552680249484, "compression_ratio": 1.5168539325842696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764397146155744e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 142500, "start": 1426.18, "end": 1429.56, "text": " The DNA and the cellular machinery are the fixed Mario physics engine.", "tokens": [50424, 440, 8272, 293, 264, 29267, 27302, 366, 264, 6806, 9343, 10649, 2848, 13, 50593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18252552680249484, "compression_ratio": 1.5168539325842696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764397146155744e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 142500, "start": 1429.78, "end": 1430.12, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50604, 1079, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18252552680249484, "compression_ratio": 1.5168539325842696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764397146155744e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 142500, "start": 1430.46, "end": 1435.32, "text": " Putting that cell in a petri dish instead of a human womb is just mashing the controller", "tokens": [50638, 31367, 300, 2815, 294, 257, 3817, 470, 5025, 2602, 295, 257, 1952, 34310, 307, 445, 2300, 571, 264, 10561, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18252552680249484, "compression_ratio": 1.5168539325842696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764397146155744e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 142500, "start": 1435.32, "end": 1440.6, "text": " buttons in a completely unprecedented way, resulting in a totally different state on the screen.", "tokens": [50881, 9905, 294, 257, 2584, 21555, 636, 11, 16505, 294, 257, 3879, 819, 1785, 322, 264, 2568, 13, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18252552680249484, "compression_ratio": 1.5168539325842696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764397146155744e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 142500, "start": 1441.2, "end": 1443.2, "text": " The rules didn't change, the inputs did.", "tokens": [51175, 440, 4474, 994, 380, 1319, 11, 264, 15743, 630, 13, 51275], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18252552680249484, "compression_ratio": 1.5168539325842696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764397146155744e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 142500, "start": 1443.7, "end": 1444.24, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51300, 48746, 736, 13, 51327], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18252552680249484, "compression_ratio": 1.5168539325842696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764397146155744e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 142500, "start": 1444.52, "end": 1446.84, "text": " Now, let's analyze large language models.", "tokens": [51341, 823, 11, 718, 311, 12477, 2416, 2856, 5245, 13, 51457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18252552680249484, "compression_ratio": 1.5168539325842696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764397146155744e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 142500, "start": 1447.16, "end": 1449.2, "text": " Where do they reside in the hierarchy?", "tokens": [51473, 2305, 360, 436, 40134, 294, 264, 22333, 30, 51575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18252552680249484, "compression_ratio": 1.5168539325842696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764397146155744e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 144920, "start": 1449.2, "end": 1455.04, "text": " Well, when I'm actually using an LLM at inference time, tapping a prompt into ChatGPT or Claude,", "tokens": [50365, 1042, 11, 562, 286, 478, 767, 1228, 364, 441, 43, 44, 412, 38253, 565, 11, 21444, 257, 12391, 666, 27503, 38, 47, 51, 420, 12947, 2303, 11, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18283708068146104, "compression_ratio": 1.4583333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490542655359097e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 144920, "start": 1455.04, "end": 1456.24, "text": " it has to be level one.", "tokens": [50657, 309, 575, 281, 312, 1496, 472, 13, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18283708068146104, "compression_ratio": 1.4583333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490542655359097e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 144920, "start": 1456.24, "end": 1456.64, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50717, 1779, 13, 50737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18283708068146104, "compression_ratio": 1.4583333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490542655359097e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 144920, "start": 1456.64, "end": 1461.8400000000001, "text": " The neural network's weights are frozen, the mechanism is fixed, my prompt goes in, the state", "tokens": [50737, 440, 18161, 3209, 311, 17443, 366, 12496, 11, 264, 7513, 307, 6806, 11, 452, 12391, 1709, 294, 11, 264, 1785, 50997], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18283708068146104, "compression_ratio": 1.4583333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490542655359097e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 144920, "start": 1461.8400000000001, "end": 1466.8, "text": " updates, text comes out, the model isn't learning or changing its parameters during our chat.", "tokens": [50997, 9205, 11, 2487, 1487, 484, 11, 264, 2316, 1943, 380, 2539, 420, 4473, 1080, 9834, 1830, 527, 5081, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18283708068146104, "compression_ratio": 1.4583333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490542655359097e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 146680, "start": 1466.8, "end": 1470.0, "text": " Which perfectly explains the episodic gap we discussed earlier.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 6239, 13948, 264, 39200, 299, 7417, 321, 7152, 3071, 13, 50525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17332308805441554, "compression_ratio": 1.4827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.5732988913400026e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 146680, "start": 1470.0, "end": 1474.48, "text": " Any level two parameter updating, the massive shifting of weights across billions of connections", "tokens": [50525, 2639, 1496, 732, 13075, 25113, 11, 264, 5994, 17573, 295, 17443, 2108, 17375, 295, 9271, 50749], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17332308805441554, "compression_ratio": 1.4827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.5732988913400026e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 146680, "start": 1474.48, "end": 1476.7, "text": " happens completely offline.", "tokens": [50749, 2314, 2584, 21857, 13, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17332308805441554, "compression_ratio": 1.4827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.5732988913400026e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 146680, "start": 1476.8, "end": 1477.74, "text": " During the training phase.", "tokens": [50865, 6842, 264, 3097, 5574, 13, 50912], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17332308805441554, "compression_ratio": 1.4827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.5732988913400026e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 146680, "start": 1478.0, "end": 1478.24, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50925, 1779, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17332308805441554, "compression_ratio": 1.4827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.5732988913400026e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 146680, "start": 1478.44, "end": 1480.78, "text": " In a server farm long before you ever said hello.", "tokens": [50947, 682, 257, 7154, 5421, 938, 949, 291, 1562, 848, 7751, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17332308805441554, "compression_ratio": 1.4827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.5732988913400026e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 146680, "start": 1481.06, "end": 1484.9199999999998, "text": " It's totally divorced from the system's lived episode of Talking to Me.", "tokens": [51078, 467, 311, 3879, 27670, 490, 264, 1185, 311, 5152, 3500, 295, 22445, 281, 1923, 13, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17332308805441554, "compression_ratio": 1.4827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.5732988913400026e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 148492, "start": 1484.92, "end": 1490.72, "text": " To stick with the analogy, it's like the AI's settings menu can only be accessed by the", "tokens": [50365, 1407, 2897, 365, 264, 21663, 11, 309, 311, 411, 264, 7318, 311, 6257, 6510, 393, 787, 312, 34211, 538, 264, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509810302217128, "compression_ratio": 1.6418918918918919, "no_speech_prob": 1.7015453716157092e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 148492, "start": 1490.72, "end": 1493.24, "text": " developers when the game is turned completely off.", "tokens": [50655, 8849, 562, 264, 1216, 307, 3574, 2584, 766, 13, 50781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509810302217128, "compression_ratio": 1.6418918918918919, "no_speech_prob": 1.7015453716157092e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 148492, "start": 1493.3200000000002, "end": 1493.66, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50785, 1079, 13, 50802], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509810302217128, "compression_ratio": 1.6418918918918919, "no_speech_prob": 1.7015453716157092e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 148492, "start": 1493.8600000000001, "end": 1498.3600000000001, "text": " While the game is running and interacting with the world, it cannot structurally learn.", "tokens": [50812, 3987, 264, 1216, 307, 2614, 293, 18017, 365, 264, 1002, 11, 309, 2644, 6594, 6512, 1466, 13, 51037], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509810302217128, "compression_ratio": 1.6418918918918919, "no_speech_prob": 1.7015453716157092e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 148492, "start": 1498.78, "end": 1502.16, "text": " It cannot update its own parameters based on our real-time conversation.", "tokens": [51058, 467, 2644, 5623, 1080, 1065, 9834, 2361, 322, 527, 957, 12, 3766, 3761, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509810302217128, "compression_ratio": 1.6418918918918919, "no_speech_prob": 1.7015453716157092e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 148492, "start": 1502.5800000000002, "end": 1506.66, "text": " And Flickjino warns extensively about the danger of conflating level two and level three.", "tokens": [51248, 400, 3235, 618, 73, 2982, 12286, 82, 32636, 466, 264, 4330, 295, 1497, 75, 990, 1496, 732, 293, 1496, 1045, 13, 51452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509810302217128, "compression_ratio": 1.6418918918918919, "no_speech_prob": 1.7015453716157092e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 148492, "start": 1507.16, "end": 1512.38, "text": " Just because a system is capable of updating its weights, which is level two, does not mean", "tokens": [51477, 1449, 570, 257, 1185, 307, 8189, 295, 25113, 1080, 17443, 11, 597, 307, 1496, 732, 11, 775, 406, 914, 51738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509810302217128, "compression_ratio": 1.6418918918918919, "no_speech_prob": 1.7015453716157092e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 151238, "start": 1512.38, "end": 1516.5400000000002, "text": " it is capable of rewriting its own fundamental architecture, level three.", "tokens": [50365, 309, 307, 8189, 295, 319, 19868, 1080, 1065, 8088, 9482, 11, 1496, 1045, 13, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1719631379650485, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881507042959543e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 151238, "start": 1516.74, "end": 1520.16, "text": " Which brings us to the lingering mystery of the Pagazzi ratchet.", "tokens": [50583, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 49542, 11422, 295, 264, 430, 559, 33910, 45885, 13, 50754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1719631379650485, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881507042959543e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 151238, "start": 1520.66, "end": 1520.98, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50779, 1079, 13, 50795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1719631379650485, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881507042959543e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 151238, "start": 1521.22, "end": 1527.0400000000002, "text": " The biological system that forgets the data, but keeps the structural upgrade in causal emergence.", "tokens": [50807, 440, 13910, 1185, 300, 2870, 82, 264, 1412, 11, 457, 5965, 264, 15067, 11484, 294, 38755, 36211, 13, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1719631379650485, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881507042959543e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 151238, "start": 1527.5400000000002, "end": 1530.4, "text": " Does that irreversible ratchet operate at level two or level three?", "tokens": [51123, 4402, 300, 16014, 840, 964, 45885, 9651, 412, 1496, 732, 420, 1496, 1045, 30, 51266], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1719631379650485, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881507042959543e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 151238, "start": 1530.7600000000002, "end": 1534.66, "text": " Flickjino concedes that this is the trickiest question and honestly leaves it unresolved,", "tokens": [51284, 3235, 618, 73, 2982, 416, 21526, 300, 341, 307, 264, 4282, 6495, 1168, 293, 6095, 5510, 309, 517, 495, 29110, 11, 51479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1719631379650485, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881507042959543e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 151238, "start": 1534.66, "end": 1540.68, "text": " because Pagazzi's underlying manuscript detailing the exact mechanisms isn't publicly available yet.", "tokens": [51479, 570, 430, 559, 33910, 311, 14217, 23928, 42459, 264, 1900, 15902, 1943, 380, 14843, 2435, 1939, 13, 51780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1719631379650485, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881507042959543e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 151238, "start": 1540.8400000000001, "end": 1541.6000000000001, "text": " Oh, that's frustrating.", "tokens": [51788, 876, 11, 300, 311, 16522, 13, 51826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1719631379650485, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881507042959543e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 154160, "start": 1541.6, "end": 1542.3799999999999, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 13, 50404], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.112298471885815, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 154160, "start": 1543.26, "end": 1548.12, "text": " Is the asymmetric ratchet simply a permanent, irreversible change in synaptic weights,", "tokens": [50448, 1119, 264, 37277, 17475, 45885, 2935, 257, 10996, 11, 16014, 840, 964, 1319, 294, 5451, 2796, 299, 17443, 11, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.112298471885815, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 154160, "start": 1548.6599999999999, "end": 1550.1, "text": " which would keep it at level two?", "tokens": [50718, 597, 576, 1066, 309, 412, 1496, 732, 30, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.112298471885815, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 154160, "start": 1550.6999999999998, "end": 1556.74, "text": " Or is the biological system literally changing its network topology, physically growing or", "tokens": [50820, 1610, 307, 264, 13910, 1185, 3736, 4473, 1080, 3209, 1192, 1793, 11, 9762, 4194, 420, 51122], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.112298471885815, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 154160, "start": 1556.74, "end": 1559.52, "text": " pruning connections, which would elevate it to level three?", "tokens": [51122, 582, 37726, 9271, 11, 597, 576, 33054, 309, 281, 1496, 1045, 30, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.112298471885815, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 154160, "start": 1559.6599999999999, "end": 1563.08, "text": " So we don't have the data to definitively say one way or the other.", "tokens": [51268, 407, 321, 500, 380, 362, 264, 1412, 281, 28152, 356, 584, 472, 636, 420, 264, 661, 13, 51439], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.112298471885815, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 154160, "start": 1563.1999999999998, "end": 1563.78, "text": " We don't.", "tokens": [51445, 492, 500, 380, 13, 51474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.112298471885815, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 154160, "start": 1563.8799999999999, "end": 1567.4399999999998, "text": " And Flickjino is careful to map out the boundaries of what we currently know.", "tokens": [51479, 400, 3235, 618, 73, 2982, 307, 5026, 281, 4471, 484, 264, 13180, 295, 437, 321, 4362, 458, 13, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.112298471885815, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 156744, "start": 1567.44, "end": 1573.46, "text": " The essay even introduces a completely alternative perspective from a researcher named Heisinger.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 16238, 754, 31472, 257, 2584, 8535, 4585, 490, 257, 21751, 4926, 634, 3436, 260, 13, 50666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11345410346984863, "compression_ratio": 1.66, "no_speech_prob": 1.635967186372489e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 156744, "start": 1573.56, "end": 1576.5, "text": " Who holds a much more radical view of biological development, right?", "tokens": [50671, 2102, 9190, 257, 709, 544, 12001, 1910, 295, 13910, 3250, 11, 558, 30, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11345410346984863, "compression_ratio": 1.66, "no_speech_prob": 1.635967186372489e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 156744, "start": 1576.74, "end": 1577.4, "text": " Very radical.", "tokens": [50830, 4372, 12001, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11345410346984863, "compression_ratio": 1.66, "no_speech_prob": 1.635967186372489e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 156744, "start": 1577.9, "end": 1584.14, "text": " Heisinger argues that in wet biology, the operator, meaning the rule, and the history, meaning the state,", "tokens": [50888, 634, 3436, 260, 38218, 300, 294, 6630, 14956, 11, 264, 12973, 11, 3620, 264, 4978, 11, 293, 264, 2503, 11, 3620, 264, 1785, 11, 51200], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11345410346984863, "compression_ratio": 1.66, "no_speech_prob": 1.635967186372489e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 156744, "start": 1584.52, "end": 1586.24, "text": " might be completely inseparable.", "tokens": [51219, 1062, 312, 2584, 33874, 42012, 13, 51305], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11345410346984863, "compression_ratio": 1.66, "no_speech_prob": 1.635967186372489e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 156744, "start": 1586.46, "end": 1590.8400000000001, "text": " Meaning you can't even split them into a mechanism and an input like we do in computer science.", "tokens": [51316, 19948, 291, 393, 380, 754, 7472, 552, 666, 257, 7513, 293, 364, 4846, 411, 321, 360, 294, 3820, 3497, 13, 51535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11345410346984863, "compression_ratio": 1.66, "no_speech_prob": 1.635967186372489e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 159084, "start": 1590.84, "end": 1591.32, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18591079065355204, "compression_ratio": 1.43125, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579869409841466e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 159084, "start": 1591.58, "end": 1595.4199999999998, "text": " Heisinger suggests they might act as a single, indivisible, ongoing computation.", "tokens": [50402, 634, 3436, 260, 13409, 436, 1062, 605, 382, 257, 2167, 11, 1016, 592, 271, 964, 11, 10452, 24903, 13, 50594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18591079065355204, "compression_ratio": 1.43125, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579869409841466e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 159084, "start": 1595.86, "end": 1596.1599999999999, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50616, 3153, 13, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18591079065355204, "compression_ratio": 1.43125, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579869409841466e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 159084, "start": 1596.32, "end": 1602.6399999999999, "text": " If Heisinger is right, Flickjino's entire mathematical separation of history becoming an operator is just an analytical approximation.", "tokens": [50639, 759, 634, 3436, 260, 307, 558, 11, 3235, 618, 73, 2982, 311, 2302, 18894, 14634, 295, 2503, 5617, 364, 12973, 307, 445, 364, 29579, 28023, 13, 50955], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18591079065355204, "compression_ratio": 1.43125, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579869409841466e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 160264, "start": 1602.64, "end": 1609.72, "text": " It's a useful theoretical map, but it fundamentally misrepresents the messy, integrated territory of living tissue.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 257, 4420, 20864, 4471, 11, 457, 309, 17879, 3346, 265, 14508, 791, 264, 16191, 11, 10919, 11360, 295, 2647, 12404, 13, 50719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14505627280787417, "compression_ratio": 1.6071428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 2.1336840714397676e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 160264, "start": 1610.26, "end": 1615.1000000000001, "text": " But regardless of whether the ratchet is level two or level three, or if Heisinger's holistic view is correct,", "tokens": [50746, 583, 10060, 295, 1968, 264, 45885, 307, 1496, 732, 420, 1496, 1045, 11, 420, 498, 634, 3436, 260, 311, 30334, 1910, 307, 3006, 11, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14505627280787417, "compression_ratio": 1.6071428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 2.1336840714397676e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 160264, "start": 1615.74, "end": 1620.9, "text": " Flickjino still isolates the central underlying mechanism that makes the ratchet possible.", "tokens": [51020, 3235, 618, 73, 2982, 920, 7381, 1024, 264, 5777, 14217, 7513, 300, 1669, 264, 45885, 1944, 13, 51278], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14505627280787417, "compression_ratio": 1.6071428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 2.1336840714397676e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 160264, "start": 1621.1000000000001, "end": 1621.3600000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51288, 1079, 13, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14505627280787417, "compression_ratio": 1.6071428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 2.1336840714397676e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 160264, "start": 1621.76, "end": 1627.0600000000002, "text": " We have to figure out under what mathematical conditions a system inherits this irreversibility.", "tokens": [51321, 492, 362, 281, 2573, 484, 833, 437, 18894, 4487, 257, 1185, 9484, 1208, 341, 16014, 840, 2841, 13, 51586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14505627280787417, "compression_ratio": 1.6071428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 2.1336840714397676e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 160264, "start": 1627.5600000000002, "end": 1631.1000000000001, "text": " Why does wiping the biological state not wipe the structural upgrade?", "tokens": [51611, 1545, 775, 40611, 264, 13910, 1785, 406, 14082, 264, 15067, 11484, 30, 51788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14505627280787417, "compression_ratio": 1.6071428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 2.1336840714397676e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 160264, "start": 1631.3400000000001, "end": 1631.6000000000001, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51800, 1033, 13, 51813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14505627280787417, "compression_ratio": 1.6071428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 2.1336840714397676e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 163160, "start": 1631.6, "end": 1640.24, "text": " To find the candidate mechanism for this irreversibility, Flickjino turns to a formalization of causal emergence developed by Eric Hull.", "tokens": [50365, 1407, 915, 264, 11532, 7513, 337, 341, 16014, 840, 2841, 11, 3235, 618, 73, 2982, 4523, 281, 257, 9860, 2144, 295, 38755, 36211, 4743, 538, 9336, 389, 858, 13, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14831582137516566, "compression_ratio": 1.6521739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947618438831191e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 163160, "start": 1640.6599999999999, "end": 1640.9399999999998, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50818, 1033, 13, 50832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14831582137516566, "compression_ratio": 1.6521739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947618438831191e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 163160, "start": 1641.04, "end": 1641.74, "text": " What does Hull say?", "tokens": [50837, 708, 775, 389, 858, 584, 30, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14831582137516566, "compression_ratio": 1.6521739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947618438831191e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 163160, "start": 1642.02, "end": 1646.84, "text": " Hull defines a concept called effective information using a very specific formula.", "tokens": [50886, 389, 858, 23122, 257, 3410, 1219, 4942, 1589, 1228, 257, 588, 2685, 8513, 13, 51127], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14831582137516566, "compression_ratio": 1.6521739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947618438831191e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 163160, "start": 1647.4599999999998, "end": 1652.02, "text": " Effective information equals determinism minus degeneracy.", "tokens": [51158, 17764, 488, 1589, 6915, 15957, 1434, 3175, 40520, 2551, 13, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14831582137516566, "compression_ratio": 1.6521739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947618438831191e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 163160, "start": 1652.28, "end": 1653.8799999999999, "text": " Determinism minus degeneracy.", "tokens": [51399, 4237, 966, 259, 1434, 3175, 40520, 2551, 13, 51479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14831582137516566, "compression_ratio": 1.6521739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947618438831191e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 163160, "start": 1653.9599999999998, "end": 1657.04, "text": " Let's translate this out of the math and back into the physical world for you listening.", "tokens": [51483, 961, 311, 13799, 341, 484, 295, 264, 5221, 293, 646, 666, 264, 4001, 1002, 337, 291, 4764, 13, 51637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14831582137516566, "compression_ratio": 1.6521739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947618438831191e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 163160, "start": 1657.26, "end": 1658.52, "text": " Let's break down the components.", "tokens": [51648, 961, 311, 1821, 760, 264, 6677, 13, 51711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14831582137516566, "compression_ratio": 1.6521739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947618438831191e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 165852, "start": 1658.52, "end": 1665.52, "text": " Causal emergence, that macro-level intelligence and agency we've been discussing, happens when you coarse-grain a system.", "tokens": [50365, 7544, 11765, 36211, 11, 300, 18887, 12, 12418, 7599, 293, 7934, 321, 600, 668, 10850, 11, 2314, 562, 291, 39312, 12, 70, 7146, 257, 1185, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14267200104733732, "compression_ratio": 1.663677130044843, "no_speech_prob": 2.634711676260948e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 165852, "start": 1665.74, "end": 1666.48, "text": " Coarse-graining?", "tokens": [50726, 3066, 11668, 12, 20735, 1760, 30, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14267200104733732, "compression_ratio": 1.663677130044843, "no_speech_prob": 2.634711676260948e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 165852, "start": 1666.66, "end": 1667.0, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50772, 1079, 13, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14267200104733732, "compression_ratio": 1.663677130044843, "no_speech_prob": 2.634711676260948e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 165852, "start": 1667.3799999999999, "end": 1669.66, "text": " Coarse-graining simply means zooming out.", "tokens": [50808, 3066, 11668, 12, 20735, 1760, 2935, 1355, 48226, 484, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14267200104733732, "compression_ratio": 1.663677130044843, "no_speech_prob": 2.634711676260948e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 165852, "start": 1669.98, "end": 1673.3, "text": " You stop looking at the individual trees and start looking at the forest.", "tokens": [50938, 509, 1590, 1237, 412, 264, 2609, 5852, 293, 722, 1237, 412, 264, 6719, 13, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14267200104733732, "compression_ratio": 1.663677130044843, "no_speech_prob": 2.634711676260948e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 165852, "start": 1673.66, "end": 1680.24, "text": " When a system coarse-grains its own internal data, two things can happen to increase its effective information.", "tokens": [51122, 1133, 257, 1185, 39312, 12, 20735, 1292, 1080, 1065, 6920, 1412, 11, 732, 721, 393, 1051, 281, 3488, 1080, 4942, 1589, 13, 51451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14267200104733732, "compression_ratio": 1.663677130044843, "no_speech_prob": 2.634711676260948e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 168024, "start": 1680.24, "end": 1683.24, "text": " First, it can sharpen determinism.", "tokens": [50365, 2386, 11, 309, 393, 31570, 15957, 1434, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21041224219582297, "compression_ratio": 1.3305084745762712, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127119392180366e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 168024, "start": 1683.88, "end": 1690.0, "text": " Meaning, macro-states lead more reliably to specific successor states than micro-states do.", "tokens": [50547, 19948, 11, 18887, 12, 372, 1024, 1477, 544, 49927, 281, 2685, 31864, 4368, 813, 4532, 12, 372, 1024, 360, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21041224219582297, "compression_ratio": 1.3305084745762712, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127119392180366e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 168024, "start": 1690.16, "end": 1691.4, "text": " Let's try an analogy for that.", "tokens": [50861, 961, 311, 853, 364, 21663, 337, 300, 13, 50923], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21041224219582297, "compression_ratio": 1.3305084745762712, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127119392180366e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 169140, "start": 1691.4, "end": 1699.4, "text": " Okay, if I look at the individual atoms of a baseball in midair, it's a chaotic mess of quantum vibrations.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 498, 286, 574, 412, 264, 2609, 16871, 295, 257, 14323, 294, 2062, 1246, 11, 309, 311, 257, 27013, 2082, 295, 13018, 32339, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10667263911320612, "compression_ratio": 1.3942857142857144, "no_speech_prob": 2.0435029536580718e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 169140, "start": 1699.76, "end": 1703.8400000000001, "text": " I cannot reliably predict where every single atom is going to be in two seconds.", "tokens": [50783, 286, 2644, 49927, 6069, 689, 633, 2167, 12018, 307, 516, 281, 312, 294, 732, 3949, 13, 50987], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10667263911320612, "compression_ratio": 1.3942857142857144, "no_speech_prob": 2.0435029536580718e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 169140, "start": 1704.0400000000002, "end": 1704.26, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50997, 1779, 13, 51008], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10667263911320612, "compression_ratio": 1.3942857142857144, "no_speech_prob": 2.0435029536580718e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 169140, "start": 1704.3200000000002, "end": 1706.92, "text": " The determinism at the micro-level is very weak.", "tokens": [51011, 440, 15957, 1434, 412, 264, 4532, 12, 12418, 307, 588, 5336, 13, 51141], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10667263911320612, "compression_ratio": 1.3942857142857144, "no_speech_prob": 2.0435029536580718e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 170692, "start": 1706.92, "end": 1715.5800000000002, "text": " But, if I coarse-grain the system, if I zoom out and just look at the macro-object we call a baseball, I can use basic physics to determine exactly where it will land.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 11, 498, 286, 39312, 12, 70, 7146, 264, 1185, 11, 498, 286, 8863, 484, 293, 445, 574, 412, 264, 18887, 12, 41070, 321, 818, 257, 14323, 11, 286, 393, 764, 3875, 10649, 281, 6997, 2293, 689, 309, 486, 2117, 13, 50798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08933479931889748, "compression_ratio": 1.5867768595041323, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302422314717677e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 170692, "start": 1716.0800000000002, "end": 1719.0800000000002, "text": " The determinism sharpens dramatically when you look at the macro-structure.", "tokens": [50823, 440, 15957, 1434, 8199, 694, 17548, 562, 291, 574, 412, 264, 18887, 12, 372, 2885, 13, 50973], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08933479931889748, "compression_ratio": 1.5867768595041323, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302422314717677e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 170692, "start": 1719.14, "end": 1719.92, "text": " A perfect illustration.", "tokens": [50976, 316, 2176, 22645, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08933479931889748, "compression_ratio": 1.5867768595041323, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302422314717677e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 170692, "start": 1720.42, "end": 1724.0800000000002, "text": " Now, the second way to increase effective information is to reduce degeneracy.", "tokens": [51040, 823, 11, 264, 1150, 636, 281, 3488, 4942, 1589, 307, 281, 5407, 40520, 2551, 13, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08933479931889748, "compression_ratio": 1.5867768595041323, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302422314717677e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 170692, "start": 1724.24, "end": 1726.0600000000002, "text": " Okay, how did degeneracy fit in here?", "tokens": [51231, 1033, 11, 577, 630, 40520, 2551, 3318, 294, 510, 30, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08933479931889748, "compression_ratio": 1.5867768595041323, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302422314717677e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 172606, "start": 1726.06, "end": 1733.48, "text": " In this specific mathematical context, degeneracy means multiple different microstates collapsing onto the exact same macro-state.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 341, 2685, 18894, 4319, 11, 40520, 2551, 1355, 3866, 819, 3123, 27494, 1024, 45339, 3911, 264, 1900, 912, 18887, 12, 15406, 13, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12144912161478182, "compression_ratio": 1.5387931034482758, "no_speech_prob": 1.427136403844842e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 172606, "start": 1733.6399999999999, "end": 1741.36, "text": " So, high degeneracy means there are a billion different messy ways the internal atoms could be arranged that still just look like a standard baseball to us.", "tokens": [50744, 407, 11, 1090, 40520, 2551, 1355, 456, 366, 257, 5218, 819, 16191, 2098, 264, 6920, 16871, 727, 312, 18721, 300, 920, 445, 574, 411, 257, 3832, 14323, 281, 505, 13, 51130], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12144912161478182, "compression_ratio": 1.5387931034482758, "no_speech_prob": 1.427136403844842e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 172606, "start": 1741.58, "end": 1741.84, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51141, 1779, 13, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12144912161478182, "compression_ratio": 1.5387931034482758, "no_speech_prob": 1.427136403844842e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 172606, "start": 1742.2, "end": 1746.44, "text": " And this leads to Fliction's grand hypothesis, conjecture 7.1.", "tokens": [51172, 400, 341, 6689, 281, 3235, 4105, 311, 2697, 17291, 11, 416, 1020, 540, 1614, 13, 16, 13, 51384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12144912161478182, "compression_ratio": 1.5387931034482758, "no_speech_prob": 1.427136403844842e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 174644, "start": 1746.44, "end": 1758.68, "text": " Fliction conjectures that structural revision inherits its irreversibility, the reason the ratchet only turns one way, specifically when the change the system undergoes, is degeneracy reducing.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 416, 1020, 1303, 300, 15067, 34218, 9484, 1208, 1080, 16014, 840, 2841, 11, 264, 1778, 264, 45885, 787, 4523, 472, 636, 11, 4682, 562, 264, 1319, 264, 1185, 26426, 279, 11, 307, 40520, 2551, 12245, 13, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10540145093744452, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295842713426323e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 174644, "start": 1758.68, "end": 1759.92, "text": " Okay, let's pause here.", "tokens": [50977, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 10465, 510, 13, 51039], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10540145093744452, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295842713426323e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 174644, "start": 1761.1000000000001, "end": 1772.5800000000002, "text": " When the system learns something that permanently reduces the number of messy microstates that collapse into a macro-state, why does that specific act make the learning irreversible?", "tokens": [51098, 1133, 264, 1185, 27152, 746, 300, 24042, 18081, 264, 1230, 295, 16191, 3123, 27494, 1024, 300, 15584, 666, 257, 18887, 12, 15406, 11, 983, 775, 300, 2685, 605, 652, 264, 2539, 16014, 840, 964, 30, 51672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10540145093744452, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295842713426323e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 177258, "start": 1773.04, "end": 1776.48, "text": " Fliction anchors this conjecture in three distinct mathematical domains.", "tokens": [50388, 3235, 4105, 12723, 830, 341, 416, 1020, 540, 294, 1045, 10644, 18894, 25514, 13, 50560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16442677468964548, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.9883777784002188e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 177258, "start": 1776.8799999999999, "end": 1778.6999999999998, "text": " The first anchor is thermodynamics.", "tokens": [50580, 440, 700, 18487, 307, 8810, 35483, 13, 50671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16442677468964548, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.9883777784002188e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 177258, "start": 1778.8799999999999, "end": 1780.02, "text": " Like heat and energy.", "tokens": [50680, 1743, 3738, 293, 2281, 13, 50737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16442677468964548, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.9883777784002188e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 177258, "start": 1780.26, "end": 1780.52, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50749, 1779, 13, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16442677468964548, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.9883777784002188e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 177258, "start": 1780.78, "end": 1785.0, "text": " In physics, the act of coarse-graining collapses distinguishable microtrajectories.", "tokens": [50775, 682, 10649, 11, 264, 605, 295, 39312, 12, 20735, 1760, 48765, 20206, 712, 3123, 10536, 424, 1020, 2083, 13, 50986], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16442677468964548, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.9883777784002188e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 177258, "start": 1785.06, "end": 1792.48, "text": " When a system compresses information to form a macro-state, it literally destroys the distinctions between the original micro-states.", "tokens": [50989, 1133, 257, 1185, 14778, 279, 1589, 281, 1254, 257, 18887, 12, 15406, 11, 309, 3736, 36714, 264, 1483, 49798, 1296, 264, 3380, 4532, 12, 372, 1024, 13, 51360], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16442677468964548, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.9883777784002188e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 177258, "start": 1792.5, "end": 1793.0, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [51361, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16442677468964548, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.9883777784002188e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 177258, "start": 1793.28, "end": 1801.6399999999999, "text": " You cannot reverse the process because the exact information needed to un-collapse it to figure out exactly which specific micro-state you started in was burned up in the compression.", "tokens": [51400, 509, 2644, 9943, 264, 1399, 570, 264, 1900, 1589, 2978, 281, 517, 12, 33891, 11145, 309, 281, 2573, 484, 2293, 597, 2685, 4532, 12, 15406, 291, 1409, 294, 390, 13490, 493, 294, 264, 19355, 13, 51818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16442677468964548, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.9883777784002188e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 180164, "start": 1801.64, "end": 1803.0400000000002, "text": " You can't un-bake a cake.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 393, 380, 517, 12, 65, 619, 257, 5908, 13, 50435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14797590155350535, "compression_ratio": 1.6954732510288066, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056251802235247e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 180164, "start": 1803.64, "end": 1806.24, "text": " The heat destroys the boundaries between the egg and the flour.", "tokens": [50465, 440, 3738, 36714, 264, 13180, 1296, 264, 3777, 293, 264, 7693, 13, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14797590155350535, "compression_ratio": 1.6954732510288066, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056251802235247e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 180164, "start": 1806.3600000000001, "end": 1807.4, "text": " You can't separate them again.", "tokens": [50601, 509, 393, 380, 4994, 552, 797, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14797590155350535, "compression_ratio": 1.6954732510288066, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056251802235247e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 180164, "start": 1807.74, "end": 1808.14, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50670, 7587, 13, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14797590155350535, "compression_ratio": 1.6954732510288066, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056251802235247e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 180164, "start": 1808.88, "end": 1816.96, "text": " The second anchor comes from Fliction's own earlier work in the ecology of distinctions, specifically a concept called the semantic horizon theorem.", "tokens": [50727, 440, 1150, 18487, 1487, 490, 3235, 4105, 311, 1065, 3071, 589, 294, 264, 39683, 295, 1483, 49798, 11, 4682, 257, 3410, 1219, 264, 47982, 18046, 20904, 13, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14797590155350535, "compression_ratio": 1.6954732510288066, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056251802235247e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 180164, "start": 1817.44, "end": 1818.7800000000002, "text": " Let's unpack that theorem.", "tokens": [51155, 961, 311, 26699, 300, 20904, 13, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14797590155350535, "compression_ratio": 1.6954732510288066, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056251802235247e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 180164, "start": 1819.0, "end": 1825.1200000000001, "text": " The semantic horizon theorem proves mathematically that recoverability falls as distinction classes merge.", "tokens": [51233, 440, 47982, 18046, 20904, 25019, 44003, 300, 8114, 2310, 8804, 382, 16844, 5359, 22183, 13, 51539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14797590155350535, "compression_ratio": 1.6954732510288066, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056251802235247e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 182512, "start": 1825.12, "end": 1838.36, "text": " So once a biological system merges two different concepts or states into a single unified memory to save space or increase efficiency, you permanently lose the ability to recover the original granular distinction.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 1564, 257, 13910, 1185, 3551, 2880, 732, 819, 10392, 420, 4368, 666, 257, 2167, 26787, 4675, 281, 3155, 1901, 420, 3488, 10493, 11, 291, 24042, 3624, 264, 3485, 281, 8114, 264, 3380, 39962, 16844, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10780938823571366, "compression_ratio": 1.5576208178438662, "no_speech_prob": 1.868609867533566e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 182512, "start": 1838.6599999999999, "end": 1838.9799999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51042, 1779, 13, 51058], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10780938823571366, "compression_ratio": 1.5576208178438662, "no_speech_prob": 1.868609867533566e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 182512, "start": 1839.1599999999999, "end": 1842.5, "text": " The semantic horizon has been crossed and you just can't see back over it.", "tokens": [51067, 440, 47982, 18046, 575, 668, 14622, 293, 291, 445, 393, 380, 536, 646, 670, 309, 13, 51234], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10780938823571366, "compression_ratio": 1.5576208178438662, "no_speech_prob": 1.868609867533566e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 182512, "start": 1842.76, "end": 1849.6599999999999, "text": " And the third anchor Fliction uses is from a paper titled History Before Function, specifically the anti-alignment theorem.", "tokens": [51247, 400, 264, 2636, 18487, 3235, 4105, 4960, 307, 490, 257, 3035, 19841, 12486, 4546, 11166, 882, 11, 4682, 264, 6061, 12, 304, 41134, 20904, 13, 51592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10780938823571366, "compression_ratio": 1.5576208178438662, "no_speech_prob": 1.868609867533566e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 184966, "start": 1849.66, "end": 1852.8200000000002, "text": " This theorem is perhaps the most profound of the three.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 20904, 307, 4317, 264, 881, 14382, 295, 264, 1045, 13, 50523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11041009993780226, "compression_ratio": 1.5950413223140496, "no_speech_prob": 1.890337929591479e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 184966, "start": 1853.52, "end": 1866.68, "text": " It demonstrates that the most efficient way to compress a complex history into an active, usable operator intentionally discards the exact diagnostic details you would need to hypothesize what the pre-training configuration was.", "tokens": [50558, 467, 31034, 300, 264, 881, 7148, 636, 281, 14778, 257, 3997, 2503, 666, 364, 4967, 11, 29975, 12973, 22062, 2983, 2287, 264, 1900, 27897, 4365, 291, 576, 643, 281, 14276, 1125, 437, 264, 659, 12, 17227, 1760, 11694, 390, 13, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11041009993780226, "compression_ratio": 1.5950413223140496, "no_speech_prob": 1.890337929591479e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 184966, "start": 1866.78, "end": 1868.5, "text": " It's actively deleting the breadcrumbs.", "tokens": [51221, 467, 311, 13022, 48946, 264, 5961, 66, 6247, 929, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11041009993780226, "compression_ratio": 1.5950413223140496, "no_speech_prob": 1.890337929591479e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 184966, "start": 1868.8400000000001, "end": 1871.7, "text": " Let's bring all this dense math back to the human experience.", "tokens": [51324, 961, 311, 1565, 439, 341, 18011, 5221, 646, 281, 264, 1952, 1752, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11041009993780226, "compression_ratio": 1.5950413223140496, "no_speech_prob": 1.890337929591479e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 187170, "start": 1871.7, "end": 1879.5800000000002, "text": " What does the intersection of thermodynamics, semantic horizons, and anti-alignment actually mean for how we live and learn?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 775, 264, 15236, 295, 8810, 35483, 11, 47982, 7937, 892, 11, 293, 6061, 12, 304, 41134, 767, 914, 337, 577, 321, 1621, 293, 1466, 30, 50759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10410001430105656, "compression_ratio": 1.6064981949458483, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427778191593911e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 187170, "start": 1880.22, "end": 1886.88, "text": " It reveals a beautiful, if slightly melancholic, physical reality about growth.", "tokens": [50791, 467, 20893, 257, 2238, 11, 498, 4748, 4795, 4778, 7940, 11, 4001, 4103, 466, 4599, 13, 51124], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10410001430105656, "compression_ratio": 1.6064981949458483, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427778191593911e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 187170, "start": 1887.2, "end": 1891.7, "text": " It means that true structural learning requires a permanent sacrifice.", "tokens": [51140, 467, 1355, 300, 2074, 15067, 2539, 7029, 257, 10996, 11521, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10410001430105656, "compression_ratio": 1.6064981949458483, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427778191593911e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 187170, "start": 1891.94, "end": 1892.7, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [51377, 467, 775, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10410001430105656, "compression_ratio": 1.6064981949458483, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427778191593911e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 187170, "start": 1892.7, "end": 1901.3600000000001, "text": " To become structurally smarter, to integrate knowledge in a way that actually upgrades your biological agency, your brain must efficiently compress its history.", "tokens": [51415, 1407, 1813, 6594, 6512, 20294, 11, 281, 13365, 3601, 294, 257, 636, 300, 767, 24868, 428, 13910, 7934, 11, 428, 3567, 1633, 19621, 14778, 1080, 2503, 13, 51848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10410001430105656, "compression_ratio": 1.6064981949458483, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427778191593911e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 190170, "start": 1901.7, "end": 1910.16, "text": " And the mathematics dictate that in doing so, your brain intentionally destroys the exact granular details of who you were before you learned it.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 18666, 36071, 300, 294, 884, 370, 11, 428, 3567, 22062, 36714, 264, 1900, 39962, 4365, 295, 567, 291, 645, 949, 291, 3264, 309, 13, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1113742342535055, "compression_ratio": 1.7147766323024054, "no_speech_prob": 2.0364725530908068e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 190170, "start": 1910.42, "end": 1910.9, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50801, 7587, 13, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1113742342535055, "compression_ratio": 1.7147766323024054, "no_speech_prob": 2.0364725530908068e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 190170, "start": 1911.0800000000002, "end": 1917.9, "text": " You literally cannot go back to the person you were before the learning happened because the bridge has been burned by your own brain's compression algorithm.", "tokens": [50834, 509, 3736, 2644, 352, 646, 281, 264, 954, 291, 645, 949, 264, 2539, 2011, 570, 264, 7283, 575, 668, 13490, 538, 428, 1065, 3567, 311, 19355, 9284, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1113742342535055, "compression_ratio": 1.7147766323024054, "no_speech_prob": 2.0364725530908068e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 190170, "start": 1917.9, "end": 1926.0800000000002, "text": " Right. Wiping the current state doesn't reverse the upgrade because the raw data required to reverse it was destroyed as fuel to create the upgrade in the first place.", "tokens": [51175, 1779, 13, 343, 46440, 264, 2190, 1785, 1177, 380, 9943, 264, 11484, 570, 264, 8936, 1412, 4739, 281, 9943, 309, 390, 8937, 382, 6616, 281, 1884, 264, 11484, 294, 264, 700, 1081, 13, 51584], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1113742342535055, "compression_ratio": 1.7147766323024054, "no_speech_prob": 2.0364725530908068e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 190170, "start": 1926.18, "end": 1927.6200000000001, "text": " That is just wow.", "tokens": [51589, 663, 307, 445, 6076, 13, 51661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1113742342535055, "compression_ratio": 1.7147766323024054, "no_speech_prob": 2.0364725530908068e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 192762, "start": 1927.62, "end": 1931.9399999999998, "text": " Learning is fundamentally an act of destruction of the past self.", "tokens": [50365, 15205, 307, 17879, 364, 605, 295, 13563, 295, 264, 1791, 2698, 13, 50581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18359510898590087, "compression_ratio": 1.470873786407767, "no_speech_prob": 1.519184626187775e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 192762, "start": 1932.4399999999998, "end": 1934.36, "text": " The irreversibility isn't a bug.", "tokens": [50606, 440, 16014, 840, 2841, 1943, 380, 257, 7426, 13, 50702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18359510898590087, "compression_ratio": 1.470873786407767, "no_speech_prob": 1.519184626187775e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 192762, "start": 1934.7199999999998, "end": 1936.6799999999998, "text": " It is the defining feature of the compression.", "tokens": [50720, 467, 307, 264, 17827, 4111, 295, 264, 19355, 13, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18359510898590087, "compression_ratio": 1.470873786407767, "no_speech_prob": 1.519184626187775e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 192762, "start": 1937.1399999999999, "end": 1938.62, "text": " That is incredibly heavy.", "tokens": [50841, 663, 307, 6252, 4676, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18359510898590087, "compression_ratio": 1.470873786407767, "no_speech_prob": 1.519184626187775e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 192762, "start": 1939.12, "end": 1945.62, "text": " And it perfectly sets up the final act of Flixian's essay, which zooms out further than anything we've discussed so far.", "tokens": [50940, 400, 309, 6239, 6352, 493, 264, 2572, 605, 295, 3235, 970, 952, 311, 16238, 11, 597, 5721, 4785, 484, 3052, 813, 1340, 321, 600, 7152, 370, 1400, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18359510898590087, "compression_ratio": 1.470873786407767, "no_speech_prob": 1.519184626187775e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 192762, "start": 1945.6399999999999, "end": 1945.9399999999998, "text": " All right.", "tokens": [51266, 1057, 558, 13, 51281], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18359510898590087, "compression_ratio": 1.470873786407767, "no_speech_prob": 1.519184626187775e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 194594, "start": 1945.94, "end": 1954.9, "text": " Because up to this point, we've only been talking about a single system, one brain, one single organism, or one AI updating itself in isolation.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 493, 281, 341, 935, 11, 321, 600, 787, 668, 1417, 466, 257, 2167, 1185, 11, 472, 3567, 11, 472, 2167, 24128, 11, 420, 472, 7318, 25113, 2564, 294, 16001, 13, 50813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11681039709793894, "compression_ratio": 1.5829383886255923, "no_speech_prob": 1.942329760570849e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 194594, "start": 1955.14, "end": 1955.3400000000001, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50825, 865, 13, 50835], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11681039709793894, "compression_ratio": 1.5829383886255923, "no_speech_prob": 1.942329760570849e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 194594, "start": 1955.76, "end": 1961.54, "text": " But what happens to this retention of history, this structural upgrade, when the continuing system is mortal?", "tokens": [50856, 583, 437, 2314, 281, 341, 22871, 295, 2503, 11, 341, 15067, 11484, 11, 562, 264, 9289, 1185, 307, 27624, 30, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11681039709793894, "compression_ratio": 1.5829383886255923, "no_speech_prob": 1.942329760570849e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 194594, "start": 1962.1000000000001, "end": 1966.06, "text": " What happens when an entire generation of original interpreters dies out?", "tokens": [51173, 708, 2314, 562, 364, 2302, 5125, 295, 3380, 17489, 1559, 2714, 484, 30, 51371], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11681039709793894, "compression_ratio": 1.5829383886255923, "no_speech_prob": 1.942329760570849e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 196606, "start": 1966.06, "end": 1970.62, "text": " This brings us to the coda of Flixian's essay, Population-Level Operator Succession.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 269, 13449, 295, 3235, 970, 952, 311, 16238, 11, 10215, 2776, 12, 11020, 779, 12480, 1639, 23669, 313, 13, 50593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1272723099281048, "compression_ratio": 1.6462882096069869, "no_speech_prob": 1.875909367080042e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 196606, "start": 1970.72, "end": 1978.54, "text": " We are stepping out of the adaptation hierarchy of a single mind and stepping into what Flixian beautifully terms the geometry of witnesses.", "tokens": [50598, 492, 366, 16821, 484, 295, 264, 21549, 22333, 295, 257, 2167, 1575, 293, 16821, 666, 437, 3235, 970, 952, 16525, 2115, 264, 18426, 295, 20217, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1272723099281048, "compression_ratio": 1.6462882096069869, "no_speech_prob": 1.875909367080042e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 196606, "start": 1978.96, "end": 1980.08, "text": " The geometry of witnesses.", "tokens": [51010, 440, 18426, 295, 20217, 13, 51066], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1272723099281048, "compression_ratio": 1.6462882096069869, "no_speech_prob": 1.875909367080042e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 196606, "start": 1980.76, "end": 1986.74, "text": " So what happens across a population when the direct carriers of a compressed history are finite and they start to disappear?", "tokens": [51100, 407, 437, 2314, 2108, 257, 4415, 562, 264, 2047, 28541, 295, 257, 30353, 2503, 366, 19362, 293, 436, 722, 281, 11596, 30, 51399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1272723099281048, "compression_ratio": 1.6462882096069869, "no_speech_prob": 1.875909367080042e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 198674, "start": 1986.74, "end": 1993.74, "text": " To illustrate this societal mechanism, Flixian highlights a striking observation from a cultural commentator known as the functional melancholic.", "tokens": [50365, 1407, 23221, 341, 33472, 7513, 11, 3235, 970, 952, 14254, 257, 18559, 14816, 490, 257, 6988, 2871, 1639, 2570, 382, 264, 11745, 4795, 4778, 7940, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10227620232965529, "compression_ratio": 1.6015625, "no_speech_prob": 2.3160429737240085e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 198674, "start": 1994.66, "end": 1996.6200000000001, "text": " The example used is Generation X.", "tokens": [50761, 440, 1365, 1143, 307, 23898, 1783, 13, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10227620232965529, "compression_ratio": 1.6015625, "no_speech_prob": 2.3160429737240085e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 198674, "start": 1996.68, "end": 1999.56, "text": " The generation born roughly between 1965 and 1980.", "tokens": [50862, 440, 5125, 4232, 9810, 1296, 33809, 293, 13626, 13, 51006], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10227620232965529, "compression_ratio": 1.6015625, "no_speech_prob": 2.3160429737240085e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 198674, "start": 1999.9, "end": 2001.36, "text": " Why are they the focal point for this?", "tokens": [51023, 1545, 366, 436, 264, 26592, 935, 337, 341, 30, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10227620232965529, "compression_ratio": 1.6015625, "no_speech_prob": 2.3160429737240085e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 198674, "start": 2001.6, "end": 2010.54, "text": " Because, as the functional melancholic points out, Gen X occupies a completely unique, unrepeatable position in human history.", "tokens": [51108, 1436, 11, 382, 264, 11745, 4795, 4778, 7940, 2793, 484, 11, 3632, 1783, 8073, 530, 257, 2584, 3845, 11, 20584, 494, 31415, 2535, 294, 1952, 2503, 13, 51555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10227620232965529, "compression_ratio": 1.6015625, "no_speech_prob": 2.3160429737240085e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 198674, "start": 2010.78, "end": 2011.24, "text": " Unrepeatable.", "tokens": [51567, 1156, 265, 494, 31415, 13, 51590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10227620232965529, "compression_ratio": 1.6015625, "no_speech_prob": 2.3160429737240085e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 201124, "start": 2011.24, "end": 2019.1, "text": " Yeah, they are the last generation to have direct, embodied, adult memory of a pre-digital information environment.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 11, 436, 366, 264, 1036, 5125, 281, 362, 2047, 11, 42046, 11, 5075, 4675, 295, 257, 659, 12, 25259, 1686, 1589, 2823, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13039881335802314, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813677608337965e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 201124, "start": 2019.5, "end": 2025.78, "text": " They lived fully formed lives before the internet, and they navigate the exact same world now, post-internet.", "tokens": [50778, 814, 5152, 4498, 8693, 2909, 949, 264, 4705, 11, 293, 436, 12350, 264, 1900, 912, 1002, 586, 11, 2183, 12, 259, 2231, 302, 13, 51092], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13039881335802314, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813677608337965e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 201124, "start": 2025.88, "end": 2028.18, "text": " They ran the old operating system and they run the new one.", "tokens": [51097, 814, 5872, 264, 1331, 7447, 1185, 293, 436, 1190, 264, 777, 472, 13, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13039881335802314, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813677608337965e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 201124, "start": 2028.24, "end": 2029.86, "text": " They literally embody the transition.", "tokens": [51215, 814, 3736, 42575, 264, 6034, 13, 51296], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13039881335802314, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813677608337965e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 201124, "start": 2029.94, "end": 2030.24, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51300, 7587, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13039881335802314, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813677608337965e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 201124, "start": 2030.44, "end": 2036.14, "text": " And Flixian makes a very sharp distinction here between two fundamentally different ways a population relates to its past.", "tokens": [51325, 400, 3235, 970, 952, 1669, 257, 588, 8199, 16844, 510, 1296, 732, 17879, 819, 2098, 257, 4415, 16155, 281, 1080, 1791, 13, 51610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13039881335802314, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813677608337965e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 201124, "start": 2036.68, "end": 2038.1200000000001, "text": " Nostalgia versus testimony.", "tokens": [51637, 426, 555, 30928, 5717, 15634, 13, 51709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13039881335802314, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813677608337965e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 201124, "start": 2038.54, "end": 2039.7, "text": " It's a crucial separation.", "tokens": [51730, 467, 311, 257, 11462, 14634, 13, 51788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13039881335802314, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813677608337965e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 203970, "start": 2039.7, "end": 2043.92, "text": " Nostalgia is a soft focus longing for a remembered past.", "tokens": [50365, 426, 555, 30928, 307, 257, 2787, 1879, 35050, 337, 257, 13745, 1791, 13, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1705873959685025, "compression_ratio": 1.4976303317535544, "no_speech_prob": 1.868323204479161e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 203970, "start": 2044.56, "end": 2046.7, "text": " It's an emotion, often hazy and idealized.", "tokens": [50608, 467, 311, 364, 8913, 11, 2049, 324, 1229, 293, 7157, 1602, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1705873959685025, "compression_ratio": 1.4976303317535544, "no_speech_prob": 1.868323204479161e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 203970, "start": 2047.44, "end": 2047.56, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50752, 1779, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1705873959685025, "compression_ratio": 1.4976303317535544, "no_speech_prob": 1.868323204479161e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 203970, "start": 2047.8, "end": 2050.14, "text": " But testimony is precise comparative access.", "tokens": [50770, 583, 15634, 307, 13600, 39292, 2105, 13, 50887], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1705873959685025, "compression_ratio": 1.4976303317535544, "no_speech_prob": 1.868323204479161e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 203970, "start": 2050.7, "end": 2059.58, "text": " It is the structural knowledge of knowing, on a mechanical level, how a prior configuration actually operated because you personally existed within its constraints.", "tokens": [50915, 467, 307, 264, 15067, 3601, 295, 5276, 11, 322, 257, 12070, 1496, 11, 577, 257, 4059, 11694, 767, 20826, 570, 291, 5665, 13135, 1951, 1080, 18491, 13, 51359], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1705873959685025, "compression_ratio": 1.4976303317535544, "no_speech_prob": 1.868323204479161e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 205958, "start": 2059.58, "end": 2075.44, "text": " Yes. If I sit down and talk to an older Gen X relative, they can give me testimony about the physical constraints of navigating a massive city with a paper map, or how people resolved a factual argument at a dinner party without immediately pulling out a smartphone to search the answer.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 759, 286, 1394, 760, 293, 751, 281, 364, 4906, 3632, 1783, 4972, 11, 436, 393, 976, 385, 15634, 466, 264, 4001, 18491, 295, 32054, 257, 5994, 2307, 365, 257, 3035, 4471, 11, 420, 577, 561, 20772, 257, 48029, 6770, 412, 257, 6148, 3595, 1553, 4258, 8407, 484, 257, 13307, 281, 3164, 264, 1867, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05518860022226969, "compression_ratio": 1.471794871794872, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106117091060912e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 207544, "start": 2075.44, "end": 2077.44, "text": " They remember the friction.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 1604, 264, 17710, 13, 50465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.3908705446455214, "compression_ratio": 1.316326530612245, "no_speech_prob": 2.1088252671885854e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 207544, "start": 2077.44, "end": 2078.02, "text": " They remember the friction of the pre-digital era.", "tokens": [50465, 814, 1604, 264, 17710, 295, 264, 659, 12, 25259, 1686, 4249, 13, 50494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.3908705446455214, "compression_ratio": 1.316326530612245, "no_speech_prob": 2.1088252671885854e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 207544, "start": 2078.44, "end": 2081.78, "text": " Future generations, millennials, Gen Z, Gen Alpha.", "tokens": [50515, 20805, 10593, 11, 45543, 11, 3632, 1176, 11, 3632, 20588, 13, 50682], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.3908705446455214, "compression_ratio": 1.316326530612245, "no_speech_prob": 2.1088252671885854e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 208178, "start": 2081.78, "end": 2087.6000000000004, "text": " We only inherit what Flixian mathematically designates as H prime sub T.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 787, 21389, 437, 3235, 970, 952, 44003, 1715, 1024, 382, 389, 5835, 1422, 314, 13, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14928237178869413, "compression_ratio": 1.3872832369942196, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622759805255295e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 208178, "start": 2088.0600000000004, "end": 2092.5600000000004, "text": " H prime sub T represents a compressed, already interpreted account of the past.", "tokens": [50679, 389, 5835, 1422, 314, 8855, 257, 30353, 11, 1217, 26749, 2696, 295, 264, 1791, 13, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14928237178869413, "compression_ratio": 1.3872832369942196, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622759805255295e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 208178, "start": 2092.7000000000003, "end": 2096.7200000000003, "text": " You inherit documentaries, historical books, Wikipedia articles about the 1980s.", "tokens": [50911, 509, 21389, 41630, 11, 8584, 3642, 11, 28999, 11290, 466, 264, 13626, 82, 13, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14928237178869413, "compression_ratio": 1.3872832369942196, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622759805255295e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 208178, "start": 2096.78, "end": 2096.9, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51115, 1779, 13, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14928237178869413, "compression_ratio": 1.3872832369942196, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622759805255295e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 209690, "start": 2096.9, "end": 2104.7200000000003, "text": " But you do not inherit H sub T, the actual lived history, the raw, uncompressed trace of existing in that environment.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 291, 360, 406, 21389, 389, 1422, 314, 11, 264, 3539, 5152, 2503, 11, 264, 8936, 11, 8585, 79, 3805, 13508, 295, 6741, 294, 300, 2823, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12316294549738319, "compression_ratio": 1.6022727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 2.380632800266791e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 209690, "start": 2104.94, "end": 2107.5, "text": " Because the uncompressed trace doesn't survive its carriers.", "tokens": [50767, 1436, 264, 8585, 79, 3805, 13508, 1177, 380, 7867, 1080, 28541, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12316294549738319, "compression_ratio": 1.6022727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 2.380632800266791e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 209690, "start": 2107.96, "end": 2111.14, "text": " Once the people who lived it die, the lived trace is gone forever.", "tokens": [50918, 3443, 264, 561, 567, 5152, 309, 978, 11, 264, 5152, 13508, 307, 2780, 5680, 13, 51077], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12316294549738319, "compression_ratio": 1.6022727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 2.380632800266791e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 209690, "start": 2111.4, "end": 2115.44, "text": " And Flixian formalizes this tragedy using the mathematics of extinction.", "tokens": [51090, 400, 3235, 970, 952, 9860, 5660, 341, 18563, 1228, 264, 18666, 295, 33163, 13, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12316294549738319, "compression_ratio": 1.6022727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 2.380632800266791e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 209690, "start": 2116.08, "end": 2121.52, "text": " The essay introduces a variable called reconstruction redundancy, denoted by the Greek letter rho.", "tokens": [51324, 440, 16238, 31472, 257, 7006, 1219, 31565, 27830, 6717, 11, 1441, 23325, 538, 264, 10281, 5063, 20293, 13, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12316294549738319, "compression_ratio": 1.6022727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 2.380632800266791e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 209690, "start": 2121.64, "end": 2122.08, "text": " Rho.", "tokens": [51602, 497, 1289, 13, 51624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12316294549738319, "compression_ratio": 1.6022727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 2.380632800266791e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 212208, "start": 2122.08, "end": 2131.7999999999997, "text": " This variable measures how many independent witnesses are left in a population who can accurately reconstruct a specific capacity or memory from direct experience.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 7006, 8000, 577, 867, 6695, 20217, 366, 1411, 294, 257, 4415, 567, 393, 20095, 31499, 257, 2685, 6042, 420, 4675, 490, 2047, 1752, 13, 50851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1128780746459961, "compression_ratio": 1.7026022304832713, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860292679886756e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 212208, "start": 2132.22, "end": 2139.48, "text": " And as the Gen X population ages, and eventually passes away over the coming decades, the number of independent witnesses shrinks.", "tokens": [50872, 400, 382, 264, 3632, 1783, 4415, 12357, 11, 293, 4728, 11335, 1314, 670, 264, 1348, 7878, 11, 264, 1230, 295, 6695, 20217, 9884, 16431, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1128780746459961, "compression_ratio": 1.7026022304832713, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860292679886756e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 212208, "start": 2140.36, "end": 2142.18, "text": " The reconstruction redundancy drops.", "tokens": [51279, 440, 31565, 27830, 6717, 11438, 13, 51370], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1128780746459961, "compression_ratio": 1.7026022304832713, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860292679886756e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 212208, "start": 2142.88, "end": 2143.7999999999997, "text": " Rho approaches one.", "tokens": [51405, 497, 1289, 11587, 472, 13, 51451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1128780746459961, "compression_ratio": 1.7026022304832713, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860292679886756e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 212208, "start": 2144.12, "end": 2148.8199999999997, "text": " In graph theory, when Rho hits one, you reach what is called an articulation point.", "tokens": [51467, 682, 4295, 5261, 11, 562, 497, 1289, 8664, 472, 11, 291, 2524, 437, 307, 1219, 364, 15228, 2776, 935, 13, 51702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1128780746459961, "compression_ratio": 1.7026022304832713, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860292679886756e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 212208, "start": 2148.94, "end": 2149.84, "text": " An articulation point.", "tokens": [51708, 1107, 15228, 2776, 935, 13, 51753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1128780746459961, "compression_ratio": 1.7026022304832713, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860292679886756e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 214984, "start": 2149.84, "end": 2154.06, "text": " An articulation point is a critical, load-bearing node in a network.", "tokens": [50365, 1107, 15228, 2776, 935, 307, 257, 4924, 11, 3677, 12, 650, 1921, 9984, 294, 257, 3209, 13, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11468868648882993, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 2.0766337868044493e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 214984, "start": 2154.5, "end": 2157.84, "text": " When that last remaining node is removed, the entire graph fractures.", "tokens": [50598, 1133, 300, 1036, 8877, 9984, 307, 7261, 11, 264, 2302, 4295, 17948, 1303, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11468868648882993, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 2.0766337868044493e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 214984, "start": 2158.56, "end": 2161.4, "text": " So the pathway connecting the past to the present is severed.", "tokens": [50801, 407, 264, 18590, 11015, 264, 1791, 281, 264, 1974, 307, 2802, 292, 13, 50943], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11468868648882993, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 2.0766337868044493e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 214984, "start": 2161.44, "end": 2161.86, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50945, 7587, 13, 50966], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11468868648882993, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 2.0766337868044493e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 214984, "start": 2162.2400000000002, "end": 2169.08, "text": " What was ordinary, gradual forgetting, suddenly undergoes a phase transition into absolute mathematical irreversibility.", "tokens": [50985, 708, 390, 10547, 11, 32890, 25428, 11, 5800, 26426, 279, 257, 5574, 6034, 666, 8236, 18894, 16014, 840, 2841, 13, 51327], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11468868648882993, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 2.0766337868044493e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 214984, "start": 2169.58, "end": 2174.1400000000003, "text": " The knowledge of how to operate under the old regime is permanently deleted from the population.", "tokens": [51352, 440, 3601, 295, 577, 281, 9651, 833, 264, 1331, 13120, 307, 24042, 22981, 490, 264, 4415, 13, 51580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11468868648882993, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 2.0766337868044493e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 217414, "start": 2174.14, "end": 2187.24, "text": " The crucial takeaway from this geometry of witnesses is that a Continuer, a person who has personally operated under two distinct regimes, has a comparative vantage point that no amount of documentary reconstruction can ever give a future generation.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 11462, 30681, 490, 341, 18426, 295, 20217, 307, 300, 257, 14674, 5486, 11, 257, 954, 567, 575, 5665, 20826, 833, 732, 10644, 45738, 11, 575, 257, 39292, 46206, 935, 300, 572, 2372, 295, 15674, 31565, 393, 1562, 976, 257, 2027, 5125, 13, 51020], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11445529739578049, "compression_ratio": 1.578512396694215, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211932833854915e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 217414, "start": 2187.3599999999997, "end": 2190.8599999999997, "text": " You cannot truly evaluate a regime without an outside vantage point.", "tokens": [51026, 509, 2644, 4908, 13059, 257, 13120, 1553, 364, 2380, 46206, 935, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11445529739578049, "compression_ratio": 1.578512396694215, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211932833854915e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 217414, "start": 2191.12, "end": 2194.2799999999997, "text": " It's the old proverb about the fact not knowing what water is.", "tokens": [51214, 467, 311, 264, 1331, 49923, 466, 264, 1186, 406, 5276, 437, 1281, 307, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11445529739578049, "compression_ratio": 1.578512396694215, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211932833854915e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 219428, "start": 2194.28, "end": 2201.6200000000003, "text": " You cannot judge the water you are swimming in unless you retain the structural memory of what it was like to breathe air.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 2644, 6995, 264, 1281, 291, 366, 11989, 294, 5969, 291, 18340, 264, 15067, 4675, 295, 437, 309, 390, 411, 281, 10192, 1988, 13, 50732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13408438648496354, "compression_ratio": 1.2448979591836735, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017366228810342e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 220162, "start": 2201.62, "end": 2216.62, "text": " A generation that has only ever lived in a hyper-connected, digital environment literally lacks the cognitive equipment, the uncompressed traces, to fully evaluate what the digital regime has cost us, or how it differs from what came before.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 5125, 300, 575, 787, 1562, 5152, 294, 257, 9848, 12, 9826, 292, 11, 4562, 2823, 3736, 31132, 264, 15605, 5927, 11, 264, 8585, 79, 3805, 26076, 11, 281, 4498, 13059, 437, 264, 4562, 13120, 575, 2063, 505, 11, 420, 577, 309, 37761, 490, 437, 1361, 949, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12698891288355776, "compression_ratio": 1.5660377358490567, "no_speech_prob": 2.399291269133963e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 220162, "start": 2217.08, "end": 2219.5, "text": " Because they only have the semantics acts of the past.", "tokens": [51138, 1436, 436, 787, 362, 264, 4361, 45298, 10672, 295, 264, 1791, 13, 51259], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12698891288355776, "compression_ratio": 1.5660377358490567, "no_speech_prob": 2.399291269133963e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 220162, "start": 2220.04, "end": 2221.62, "text": " They know the dates and the events.", "tokens": [51286, 814, 458, 264, 11691, 293, 264, 3931, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12698891288355776, "compression_ratio": 1.5660377358490567, "no_speech_prob": 2.399291269133963e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 222162, "start": 2221.62, "end": 2225.56, "text": " But they lack the episodic indexicality of living it.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 436, 5011, 264, 39200, 299, 8186, 804, 507, 295, 2647, 309, 13, 50562], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18092415683953336, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363731116658675e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 222162, "start": 2225.7999999999997, "end": 2226.14, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50574, 48746, 736, 13, 50591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18092415683953336, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363731116658675e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 222162, "start": 2226.2999999999997, "end": 2228.9, "text": " They have the storage, but they lack the biological memory.", "tokens": [50599, 814, 362, 264, 6725, 11, 457, 436, 5011, 264, 13910, 4675, 13, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18092415683953336, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363731116658675e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 222162, "start": 2229.42, "end": 2231.24, "text": " The societal ratchet has turned.", "tokens": [50755, 440, 33472, 45885, 575, 3574, 13, 50846], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18092415683953336, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363731116658675e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 222162, "start": 2231.56, "end": 2231.8599999999997, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50862, 3153, 13, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18092415683953336, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363731116658675e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 222162, "start": 2232.54, "end": 2234.64, "text": " This has been an absolutely mind-bending journey.", "tokens": [50911, 639, 575, 668, 364, 3122, 1575, 12, 65, 2029, 4671, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18092415683953336, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363731116658675e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 222162, "start": 2234.7799999999997, "end": 2238.38, "text": " We've covered an immense amount of ground today, so let's synthesize where we've been.", "tokens": [51023, 492, 600, 5343, 364, 22920, 2372, 295, 2727, 965, 11, 370, 718, 311, 26617, 1125, 689, 321, 600, 668, 13, 51203], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18092415683953336, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363731116658675e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 222162, "start": 2238.54, "end": 2239.02, "text": " Sounds good.", "tokens": [51211, 14576, 665, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18092415683953336, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363731116658675e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 222162, "start": 2239.02, "end": 2242.88, "text": " We started by completely dismantling the idea that memory is a hard drive.", "tokens": [51235, 492, 1409, 538, 2584, 30506, 1688, 264, 1558, 300, 4675, 307, 257, 1152, 3332, 13, 51428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18092415683953336, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363731116658675e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 222162, "start": 2243.4, "end": 2245.2, "text": " It's not a system for perfect storage.", "tokens": [51454, 467, 311, 406, 257, 1185, 337, 2176, 6725, 13, 51544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18092415683953336, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363731116658675e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 222162, "start": 2245.48, "end": 2248.42, "text": " It's an active interpretive constraint on your future.", "tokens": [51558, 467, 311, 364, 4967, 7302, 488, 25534, 322, 428, 2027, 13, 51705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18092415683953336, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363731116658675e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 224842, "start": 2248.42, "end": 2258.28, "text": " We saw how biological systems prioritize creativity of interpretation over the fidelity of the trace, and how that very unreliability gives rise to genuine agency.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 1866, 577, 13910, 3652, 25164, 12915, 295, 14174, 670, 264, 46404, 295, 264, 13508, 11, 293, 577, 300, 588, 20584, 2081, 2310, 2709, 6272, 281, 16699, 7934, 13, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07602470215052774, "compression_ratio": 1.6331877729257642, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417287230536704e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 224842, "start": 2258.7200000000003, "end": 2270.4, "text": " And then we looked at the causal emergence ratchet, how the act of learning creates a permanent irreversible structural upgrade in the biological system, even if the specific semantic facts are later forgotten.", "tokens": [50880, 400, 550, 321, 2956, 412, 264, 38755, 36211, 45885, 11, 577, 264, 605, 295, 2539, 7829, 257, 10996, 16014, 840, 964, 15067, 11484, 294, 264, 13910, 1185, 11, 754, 498, 264, 2685, 47982, 9130, 366, 1780, 11832, 13, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07602470215052774, "compression_ratio": 1.6331877729257642, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417287230536704e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 227040, "start": 2270.4, "end": 2281.58, "text": " We explored the mathematics of how that irreversibility works, proving that structural learning requires degeneracy-reducing compression that permanently burns the bridge to your past self.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 24016, 264, 18666, 295, 577, 300, 16014, 840, 2841, 1985, 11, 27221, 300, 15067, 2539, 7029, 40520, 2551, 12, 265, 769, 2175, 19355, 300, 24042, 22684, 264, 7283, 281, 428, 1791, 2698, 13, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06351855683000121, "compression_ratio": 1.5780590717299579, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281773885199914e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 227040, "start": 2281.9, "end": 2292.4, "text": " And finally, we looked at the tragic geometry of witnesses, how a society permanently loses its comparative outside vantage point on its own history when the original interpreters die.", "tokens": [50940, 400, 2721, 11, 321, 2956, 412, 264, 20385, 18426, 295, 20217, 11, 577, 257, 4086, 24042, 18293, 1080, 39292, 2380, 46206, 935, 322, 1080, 1065, 2503, 562, 264, 3380, 17489, 1559, 978, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06351855683000121, "compression_ratio": 1.5780590717299579, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281773885199914e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 229240, "start": 2292.4, "end": 2302.92, "text": " It is a stunning unified theory from affliction, mapping how the past acts on the present, scaling all the way from a single strand of DNA up to generational sociology.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 18550, 26787, 5261, 490, 2096, 75, 4105, 11, 18350, 577, 264, 1791, 10672, 322, 264, 1974, 11, 21589, 439, 264, 636, 490, 257, 2167, 14955, 295, 8272, 493, 281, 48320, 41744, 13, 50891], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09984468927188796, "compression_ratio": 1.5903614457831325, "no_speech_prob": 1.675172045349782e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 229240, "start": 2303.28, "end": 2305.64, "text": " I want to leave you with a final thought to ponder today.", "tokens": [50909, 286, 528, 281, 1856, 291, 365, 257, 2572, 1194, 281, 280, 8548, 965, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09984468927188796, "compression_ratio": 1.5903614457831325, "no_speech_prob": 1.675172045349782e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 229240, "start": 2305.78, "end": 2312.12, "text": " It's something that wasn't directly stated in affliction's text, but it has been looming over this entire deep dive.", "tokens": [51034, 467, 311, 746, 300, 2067, 380, 3838, 11323, 294, 2096, 75, 4105, 311, 2487, 11, 457, 309, 575, 668, 450, 10539, 670, 341, 2302, 2452, 9192, 13, 51351], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09984468927188796, "compression_ratio": 1.5903614457831325, "no_speech_prob": 1.675172045349782e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 229240, "start": 2312.36, "end": 2314.1, "text": " I think I know exactly where you're going with this.", "tokens": [51363, 286, 519, 286, 458, 2293, 689, 291, 434, 516, 365, 341, 13, 51450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09984468927188796, "compression_ratio": 1.5903614457831325, "no_speech_prob": 1.675172045349782e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 231410, "start": 2314.1, "end": 2341.54, "text": " If biological memory, genuine agency, and true structural learning actually thrive on creative misinterpretation, on the noise of wet biology, on the permanent destructive compression of contextual constraints, and right now, humanity is pouring trillions of dollars into building superintelligent AI systems that are defined by perfect memory fidelity, perfect data retrieval, and massive decontextualized semantic embedding spaces.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 13910, 4675, 11, 16699, 7934, 11, 293, 2074, 15067, 2539, 767, 21233, 322, 5880, 3346, 41935, 399, 11, 322, 264, 5658, 295, 6630, 14956, 11, 322, 264, 10996, 26960, 19355, 295, 35526, 18491, 11, 293, 558, 586, 11, 10243, 307, 20450, 504, 46279, 295, 3808, 666, 2390, 1687, 20761, 25002, 7318, 3652, 300, 366, 7642, 538, 2176, 4675, 46404, 11, 2176, 1412, 19817, 3337, 11, 293, 5994, 979, 896, 3828, 901, 1602, 47982, 12240, 3584, 7673, 13, 51737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04259010059077565, "compression_ratio": 1.6848249027237354, "no_speech_prob": 2.2539314165070934e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 234154, "start": 2341.54, "end": 2345.2599999999998, "text": " Are we accidentally programming out the very prerequisite for genuine adaptability?", "tokens": [50365, 2014, 321, 15715, 9410, 484, 264, 588, 38333, 34152, 337, 16699, 6231, 2310, 30, 50551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10162651949915393, "compression_ratio": 1.635258358662614, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922335065005067e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 234154, "start": 2345.2599999999998, "end": 2350.3, "text": " Exactly. Are we building minds that can perfectly remember everything, but structurally learn nothing?", "tokens": [50551, 7587, 13, 2014, 321, 2390, 9634, 300, 393, 6239, 1604, 1203, 11, 457, 6594, 6512, 1466, 1825, 30, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10162651949915393, "compression_ratio": 1.635258358662614, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922335065005067e-12}, {"id": 682, "seek": 234154, "start": 2351.0, "end": 2360.96, "text": " We want artificial intelligence to be like us, to reason and adapt like us, but we're explicitly designing it to be the exact opposite of the messy biological reality that makes us human.", "tokens": [50838, 492, 528, 11677, 7599, 281, 312, 411, 505, 11, 281, 1778, 293, 6231, 411, 505, 11, 457, 321, 434, 20803, 14685, 309, 281, 312, 264, 1900, 6182, 295, 264, 16191, 13910, 4103, 300, 1669, 505, 1952, 13, 51336], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10162651949915393, "compression_ratio": 1.635258358662614, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922335065005067e-12}, {"id": 683, "seek": 234154, "start": 2361.38, "end": 2361.6, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51357, 1779, 13, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10162651949915393, "compression_ratio": 1.635258358662614, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922335065005067e-12}, {"id": 684, "seek": 234154, "start": 2361.8, "end": 2370.4, "text": " The pristine, error-free x-ray machine of engineering precision might just be blinding us to the murky, noisy waters where true intelligence actually swims.", "tokens": [51378, 440, 582, 42745, 11, 6713, 12, 10792, 2031, 12, 3458, 3479, 295, 7043, 18356, 1062, 445, 312, 6865, 278, 505, 281, 264, 5257, 4133, 11, 24518, 12975, 689, 2074, 7599, 767, 42357, 13, 51808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10162651949915393, "compression_ratio": 1.635258358662614, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922335065005067e-12}, {"id": 685, "seek": 237040, "start": 2370.4, "end": 2374.44, "text": " It is a profound and frankly slightly terrifying corner leave-on.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 14382, 293, 11939, 4748, 18106, 4538, 1856, 12, 266, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15600258653814142, "compression_ratio": 1.5806451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 2.9622324558553625e-12}, {"id": 686, "seek": 237040, "start": 2375.02, "end": 2379.26, "text": " If perfect memory is the enemy of structural learning, we might be engineering ourselves into a corner.", "tokens": [50596, 759, 2176, 4675, 307, 264, 5945, 295, 15067, 2539, 11, 321, 1062, 312, 7043, 4175, 666, 257, 4538, 13, 50808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15600258653814142, "compression_ratio": 1.5806451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 2.9622324558553625e-12}, {"id": 687, "seek": 237040, "start": 2379.7000000000003, "end": 2382.08, "text": " Thank you so much for joining us on this deep dive.", "tokens": [50830, 1044, 291, 370, 709, 337, 5549, 505, 322, 341, 2452, 9192, 13, 50949], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15600258653814142, "compression_ratio": 1.5806451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 2.9622324558553625e-12}, {"id": 688, "seek": 237040, "start": 2382.44, "end": 2384.46, "text": " Keep questioning your own interpretive frameworks.", "tokens": [50967, 5527, 21257, 428, 1065, 7302, 488, 29834, 13, 51068], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15600258653814142, "compression_ratio": 1.5806451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 2.9622324558553625e-12}, {"id": 689, "seek": 237040, "start": 2385.2200000000003, "end": 2389.58, "text": " Keep wondering how your personal history is actively constraining your admissible futures.", "tokens": [51106, 5527, 6359, 577, 428, 2973, 2503, 307, 13022, 11525, 1760, 428, 5910, 41073, 26071, 13, 51324], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15600258653814142, "compression_ratio": 1.5806451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 2.9622324558553625e-12}, {"id": 690, "seek": 237040, "start": 2390.14, "end": 2391.1600000000003, "text": " And we'll see you next time.", "tokens": [51352, 400, 321, 603, 536, 291, 958, 565, 13, 51403], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15600258653814142, "compression_ratio": 1.5806451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 2.9622324558553625e-12}], "language": "en"}
