0, 38359, 746, 13, 51207], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1462384081901388, "compression_ratio": 1.7039473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051328460149004e-12}, {"id": 6, "seek": 0, "start": 17.14, "end": 20.92, "text": " Right, you think the past has just been cleanly wiped away to make room for the present.", "tokens": [51222, 1779, 11, 291, 519, 264, 1791, 575, 445, 668, 2541, 356, 26879, 1314, 281, 652, 1808, 337, 264, 1974, 13, 51411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1462384081901388, "compression_ratio": 1.7039473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051328460149004e-12}, {"id": 7, "seek": 0, "start": 21.1, "end": 21.54, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51420, 7587, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1462384081901388, "compression_ratio": 1.7039473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051328460149004e-12}, {"id": 8, "seek": 0, "start": 21.84, "end": 26.560000000000002, "text": " But in the physical universe, erasure is actually a thermodynamic illusion.", "tokens": [51457, 583, 294, 264, 4001, 6445, 11, 1189, 2508, 307, 767, 257, 8810, 34988, 18854, 13, 51693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1462384081901388, "compression_ratio": 1.7039473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051328460149004e-12}, {"id": 9, "seek": 0, "start": 26.84, "end": 27.060000000000002, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51707, 865, 13, 51718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1462384081901388, "compression_ratio": 1.7039473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051328460149004e-12}, {"id": 10, "seek": 2706, "start": 27.06, "end": 33.54, "text": " And pretending that this illusion is real, that we can just overwrite history without paying a cost,", "tokens": [50365, 400, 22106, 300, 341, 18854, 307, 957, 11, 300, 321, 393, 445, 670, 21561, 2503, 1553, 6229, 257, 2063, 11, 50689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12809672977613365, "compression_ratio": 1.6262626262626263, "no_speech_prob": 7.492239792981914e-13}, {"id": 11, "seek": 2706, "start": 34.0, "end": 38.18, "text": " that's exactly why our digital world, and honestly, arguably our own minds,", "tokens": [50712, 300, 311, 2293, 983, 527, 4562, 1002, 11, 293, 6095, 11, 26771, 527, 1065, 9634, 11, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12809672977613365, "compression_ratio": 1.6262626262626263, "no_speech_prob": 7.492239792981914e-13}, {"id": 12, "seek": 2706, "start": 38.3, "end": 41.64, "text": " are constantly on the verge of collapsing under their own accumulated weight.", "tokens": [50927, 366, 6460, 322, 264, 37164, 295, 45339, 833, 641, 1065, 31346, 3364, 13, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12809672977613365, "compression_ratio": 1.6262626262626263, "no_speech_prob": 7.492239792981914e-13}, {"id": 13, "seek": 2706, "start": 41.8, "end": 45.739999999999995, "text": " We build these sprawling, just monumental systems, right?", "tokens": [51102, 492, 1322, 613, 22734, 1688, 11, 445, 43105, 3652, 11, 558, 30, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12809672977613365, "compression_ratio": 1.6262626262626263, "no_speech_prob": 7.492239792981914e-13}, {"id": 14, "seek": 2706, "start": 45.9, "end": 50.08, "text": " Massive corporate databases, millions of lines of legacy code,", "tokens": [51307, 10482, 488, 10896, 22380, 11, 6803, 295, 3876, 295, 11711, 3089, 11, 51516], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12809672977613365, "compression_ratio": 1.6262626262626263, "no_speech_prob": 7.492239792981914e-13}, {"id": 15, "seek": 2706, "start": 50.099999999999994, "end": 53.42, "text": " or even just the disorganized filing cabinets of our own daily notes.", "tokens": [51517, 420, 754, 445, 264, 717, 12372, 1602, 26854, 37427, 295, 527, 1065, 5212, 5570, 13, 51683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12809672977613365, "compression_ratio": 1.6262626262626263, "no_speech_prob": 7.492239792981914e-13}, {"id": 16, "seek": 2706, "start": 53.46, "end": 55.14, "text": " Oh, yeah. My notes app is a disaster.", "tokens": [51685, 876, 11, 1338, 13, 1222, 5570, 724, 307, 257, 11293, 13, 51769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12809672977613365, "compression_ratio": 1.6262626262626263, "no_speech_prob": 7.492239792981914e-13}, {"id": 17, "seek": 5514, "start": 55.14, "end": 57.84, "text": " Right. And then we just stare at them, completely paralyzed,", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 400, 550, 321, 445, 22432, 412, 552, 11, 2584, 41919, 11, 50500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10197769511829723, "compression_ratio": 1.5884773662551441, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147382689111645e-12}, {"id": 18, "seek": 5514, "start": 58.44, "end": 63.18, "text": " wondering how the tool we built to solve our problems somehow became the problem itself.", "tokens": [50530, 6359, 577, 264, 2290, 321, 3094, 281, 5039, 527, 2740, 6063, 3062, 264, 1154, 2564, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10197769511829723, "compression_ratio": 1.5884773662551441, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147382689111645e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 5514, "start": 63.38, "end": 68.9, "text": " We end up spending way more cognitive energy just managing the sedimentary layers of our own history", "tokens": [50777, 492, 917, 493, 6434, 636, 544, 15605, 2281, 445, 11642, 264, 32362, 822, 7914, 295, 527, 1065, 2503, 51053], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10197769511829723, "compression_ratio": 1.5884773662551441, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147382689111645e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 5514, "start": 68.9, "end": 71.58, "text": " than we do actually navigating the present moment.", "tokens": [51053, 813, 321, 360, 767, 32054, 264, 1974, 1623, 13, 51187], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10197769511829723, "compression_ratio": 1.5884773662551441, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147382689111645e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 5514, "start": 71.88, "end": 75.5, "text": " So today we are going on a deep dive into the architecture of that paralysis.", "tokens": [51202, 407, 965, 321, 366, 516, 322, 257, 2452, 9192, 666, 264, 9482, 295, 300, 49507, 13, 51383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10197769511829723, "compression_ratio": 1.5884773662551441, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147382689111645e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 5514, "start": 75.76, "end": 75.92, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51396, 1779, 13, 51404], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10197769511829723, "compression_ratio": 1.5884773662551441, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147382689111645e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 7592, "start": 75.92, "end": 80.24000000000001, "text": " And we have a truly staggering set of sources to guide us today.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 321, 362, 257, 4908, 42974, 992, 295, 7139, 281, 5934, 505, 965, 13, 50581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12725143597043795, "compression_ratio": 1.537953795379538, "no_speech_prob": 1.597737784089781e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 7592, "start": 80.4, "end": 87.38, "text": " It's a trilogy of essays that were published in July of 2026 by a pseudonymous author named Fliction.", "tokens": [50589, 467, 311, 257, 34030, 295, 35123, 300, 645, 6572, 294, 7370, 295, 945, 10880, 538, 257, 25505, 532, 18092, 3793, 4926, 3235, 4105, 13, 50938], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12725143597043795, "compression_ratio": 1.537953795379538, "no_speech_prob": 1.597737784089781e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 7592, "start": 87.92, "end": 91.46000000000001, "text": " Yeah. The texts are titled Against the Kitchen Sink, What Collapse Should Forget,", "tokens": [50965, 865, 13, 440, 15765, 366, 19841, 29995, 264, 23135, 318, 475, 11, 708, 4586, 11145, 6454, 18675, 11, 51142], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12725143597043795, "compression_ratio": 1.537953795379538, "no_speech_prob": 1.597737784089781e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 7592, "start": 91.72, "end": 94.34, "text": " and Selective Retention and the Geometry of Continuation.", "tokens": [51155, 293, 13638, 488, 11495, 1251, 293, 264, 2876, 34730, 295, 14674, 16073, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12725143597043795, "compression_ratio": 1.537953795379538, "no_speech_prob": 1.597737784089781e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 7592, "start": 94.62, "end": 96.46000000000001, "text": " Which, I mean, those titles alone.", "tokens": [51300, 3013, 11, 286, 914, 11, 729, 12992, 3312, 13, 51392], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12725143597043795, "compression_ratio": 1.537953795379538, "no_speech_prob": 1.597737784089781e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 7592, "start": 96.58, "end": 97.26, "text": " They're intense.", "tokens": [51398, 814, 434, 9447, 13, 51432], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12725143597043795, "compression_ratio": 1.537953795379538, "no_speech_prob": 1.597737784089781e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 7592, "start": 97.56, "end": 103.02000000000001, "text": " Those titles suggest we are dealing with something far, far beyond standard software engineering critiques.", "tokens": [51447, 3950, 12992, 3402, 321, 366, 6260, 365, 746, 1400, 11, 1400, 4399, 3832, 4722, 7043, 3113, 4911, 13, 51720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12725143597043795, "compression_ratio": 1.537953795379538, "no_speech_prob": 1.597737784089781e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 10302, "start": 103.02, "end": 104.7, "text": " Okay. Let's unpack this.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 961, 311, 26699, 341, 13, 50449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17428156272652223, "compression_ratio": 1.5371024734982333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158275246645147e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 10302, "start": 105.06, "end": 112.8, "text": " Our mission today is to take these incredibly dense, mathematically rigorous and highly technical essays", "tokens": [50467, 2621, 4447, 965, 307, 281, 747, 613, 6252, 18011, 11, 44003, 29882, 293, 5405, 6191, 35123, 50854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17428156272652223, "compression_ratio": 1.5371024734982333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158275246645147e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 10302, "start": 112.8, "end": 116.96, "text": " and trace the profound philosophical thread that's woven through them.", "tokens": [50854, 293, 13508, 264, 14382, 25066, 7207, 300, 311, 39221, 807, 552, 13, 51062], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17428156272652223, "compression_ratio": 1.5371024734982333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158275246645147e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 10302, "start": 117.17999999999999, "end": 123.0, "text": " Because what begins as a very specific, almost bitter grievance against modern programming languages,", "tokens": [51073, 1436, 437, 7338, 382, 257, 588, 2685, 11, 1920, 13871, 49260, 719, 1970, 4363, 9410, 8650, 11, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17428156272652223, "compression_ratio": 1.5371024734982333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158275246645147e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 10302, "start": 123.38, "end": 125.97999999999999, "text": " specifically C++, Swift, and Python,", "tokens": [51383, 4682, 383, 25472, 11, 25539, 11, 293, 15329, 11, 51513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17428156272652223, "compression_ratio": 1.5371024734982333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158275246645147e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 10302, "start": 126.52, "end": 130.56, "text": " it somehow evolves into this grand, unified theory of memory.", "tokens": [51540, 309, 6063, 43737, 666, 341, 2697, 11, 26787, 5261, 295, 4675, 13, 51742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17428156272652223, "compression_ratio": 1.5371024734982333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158275246645147e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 10302, "start": 130.72, "end": 132.34, "text": " It really does. It's fascinating.", "tokens": [51750, 467, 534, 775, 13, 467, 311, 10343, 13, 51831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17428156272652223, "compression_ratio": 1.5371024734982333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158275246645147e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 13234, "start": 132.34, "end": 137.52, "text": " We're going to explore how computers, human brains, and even the scientific method itself", "tokens": [50365, 492, 434, 516, 281, 6839, 577, 10807, 11, 1952, 15442, 11, 293, 754, 264, 8134, 3170, 2564, 50624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11600242742971212, "compression_ratio": 1.6103896103896105, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900326403433309e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 13234, "start": 137.52, "end": 139.34, "text": " decide what is actually worth remembering.", "tokens": [50624, 4536, 437, 307, 767, 3163, 20719, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11600242742971212, "compression_ratio": 1.6103896103896105, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900326403433309e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 13234, "start": 139.82, "end": 143.2, "text": " And, of course, the catastrophic costs of forgetting the wrong things.", "tokens": [50739, 400, 11, 295, 1164, 11, 264, 34915, 5497, 295, 25428, 264, 2085, 721, 13, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11600242742971212, "compression_ratio": 1.6103896103896105, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900326403433309e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 13234, "start": 143.32, "end": 144.94, "text": " If we connect this to the bigger picture,", "tokens": [50914, 759, 321, 1745, 341, 281, 264, 3801, 3036, 11, 50995], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11600242742971212, "compression_ratio": 1.6103896103896105, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900326403433309e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 13234, "start": 145.2, "end": 149.64000000000001, "text": " affliction is really forcing us to confront a foundational question about the nature of reality.", "tokens": [51008, 2096, 75, 4105, 307, 534, 19030, 505, 281, 12422, 257, 32195, 1168, 466, 264, 3687, 295, 4103, 13, 51230], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11600242742971212, "compression_ratio": 1.6103896103896105, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900326403433309e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 13234, "start": 150.14000000000001, "end": 153.18, "text": " Like, is the present moment just a fleeting, isolated state?", "tokens": [51255, 1743, 11, 307, 264, 1974, 1623, 445, 257, 7025, 9880, 11, 14621, 1785, 30, 51407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11600242742971212, "compression_ratio": 1.6103896103896105, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900326403433309e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 13234, "start": 153.36, "end": 158.36, "text": " Or is it the inescapable sum total of every single historical event that preceded it?", "tokens": [51416, 1610, 307, 309, 264, 294, 279, 9485, 712, 2408, 3217, 295, 633, 2167, 8584, 2280, 300, 16969, 292, 309, 30, 51666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11600242742971212, "compression_ratio": 1.6103896103896105, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900326403433309e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 13234, "start": 158.42000000000002, "end": 158.56, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51669, 1779, 13, 51676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11600242742971212, "compression_ratio": 1.6103896103896105, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900326403433309e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 15856, "start": 158.56, "end": 162.74, "text": " And when we build systems, whether they are digital, biological, or societal,", "tokens": [50365, 400, 562, 321, 1322, 3652, 11, 1968, 436, 366, 4562, 11, 13910, 11, 420, 33472, 11, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12973202744575396, "compression_ratio": 1.54, "no_speech_prob": 2.385312000002804e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 15856, "start": 163.24, "end": 166.42000000000002, "text": " which of those two realities are we actually forcing them to adopt?", "tokens": [50599, 597, 295, 729, 732, 27785, 366, 321, 767, 19030, 552, 281, 6878, 30, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12973202744575396, "compression_ratio": 1.54, "no_speech_prob": 2.385312000002804e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 15856, "start": 166.74, "end": 173.68, "text": " But before we can talk about memory or thermodynamics or, you know, time traveling through data,", "tokens": [50774, 583, 949, 321, 393, 751, 466, 4675, 420, 8810, 35483, 420, 11, 291, 458, 11, 565, 9712, 807, 1412, 11, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12973202744575396, "compression_ratio": 1.54, "no_speech_prob": 2.385312000002804e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 15856, "start": 173.94, "end": 177.54, "text": " we have to look at the absolute mess we are currently sitting in.", "tokens": [51134, 321, 362, 281, 574, 412, 264, 8236, 2082, 321, 366, 4362, 3798, 294, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12973202744575396, "compression_ratio": 1.54, "no_speech_prob": 2.385312000002804e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 17754, "start": 177.54, "end": 184.32, "text": " We need to examine what the author calls the kitchen sink of modern coding.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 643, 281, 17496, 437, 264, 3793, 5498, 264, 6525, 9500, 295, 4363, 17720, 13, 50704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18105380431465481, "compression_ratio": 1.5391304347826087, "no_speech_prob": 2.0599789235520305e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 17754, "start": 185.26, "end": 188.64, "text": " Fliction opens the first essay, Against the Kitchen Sink,", "tokens": [50751, 3235, 4105, 9870, 264, 700, 16238, 11, 29995, 264, 23135, 318, 475, 11, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18105380431465481, "compression_ratio": 1.5391304347826087, "no_speech_prob": 2.0599789235520305e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 17754, "start": 188.85999999999999, "end": 193.78, "text": " with this incredibly visceral description of pure, unadulterated exhaustion.", "tokens": [50931, 365, 341, 6252, 1452, 47879, 3855, 295, 6075, 11, 517, 345, 425, 391, 770, 47408, 13, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18105380431465481, "compression_ratio": 1.5391304347826087, "no_speech_prob": 2.0599789235520305e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 17754, "start": 194.01999999999998, "end": 196.98, "text": " Oh, the fatigue is palpable in the writing.", "tokens": [51189, 876, 11, 264, 20574, 307, 3984, 30454, 294, 264, 3579, 13, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18105380431465481, "compression_ratio": 1.5391304347826087, "no_speech_prob": 2.0599789235520305e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 17754, "start": 197.04, "end": 200.64, "text": " It's the exhaustion of simply opening a C++ or Swift file.", "tokens": [51340, 467, 311, 264, 47408, 295, 2935, 5193, 257, 383, 25472, 420, 25539, 3991, 13, 51520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18105380431465481, "compression_ratio": 1.5391304347826087, "no_speech_prob": 2.0599789235520305e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 17754, "start": 201.32, "end": 203.92, "text": " The author writes that in C++ operation,", "tokens": [51554, 440, 3793, 13657, 300, 294, 383, 25472, 6916, 11, 51684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18105380431465481, "compression_ratio": 1.5391304347826087, "no_speech_prob": 2.0599789235520305e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 20392, "start": 203.92, "end": 207.94, "text": " before you can write a single line of actual logic to solve your actual problem,", "tokens": [50365, 949, 291, 393, 2464, 257, 2167, 1622, 295, 3539, 9952, 281, 5039, 428, 3539, 1154, 11, 50566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304130162948218, "compression_ratio": 1.5154185022026432, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251325593060305e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 20392, "start": 208.14, "end": 213.22, "text": " you have to mentally negotiate with 40 years of syntax that no one ever dared to throw away.", "tokens": [50576, 291, 362, 281, 17072, 21713, 365, 3356, 924, 295, 28431, 300, 572, 472, 1562, 44564, 281, 3507, 1314, 13, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304130162948218, "compression_ratio": 1.5154185022026432, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251325593060305e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 20392, "start": 213.98, "end": 214.17999999999998, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50868, 865, 13, 50878], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304130162948218, "compression_ratio": 1.5154185022026432, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251325593060305e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 20392, "start": 214.33999999999997, "end": 217.39999999999998, "text": " Infliction categorizes this exhaustion through this concept of gravity.", "tokens": [50886, 682, 3423, 4105, 19250, 5660, 341, 47408, 807, 341, 3410, 295, 12110, 13, 51039], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304130162948218, "compression_ratio": 1.5154185022026432, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251325593060305e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 20392, "start": 217.64, "end": 221.51999999999998, "text": " Modern programming languages are trapped in different gravitational wells, basically.", "tokens": [51051, 19814, 9410, 8650, 366, 14994, 294, 819, 28538, 30984, 11, 1936, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304130162948218, "compression_ratio": 1.5154185022026432, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251325593060305e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 20392, "start": 221.66, "end": 221.77999999999997, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51252, 1779, 13, 51258], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304130162948218, "compression_ratio": 1.5154185022026432, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251325593060305e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 22178, "start": 221.78, "end": 224.52, "text": " So C++ suffers from what the author calls committee gravity.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 383, 25472, 33776, 490, 437, 264, 3793, 5498, 7482, 12110, 13, 50502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.145306071528682, "compression_ratio": 1.5731343283582089, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761187907725187e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 22178, "start": 225.0, "end": 227.7, "text": " C++ is governed by an ISO standardization committee,", "tokens": [50526, 383, 25472, 307, 35529, 538, 364, 25042, 3832, 2144, 7482, 11, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.145306071528682, "compression_ratio": 1.5731343283582089, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761187907725187e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 22178, "start": 227.84, "end": 229.46, "text": " which means every single new feature,", "tokens": [50668, 597, 1355, 633, 2167, 777, 4111, 11, 50749], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.145306071528682, "compression_ratio": 1.5731343283582089, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761187907725187e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 22178, "start": 229.86, "end": 231.28, "text": " every proposed change,", "tokens": [50769, 633, 10348, 1319, 11, 50840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.145306071528682, "compression_ratio": 1.5731343283582089, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761187907725187e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 22178, "start": 231.62, "end": 234.74, "text": " has to survive this brutal political and technical gauntlet.", "tokens": [50857, 575, 281, 7867, 341, 17878, 3905, 293, 6191, 5959, 2760, 2631, 13, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.145306071528682, "compression_ratio": 1.5731343283582089, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761187907725187e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 22178, "start": 235.0, "end": 240.62, "text": " Because there are billions of lines of C++ running critical infrastructure all over the world, right?", "tokens": [51026, 1436, 456, 366, 17375, 295, 3876, 295, 383, 25472, 2614, 4924, 6896, 439, 670, 264, 1002, 11, 558, 30, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.145306071528682, "compression_ratio": 1.5731343283582089, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761187907725187e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 22178, "start": 240.62, "end": 241.02, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51307, 7587, 13, 51327], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.145306071528682, "compression_ratio": 1.5731343283582089, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761187907725187e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 22178, "start": 241.24, "end": 243.24, "text": " Backward compatibility is a religion there.", "tokens": [51338, 5833, 1007, 34237, 307, 257, 7561, 456, 13, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.145306071528682, "compression_ratio": 1.5731343283582089, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761187907725187e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 22178, "start": 243.32, "end": 245.46, "text": " You absolutely cannot break the old code.", "tokens": [51442, 509, 3122, 2644, 1821, 264, 1331, 3089, 13, 51549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.145306071528682, "compression_ratio": 1.5731343283582089, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761187907725187e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 22178, "start": 245.56, "end": 247.5, "text": " So the language never revises itself.", "tokens": [51554, 407, 264, 2856, 1128, 3698, 3598, 2564, 13, 51651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.145306071528682, "compression_ratio": 1.5731343283582089, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761187907725187e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 22178, "start": 247.76, "end": 248.7, "text": " It just accretes.", "tokens": [51664, 467, 445, 1317, 1505, 279, 13, 51711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.145306071528682, "compression_ratio": 1.5731343283582089, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761187907725187e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 22178, "start": 248.9, "end": 249.18, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51721, 865, 13, 51735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.145306071528682, "compression_ratio": 1.5731343283582089, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761187907725187e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 22178, "start": 249.3, "end": 250.84, "text": " It acts like a sedimentary rock.", "tokens": [51741, 467, 10672, 411, 257, 32362, 822, 3727, 13, 51818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.145306071528682, "compression_ratio": 1.5731343283582089, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761187907725187e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 25084, "start": 250.84, "end": 254.84, "text": " You have the 1980s layer, the 1990s layer, the C++ 11 layer,", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 264, 13626, 82, 4583, 11, 264, 13384, 82, 4583, 11, 264, 383, 25472, 2975, 4583, 11, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16803118008286205, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126349809495125e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 25084, "start": 254.88, "end": 256.4, "text": " and they all just sit on top of each other.", "tokens": [50567, 293, 436, 439, 445, 1394, 322, 1192, 295, 1184, 661, 13, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16803118008286205, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126349809495125e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 25084, "start": 256.7, "end": 256.98, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50658, 3153, 13, 50672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16803118008286205, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126349809495125e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 25084, "start": 257.06, "end": 260.0, "text": " And then you have vendor gravity, which is the trap that Swift is in.", "tokens": [50676, 400, 550, 291, 362, 24321, 12110, 11, 597, 307, 264, 11487, 300, 25539, 307, 294, 13, 50823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16803118008286205, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126349809495125e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 25084, "start": 260.04, "end": 260.78000000000003, "text": " Okay, Swift, yeah.", "tokens": [50825, 1033, 11, 25539, 11, 1338, 13, 50862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16803118008286205, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126349809495125e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 25084, "start": 260.9, "end": 262.94, "text": " Swift is technically open source,", "tokens": [50868, 25539, 307, 12120, 1269, 4009, 11, 50970], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16803118008286205, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126349809495125e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 25084, "start": 263.12, "end": 266.36, "text": " but its center of mass is entirely dictated by Apple.", "tokens": [50979, 457, 1080, 3056, 295, 2758, 307, 7696, 12569, 770, 538, 6373, 13, 51141], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16803118008286205, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126349809495125e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 25084, "start": 266.98, "end": 269.26, "text": " Apple's internal corporate priorities,", "tokens": [51172, 6373, 311, 6920, 10896, 15503, 11, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16803118008286205, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126349809495125e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 25084, "start": 270.0, "end": 271.58, "text": " their hardware release cadence,", "tokens": [51323, 641, 8837, 4374, 46109, 11, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16803118008286205, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126349809495125e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 25084, "start": 271.58, "end": 274.86, "text": " and their proprietary frameworks completely dictate", "tokens": [51402, 293, 641, 38992, 29834, 2584, 36071, 51566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16803118008286205, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126349809495125e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 25084, "start": 274.86, "end": 277.0, "text": " which idioms in the language flourish", "tokens": [51566, 597, 18014, 4785, 294, 264, 2856, 38311, 51673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16803118008286205, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126349809495125e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 25084, "start": 277.0, "end": 279.1, "text": " and which ones just die on the vine.", "tokens": [51673, 293, 597, 2306, 445, 978, 322, 264, 12755, 13, 51778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16803118008286205, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126349809495125e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 25084, "start": 279.22, "end": 279.38, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51784, 1779, 13, 51792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16803118008286205, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126349809495125e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 27938, "start": 279.38, "end": 283.56, "text": " So you can theoretically write Swift completely divorced from the Apple ecosystem.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 291, 393, 29400, 2464, 25539, 2584, 27670, 490, 264, 6373, 11311, 13, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23790631612141927, "compression_ratio": 1.4788732394366197, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130309114971818e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 27938, "start": 283.65999999999997, "end": 283.86, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50579, 865, 13, 50589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23790631612141927, "compression_ratio": 1.4788732394366197, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130309114971818e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 27938, "start": 283.86, "end": 289.21999999999997, "text": " But the gravitational pull of the vendor makes it practically impossible for most people.", "tokens": [50589, 583, 264, 28538, 2235, 295, 264, 24321, 1669, 309, 15667, 6243, 337, 881, 561, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23790631612141927, "compression_ratio": 1.4788732394366197, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130309114971818e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 27938, "start": 289.48, "end": 289.86, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50870, 48746, 736, 13, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23790631612141927, "compression_ratio": 1.4788732394366197, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130309114971818e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 27938, "start": 290.06, "end": 292.44, "text": " You end up learning Apple's corporate philosophy,", "tokens": [50899, 509, 917, 493, 2539, 6373, 311, 10896, 10675, 11, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23790631612141927, "compression_ratio": 1.4788732394366197, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130309114971818e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 27938, "start": 292.71999999999997, "end": 294.7, "text": " not the pure mathematics of computation.", "tokens": [51032, 406, 264, 6075, 18666, 295, 24903, 13, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23790631612141927, "compression_ratio": 1.4788732394366197, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130309114971818e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 27938, "start": 295.02, "end": 296.36, "text": " That's such a great way to put it.", "tokens": [51147, 663, 311, 1270, 257, 869, 636, 281, 829, 309, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23790631612141927, "compression_ratio": 1.4788732394366197, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130309114971818e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 29636, "start": 296.36, "end": 301.42, "text": " And then the third type of gravity Fliction identifies is ecosystem gravity,", "tokens": [50365, 400, 550, 264, 2636, 2010, 295, 12110, 3235, 4105, 34597, 307, 11311, 12110, 11, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.25349579848252335, "compression_ratio": 1.492822966507177, "no_speech_prob": 1.6137629427204203e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 29636, "start": 301.92, "end": 302.82, "text": " which applies to Python.", "tokens": [50643, 597, 13165, 281, 15329, 13, 50688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.25349579848252335, "compression_ratio": 1.492822966507177, "no_speech_prob": 1.6137629427204203e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 29636, "start": 302.82, "end": 303.18, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50688, 1779, 13, 50706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.25349579848252335, "compression_ratio": 1.492822966507177, "no_speech_prob": 1.6137629427204203e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 29636, "start": 303.18, "end": 307.1, "text": " Python doesn't have a strict ISO committee or a single corporate overlord,", "tokens": [50706, 15329, 1177, 380, 362, 257, 10910, 25042, 7482, 420, 257, 2167, 10896, 15986, 765, 11, 50902], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.25349579848252335, "compression_ratio": 1.492822966507177, "no_speech_prob": 1.6137629427204203e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 29636, "start": 307.18, "end": 313.04, "text": " but it has this massive sprawling community and millions of third-party libraries.", "tokens": [50906, 457, 309, 575, 341, 5994, 22734, 1688, 1768, 293, 6803, 295, 2636, 12, 23409, 15148, 13, 51199], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.25349579848252335, "compression_ratio": 1.492822966507177, "no_speech_prob": 1.6137629427204203e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 29636, "start": 313.42, "end": 313.52000000000004, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51218, 865, 13, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.25349579848252335, "compression_ratio": 1.492822966507177, "no_speech_prob": 1.6137629427204203e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 29636, "start": 313.72, "end": 315.62, "text": " Python's gravity is highly distributed.", "tokens": [51233, 15329, 311, 12110, 307, 5405, 12631, 13, 51328], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.25349579848252335, "compression_ratio": 1.492822966507177, "no_speech_prob": 1.6137629427204203e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 31562, "start": 315.62, "end": 320.38, "text": " It permits many different ways of solving a problem rather than enforcing one strict paradigm.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 30990, 867, 819, 2098, 295, 12606, 257, 1154, 2831, 813, 25495, 2175, 472, 10910, 24709, 13, 50603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16187169416895453, "compression_ratio": 1.5777027027027026, "no_speech_prob": 1.5516139805285545e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 31562, "start": 320.9, "end": 326.84000000000003, "text": " But, you know, the sheer weight of community expectations still heavily constrains the future of the language.", "tokens": [50629, 583, 11, 291, 458, 11, 264, 23061, 3364, 295, 1768, 9843, 920, 10950, 11525, 1292, 264, 2027, 295, 264, 2856, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16187169416895453, "compression_ratio": 1.5777027027027026, "no_speech_prob": 1.5516139805285545e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 31562, "start": 326.84000000000003, "end": 329.2, "text": " Because everyone expects it to work a certain way.", "tokens": [50926, 1436, 1518, 33280, 309, 281, 589, 257, 1629, 636, 13, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16187169416895453, "compression_ratio": 1.5777027027027026, "no_speech_prob": 1.5516139805285545e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 31562, "start": 329.3, "end": 329.6, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51049, 7587, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16187169416895453, "compression_ratio": 1.5777027027027026, "no_speech_prob": 1.5516139805285545e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 31562, "start": 329.96, "end": 330.12, "text": " What?", "tokens": [51082, 708, 30, 51090], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16187169416895453, "compression_ratio": 1.5777027027027026, "no_speech_prob": 1.5516139805285545e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 31562, "start": 330.26, "end": 334.06, "text": " The difference is that Python's distributed gravity is somewhat permissive,", "tokens": [51097, 440, 2649, 307, 300, 15329, 311, 12631, 12110, 307, 8344, 4784, 891, 488, 11, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16187169416895453, "compression_ratio": 1.5777027027027026, "no_speech_prob": 1.5516139805285545e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 31562, "start": 334.1, "end": 338.52, "text": " whereas the concentrated gravity of a committee or a vendor produces a very sharp,", "tokens": [51289, 9735, 264, 21321, 12110, 295, 257, 7482, 420, 257, 24321, 14725, 257, 588, 8199, 11, 51510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16187169416895453, "compression_ratio": 1.5777027027027026, "no_speech_prob": 1.5516139805285545e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 31562, "start": 338.72, "end": 340.62, "text": " exclusionary form of cognitive load.", "tokens": [51520, 33049, 822, 1254, 295, 15605, 3677, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16187169416895453, "compression_ratio": 1.5777027027027026, "no_speech_prob": 1.5516139805285545e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 34062, "start": 340.62, "end": 343.18, "text": " And the author builds on a legendary framework here, right?", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 3793, 15182, 322, 257, 16698, 8388, 510, 11, 558, 30, 50493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14381299325085561, "compression_ratio": 1.6944444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810667863107145e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 34062, "start": 343.78000000000003, "end": 348.18, "text": " Back in the 1980s, the computer scientist Fred Brooks wrote about the difference between", "tokens": [50523, 5833, 294, 264, 13626, 82, 11, 264, 3820, 12662, 10112, 33493, 4114, 466, 264, 2649, 1296, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14381299325085561, "compression_ratio": 1.6944444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810667863107145e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 34062, "start": 348.18, "end": 351.5, "text": " essential complexity and accidental complexity.", "tokens": [50743, 7115, 14024, 293, 38094, 14024, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14381299325085561, "compression_ratio": 1.6944444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810667863107145e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 34062, "start": 351.66, "end": 352.96, "text": " Yes, a classic distinction.", "tokens": [50917, 1079, 11, 257, 7230, 16844, 13, 50982], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14381299325085561, "compression_ratio": 1.6944444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810667863107145e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 34062, "start": 353.36, "end": 356.8, "text": " Essential complexity is the unavoidable difficulty of the problem itself.", "tokens": [51002, 49736, 14024, 307, 264, 36541, 17079, 712, 10360, 295, 264, 1154, 2564, 13, 51174], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14381299325085561, "compression_ratio": 1.6944444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810667863107145e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 34062, "start": 357.48, "end": 362.18, "text": " Like, if you were trying to land a rover on Mars, orbital mechanics are complex.", "tokens": [51208, 1743, 11, 498, 291, 645, 1382, 281, 2117, 257, 45767, 322, 9692, 11, 27677, 12939, 366, 3997, 13, 51443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14381299325085561, "compression_ratio": 1.6944444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810667863107145e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 34062, "start": 362.62, "end": 363.38, "text": " That is essential.", "tokens": [51465, 663, 307, 7115, 13, 51503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14381299325085561, "compression_ratio": 1.6944444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810667863107145e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 34062, "start": 364.12, "end": 368.88, "text": " Accidental complexity is the friction caused by using clumsy tools to solve that problem,", "tokens": [51540, 5725, 47023, 14024, 307, 264, 17710, 7008, 538, 1228, 44640, 3873, 281, 5039, 300, 1154, 11, 51778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14381299325085561, "compression_ratio": 1.6944444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810667863107145e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 36888, "start": 368.88, "end": 372.44, "text": " like trying to calculate those orbital mechanics using Roman numerals.", "tokens": [50365, 411, 1382, 281, 8873, 729, 27677, 12939, 1228, 8566, 7866, 1124, 13, 50543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15440302309782608, "compression_ratio": 1.5758620689655172, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830503783525242e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 36888, "start": 373.08, "end": 373.15999999999997, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50575, 1779, 13, 50579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15440302309782608, "compression_ratio": 1.5758620689655172, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830503783525242e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 36888, "start": 373.28, "end": 377.94, "text": " And friction introduces a vital third category here, which is historical complexity.", "tokens": [50585, 400, 17710, 31472, 257, 11707, 2636, 7719, 510, 11, 597, 307, 8584, 14024, 13, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15440302309782608, "compression_ratio": 1.5758620689655172, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830503783525242e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 36888, "start": 378.14, "end": 378.26, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50828, 1033, 13, 50834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15440302309782608, "compression_ratio": 1.5758620689655172, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830503783525242e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 36888, "start": 378.5, "end": 379.34, "text": " Define that for us.", "tokens": [50846, 9548, 533, 300, 337, 505, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15440302309782608, "compression_ratio": 1.5758620689655172, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830503783525242e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 36888, "start": 379.44, "end": 385.12, "text": " This is the unavoidable residue of a system that has never been permitted to forget anything at once committed to.", "tokens": [50893, 639, 307, 264, 36541, 17079, 712, 34799, 295, 257, 1185, 300, 575, 1128, 668, 28658, 281, 2870, 1340, 412, 1564, 7784, 281, 13, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15440302309782608, "compression_ratio": 1.5758620689655172, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830503783525242e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 36888, "start": 385.88, "end": 389.5, "text": " Fliction uses memory management in C++ as the prime example.", "tokens": [51215, 3235, 4105, 4960, 4675, 4592, 294, 383, 25472, 382, 264, 5835, 1365, 13, 51396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15440302309782608, "compression_ratio": 1.5758620689655172, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830503783525242e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 36888, "start": 389.65999999999997, "end": 389.86, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51404, 1779, 13, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15440302309782608, "compression_ratio": 1.5758620689655172, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830503783525242e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 36888, "start": 390.02, "end": 392.36, "text": " So in the early days, you had raw pointers.", "tokens": [51422, 407, 294, 264, 2440, 1708, 11, 291, 632, 8936, 44548, 13, 51539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15440302309782608, "compression_ratio": 1.5758620689655172, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830503783525242e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 36888, "start": 392.74, "end": 395.36, "text": " They were incredibly fast, but dangerous.", "tokens": [51558, 814, 645, 6252, 2370, 11, 457, 5795, 13, 51689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15440302309782608, "compression_ratio": 1.5758620689655172, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830503783525242e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 39536, "start": 395.36, "end": 398.72, "text": " I mean, they caused memory leaks and crashes if you weren't extremely careful.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 914, 11, 436, 7008, 4675, 28885, 293, 28642, 498, 291, 4999, 380, 4664, 5026, 13, 50533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1356287436051802, "compression_ratio": 1.7264150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 1.5186296230956797e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 39536, "start": 399.06, "end": 403.12, "text": " So years later, the committee added smart pointers to automate the safety.", "tokens": [50550, 407, 924, 1780, 11, 264, 7482, 3869, 4069, 44548, 281, 31605, 264, 4514, 13, 50753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1356287436051802, "compression_ratio": 1.7264150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 1.5186296230956797e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 39536, "start": 403.72, "end": 407.22, "text": " But they couldn't remove the raw pointers because of committee gravity.", "tokens": [50783, 583, 436, 2809, 380, 4159, 264, 8936, 44548, 570, 295, 7482, 12110, 13, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1356287436051802, "compression_ratio": 1.7264150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 1.5186296230956797e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 39536, "start": 407.46000000000004, "end": 407.66, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50970, 1779, 13, 50980], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1356287436051802, "compression_ratio": 1.7264150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 1.5186296230956797e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 39536, "start": 407.72, "end": 408.94, "text": " They can't break the old code.", "tokens": [50983, 814, 393, 380, 1821, 264, 1331, 3089, 13, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1356287436051802, "compression_ratio": 1.7264150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 1.5186296230956797e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 39536, "start": 409.2, "end": 410.76, "text": " So then they just kept adding to it.", "tokens": [51057, 407, 550, 436, 445, 4305, 5127, 281, 309, 13, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1356287436051802, "compression_ratio": 1.7264150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 1.5186296230956797e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 39536, "start": 410.84000000000003, "end": 414.26, "text": " They added unique pointers and shared pointers and move semantics.", "tokens": [51139, 814, 3869, 3845, 44548, 293, 5507, 44548, 293, 1286, 4361, 45298, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1356287436051802, "compression_ratio": 1.7264150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 1.5186296230956797e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 39536, "start": 414.98, "end": 419.1, "text": " If you want to know who owns a piece of data in C++, when it can be safely deleted,", "tokens": [51346, 759, 291, 528, 281, 458, 567, 19143, 257, 2522, 295, 1412, 294, 383, 25472, 11, 562, 309, 393, 312, 11750, 22981, 11, 51552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1356287436051802, "compression_ratio": 1.7264150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 1.5186296230956797e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 39536, "start": 419.40000000000003, "end": 425.04, "text": " you now have five different partially overlapping frameworks, all of which are technically valid.", "tokens": [51567, 291, 586, 362, 1732, 819, 18886, 33535, 29834, 11, 439, 295, 597, 366, 12120, 7363, 13, 51849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1356287436051802, "compression_ratio": 1.7264150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 1.5186296230956797e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 42504, "start": 425.04, "end": 428.62, "text": " And this is where the cognitive load just becomes suffocating.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 307, 689, 264, 15605, 3677, 445, 3643, 3889, 905, 990, 13, 50544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12513322169237798, "compression_ratio": 1.553191489361702, "no_speech_prob": 1.4950824866327705e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 42504, "start": 428.92, "end": 432.26000000000005, "text": " These overlapping features actively distort one another.", "tokens": [50559, 1981, 33535, 4122, 13022, 37555, 472, 1071, 13, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12513322169237798, "compression_ratio": 1.553191489361702, "no_speech_prob": 1.4950824866327705e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 42504, "start": 432.46000000000004, "end": 439.14000000000004, "text": " If you write a generic template in C++, you have to reason about how it will interact with ownership semantics", "tokens": [50736, 759, 291, 2464, 257, 19577, 12379, 294, 383, 25472, 11, 291, 362, 281, 1778, 466, 577, 309, 486, 4648, 365, 15279, 4361, 45298, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12513322169237798, "compression_ratio": 1.553191489361702, "no_speech_prob": 1.4950824866327705e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 42504, "start": 439.14000000000004, "end": 442.40000000000003, "text": " that didn't even exist when the concept of templates was first introduced.", "tokens": [51070, 300, 994, 380, 754, 2514, 562, 264, 3410, 295, 21165, 390, 700, 7268, 13, 51233], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12513322169237798, "compression_ratio": 1.553191489361702, "no_speech_prob": 1.4950824866327705e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 42504, "start": 442.6, "end": 445.32000000000005, "text": " Let me play devil's advocate here, though, or just push back on this a bit.", "tokens": [51243, 961, 385, 862, 13297, 311, 14608, 510, 11, 1673, 11, 420, 445, 2944, 646, 322, 341, 257, 857, 13, 51379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12513322169237798, "compression_ratio": 1.553191489361702, "no_speech_prob": 1.4950824866327705e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 42504, "start": 445.66, "end": 448.96000000000004, "text": " Are we absolutely sure more features are inherently bad?", "tokens": [51396, 2014, 321, 3122, 988, 544, 4122, 366, 27993, 1578, 30, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12513322169237798, "compression_ratio": 1.553191489361702, "no_speech_prob": 1.4950824866327705e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 44896, "start": 448.96, "end": 452.5, "text": " Like, if I am a mechanic, I want a massive toolbox.", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 11, 498, 286, 669, 257, 23860, 11, 286, 528, 257, 5994, 44593, 13, 50542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325856844584147, "compression_ratio": 1.6058394160583942, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171600733874691e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 44896, "start": 452.7, "end": 456.76, "text": " I want the Phillips head, the flathead, the Torx wrench, the socket set.", "tokens": [50552, 286, 528, 264, 24565, 1378, 11, 264, 4962, 1934, 11, 264, 7160, 87, 25406, 11, 264, 19741, 992, 13, 50755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325856844584147, "compression_ratio": 1.6058394160583942, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171600733874691e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 44896, "start": 457.02, "end": 459.2, "text": " I don't want a single theoretical multi-tool.", "tokens": [50768, 286, 500, 380, 528, 257, 2167, 20864, 4825, 12, 83, 1092, 13, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325856844584147, "compression_ratio": 1.6058394160583942, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171600733874691e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 44896, "start": 459.64, "end": 463.58, "text": " Why is having 40 years of highly specific tools considered a burden?", "tokens": [50899, 1545, 307, 1419, 3356, 924, 295, 5405, 2685, 3873, 4888, 257, 12578, 30, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325856844584147, "compression_ratio": 1.6058394160583942, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171600733874691e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 44896, "start": 464.28, "end": 467.94, "text": " Isn't that exactly why C++ is trusted to run the Mars rover?", "tokens": [51131, 6998, 380, 300, 2293, 983, 383, 25472, 307, 16034, 281, 1190, 264, 9692, 45767, 30, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325856844584147, "compression_ratio": 1.6058394160583942, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171600733874691e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 44896, "start": 468.35999999999996, "end": 472.46, "text": " While these theoretical academic languages never leave the white paper stage,", "tokens": [51335, 3987, 613, 20864, 7778, 8650, 1128, 1856, 264, 2418, 3035, 3233, 11, 51540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325856844584147, "compression_ratio": 1.6058394160583942, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171600733874691e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 44896, "start": 473.0, "end": 476.46, "text": " reliability comes from age and a massive toolbox, doesn't it?", "tokens": [51567, 24550, 1487, 490, 3205, 293, 257, 5994, 44593, 11, 1177, 380, 309, 30, 51740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325856844584147, "compression_ratio": 1.6058394160583942, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171600733874691e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 47646, "start": 476.46, "end": 483.68, "text": " It's a fair question, but viewing a programming language as a mere toolbox is actually a category error, according to Fliction.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 257, 3143, 1168, 11, 457, 17480, 257, 9410, 2856, 382, 257, 8401, 44593, 307, 767, 257, 7719, 6713, 11, 4650, 281, 3235, 4105, 13, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12070699323687636, "compression_ratio": 1.6156462585034013, "no_speech_prob": 1.7971933620117286e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 47646, "start": 484.03999999999996, "end": 485.09999999999997, "text": " Oh, really? How so?", "tokens": [50744, 876, 11, 534, 30, 1012, 370, 30, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12070699323687636, "compression_ratio": 1.6156462585034013, "no_speech_prob": 1.7971933620117286e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 47646, "start": 485.29999999999995, "end": 488.38, "text": " Well, a toolbox implies independent tools.", "tokens": [50807, 1042, 11, 257, 44593, 18779, 6695, 3873, 13, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12070699323687636, "compression_ratio": 1.6156462585034013, "no_speech_prob": 1.7971933620117286e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 47646, "start": 488.56, "end": 492.82, "text": " If you add a new wrench to your toolbox, it doesn't change the physical properties of the hammer, right?", "tokens": [50970, 759, 291, 909, 257, 777, 25406, 281, 428, 44593, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 1319, 264, 4001, 7221, 295, 264, 13017, 11, 558, 30, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12070699323687636, "compression_ratio": 1.6156462585034013, "no_speech_prob": 1.7971933620117286e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 47646, "start": 492.9, "end": 493.38, "text": " That's true.", "tokens": [51187, 663, 311, 2074, 13, 51211], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12070699323687636, "compression_ratio": 1.6156462585034013, "no_speech_prob": 1.7971933620117286e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 47646, "start": 493.52, "end": 497.53999999999996, "text": " But in a highly complex programming language, features are deeply entangled.", "tokens": [51218, 583, 294, 257, 5405, 3997, 9410, 2856, 11, 4122, 366, 8760, 948, 39101, 13, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12070699323687636, "compression_ratio": 1.6156462585034013, "no_speech_prob": 1.7971933620117286e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 47646, "start": 498.09999999999997, "end": 503.06, "text": " The existence of move semantics fundamentally alters how a basic function return behaves.", "tokens": [51447, 440, 9123, 295, 1286, 4361, 45298, 17879, 419, 1559, 577, 257, 3875, 2445, 2736, 36896, 13, 51695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12070699323687636, "compression_ratio": 1.6156462585034013, "no_speech_prob": 1.7971933620117286e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 50306, "start": 503.06, "end": 507.66, "text": " Fliction argues this isn't a toolbox at all. It is an initiation rite.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 38218, 341, 1943, 380, 257, 44593, 412, 439, 13, 467, 307, 364, 43569, 367, 642, 13, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17603427039252387, "compression_ratio": 1.515695067264574, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995385796453097e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 50306, "start": 507.88, "end": 509.62, "text": " An initiation rite. That's quite a term.", "tokens": [50606, 1107, 43569, 367, 642, 13, 663, 311, 1596, 257, 1433, 13, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17603427039252387, "compression_ratio": 1.515695067264574, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995385796453097e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 50306, "start": 509.72, "end": 509.94, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50698, 865, 13, 50709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17603427039252387, "compression_ratio": 1.515695067264574, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995385796453097e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 50306, "start": 510.6, "end": 517.12, "text": " Think about the rule of five in C++ VAP, or the desperate need to avoid strong reference cycles and swift closures.", "tokens": [50742, 6557, 466, 264, 4978, 295, 1732, 294, 383, 25472, 691, 4715, 11, 420, 264, 17601, 643, 281, 5042, 2068, 6408, 17796, 293, 29184, 2611, 1303, 13, 51068], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17603427039252387, "compression_ratio": 1.515695067264574, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995385796453097e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 50306, "start": 517.52, "end": 522.04, "text": " These are not universal mathematical laws of computation. They are just historical quirks.", "tokens": [51088, 1981, 366, 406, 11455, 18894, 6064, 295, 24903, 13, 814, 366, 445, 8584, 35645, 1694, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17603427039252387, "compression_ratio": 1.515695067264574, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995385796453097e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 50306, "start": 522.3, "end": 523.0, "text": " Just baggage.", "tokens": [51327, 1449, 41567, 13, 51362], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17603427039252387, "compression_ratio": 1.515695067264574, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995385796453097e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 52300, "start": 523.0, "end": 528.74, "text": " Exactly. There are unwritten rules passed down through code reviews, stack overflow threads, and tribal knowledge.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 821, 366, 517, 26859, 4474, 4678, 760, 807, 3089, 10229, 11, 8630, 37772, 19314, 11, 293, 20958, 3601, 13, 50652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041714072227478, "compression_ratio": 1.51417004048583, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349468216243391e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 52300, "start": 529.22, "end": 534.5, "text": " If a newcomer cannot look at the basic primitives of a language and logically deduce the correct behavior,", "tokens": [50676, 759, 257, 40014, 260, 2644, 574, 412, 264, 3875, 2886, 38970, 295, 257, 2856, 293, 38887, 4172, 4176, 264, 3006, 5223, 11, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041714072227478, "compression_ratio": 1.51417004048583, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349468216243391e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 52300, "start": 534.98, "end": 542.42, "text": " but instead has to memorize a massive supplemental body of community lore just to avoid crashing their program well,", "tokens": [50964, 457, 2602, 575, 281, 27478, 257, 5994, 48604, 1772, 295, 1768, 27258, 445, 281, 5042, 26900, 641, 1461, 731, 11, 51336], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041714072227478, "compression_ratio": 1.51417004048583, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349468216243391e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 52300, "start": 542.92, "end": 544.56, "text": " the language has become a fortress.", "tokens": [51361, 264, 2856, 575, 1813, 257, 31826, 13, 51443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041714072227478, "compression_ratio": 1.51417004048583, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349468216243391e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 54456, "start": 544.56, "end": 552.7399999999999, "text": " Oh, I see. The knowledge isn't about solving the problem anymore. The knowledge is literally just knowing how to survive the tool.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 440, 3601, 1943, 380, 466, 12606, 264, 1154, 3602, 13, 440, 3601, 307, 3736, 445, 5276, 577, 281, 7867, 264, 2290, 13, 50774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1357518434524536, "compression_ratio": 1.6774193548387097, "no_speech_prob": 1.5797025146313537e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 54456, "start": 553.2199999999999, "end": 553.66, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50798, 48746, 736, 13, 50820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1357518434524536, "compression_ratio": 1.6774193548387097, "no_speech_prob": 1.5797025146313537e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 54456, "start": 553.88, "end": 557.5999999999999, "text": " I want you listening to think about the software you use at your own job.", "tokens": [50831, 286, 528, 291, 4764, 281, 519, 466, 264, 4722, 291, 764, 412, 428, 1065, 1691, 13, 51017], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1357518434524536, "compression_ratio": 1.6774193548387097, "no_speech_prob": 1.5797025146313537e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 54456, "start": 558.1999999999999, "end": 561.54, "text": " How much of your daily expertise is just navigating historical complexity?", "tokens": [51047, 1012, 709, 295, 428, 5212, 11769, 307, 445, 32054, 8584, 14024, 30, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1357518434524536, "compression_ratio": 1.6774193548387097, "no_speech_prob": 1.5797025146313537e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 54456, "start": 562.18, "end": 568.6999999999999, "text": " How much of your perceived skill is just knowing that, you know, if you click export before unchecking a specific hidden box,", "tokens": [51246, 1012, 709, 295, 428, 19049, 5389, 307, 445, 5276, 300, 11, 291, 458, 11, 498, 291, 2052, 10725, 949, 46672, 278, 257, 2685, 7633, 2424, 11, 51572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1357518434524536, "compression_ratio": 1.6774193548387097, "no_speech_prob": 1.5797025146313537e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 56870, "start": 568.7, "end": 576.44, "text": " the whole application freezes. You aren't doing your job. You are just managing the historical baggage of the people who coded that software a decade ago.", "tokens": [50365, 264, 1379, 3861, 1737, 12214, 13, 509, 3212, 380, 884, 428, 1691, 13, 509, 366, 445, 11642, 264, 8584, 41567, 295, 264, 561, 567, 34874, 300, 4722, 257, 10378, 2057, 13, 50752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14201613729314286, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396395518038844e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 56870, "start": 576.72, "end": 580.62, "text": " And that cognitive load is mental RAM you cannot spend on the actual domain problem.", "tokens": [50766, 400, 300, 15605, 3677, 307, 4973, 14561, 291, 2644, 3496, 322, 264, 3539, 9274, 1154, 13, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14201613729314286, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396395518038844e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 56870, "start": 581.0, "end": 585.5, "text": " You are basically paying a constant compounding tax just to exist in that environment.", "tokens": [50980, 509, 366, 1936, 6229, 257, 5754, 14154, 278, 3366, 445, 281, 2514, 294, 300, 2823, 13, 51205], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14201613729314286, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396395518038844e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 56870, "start": 585.72, "end": 592.5, "text": " Right. So if the current ecosystem is this bloated, sedimentary fossil record, we obviously need an escape hatch.", "tokens": [51216, 1779, 13, 407, 498, 264, 2190, 11311, 307, 341, 1749, 770, 11, 32362, 822, 18737, 2136, 11, 321, 2745, 643, 364, 7615, 17387, 13, 51555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14201613729314286, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396395518038844e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 56870, "start": 592.7, "end": 592.94, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51565, 865, 13, 51577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14201613729314286, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396395518038844e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 56870, "start": 592.94, "end": 595.2, "text": " And Fliction actually introduces one in the text.", "tokens": [51577, 400, 3235, 4105, 767, 31472, 472, 294, 264, 2487, 13, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14201613729314286, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396395518038844e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 56870, "start": 595.36, "end": 595.5400000000001, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51698, 865, 13, 51707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14201613729314286, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396395518038844e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 56870, "start": 595.76, "end": 597.94, "text": " A radical new programming paradigm called SpherePop.", "tokens": [51718, 316, 12001, 777, 9410, 24709, 1219, 318, 6605, 38677, 13, 51827], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14201613729314286, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396395518038844e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 59794, "start": 597.94, "end": 598.46, "text": " SpherePop.", "tokens": [50365, 318, 6605, 38677, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13935382742630809, "compression_ratio": 1.6158940397350994, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503344252103094e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 59794, "start": 598.6600000000001, "end": 605.3800000000001, "text": " Yes. SpherePop. And Fliction is very careful to position SpherePop not as some isolated magical invention out of nowhere,", "tokens": [50401, 1079, 13, 318, 6605, 38677, 13, 400, 3235, 4105, 307, 588, 5026, 281, 2535, 318, 6605, 38677, 406, 382, 512, 14621, 12066, 22265, 484, 295, 11159, 11, 50737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13935382742630809, "compression_ratio": 1.6158940397350994, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503344252103094e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 59794, "start": 605.6400000000001, "end": 609.1600000000001, "text": " but as the continuation of a very specific historical lineage.", "tokens": [50750, 457, 382, 264, 29357, 295, 257, 588, 2685, 8584, 38257, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13935382742630809, "compression_ratio": 1.6158940397350994, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503344252103094e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 59794, "start": 609.22, "end": 610.36, "text": " It's building on giants.", "tokens": [50929, 467, 311, 2390, 322, 31894, 13, 50986], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13935382742630809, "compression_ratio": 1.6158940397350994, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503344252103094e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 59794, "start": 610.48, "end": 617.7, "text": " Exactly. It follows Alonzo Church, who sought the minimal mathematical foundation of computation through lambda calculus.", "tokens": [50992, 7587, 13, 467, 10002, 967, 266, 4765, 7882, 11, 567, 17532, 264, 13206, 18894, 7030, 295, 24903, 807, 13607, 33400, 13, 51353], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13935382742630809, "compression_ratio": 1.6158940397350994, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503344252103094e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 59794, "start": 617.7, "end": 627.1400000000001, "text": " It follows John McCarthy, who created Lisp, and demonstrated how a tiny handful of primitives could bootstrap an entire self-describing language.", "tokens": [51353, 467, 10002, 2619, 44085, 11, 567, 2942, 441, 7631, 11, 293, 18772, 577, 257, 5870, 16458, 295, 2886, 38970, 727, 11450, 372, 4007, 364, 2302, 2698, 12, 14792, 39541, 2856, 13, 51825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13935382742630809, "compression_ratio": 1.6158940397350994, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503344252103094e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 62714, "start": 627.14, "end": 628.3199999999999, "text": " Yeah, and Alan Kay, right.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 11, 293, 16442, 14179, 11, 558, 13, 50424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21134028611359773, "compression_ratio": 1.406060606060606, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014868688656424e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 62714, "start": 628.36, "end": 634.6999999999999, "text": " Yes. Alan Kay, whose original vision for object-oriented programming wasn't the bloated class hierarchies we have today,", "tokens": [50426, 1079, 13, 16442, 14179, 11, 6104, 3380, 5201, 337, 2657, 12, 27414, 9410, 2067, 380, 264, 1749, 770, 1508, 35250, 530, 321, 362, 965, 11, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21134028611359773, "compression_ratio": 1.406060606060606, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014868688656424e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 62714, "start": 634.6999999999999, "end": 639.9, "text": " but minimal, independent biological cells basically passing messages to one another.", "tokens": [50743, 457, 13206, 11, 6695, 13910, 5438, 1936, 8437, 7897, 281, 472, 1071, 13, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21134028611359773, "compression_ratio": 1.406060606060606, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014868688656424e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 63990, "start": 639.9, "end": 647.4599999999999, "text": " So all those pioneers were searching for the atomic foundation of computing, but they were looking for the foundation of state or values.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 439, 729, 47381, 645, 10808, 337, 264, 22275, 7030, 295, 15866, 11, 457, 436, 645, 1237, 337, 264, 7030, 295, 1785, 420, 4190, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16387202134772913, "compression_ratio": 1.6342857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.8982163930980622e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 63990, "start": 647.98, "end": 650.52, "text": " SpherePop takes a violently different angle. It asks,", "tokens": [50769, 318, 6605, 38677, 2516, 257, 46728, 819, 5802, 13, 467, 8962, 11, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16387202134772913, "compression_ratio": 1.6342857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.8982163930980622e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 63990, "start": 651.18, "end": 655.9, "text": " What if the foundational atomic unit of computation isn't the data itself, but the event?", "tokens": [50929, 708, 498, 264, 32195, 22275, 4985, 295, 24903, 1943, 380, 264, 1412, 2564, 11, 457, 264, 2280, 30, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16387202134772913, "compression_ratio": 1.6342857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.8982163930980622e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 63990, "start": 656.34, "end": 656.72, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51187, 1079, 13, 51206], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16387202134772913, "compression_ratio": 1.6342857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.8982163930980622e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 65672, "start": 656.72, "end": 665.28, "text": " And SpherePop's central thesis is honestly the most provocative claim in the entire trilogy. History is primary, state is derived.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 318, 6605, 38677, 311, 5777, 22288, 307, 6095, 264, 881, 47663, 3932, 294, 264, 2302, 34030, 13, 12486, 307, 6194, 11, 1785, 307, 18949, 13, 50793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12452351129972018, "compression_ratio": 1.6029962546816479, "no_speech_prob": 1.8908069554512963e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 65672, "start": 665.58, "end": 671.94, "text": " It's a massive paradigm shift, and to grasp what that actually means, we really have to look at the machinery of SpherePop.", "tokens": [50808, 467, 311, 257, 5994, 24709, 5513, 11, 293, 281, 21743, 437, 300, 767, 1355, 11, 321, 534, 362, 281, 574, 412, 264, 27302, 295, 318, 6605, 38677, 13, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12452351129972018, "compression_ratio": 1.6029962546816479, "no_speech_prob": 1.8908069554512963e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 65672, "start": 672.4200000000001, "end": 676.32, "text": " In this language, there are no variables in the traditional sense.", "tokens": [51150, 682, 341, 2856, 11, 456, 366, 572, 9102, 294, 264, 5164, 2020, 13, 51345], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12452351129972018, "compression_ratio": 1.6029962546816479, "no_speech_prob": 1.8908069554512963e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 65672, "start": 676.4, "end": 677.6800000000001, "text": " Wait, no variables at all?", "tokens": [51349, 3802, 11, 572, 9102, 412, 439, 30, 51413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12452351129972018, "compression_ratio": 1.6029962546816479, "no_speech_prob": 1.8908069554512963e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 65672, "start": 677.78, "end": 682.88, "text": " None. There are only four fundamental primitives, four verbs. The first is pop.", "tokens": [51418, 14492, 13, 821, 366, 787, 1451, 8088, 2886, 38970, 11, 1451, 30051, 13, 440, 700, 307, 1665, 13, 51673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12452351129972018, "compression_ratio": 1.6029962546816479, "no_speech_prob": 1.8908069554512963e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 68288, "start": 682.88, "end": 693.06, "text": " To pop is to select an option from a defined space of possibilities. When you make that selection, the entropy of the system strictly decreases because a choice has been finalized.", "tokens": [50365, 1407, 1665, 307, 281, 3048, 364, 3614, 490, 257, 7642, 1901, 295, 12178, 13, 1133, 291, 652, 300, 9450, 11, 264, 30867, 295, 264, 1185, 20792, 24108, 570, 257, 3922, 575, 668, 2572, 1602, 13, 50874], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10273682089412914, "compression_ratio": 1.5584415584415585, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735366568764286e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 68288, "start": 693.08, "end": 700.26, "text": " Okay, so you reach a fork in a maze, and you choose to walk down the left corridor. That physical commitment is a pop.", "tokens": [50875, 1033, 11, 370, 291, 2524, 257, 17716, 294, 257, 33032, 11, 293, 291, 2826, 281, 1792, 760, 264, 1411, 25602, 13, 663, 4001, 8371, 307, 257, 1665, 13, 51234], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10273682089412914, "compression_ratio": 1.5584415584415585, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735366568764286e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 68288, "start": 700.52, "end": 703.56, "text": " That's a great analogy, yes. The second primitive is refuse.", "tokens": [51247, 663, 311, 257, 869, 21663, 11, 2086, 13, 440, 1150, 28540, 307, 16791, 13, 51399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10273682089412914, "compression_ratio": 1.5584415584415585, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735366568764286e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 70356, "start": 703.56, "end": 712.5999999999999, "text": " Geometrically, refuse is identical to pop. It is a choice made at a junction, but semantically, it is marked as a rejection rather than a selection.", "tokens": [50365, 2876, 649, 81, 984, 11, 16791, 307, 14800, 281, 1665, 13, 467, 307, 257, 3922, 1027, 412, 257, 33718, 11, 457, 4361, 49505, 11, 309, 307, 12658, 382, 257, 26044, 2831, 813, 257, 9450, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12542293772977942, "compression_ratio": 1.5947136563876652, "no_speech_prob": 2.0599518184977184e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 70356, "start": 712.9, "end": 714.38, "text": " How is that different from normal code?", "tokens": [50832, 1012, 307, 300, 819, 490, 2710, 3089, 30, 50906], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12542293772977942, "compression_ratio": 1.5947136563876652, "no_speech_prob": 2.0599518184977184e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 70356, "start": 714.64, "end": 726.9, "text": " While most modern languages do not recognize refusal as a distinct causal action, if an if statement evaluates to false, the language just silently skips that block of code.", "tokens": [50919, 3987, 881, 4363, 8650, 360, 406, 5521, 48948, 382, 257, 10644, 38755, 3069, 11, 498, 364, 498, 5629, 6133, 1024, 281, 7908, 11, 264, 2856, 445, 40087, 1110, 2600, 300, 3461, 295, 3089, 13, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12542293772977942, "compression_ratio": 1.5947136563876652, "no_speech_prob": 2.0599518184977184e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 72690, "start": 726.9, "end": 734.4599999999999, "text": " SpherePop argues that actively rejecting a path is a profound causal event that must be structurally recorded in the history.", "tokens": [50365, 318, 6605, 38677, 38218, 300, 13022, 45401, 257, 3100, 307, 257, 14382, 38755, 2280, 300, 1633, 312, 6594, 6512, 8287, 294, 264, 2503, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11999247047338593, "compression_ratio": 1.5965665236051503, "no_speech_prob": 1.383355778018791e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 72690, "start": 734.4599999999999, "end": 746.9399999999999, "text": " Okay, so pop is, I am walking down the left corridor. Refuse is, I tested the right corridor, I found a locked door, and I am permanently carving a warning into the map, so history remembers this path failed.", "tokens": [50743, 1033, 11, 370, 1665, 307, 11, 286, 669, 4494, 760, 264, 1411, 25602, 13, 16957, 438, 307, 11, 286, 8246, 264, 558, 25602, 11, 286, 1352, 257, 9376, 2853, 11, 293, 286, 669, 24042, 31872, 257, 9164, 666, 264, 4471, 11, 370, 2503, 26228, 341, 3100, 7612, 13, 51367], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11999247047338593, "compression_ratio": 1.5965665236051503, "no_speech_prob": 1.383355778018791e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 72690, "start": 747.12, "end": 749.04, "text": " Exactly. The map retains the failure.", "tokens": [51376, 7587, 13, 440, 4471, 1533, 2315, 264, 7763, 13, 51472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11999247047338593, "compression_ratio": 1.5965665236051503, "no_speech_prob": 1.383355778018791e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 74904, "start": 749.04, "end": 758.9, "text": " The third primitive is bind. Binding is the act of narrowing the admissible future continuations without actually committing to a choice just yet. It imposes a construct.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2636, 28540, 307, 14786, 13, 363, 9245, 307, 264, 605, 295, 9432, 278, 264, 5910, 41073, 2027, 2993, 763, 1553, 767, 26659, 281, 257, 3922, 445, 1939, 13, 467, 704, 4201, 257, 7690, 13, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07412332646987017, "compression_ratio": 1.5940959409594095, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942088586058055e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 74904, "start": 758.98, "end": 765.64, "text": " So you haven't taken a step yet, but you've drawn a boundary on the map and said, from this point forward, we will only consider paths that lead uphill.", "tokens": [50862, 407, 291, 2378, 380, 2726, 257, 1823, 1939, 11, 457, 291, 600, 10117, 257, 12866, 322, 264, 4471, 293, 848, 11, 490, 341, 935, 2128, 11, 321, 486, 787, 1949, 14518, 300, 1477, 39132, 13, 51195], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07412332646987017, "compression_ratio": 1.5940959409594095, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942088586058055e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 74904, "start": 765.76, "end": 771.16, "text": " Perfect, yes. And finally, the fourth primitive, and actually the namesake of the second essay, is collapse.", "tokens": [51201, 10246, 11, 2086, 13, 400, 2721, 11, 264, 6409, 28540, 11, 293, 767, 264, 5288, 619, 295, 264, 1150, 16238, 11, 307, 15584, 13, 51471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07412332646987017, "compression_ratio": 1.5940959409594095, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942088586058055e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 77116, "start": 771.16, "end": 782.02, "text": " Collapse is the operation that takes this massive accumulating ledger of pops, refusals, and binds, and projects it onto an observable present state.", "tokens": [50365, 4586, 11145, 307, 264, 6916, 300, 2516, 341, 5994, 12989, 12162, 4684, 1321, 295, 16795, 11, 1895, 301, 1124, 11, 293, 41515, 11, 293, 4455, 309, 3911, 364, 9951, 712, 1974, 1785, 13, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058983453429571474, "compression_ratio": 1.6179775280898876, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688888548361703e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 77116, "start": 782.5, "end": 788.24, "text": " And crucially, the act of collapsing irreversibly destroys the historical provenance of how that state was reached.", "tokens": [50932, 400, 5140, 1909, 11, 264, 605, 295, 45339, 16014, 840, 3545, 36714, 264, 8584, 12785, 719, 295, 577, 300, 1785, 390, 6488, 13, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058983453429571474, "compression_ratio": 1.6179775280898876, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688888548361703e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 77116, "start": 788.42, "end": 795.6, "text": " Okay, let me make sure I have this. Standard programming languages, the ones running our phones, our banks, our cars, they are like a teacher writing on a blackboard.", "tokens": [51228, 1033, 11, 718, 385, 652, 988, 286, 362, 341, 13, 21298, 9410, 8650, 11, 264, 2306, 2614, 527, 10216, 11, 527, 10237, 11, 527, 5163, 11, 436, 366, 411, 257, 5027, 3579, 322, 257, 2211, 3787, 13, 51587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058983453429571474, "compression_ratio": 1.6179775280898876, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688888548361703e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 79560, "start": 795.6, "end": 802.12, "text": " You write the number five. Then the program tells you to add three. So you take an eraser, wipe away the five, and write an eight.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 2464, 264, 1230, 1732, 13, 1396, 264, 1461, 5112, 291, 281, 909, 1045, 13, 407, 291, 747, 364, 46018, 11, 14082, 1314, 264, 1732, 11, 293, 2464, 364, 3180, 13, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09204713445510307, "compression_ratio": 1.7843137254901962, "no_speech_prob": 1.748719658661857e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 79560, "start": 802.24, "end": 802.44, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50697, 1779, 13, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09204713445510307, "compression_ratio": 1.7843137254901962, "no_speech_prob": 1.748719658661857e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 79560, "start": 802.66, "end": 809.34, "text": " You only ever possess the current snapshot. The history of how you arrived at eight is literally chalk dust on the floor.", "tokens": [50718, 509, 787, 1562, 17490, 264, 2190, 30163, 13, 440, 2503, 295, 577, 291, 6678, 412, 3180, 307, 3736, 28660, 8634, 322, 264, 4123, 13, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09204713445510307, "compression_ratio": 1.7843137254901962, "no_speech_prob": 1.748719658661857e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 79560, "start": 810.02, "end": 817.82, "text": " But Searpop is an accountant's ledger written in permanent ink. You never erase. You write initialized at five. The next line says added three.", "tokens": [51086, 583, 1100, 6529, 404, 307, 364, 43898, 311, 4684, 1321, 3720, 294, 10996, 11276, 13, 509, 1128, 23525, 13, 509, 2464, 5883, 1602, 412, 1732, 13, 440, 958, 1622, 1619, 3869, 1045, 13, 51476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09204713445510307, "compression_ratio": 1.7843137254901962, "no_speech_prob": 1.748719658661857e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 79560, "start": 818.0400000000001, "end": 824.6800000000001, "text": " If you want to know the current value, you must read the entire ledger and tally it up. That act of tallying up the history to get a snapshot.", "tokens": [51487, 759, 291, 528, 281, 458, 264, 2190, 2158, 11, 291, 1633, 1401, 264, 2302, 4684, 1321, 293, 256, 379, 309, 493, 13, 663, 605, 295, 256, 379, 278, 493, 264, 2503, 281, 483, 257, 30163, 13, 51819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09204713445510307, "compression_ratio": 1.7843137254901962, "no_speech_prob": 1.748719658661857e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 82560, "start": 825.6, "end": 826.44, "text": " That is collapse.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 15584, 13, 50407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12256600189208984, "compression_ratio": 1.5755627009646302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310935028503558e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 82560, "start": 826.62, "end": 832.82, "text": " That is a phenomenal analogy. And Flickshan provides a concrete example in the text to demonstrate the elegance of this.", "tokens": [50416, 663, 307, 257, 17778, 21663, 13, 400, 3235, 618, 2716, 282, 6417, 257, 9859, 1365, 294, 264, 2487, 281, 11698, 264, 14459, 719, 295, 341, 13, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12256600189208984, "compression_ratio": 1.5755627009646302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310935028503558e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 82560, "start": 833.22, "end": 838.96, "text": " Imagine a simple task. You have a list of numbers, and you want to find the sum of only the positive ones.", "tokens": [50746, 11739, 257, 2199, 5633, 13, 509, 362, 257, 1329, 295, 3547, 11, 293, 291, 528, 281, 915, 264, 2408, 295, 787, 264, 3353, 2306, 13, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12256600189208984, "compression_ratio": 1.5755627009646302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310935028503558e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 82560, "start": 839.28, "end": 840.46, "text": " Okay, sounds simple enough.", "tokens": [51049, 1033, 11, 3263, 2199, 1547, 13, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12256600189208984, "compression_ratio": 1.5755627009646302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310935028503558e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 82560, "start": 840.46, "end": 848.5, "text": " In a language like Python, it's a relatively clean generator expression. In C++A, you have to wade right back into the kitchen sink.", "tokens": [51108, 682, 257, 2856, 411, 15329, 11, 309, 311, 257, 7226, 2541, 19265, 6114, 13, 682, 383, 25472, 32, 11, 291, 362, 281, 261, 762, 558, 646, 666, 264, 6525, 9500, 13, 51510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12256600189208984, "compression_ratio": 1.5755627009646302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310935028503558e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 82560, "start": 849.1, "end": 853.76, "text": " Do you use a raw for loop? Do you use the accumulate function with a custom lambda?", "tokens": [51540, 1144, 291, 764, 257, 8936, 337, 6367, 30, 1144, 291, 764, 264, 33384, 2445, 365, 257, 2375, 13607, 30, 51773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12256600189208984, "compression_ratio": 1.5755627009646302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310935028503558e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 85376, "start": 853.76, "end": 861.36, "text": " Do you use the newer ranges library? Each choice carries immense historical baggage regarding memory allocation and iteration rules.", "tokens": [50365, 1144, 291, 764, 264, 17628, 22526, 6405, 30, 6947, 3922, 16402, 22920, 8584, 41567, 8595, 4675, 27599, 293, 24784, 4474, 13, 50745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11042549361043902, "compression_ratio": 1.441025641025641, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431019092723708e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 85376, "start": 861.6, "end": 865.62, "text": " But in Searpop, you don't even have a loop keyword, right? You don't have a nif statement.", "tokens": [50757, 583, 294, 1100, 6529, 404, 11, 291, 500, 380, 754, 362, 257, 6367, 20428, 11, 558, 30, 509, 500, 380, 362, 257, 297, 351, 5629, 13, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11042549361043902, "compression_ratio": 1.441025641025641, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431019092723708e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 85376, "start": 865.92, "end": 868.96, "text": " So how do you build a program without basic control flow?", "tokens": [50973, 407, 577, 360, 291, 1322, 257, 1461, 1553, 3875, 1969, 3095, 30, 51125], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11042549361043902, "compression_ratio": 1.441025641025641, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431019092723708e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 86896, "start": 868.96, "end": 877.22, "text": " You build it purely through the composition of those four primitives. You use a bind to filter the list, establishing the constraint that only positive numbers are admissible.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 1322, 309, 17491, 807, 264, 12686, 295, 729, 1451, 2886, 38970, 13, 509, 764, 257, 14786, 281, 6608, 264, 1329, 11, 22494, 264, 25534, 300, 787, 3353, 3547, 366, 5910, 41073, 13, 50778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10106091866126428, "compression_ratio": 1.6030927835051547, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363601012397977e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 86896, "start": 877.6, "end": 884.9000000000001, "text": " Then you iterate through the elements, using pop to include them in the running history, or refuse if they violate the bind constraint.", "tokens": [50797, 1396, 291, 44497, 807, 264, 4959, 11, 1228, 1665, 281, 4090, 552, 294, 264, 2614, 2503, 11, 420, 16791, 498, 436, 37478, 264, 14786, 25534, 13, 51162], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10106091866126428, "compression_ratio": 1.6030927835051547, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363601012397977e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 88490, "start": 884.9, "end": 894.9399999999999, "text": " Finally, you execute a collapse to yield the final sum. Filtering, iteration, branching logic, and accumulation are not separate language features.", "tokens": [50365, 6288, 11, 291, 14483, 257, 15584, 281, 11257, 264, 2572, 2408, 13, 7905, 34200, 11, 24784, 11, 9819, 278, 9952, 11, 293, 35647, 366, 406, 4994, 2856, 4122, 13, 50867], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13050384322802225, "compression_ratio": 1.4088050314465408, "no_speech_prob": 1.5430971387828119e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 88490, "start": 895.36, "end": 899.22, "text": " They are just different geometric arrangements of the exact same four verbs.", "tokens": [50888, 814, 366, 445, 819, 33246, 22435, 295, 264, 1900, 912, 1451, 30051, 13, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13050384322802225, "compression_ratio": 1.4088050314465408, "no_speech_prob": 1.5430971387828119e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 89922, "start": 899.22, "end": 905.88, "text": " So an if statement is just a pop over two options where you select one and refuse the other. That is honestly mind-bending.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 364, 498, 5629, 307, 445, 257, 1665, 670, 732, 3956, 689, 291, 3048, 472, 293, 16791, 264, 661, 13, 663, 307, 6095, 1575, 12, 65, 2029, 13, 50698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.128698449976304, "compression_ratio": 1.5373831775700935, "no_speech_prob": 1.635960681159454e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 89922, "start": 906.72, "end": 914.32, "text": " But there is a reason fliction insists on this ledger-based reality, and it ties back to the actual physical laws of the universe, right?", "tokens": [50740, 583, 456, 307, 257, 1778, 932, 4105, 50137, 322, 341, 4684, 1321, 12, 6032, 4103, 11, 293, 309, 14039, 646, 281, 264, 3539, 4001, 6064, 295, 264, 6445, 11, 558, 30, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.128698449976304, "compression_ratio": 1.5373831775700935, "no_speech_prob": 1.635960681159454e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 89922, "start": 914.72, "end": 916.72, "text": " The text brings up Landauer's principle.", "tokens": [51140, 440, 2487, 5607, 493, 6607, 18120, 311, 8665, 13, 51240], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.128698449976304, "compression_ratio": 1.5373831775700935, "no_speech_prob": 1.635960681159454e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 89922, "start": 916.9200000000001, "end": 917.94, "text": " Yes, Landauer's principle.", "tokens": [51250, 1079, 11, 6607, 18120, 311, 8665, 13, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.128698449976304, "compression_ratio": 1.5373831775700935, "no_speech_prob": 1.635960681159454e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 91794, "start": 917.94, "end": 935.32, "text": " So you cannot destroy information for free.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 291, 2644, 5293, 1589, 337, 1737, 13, 51234], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.515975554784139, "compression_ratio": 0.8775510204081632, "no_speech_prob": 1.67475679591772e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 93532, "start": 935.32, "end": 945.94, "text": " Exactly. When you write x equals 5 in standard code, and then on the next line you write x equals 9, the programming language act as if that 5 just magically vanished into the ether.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 1133, 291, 2464, 2031, 6915, 1025, 294, 3832, 3089, 11, 293, 550, 322, 264, 958, 1622, 291, 2464, 2031, 6915, 1722, 11, 264, 9410, 2856, 605, 382, 498, 300, 1025, 445, 39763, 37518, 666, 264, 37096, 13, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09303686929785687, "compression_ratio": 1.611336032388664, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832580894051487e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 93532, "start": 946.46, "end": 948.74, "text": " It pretends erasure is a costless event.", "tokens": [50922, 467, 1162, 2581, 1189, 2508, 307, 257, 2063, 1832, 2280, 13, 51036], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09303686929785687, "compression_ratio": 1.611336032388664, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832580894051487e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 93532, "start": 949.12, "end": 952.4000000000001, "text": " But physics demands a toll. The heat must be dissipated.", "tokens": [51055, 583, 10649, 15107, 257, 16629, 13, 440, 3738, 1633, 312, 29544, 770, 13, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09303686929785687, "compression_ratio": 1.611336032388664, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832580894051487e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 93532, "start": 952.8000000000001, "end": 958.84, "text": " Conventional languages basically construct a towering philosophical lie by pretending erasure is free and reversible.", "tokens": [51239, 26793, 304, 8650, 1936, 7690, 257, 10567, 278, 25066, 4544, 538, 22106, 1189, 2508, 307, 1737, 293, 44788, 13, 51541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09303686929785687, "compression_ratio": 1.611336032388664, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832580894051487e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 95884, "start": 958.84, "end": 962.14, "text": " SpherePop refuses to participate in that lie.", "tokens": [50365, 318, 6605, 38677, 33222, 281, 8197, 294, 300, 4544, 13, 50530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1639863650004069, "compression_ratio": 1.5545454545454545, "no_speech_prob": 2.262409010134192e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 95884, "start": 962.8000000000001, "end": 966.26, "text": " It aligns its software architecture with the physical architecture of the universe.", "tokens": [50563, 467, 7975, 82, 1080, 4722, 9482, 365, 264, 4001, 9482, 295, 264, 6445, 13, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1639863650004069, "compression_ratio": 1.5545454545454545, "no_speech_prob": 2.262409010134192e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 95884, "start": 967.0400000000001, "end": 973.46, "text": " Every choice decreases entropy, and that physical reality must be explicitly accounted for in the system's history.", "tokens": [50775, 2048, 3922, 24108, 30867, 11, 293, 300, 4001, 4103, 1633, 312, 20803, 43138, 337, 294, 264, 1185, 311, 2503, 13, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1639863650004069, "compression_ratio": 1.5545454545454545, "no_speech_prob": 2.262409010134192e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 95884, "start": 973.62, "end": 979.1800000000001, "text": " Just imagine the friction we would experience if every digital tool we used functioned this way.", "tokens": [51104, 1449, 3811, 264, 17710, 321, 576, 1752, 498, 633, 4562, 2290, 321, 1143, 2445, 292, 341, 636, 13, 51382], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1639863650004069, "compression_ratio": 1.5545454545454545, "no_speech_prob": 2.262409010134192e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 97918, "start": 979.18, "end": 989.64, "text": " Like, imagine if Microsoft's Word didn't just save the final draft of your essay, but permanently encoded every single typo, every backspace, every frantic copy and paste at 2am,", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 11, 3811, 498, 8116, 311, 8725, 994, 380, 445, 3155, 264, 2572, 11206, 295, 428, 16238, 11, 457, 24042, 2058, 12340, 633, 2167, 2125, 78, 11, 633, 646, 24824, 11, 633, 431, 7128, 5055, 293, 9163, 412, 568, 335, 11, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07468437353769938, "compression_ratio": 1.638157894736842, "no_speech_prob": 2.2624326457415522e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 97918, "start": 990.16, "end": 997.8599999999999, "text": " treating the entire chaotic history as the primary reality of the document, and the final readable text as merely a temporary collapse.", "tokens": [50914, 15083, 264, 2302, 27013, 2503, 382, 264, 6194, 4103, 295, 264, 4166, 11, 293, 264, 2572, 49857, 2487, 382, 17003, 257, 13413, 15584, 13, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07468437353769938, "compression_ratio": 1.638157894736842, "no_speech_prob": 2.2624326457415522e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 97918, "start": 998.0799999999999, "end": 1004.3, "text": " You wouldn't have to imagine it, actually, because as esoteric as SpherePop sounds, Fliction points out a devastating irony here.", "tokens": [51310, 509, 2759, 380, 362, 281, 3811, 309, 11, 767, 11, 570, 382, 785, 21585, 299, 382, 318, 6605, 38677, 3263, 11, 3235, 4105, 2793, 484, 257, 21280, 35365, 510, 13, 51621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07468437353769938, "compression_ratio": 1.638157894736842, "no_speech_prob": 2.2624326457415522e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 97918, "start": 1004.5799999999999, "end": 1006.66, "text": " We are already living in a SpherePop reality.", "tokens": [51635, 492, 366, 1217, 2647, 294, 257, 318, 6605, 38677, 4103, 13, 51739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07468437353769938, "compression_ratio": 1.638157894736842, "no_speech_prob": 2.2624326457415522e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 97918, "start": 1006.88, "end": 1007.16, "text": " Really?", "tokens": [51750, 4083, 30, 51764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07468437353769938, "compression_ratio": 1.638157894736842, "no_speech_prob": 2.2624326457415522e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 100716, "start": 1007.16, "end": 1009.6999999999999, "text": " Every major software system already does this.", "tokens": [50365, 2048, 2563, 4722, 1185, 1217, 775, 341, 13, 50492], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12194951664317738, "compression_ratio": 1.598705501618123, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234913803939155e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 100716, "start": 1009.8, "end": 1011.8199999999999, "text": " They just lack the vocabulary to admit it.", "tokens": [50497, 814, 445, 5011, 264, 19864, 281, 9796, 309, 13, 50598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12194951664317738, "compression_ratio": 1.598705501618123, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234913803939155e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 100716, "start": 1012.0, "end": 1013.3399999999999, "text": " Here's where it gets really interesting.", "tokens": [50607, 1692, 311, 689, 309, 2170, 534, 1880, 13, 50674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12194951664317738, "compression_ratio": 1.598705501618123, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234913803939155e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 100716, "start": 1014.0, "end": 1019.38, "text": " The concept of collapse is happening millions of times a second on the device you are holding right now.", "tokens": [50707, 440, 3410, 295, 15584, 307, 2737, 6803, 295, 1413, 257, 1150, 322, 264, 4302, 291, 366, 5061, 558, 586, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12194951664317738, "compression_ratio": 1.598705501618123, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234913803939155e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 100716, "start": 1020.18, "end": 1027.82, "text": " Fliction notes that rendering a user interface like drawing the pixels of an app on your screen is a massive collapse.", "tokens": [51016, 3235, 4105, 5570, 300, 22407, 257, 4195, 9226, 411, 6316, 264, 18668, 295, 364, 724, 322, 428, 2568, 307, 257, 5994, 15584, 13, 51398], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12194951664317738, "compression_ratio": 1.598705501618123, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234913803939155e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 100716, "start": 1028.0, "end": 1028.98, "text": " Yeah, think about it.", "tokens": [51407, 865, 11, 519, 466, 309, 13, 51456], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12194951664317738, "compression_ratio": 1.598705501618123, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234913803939155e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 100716, "start": 1029.24, "end": 1035.5, "text": " The application has a complex, continuous history of network responses, background threads, and user mouse movements.", "tokens": [51469, 440, 3861, 575, 257, 3997, 11, 10957, 2503, 295, 3209, 13019, 11, 3678, 19314, 11, 293, 4195, 9719, 9981, 13, 51782], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12194951664317738, "compression_ratio": 1.598705501618123, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234913803939155e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 103550, "start": 1035.5, "end": 1039.88, "text": " But a monitor can only display a single static frame at a time.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 257, 6002, 393, 787, 4674, 257, 2167, 13437, 3920, 412, 257, 565, 13, 50584], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19365609775890003, "compression_ratio": 0.9722222222222222, "no_speech_prob": 2.076441232498616e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 103550, "start": 1040.08, "end": 1040.24, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50594, 1779, 13, 50602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19365609775890003, "compression_ratio": 0.9722222222222222, "no_speech_prob": 2.076441232498616e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 104024, "start": 1040.24, "end": 1046.26, "text": " The system must collapse all that rich, chaotic history into a single 2D grid of colored pixels.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1185, 1633, 15584, 439, 300, 4593, 11, 27013, 2503, 666, 257, 2167, 568, 35, 10748, 295, 14332, 18668, 13, 50666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07766881231534278, "compression_ratio": 1.667785234899329, "no_speech_prob": 1.513266074948394e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 104024, "start": 1046.7, "end": 1053.58, "text": " And the instant the next frame is drawn, 16 milliseconds later, the causality of the previous frame is thrown into the incinerator.", "tokens": [50688, 400, 264, 9836, 264, 958, 3920, 307, 10117, 11, 3165, 34184, 1780, 11, 264, 3302, 1860, 295, 264, 3894, 3920, 307, 11732, 666, 264, 834, 4564, 1639, 13, 51032], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07766881231534278, "compression_ratio": 1.667785234899329, "no_speech_prob": 1.513266074948394e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 104024, "start": 1053.66, "end": 1053.94, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51036, 3153, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07766881231534278, "compression_ratio": 1.667785234899329, "no_speech_prob": 1.513266074948394e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 104024, "start": 1054.3, "end": 1056.82, "text": " And serializing an object to a database is a collapse.", "tokens": [51068, 400, 17436, 3319, 364, 2657, 281, 257, 8149, 307, 257, 15584, 13, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07766881231534278, "compression_ratio": 1.667785234899329, "no_speech_prob": 1.513266074948394e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 104024, "start": 1057.16, "end": 1058.84, "text": " Executing a search query is a collapse.", "tokens": [51211, 17662, 10861, 257, 3164, 14581, 307, 257, 15584, 13, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07766881231534278, "compression_ratio": 1.667785234899329, "no_speech_prob": 1.513266074948394e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 104024, "start": 1059.22, "end": 1067.44, "text": " The search results you see are just a snapshot valid for the exact microsecond the database calculated them, derived from a continuously mutating ledger of global data.", "tokens": [51314, 440, 3164, 3542, 291, 536, 366, 445, 257, 30163, 7363, 337, 264, 1900, 3123, 37841, 18882, 264, 8149, 15598, 552, 11, 18949, 490, 257, 15684, 5839, 990, 4684, 1321, 295, 4338, 1412, 13, 51725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07766881231534278, "compression_ratio": 1.667785234899329, "no_speech_prob": 1.513266074948394e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 106744, "start": 1067.44, "end": 1075.26, "text": " The fact that state primitive languages throw away history by default is the root cause of almost all modern software engineering misery.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1186, 300, 1785, 28540, 8650, 3507, 1314, 2503, 538, 7576, 307, 264, 5593, 3082, 295, 1920, 439, 4363, 4722, 7043, 32309, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11031206846237182, "compression_ratio": 1.5654008438818565, "no_speech_prob": 1.694759567058557e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 106744, "start": 1076.1000000000001, "end": 1085.98, "text": " It causes aliasing bugs where two different parts of a program are staring at the same mutable piece of data, both trying to change it, completely unaware of the other's history.", "tokens": [50798, 467, 7700, 10198, 3349, 15120, 689, 732, 819, 3166, 295, 257, 1461, 366, 18043, 412, 264, 912, 5839, 712, 2522, 295, 1412, 11, 1293, 1382, 281, 1319, 309, 11, 2584, 32065, 295, 264, 661, 311, 2503, 13, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11031206846237182, "compression_ratio": 1.5654008438818565, "no_speech_prob": 1.694759567058557e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 106744, "start": 1086.18, "end": 1088.3, "text": " That's exactly why multithreading is such a nightmare.", "tokens": [51302, 663, 311, 2293, 983, 2120, 355, 35908, 307, 1270, 257, 18724, 13, 51408], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11031206846237182, "compression_ratio": 1.5654008438818565, "no_speech_prob": 1.694759567058557e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 108830, "start": 1088.3, "end": 1096.76, "text": " Yes. Leslie Lamport, a Turing Award winner, proved decades ago that events in a distributed system form a partial order of history.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 28140, 441, 1215, 477, 11, 257, 314, 1345, 13894, 8507, 11, 14617, 7878, 2057, 300, 3931, 294, 257, 12631, 1185, 1254, 257, 14641, 1668, 295, 2503, 13, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06900762376331147, "compression_ratio": 1.5308641975308641, "no_speech_prob": 2.2539563531570606e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 108830, "start": 1097.34, "end": 1099.98, "text": " They do not form a single objective shared state.", "tokens": [50817, 814, 360, 406, 1254, 257, 2167, 10024, 5507, 1785, 13, 50949], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06900762376331147, "compression_ratio": 1.5308641975308641, "no_speech_prob": 2.2539563531570606e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 108830, "start": 1100.34, "end": 1112.48, "text": " But because our languages force us to use shared state, we have to invent incredibly fragile, complex locking mechanisms like mutexes and semaphores to stop threads from corrupting the data.", "tokens": [50967, 583, 570, 527, 8650, 3464, 505, 281, 764, 5507, 1785, 11, 321, 362, 281, 7962, 6252, 23847, 11, 3997, 23954, 15902, 411, 24523, 47047, 293, 4361, 13957, 2706, 281, 1590, 19314, 490, 17366, 278, 264, 1412, 13, 51574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06900762376331147, "compression_ratio": 1.5308641975308641, "no_speech_prob": 2.2539563531570606e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 111248, "start": 1112.48, "end": 1116.6200000000001, "text": " We spent half our engineering time building barricades to protect the lie of a shared present.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 4418, 1922, 527, 7043, 565, 2390, 2159, 1341, 2977, 281, 2371, 264, 4544, 295, 257, 5507, 1974, 13, 50572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12993411013954564, "compression_ratio": 1.6033898305084746, "no_speech_prob": 2.6873097930951717e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 111248, "start": 1116.94, "end": 1117.38, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50588, 7587, 13, 50610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12993411013954564, "compression_ratio": 1.6033898305084746, "no_speech_prob": 2.6873097930951717e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 111248, "start": 1117.76, "end": 1121.0, "text": " And this leads to the most painfully accurate insight in the first essay.", "tokens": [50629, 400, 341, 6689, 281, 264, 881, 1822, 2277, 8559, 11269, 294, 264, 700, 16238, 13, 50791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12993411013954564, "compression_ratio": 1.6033898305084746, "no_speech_prob": 2.6873097930951717e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 111248, "start": 1121.92, "end": 1123.28, "text": " Debugging is archaeology.", "tokens": [50837, 27347, 697, 3249, 307, 21894, 1793, 13, 50905], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12993411013954564, "compression_ratio": 1.6033898305084746, "no_speech_prob": 2.6873097930951717e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 111248, "start": 1123.8600000000001, "end": 1125.96, "text": " Think about what happens when an app crashes on your phone.", "tokens": [50934, 6557, 466, 437, 2314, 562, 364, 724, 28642, 322, 428, 2593, 13, 51039], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12993411013954564, "compression_ratio": 1.6033898305084746, "no_speech_prob": 2.6873097930951717e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 111248, "start": 1126.7, "end": 1131.28, "text": " In a state primitive system, the application has intentionally discarded the causal path.", "tokens": [51076, 682, 257, 1785, 28540, 1185, 11, 264, 3861, 575, 22062, 45469, 264, 38755, 3100, 13, 51305], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12993411013954564, "compression_ratio": 1.6033898305084746, "no_speech_prob": 2.6873097930951717e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 111248, "start": 1131.6, "end": 1134.64, "text": " The program just halts and says, error, this variable is negative.", "tokens": [51321, 440, 1461, 445, 7523, 1373, 293, 1619, 11, 6713, 11, 341, 7006, 307, 3671, 13, 51473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12993411013954564, "compression_ratio": 1.6033898305084746, "no_speech_prob": 2.6873097930951717e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 111248, "start": 1135.0, "end": 1138.0, "text": " And the programmer asks, how did it become negative?", "tokens": [51491, 400, 264, 32116, 8962, 11, 577, 630, 309, 1813, 3671, 30, 51641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12993411013954564, "compression_ratio": 1.6033898305084746, "no_speech_prob": 2.6873097930951717e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 113800, "start": 1138.0, "end": 1144.1, "text": " Right. And the programmer replies, I have absolutely no idea. I am only aware of the current state of the universe.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 400, 264, 32116, 42289, 11, 286, 362, 3122, 572, 1558, 13, 286, 669, 787, 3650, 295, 264, 2190, 1785, 295, 264, 6445, 13, 50670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1375449543267908, "compression_ratio": 1.527363184079602, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619908574377895e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 113800, "start": 1144.3, "end": 1149.42, "text": " So what do programmers do? They build external, desperate systems to reconstruct the history.", "tokens": [50680, 407, 437, 360, 41504, 360, 30, 814, 1322, 8320, 11, 17601, 3652, 281, 31499, 264, 2503, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1375449543267908, "compression_ratio": 1.527363184079602, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619908574377895e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 113800, "start": 1149.76, "end": 1155.16, "text": " They write exhaustive log files. They build time travel debuggers. They pore over stacked traces.", "tokens": [50953, 814, 2464, 14687, 488, 3565, 7098, 13, 814, 1322, 565, 3147, 3001, 3562, 433, 13, 814, 41459, 670, 28867, 26076, 13, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1375449543267908, "compression_ratio": 1.527363184079602, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619908574377895e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 115516, "start": 1155.16, "end": 1169.8600000000001, "text": " They are essentially sifting through the dirt like archaeologists, trying to piece together a sequence of historical events from tiny, shattered fragments of pottery, entirely because the foundational language was designed to be amnesiac.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 366, 4476, 262, 10106, 807, 264, 11483, 411, 21894, 12256, 11, 1382, 281, 2522, 1214, 257, 8310, 295, 8584, 3931, 490, 5870, 11, 35209, 29197, 295, 45272, 11, 7696, 570, 264, 32195, 2856, 390, 4761, 281, 312, 669, 4081, 13921, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0840587564136671, "compression_ratio": 1.4691358024691359, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815741507580917e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 116986, "start": 1169.86, "end": 1185.1799999999998, "text": " I have to stop you there, though. Because if state primitive systems are this fundamentally broken, if they cause infinite bugs, demand complex locks, and require us to act like digital archaeologists just to fix a typo, why do they run the world?", "tokens": [50365, 286, 362, 281, 1590, 291, 456, 11, 1673, 13, 1436, 498, 1785, 28540, 3652, 366, 341, 17879, 5463, 11, 498, 436, 3082, 13785, 15120, 11, 4733, 3997, 20703, 11, 293, 3651, 505, 281, 605, 411, 4562, 21894, 12256, 445, 281, 3191, 257, 2125, 78, 11, 983, 360, 436, 1190, 264, 1002, 30, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0795095258829545, "compression_ratio": 1.5075187969924813, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832006487736307e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 116986, "start": 1185.32, "end": 1188.0, "text": " I mean, why aren't we all coding in SpherePop or Lisp?", "tokens": [51138, 286, 914, 11, 983, 3212, 380, 321, 439, 17720, 294, 318, 6605, 38677, 420, 441, 7631, 30, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0795095258829545, "compression_ratio": 1.5075187969924813, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832006487736307e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 116986, "start": 1188.6, "end": 1193.52, "text": " Capitalism ruthlessly optimizes for efficiency. If state was so inefficient, it wouldn't have won.", "tokens": [51302, 21502, 1434, 38225, 12048, 5028, 5660, 337, 10493, 13, 759, 1785, 390, 370, 43495, 11, 309, 2759, 380, 362, 1582, 13, 51548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0795095258829545, "compression_ratio": 1.5075187969924813, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832006487736307e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 119352, "start": 1193.52, "end": 1202.28, "text": " The tragedy, according to Flixion, is that state didn't actually win. Engineers under real-world pressure eventually realized that state was insufficient.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 18563, 11, 4650, 281, 3235, 970, 313, 11, 307, 300, 1785, 994, 380, 767, 1942, 13, 43950, 833, 957, 12, 13217, 3321, 4728, 5334, 300, 1785, 390, 41709, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11282923817634583, "compression_ratio": 1.583941605839416, "no_speech_prob": 1.7487630267487564e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 119352, "start": 1203.0, "end": 1209.06, "text": " So they spent the last 20 years frantically building history-first structures on top of state-first languages.", "tokens": [50839, 407, 436, 4418, 264, 1036, 945, 924, 431, 49505, 2390, 2503, 12, 29581, 9227, 322, 1192, 295, 1785, 12, 29581, 8650, 13, 51142], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11282923817634583, "compression_ratio": 1.583941605839416, "no_speech_prob": 1.7487630267487564e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 119352, "start": 1209.52, "end": 1211.24, "text": " The ultimate example of this is Git.", "tokens": [51165, 440, 9705, 1365, 295, 341, 307, 16939, 13, 51251], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11282923817634583, "compression_ratio": 1.583941605839416, "no_speech_prob": 1.7487630267487564e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 119352, "start": 1211.6399999999999, "end": 1219.2, "text": " Git is the perfect vindication of SpherePop. Git is the version control system used by virtually every software developer on Earth.", "tokens": [51271, 16939, 307, 264, 2176, 20168, 8758, 295, 318, 6605, 38677, 13, 16939, 307, 264, 3037, 1969, 1185, 1143, 538, 14103, 633, 4722, 10754, 322, 4755, 13, 51649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11282923817634583, "compression_ratio": 1.583941605839416, "no_speech_prob": 1.7487630267487564e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 121920, "start": 1219.2, "end": 1229.38, "text": " When you look at a project in Git, nobody believes that the files currently sitting in the folder, the working tree, represent the fundamental truth of the project.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 291, 574, 412, 257, 1716, 294, 16939, 11, 5079, 12307, 300, 264, 7098, 4362, 3798, 294, 264, 10820, 11, 264, 1364, 4230, 11, 2906, 264, 8088, 3494, 295, 264, 1716, 13, 50874], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1151678768205054, "compression_ratio": 1.5821596244131455, "no_speech_prob": 1.9506384354994744e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 121920, "start": 1229.5, "end": 1230.2, "text": " No, not at all.", "tokens": [50880, 883, 11, 406, 412, 439, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1151678768205054, "compression_ratio": 1.5821596244131455, "no_speech_prob": 1.9506384354994744e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 121920, "start": 1230.3400000000001, "end": 1232.64, "text": " The absolute truth is the commit history.", "tokens": [50922, 440, 8236, 3494, 307, 264, 5599, 2503, 13, 51037], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1151678768205054, "compression_ratio": 1.5821596244131455, "no_speech_prob": 1.9506384354994744e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 121920, "start": 1233.18, "end": 1240.68, "text": " The immutable, cryptographic ledger of every single line of code ever added, changed, or deleted by any developer.", "tokens": [51064, 440, 3397, 32148, 11, 9844, 12295, 4684, 1321, 295, 633, 2167, 1622, 295, 3089, 1562, 3869, 11, 3105, 11, 420, 22981, 538, 604, 10754, 13, 51439], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1151678768205054, "compression_ratio": 1.5821596244131455, "no_speech_prob": 1.9506384354994744e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 124068, "start": 1240.68, "end": 1245.3, "text": " The files you see on your screen are just a disposable, temporary collapse of that history.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 7098, 291, 536, 322, 428, 2568, 366, 445, 257, 41578, 11, 13413, 15584, 295, 300, 2503, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09071919087613567, "compression_ratio": 1.6095617529880477, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011312063858197e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 124068, "start": 1245.54, "end": 1252.3, "text": " You can delete your entire working folder, and as long as you have the hidden Git history folder, you can perfectly reconstruct the present.", "tokens": [50608, 509, 393, 12097, 428, 2302, 1364, 10820, 11, 293, 382, 938, 382, 291, 362, 264, 7633, 16939, 2503, 10820, 11, 291, 393, 6239, 31499, 264, 1974, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09071919087613567, "compression_ratio": 1.6095617529880477, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011312063858197e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 124068, "start": 1253.0, "end": 1260.04, "text": " Git is a history-native paradigm that developers were forced to build as an afterthought because their native languages couldn't track time.", "tokens": [50981, 16939, 307, 257, 2503, 12, 77, 1166, 24709, 300, 8849, 645, 7579, 281, 1322, 382, 364, 934, 43135, 570, 641, 8470, 8650, 2809, 380, 2837, 565, 13, 51333], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09071919087613567, "compression_ratio": 1.6095617529880477, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011312063858197e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 124068, "start": 1260.3, "end": 1262.48, "text": " And it extends far beyond Git.", "tokens": [51346, 400, 309, 26448, 1400, 4399, 16939, 13, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09071919087613567, "compression_ratio": 1.6095617529880477, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011312063858197e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 126248, "start": 1262.48, "end": 1275.14, "text": " Look at enterprise backend architecture, database write-ahead logs, event sourcing patterns where financial transactions are stored as an append-only log of events rather than updating a single balance column.", "tokens": [50365, 2053, 412, 14132, 38087, 9482, 11, 8149, 2464, 12, 545, 2056, 20820, 11, 2280, 11006, 2175, 8294, 689, 4669, 16856, 366, 12187, 382, 364, 34116, 12, 25202, 3565, 295, 3931, 2831, 813, 25113, 257, 2167, 4772, 7738, 13, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09270232457381028, "compression_ratio": 1.5770491803278688, "no_speech_prob": 1.818202706449501e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 126248, "start": 1275.88, "end": 1281.76, "text": " Consensus protocols like Paxos and Raft, which allow distributed servers to agree on a sequence of history.", "tokens": [51035, 6923, 10983, 20618, 411, 430, 2797, 329, 293, 7591, 844, 11, 597, 2089, 12631, 15909, 281, 3986, 322, 257, 8310, 295, 2503, 13, 51329], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09270232457381028, "compression_ratio": 1.5770491803278688, "no_speech_prob": 1.818202706449501e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 126248, "start": 1282.08, "end": 1291.08, "text": " These are all massive, billion-dollar systems built to implement the philosophy of SpherePop, bolted clumsily onto languages that fight them every step of the way.", "tokens": [51345, 1981, 366, 439, 5994, 11, 5218, 12, 40485, 3652, 3094, 281, 4445, 264, 10675, 295, 318, 6605, 38677, 11, 13436, 292, 596, 8099, 953, 3911, 8650, 300, 2092, 552, 633, 1823, 295, 264, 636, 13, 51795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09270232457381028, "compression_ratio": 1.5770491803278688, "no_speech_prob": 1.818202706449501e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 129108, "start": 1291.08, "end": 1296.6599999999999, "text": " Have you ever been writing a long email or a document, and you accidentally highlight the whole thing and hit delete?", "tokens": [50365, 3560, 291, 1562, 668, 3579, 257, 938, 3796, 420, 257, 4166, 11, 293, 291, 15715, 5078, 264, 1379, 551, 293, 2045, 12097, 30, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10060023409979683, "compression_ratio": 1.6333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.176289313690627e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 129108, "start": 1296.84, "end": 1298.3799999999999, "text": " Oh, the worst feeling.", "tokens": [50653, 876, 11, 264, 5855, 2633, 13, 50730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10060023409979683, "compression_ratio": 1.6333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.176289313690627e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 129108, "start": 1298.54, "end": 1305.9399999999998, "text": " The panic that sets in is so visceral, you immediately hit Command-Z, praying that the software retained the history of your keystrokes.", "tokens": [50738, 440, 14783, 300, 6352, 294, 307, 370, 1452, 47879, 11, 291, 4258, 2045, 17901, 12, 57, 11, 15611, 300, 264, 4722, 33438, 264, 2503, 295, 428, 2141, 27616, 5993, 13, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10060023409979683, "compression_ratio": 1.6333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.176289313690627e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 129108, "start": 1306.4199999999998, "end": 1312.54, "text": " That feeling of relief when the text reappears is the human nervous system demanding a history-primitive architecture.", "tokens": [51132, 663, 2633, 295, 10915, 562, 264, 2487, 35638, 68, 685, 307, 264, 1952, 6296, 1185, 19960, 257, 2503, 12, 1424, 332, 2187, 9482, 13, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10060023409979683, "compression_ratio": 1.6333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.176289313690627e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 129108, "start": 1313.1, "end": 1318.24, "text": " When disaster strikes, we inherently trust the historical ledger more than the current state.", "tokens": [51466, 1133, 11293, 16750, 11, 321, 27993, 3361, 264, 8584, 4684, 1321, 544, 813, 264, 2190, 1785, 13, 51723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10060023409979683, "compression_ratio": 1.6333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.176289313690627e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 131824, "start": 1318.24, "end": 1324.76, "text": " The problem with the ledger, however, is thermodynamics, which brings us to the fatal flaw of unbounded history.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1154, 365, 264, 4684, 1321, 11, 4461, 11, 307, 8810, 35483, 11, 597, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 24069, 13717, 295, 517, 18767, 292, 2503, 13, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10921806874482529, "compression_ratio": 1.564, "no_speech_prob": 2.7719510714563356e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 131824, "start": 1325.2, "end": 1333.38, "text": " Right. If you record every thermodynamic change, every mouse twitch, every microsecond of network latency, you will fill up the world's hard drives in an afternoon.", "tokens": [50713, 1779, 13, 759, 291, 2136, 633, 8810, 34988, 1319, 11, 633, 9719, 34167, 11, 633, 3123, 37841, 18882, 295, 3209, 27043, 11, 291, 486, 2836, 493, 264, 1002, 311, 1152, 11754, 294, 364, 6499, 13, 51122], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10921806874482529, "compression_ratio": 1.564, "no_speech_prob": 2.7719510714563356e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 131824, "start": 1333.88, "end": 1335.64, "text": " You cannot keep everything forever.", "tokens": [51147, 509, 2644, 1066, 1203, 5680, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10921806874482529, "compression_ratio": 1.564, "no_speech_prob": 2.7719510714563356e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 131824, "start": 1335.88, "end": 1340.16, "text": " Which seamlessly bridges us to the second essay, What Collapse Should Forget.", "tokens": [51247, 3013, 38083, 21114, 505, 281, 264, 1150, 16238, 11, 708, 4586, 11145, 6454, 18675, 13, 51461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10921806874482529, "compression_ratio": 1.564, "no_speech_prob": 2.7719510714563356e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 134016, "start": 1340.16, "end": 1348.3200000000002, "text": " Fliction realizes that the purest division of SpherePop, never deleting anything, is mathematically unjustifiable in reality.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 29316, 300, 264, 6075, 372, 10044, 295, 318, 6605, 38677, 11, 1128, 48946, 1340, 11, 307, 44003, 37046, 30876, 294, 4103, 13, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12440540022769217, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279107390385297e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 134016, "start": 1348.68, "end": 1356.92, "text": " The author concedes that unbounded history retention is only mathematically forced if you have absolutely no idea what questions the future will ask of you.", "tokens": [50791, 440, 3793, 416, 21526, 300, 517, 18767, 292, 2503, 22871, 307, 787, 44003, 7579, 498, 291, 362, 3122, 572, 1558, 437, 1651, 264, 2027, 486, 1029, 295, 291, 13, 51203], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12440540022769217, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279107390385297e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 135692, "start": 1356.92, "end": 1363.6000000000001, "text": " The text introduces a formal framework here. Rate distortion theory. This is basically the math of compression.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2487, 31472, 257, 9860, 8388, 510, 13, 49583, 28426, 5261, 13, 639, 307, 1936, 264, 5221, 295, 19355, 13, 50699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14813625812530518, "compression_ratio": 1.5026455026455026, "no_speech_prob": 1.8761509273240717e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 135692, "start": 1364.24, "end": 1372.6000000000001, "text": " If you have a massive, sprawling history and you are forced by physics or budget to compress it, how do you decide which bits to throw into the fire and which bits to save?", "tokens": [50731, 759, 291, 362, 257, 5994, 11, 22734, 1688, 2503, 293, 291, 366, 7579, 538, 10649, 420, 4706, 281, 14778, 309, 11, 577, 360, 291, 4536, 597, 9239, 281, 3507, 666, 264, 2610, 293, 597, 9239, 281, 3155, 30, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14813625812530518, "compression_ratio": 1.5026455026455026, "no_speech_prob": 1.8761509273240717e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 137260, "start": 1372.6, "end": 1380.28, "text": " You look at the future. You define a set called Q, the class of future queries. These are the questions the system will actually need to answer later.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 574, 412, 264, 2027, 13, 509, 6964, 257, 992, 1219, 1249, 11, 264, 1508, 295, 2027, 24109, 13, 1981, 366, 264, 1651, 264, 1185, 486, 767, 643, 281, 1867, 1780, 13, 50749], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09280292554335161, "compression_ratio": 1.6506024096385543, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783896763043147e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 137260, "start": 1380.76, "end": 1389.6, "text": " A compression of history is considered sufficient if and only if every future query in Q can still be answered with perfect accuracy using only the compressed state.", "tokens": [50773, 316, 19355, 295, 2503, 307, 4888, 11563, 498, 293, 787, 498, 633, 2027, 14581, 294, 1249, 393, 920, 312, 10103, 365, 2176, 14170, 1228, 787, 264, 30353, 1785, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09280292554335161, "compression_ratio": 1.6506024096385543, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783896763043147e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 137260, "start": 1389.9199999999998, "end": 1394.3999999999999, "text": " And this relies on a concept called sufficient statistics. Let's break this down for a second.", "tokens": [51231, 400, 341, 30910, 322, 257, 3410, 1219, 11563, 12523, 13, 961, 311, 1821, 341, 760, 337, 257, 1150, 13, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09280292554335161, "compression_ratio": 1.6506024096385543, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783896763043147e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 139440, "start": 1394.4, "end": 1400.52, "text": " If I'm tracking the temperatures in a city over a century, I have tens of thousands of daily data points.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 286, 478, 11603, 264, 12633, 294, 257, 2307, 670, 257, 4901, 11, 286, 362, 10688, 295, 5383, 295, 5212, 1412, 2793, 13, 50671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10801529687298231, "compression_ratio": 1.7210884353741496, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363736537669538e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 139440, "start": 1400.92, "end": 1400.96, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50691, 1779, 13, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10801529687298231, "compression_ratio": 1.7210884353741496, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363736537669538e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 139440, "start": 1401.3600000000001, "end": 1406.1200000000001, "text": " But if the only query the future will ever ask is, what was the all-time highest temperature?", "tokens": [50713, 583, 498, 264, 787, 14581, 264, 2027, 486, 1562, 1029, 307, 11, 437, 390, 264, 439, 12, 3766, 6343, 4292, 30, 50951], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10801529687298231, "compression_ratio": 1.7210884353741496, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363736537669538e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 139440, "start": 1406.8200000000002, "end": 1411.8200000000002, "text": " I don't need to save the history. I only need to save a single number, the running maximum.", "tokens": [50986, 286, 500, 380, 643, 281, 3155, 264, 2503, 13, 286, 787, 643, 281, 3155, 257, 2167, 1230, 11, 264, 2614, 6674, 13, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10801529687298231, "compression_ratio": 1.7210884353741496, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363736537669538e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 139440, "start": 1412.26, "end": 1418.8000000000002, "text": " As each new day comes in, I compare it to the maximum, update it if necessary, and permanently delete the daily record.", "tokens": [51258, 1018, 1184, 777, 786, 1487, 294, 11, 286, 6794, 309, 281, 264, 6674, 11, 5623, 309, 498, 4818, 11, 293, 24042, 12097, 264, 5212, 2136, 13, 51585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10801529687298231, "compression_ratio": 1.7210884353741496, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363736537669538e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 139440, "start": 1418.98, "end": 1423.94, "text": " Because that single number is the minimal sufficient statistic for that specific query.", "tokens": [51594, 1436, 300, 2167, 1230, 307, 264, 13206, 11563, 29588, 337, 300, 2685, 14581, 13, 51842], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10801529687298231, "compression_ratio": 1.7210884353741496, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363736537669538e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 142440, "start": 1424.4, "end": 1428.66, "text": " You can destroy a century of history and lose absolutely zero fidelity.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 393, 5293, 257, 4901, 295, 2503, 293, 3624, 3122, 4018, 46404, 13, 50578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1405012373830758, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.818372384089495e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 142440, "start": 1428.92, "end": 1435.7, "text": " This is a brilliant concession by Fliction because it admits that traditional languages like C++ aren't universally wrong.", "tokens": [50591, 639, 307, 257, 10248, 416, 29881, 538, 3235, 4105, 570, 309, 46682, 300, 5164, 8650, 411, 383, 25472, 3212, 380, 43995, 2085, 13, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1405012373830758, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.818372384089495e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 142440, "start": 1436.0800000000002, "end": 1437.3600000000001, "text": " They're just locally rational.", "tokens": [50949, 814, 434, 445, 16143, 15090, 13, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1405012373830758, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.818372384089495e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 142440, "start": 1437.5800000000002, "end": 1442.92, "text": " Exactly. Think about a standard loop counter variable, usually called I, in a simple C program.", "tokens": [51024, 7587, 13, 6557, 466, 257, 3832, 6367, 5682, 7006, 11, 2673, 1219, 286, 11, 294, 257, 2199, 383, 1461, 13, 51291], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1405012373830758, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.818372384089495e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 142440, "start": 1443.0800000000002, "end": 1447.88, "text": " It just counts from 1 to 100. That variable faces exactly one query from the system.", "tokens": [51299, 467, 445, 14893, 490, 502, 281, 2319, 13, 663, 7006, 8475, 2293, 472, 14581, 490, 264, 1185, 13, 51539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1405012373830758, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.818372384089495e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 142440, "start": 1448.3200000000002, "end": 1450.0600000000002, "text": " What is your current value right now?", "tokens": [51561, 708, 307, 428, 2190, 2158, 558, 586, 30, 51648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1405012373830758, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.818372384089495e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 145006, "start": 1450.06, "end": 1457.8999999999999, "text": " And for that highly restricted query, throwing away the entire history of previous values, is the mathematically flawless optimal compression.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 337, 300, 5405, 20608, 14581, 11, 10238, 1314, 264, 2302, 2503, 295, 3894, 4190, 11, 307, 264, 44003, 45693, 16252, 19355, 13, 50757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2156374113900321, "compression_ratio": 1.3421052631578947, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684881557968434e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 145006, "start": 1458.86, "end": 1463.52, "text": " C++ optimizes perfectly for the microscopic queries of a CPU.", "tokens": [50805, 383, 25472, 5028, 5660, 6239, 337, 264, 47897, 24109, 295, 257, 13199, 13, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2156374113900321, "compression_ratio": 1.3421052631578947, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684881557968434e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 146352, "start": 1463.52, "end": 1471.08, "text": " The essay introduces a mathematical dial to represent this trade-off, using the Lagrange multiplier, the Greek letter lambda.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 16238, 31472, 257, 18894, 5502, 281, 2906, 341, 4923, 12, 4506, 11, 1228, 264, 24886, 14521, 44106, 11, 264, 10281, 5063, 13607, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1616002768278122, "compression_ratio": 1.4974093264248705, "no_speech_prob": 2.051938046560009e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 146352, "start": 1471.78, "end": 1478.9, "text": " This dial balances the cost of storing data against the expected catastrophic cost of failing to answer a future query.", "tokens": [50778, 639, 5502, 33993, 264, 2063, 295, 26085, 1412, 1970, 264, 5176, 34915, 2063, 295, 18223, 281, 1867, 257, 2027, 14581, 13, 51134], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1616002768278122, "compression_ratio": 1.4974093264248705, "no_speech_prob": 2.051938046560009e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 146352, "start": 1479.32, "end": 1481.16, "text": " So let's look at the extremes of that dial.", "tokens": [51155, 407, 718, 311, 574, 412, 264, 41119, 295, 300, 5502, 13, 51247], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1616002768278122, "compression_ratio": 1.4974093264248705, "no_speech_prob": 2.051938046560009e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 148116, "start": 1481.16, "end": 1492.0400000000002, "text": " If storage space is functionally infinite and cheap, and the penalty for failing a query is catastrophic like a medical record or a legal chain of custody, lambda approaches zero.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 6725, 1901, 307, 2445, 379, 13785, 293, 7084, 11, 293, 264, 16263, 337, 18223, 257, 14581, 307, 34915, 411, 257, 4625, 2136, 420, 257, 5089, 5021, 295, 26976, 11, 13607, 11587, 4018, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0829236858031329, "compression_ratio": 1.4595959595959596, "no_speech_prob": 2.028037677029304e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 148116, "start": 1492.26, "end": 1497.68, "text": " Right. You compress nothing. You keep the raw, unbounded history. This is Git. This is the purest sphere pop.", "tokens": [50920, 1779, 13, 509, 14778, 1825, 13, 509, 1066, 264, 8936, 11, 517, 18767, 292, 2503, 13, 639, 307, 16939, 13, 639, 307, 264, 6075, 372, 16687, 1665, 13, 51191], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0829236858031329, "compression_ratio": 1.4595959595959596, "no_speech_prob": 2.028037677029304e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 149768, "start": 1497.68, "end": 1509.0, "text": " But if storage is highly constrained, and the penalty for forgetting is trivial like our loop counter, I, Lamanda, approaches infinity, you ruthlessly destroy the history and keep only the slimest possible state.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 6725, 307, 5405, 38901, 11, 293, 264, 16263, 337, 25428, 307, 26703, 411, 527, 6367, 5682, 11, 286, 11, 18825, 5575, 11, 11587, 13202, 11, 291, 38225, 12048, 5293, 264, 2503, 293, 1066, 787, 264, 25357, 377, 1944, 1785, 13, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08945532441139221, "compression_ratio": 1.5880149812734083, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381168781871234e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 149768, "start": 1509.1000000000001, "end": 1519.72, "text": " Fliction points out that researchers in artificial intelligence, specifically in reinforcement learning, arrived at this exact same mathematical truth independently, calling it the information bottleneck method.", "tokens": [50936, 3235, 4105, 2793, 484, 300, 10309, 294, 11677, 7599, 11, 4682, 294, 29280, 2539, 11, 6678, 412, 341, 1900, 912, 18894, 3494, 21761, 11, 5141, 309, 264, 1589, 44641, 547, 3170, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08945532441139221, "compression_ratio": 1.5880149812734083, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381168781871234e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 151972, "start": 1519.72, "end": 1520.72, "text": " Oh, interesting.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 1880, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1523535182175127, "compression_ratio": 1.6076388888888888, "no_speech_prob": 2.07643949777514e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 151972, "start": 1521.04, "end": 1530.92, "text": " When an AI agent is trying to navigate a complex environment, it cannot memorize every pixel of every frame it ever saw. It has to abstract the state.", "tokens": [50431, 1133, 364, 7318, 9461, 307, 1382, 281, 12350, 257, 3997, 2823, 11, 309, 2644, 27478, 633, 19261, 295, 633, 3920, 309, 1562, 1866, 13, 467, 575, 281, 12649, 264, 1785, 13, 50925], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1523535182175127, "compression_ratio": 1.6076388888888888, "no_speech_prob": 2.07643949777514e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 151972, "start": 1531.28, "end": 1539.0, "text": " The rule the AI learns is, retain exactly the information that distinguishes futures that matter, and annihilate everything else.", "tokens": [50943, 440, 4978, 264, 7318, 27152, 307, 11, 18340, 2293, 264, 1589, 300, 11365, 16423, 26071, 300, 1871, 11, 293, 40430, 48104, 1203, 1646, 13, 51329], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1523535182175127, "compression_ratio": 1.6076388888888888, "no_speech_prob": 2.07643949777514e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 151972, "start": 1539.48, "end": 1544.74, "text": " The text grounds this with a fantastic concrete example of a bank's financial server.", "tokens": [51353, 440, 2487, 19196, 341, 365, 257, 5456, 9859, 1365, 295, 257, 3765, 311, 4669, 7154, 13, 51616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1523535182175127, "compression_ratio": 1.6076388888888888, "no_speech_prob": 2.07643949777514e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 151972, "start": 1544.74, "end": 1548.74, "text": " Let's walk through this architecture, because it proves this isn't just theory.", "tokens": [51616, 961, 311, 1792, 807, 341, 9482, 11, 570, 309, 25019, 341, 1943, 380, 445, 5261, 13, 51816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1523535182175127, "compression_ratio": 1.6076388888888888, "no_speech_prob": 2.07643949777514e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 154874, "start": 1548.74, "end": 1552.72, "text": " The bank's database faces three distinct queries.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3765, 311, 8149, 8475, 1045, 10644, 24109, 13, 50564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14468494681424873, "compression_ratio": 1.6305732484076434, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996677081240527e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 154874, "start": 1553.0, "end": 1553.6, "text": " Query 1.", "tokens": [50578, 2326, 2109, 502, 13, 50608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14468494681424873, "compression_ratio": 1.6305732484076434, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996677081240527e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 154874, "start": 1554.14, "end": 1557.8, "text": " When a customer logs into the app, they ask, what is my current balance?", "tokens": [50635, 1133, 257, 5474, 20820, 666, 264, 724, 11, 436, 1029, 11, 437, 307, 452, 2190, 4772, 30, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14468494681424873, "compression_ratio": 1.6305732484076434, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996677081240527e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 154874, "start": 1558.1, "end": 1562.86, "text": " To answer query 1, the minimal sufficient statistic is a single integer, the running sum.", "tokens": [50833, 1407, 1867, 14581, 502, 11, 264, 13206, 11563, 29588, 307, 257, 2167, 24922, 11, 264, 2614, 2408, 13, 51071], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14468494681424873, "compression_ratio": 1.6305732484076434, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996677081240527e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 154874, "start": 1563.2, "end": 1566.56, "text": " You do not need to read the history of every coffee they ever bought to display the balance.", "tokens": [51088, 509, 360, 406, 643, 281, 1401, 264, 2503, 295, 633, 4982, 436, 1562, 4243, 281, 4674, 264, 4772, 13, 51256], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14468494681424873, "compression_ratio": 1.6305732484076434, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996677081240527e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 154874, "start": 1566.92, "end": 1568.44, "text": " You just look at the compressed state.", "tokens": [51274, 509, 445, 574, 412, 264, 30353, 1785, 13, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14468494681424873, "compression_ratio": 1.6305732484076434, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996677081240527e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 154874, "start": 1568.68, "end": 1570.58, "text": " Query 2 comes from the compliance department.", "tokens": [51362, 2326, 2109, 568, 1487, 490, 264, 15882, 5882, 13, 51457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14468494681424873, "compression_ratio": 1.6305732484076434, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996677081240527e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 154874, "start": 1571.1200000000001, "end": 1575.14, "text": " Did this account execute a transaction over $10,000 in the last 30 days?", "tokens": [51484, 2589, 341, 2696, 14483, 257, 14425, 670, 1848, 3279, 11, 1360, 294, 264, 1036, 2217, 1708, 30, 51685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14468494681424873, "compression_ratio": 1.6305732484076434, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996677081240527e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 154874, "start": 1575.52, "end": 1577.16, "text": " And the running sum cannot answer that.", "tokens": [51704, 400, 264, 2614, 2408, 2644, 1867, 300, 13, 51786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14468494681424873, "compression_ratio": 1.6305732484076434, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996677081240527e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 157716, "start": 1577.16, "end": 1578.96, "text": " But it lacks the requisite distinctions.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 309, 31132, 264, 49878, 642, 1483, 49798, 13, 50455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14766145026546784, "compression_ratio": 1.4514767932489452, "no_speech_prob": 1.3251844283371228e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 157716, "start": 1579.5600000000002, "end": 1586.96, "text": " So to satisfy query 2, the system must retain the full, uncompressed transactional history, but strictly bounded by a 30-day sliding window.", "tokens": [50485, 407, 281, 19319, 14581, 568, 11, 264, 1185, 1633, 18340, 264, 1577, 11, 8585, 79, 3805, 46688, 1966, 2503, 11, 457, 20792, 37498, 538, 257, 2217, 12, 810, 21169, 4910, 13, 50855], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14766145026546784, "compression_ratio": 1.4514767932489452, "no_speech_prob": 1.3251844283371228e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 157716, "start": 1587.38, "end": 1589.3000000000002, "text": " Okay, and query 3 is the nightmare scenario.", "tokens": [50876, 1033, 11, 293, 14581, 805, 307, 264, 18724, 9005, 13, 50972], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14766145026546784, "compression_ratio": 1.4514767932489452, "no_speech_prob": 1.3251844283371228e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 157716, "start": 1590.0800000000002, "end": 1597.46, "text": " The IRS issues a subpoena and says, we're doing a deep forensic audit of this account's activity from five years ago.", "tokens": [51011, 440, 33848, 2663, 257, 1422, 2259, 4118, 293, 1619, 11, 321, 434, 884, 257, 2452, 39084, 17748, 295, 341, 2696, 311, 5191, 490, 1732, 924, 2057, 13, 51380], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14766145026546784, "compression_ratio": 1.4514767932489452, "no_speech_prob": 1.3251844283371228e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 159746, "start": 1597.46, "end": 1601.2, "text": " Right. So bank engineers are effectively tuning the lambda dial every day.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 407, 3765, 11955, 366, 8659, 15164, 264, 13607, 5502, 633, 786, 13, 50552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15760567313746401, "compression_ratio": 1.5185185185185186, "no_speech_prob": 1.989108964345343e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 159746, "start": 1601.6200000000001, "end": 1604.24, "text": " They keep the running sum unconditionally in fast memory.", "tokens": [50573, 814, 1066, 264, 2614, 2408, 34959, 15899, 294, 2370, 4675, 13, 50704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15760567313746401, "compression_ratio": 1.5185185185185186, "no_speech_prob": 1.989108964345343e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 159746, "start": 1604.64, "end": 1610.1000000000001, "text": " They keep 30 days of raw history in live databases because regulatory fines are exorbitant.", "tokens": [50724, 814, 1066, 2217, 1708, 295, 8936, 2503, 294, 1621, 22380, 570, 18260, 37989, 366, 454, 284, 5260, 394, 13, 50997], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15760567313746401, "compression_ratio": 1.5185185185185186, "no_speech_prob": 1.989108964345343e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 159746, "start": 1610.48, "end": 1615.88, "text": " But for the five-year audit, the probability of that query is low and the speed requirement is relaxed.", "tokens": [51016, 583, 337, 264, 1732, 12, 5294, 17748, 11, 264, 8482, 295, 300, 14581, 307, 2295, 293, 264, 3073, 11695, 307, 14628, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15760567313746401, "compression_ratio": 1.5185185185185186, "no_speech_prob": 1.989108964345343e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 161588, "start": 1615.88, "end": 1624.4, "text": " So they collapse the ancient history into monthly summaries, burn the raw data to cold storage magnetic tapes, and ship them to a salt mine in Utah.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 436, 15584, 264, 7832, 2503, 666, 12878, 8367, 4889, 11, 5064, 264, 8936, 1412, 281, 3554, 6725, 12688, 31349, 11, 293, 5374, 552, 281, 257, 5139, 3892, 294, 20226, 13, 50791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10976135547344501, "compression_ratio": 1.5075376884422111, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668384558548132e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 161588, "start": 1624.68, "end": 1627.3600000000001, "text": " They are doing rate distortion optimization in the real world.", "tokens": [50805, 814, 366, 884, 3314, 28426, 19618, 294, 264, 957, 1002, 13, 50939], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10976135547344501, "compression_ratio": 1.5075376884422111, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668384558548132e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 161588, "start": 1627.7600000000002, "end": 1632.18, "text": " But this bank example actually exposes the terrifying vulnerability of the whole system.", "tokens": [50959, 583, 341, 3765, 1365, 767, 1278, 4201, 264, 18106, 24210, 295, 264, 1379, 1185, 13, 51180], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10976135547344501, "compression_ratio": 1.5075376884422111, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668384558548132e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 163218, "start": 1632.18, "end": 1634.8400000000001, "text": " You optimize perfectly for those three queries.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 19719, 6239, 337, 729, 1045, 24109, 13, 50498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16064459554265054, "compression_ratio": 1.523465703971119, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439502954744393e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 163218, "start": 1634.98, "end": 1636.04, "text": " You ship the tapes to Utah.", "tokens": [50505, 509, 5374, 264, 31349, 281, 20226, 13, 50558], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16064459554265054, "compression_ratio": 1.523465703971119, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439502954744393e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 163218, "start": 1636.48, "end": 1646.28, "text": " What happens when a new regulatory law passes tomorrow, and suddenly the government demands 90 days of live, granular transaction history, and you've already incinerated days 31 through 90?", "tokens": [50580, 708, 2314, 562, 257, 777, 18260, 2101, 11335, 4153, 11, 293, 5800, 264, 2463, 15107, 4289, 1708, 295, 1621, 11, 39962, 14425, 2503, 11, 293, 291, 600, 1217, 834, 4564, 770, 1708, 10353, 807, 4289, 30, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16064459554265054, "compression_ratio": 1.523465703971119, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439502954744393e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 163218, "start": 1646.44, "end": 1647.3600000000001, "text": " The system collapses.", "tokens": [51078, 440, 1185, 48765, 13, 51124], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16064459554265054, "compression_ratio": 1.523465703971119, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439502954744393e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 163218, "start": 1647.98, "end": 1655.8400000000001, "text": " And this catastrophic vulnerability is the subject of the third and final essay, selective retention and the geometry of continuation.", "tokens": [51155, 400, 341, 34915, 24210, 307, 264, 3983, 295, 264, 2636, 293, 2572, 16238, 11, 33930, 22871, 293, 264, 18426, 295, 29357, 13, 51548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16064459554265054, "compression_ratio": 1.523465703971119, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439502954744393e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 165584, "start": 1655.84, "end": 1663.6, "text": " Affliction realizes here that the entire debate framing the first essay state versus history was a false dichotomy.", "tokens": [50365, 12840, 75, 4105, 29316, 510, 300, 264, 2302, 7958, 28971, 264, 700, 16238, 1785, 5717, 2503, 390, 257, 7908, 10390, 310, 8488, 13, 50753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16319455157269488, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.854059223857507e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 165584, "start": 1663.84, "end": 1665.4199999999998, "text": " Neither one has intrinsic value.", "tokens": [50765, 23956, 472, 575, 35698, 2158, 13, 50844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16319455157269488, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.854059223857507e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 165584, "start": 1665.6, "end": 1665.84, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50853, 1779, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16319455157269488, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.854059223857507e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 165584, "start": 1666.28, "end": 1671.9599999999998, "text": " The true fundamental unit of computational and existential value is the continuation.", "tokens": [50887, 440, 2074, 8088, 4985, 295, 28270, 293, 37133, 2158, 307, 264, 29357, 13, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16319455157269488, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.854059223857507e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 165584, "start": 1672.3999999999999, "end": 1680.0, "text": " A continuation is the space of admissible future trajectories that are still physically and logically readable from where the system currently stands.", "tokens": [51193, 316, 29357, 307, 264, 1901, 295, 5910, 41073, 2027, 18257, 2083, 300, 366, 920, 9762, 293, 38887, 49857, 490, 689, 264, 1185, 4362, 7382, 13, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16319455157269488, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.854059223857507e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 165584, "start": 1680.26, "end": 1682.02, "text": " It is your capacity to keep going.", "tokens": [51586, 467, 307, 428, 6042, 281, 1066, 516, 13, 51674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16319455157269488, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.854059223857507e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 168202, "start": 1682.02, "end": 1687.08, "text": " A terabyte of perfectly preserved history is useless if it doesn't help you answer tomorrow's questions.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 1796, 34529, 295, 6239, 22242, 2503, 307, 14115, 498, 309, 1177, 380, 854, 291, 1867, 4153, 311, 1651, 13, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12405106780725882, "compression_ratio": 1.858695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4440963615885982e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 168202, "start": 1687.54, "end": 1693.28, "text": " And a highly optimized compressed state is useless if it destroyed the very information required to take the next step.", "tokens": [50641, 400, 257, 5405, 26941, 30353, 1785, 307, 14115, 498, 309, 8937, 264, 588, 1589, 4739, 281, 747, 264, 958, 1823, 13, 50928], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12405106780725882, "compression_ratio": 1.858695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4440963615885982e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 168202, "start": 1693.98, "end": 1695.72, "text": " Affliction proposes a new triad.", "tokens": [50963, 12840, 75, 4105, 2365, 4201, 257, 777, 1376, 345, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12405106780725882, "compression_ratio": 1.858695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4440963615885982e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 168202, "start": 1696.34, "end": 1699.54, "text": " History flows into compression, and compression flows into continuation.", "tokens": [51081, 12486, 12867, 666, 19355, 11, 293, 19355, 12867, 666, 29357, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12405106780725882, "compression_ratio": 1.858695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4440963615885982e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 168202, "start": 1700.02, "end": 1702.62, "text": " So the purpose of compression isn't to save hard drive space.", "tokens": [51265, 407, 264, 4334, 295, 19355, 1943, 380, 281, 3155, 1152, 3332, 1901, 13, 51395], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12405106780725882, "compression_ratio": 1.858695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4440963615885982e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 168202, "start": 1702.74, "end": 1708.24, "text": " The purpose of compression is to preserve the specific critical distinctions that your future continuations will demand.", "tokens": [51401, 440, 4334, 295, 19355, 307, 281, 15665, 264, 2685, 4924, 1483, 49798, 300, 428, 2027, 2993, 763, 486, 4733, 13, 51676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12405106780725882, "compression_ratio": 1.858695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4440963615885982e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 170824, "start": 1708.24, "end": 1714.66, "text": " Exactly. And when you compress too aggressively, you suffer what the text calls a continuation deficit.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 400, 562, 291, 14778, 886, 32024, 11, 291, 9753, 437, 264, 2487, 5498, 257, 29357, 22132, 13, 50686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11985913444967831, "compression_ratio": 1.703448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.818439604624189e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 170824, "start": 1715.22, "end": 1716.78, "text": " This is a calculated risk.", "tokens": [50714, 639, 307, 257, 15598, 3148, 13, 50792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11985913444967831, "compression_ratio": 1.703448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.818439604624189e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 170824, "start": 1717.22, "end": 1721.88, "text": " It is the known probability that you threw away a distinction you might actually need.", "tokens": [50814, 467, 307, 264, 2570, 8482, 300, 291, 11918, 1314, 257, 16844, 291, 1062, 767, 643, 13, 51047], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11985913444967831, "compression_ratio": 1.703448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.818439604624189e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 170824, "start": 1722.0, "end": 1726.8, "text": " Think of it like throwing away your tax receipts at the end of the year to save space in your filing cabinet.", "tokens": [51053, 6557, 295, 309, 411, 10238, 1314, 428, 3366, 2268, 48908, 412, 264, 917, 295, 264, 1064, 281, 3155, 1901, 294, 428, 26854, 15188, 13, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11985913444967831, "compression_ratio": 1.703448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.818439604624189e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 170824, "start": 1727.26, "end": 1728.7, "text": " You understand what a receipt is.", "tokens": [51316, 509, 1223, 437, 257, 33882, 307, 13, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11985913444967831, "compression_ratio": 1.703448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.818439604624189e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 170824, "start": 1728.76, "end": 1730.84, "text": " You understand what an IRS audit is.", "tokens": [51391, 509, 1223, 437, 364, 33848, 17748, 307, 13, 51495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11985913444967831, "compression_ratio": 1.703448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.818439604624189e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 170824, "start": 1731.2, "end": 1734.52, "text": " You are simply making a statistical gamble that the audit won't happen.", "tokens": [51513, 509, 366, 2935, 1455, 257, 22820, 44128, 300, 264, 17748, 1582, 380, 1051, 13, 51679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11985913444967831, "compression_ratio": 1.703448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.818439604624189e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 170824, "start": 1734.7, "end": 1735.64, "text": " Right. You took a risk.", "tokens": [51688, 1779, 13, 509, 1890, 257, 3148, 13, 51735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11985913444967831, "compression_ratio": 1.703448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.818439604624189e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 173564, "start": 1735.64, "end": 1738.5400000000002, "text": " If the IRS knocks on your door, you have a continuation deficit.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 33848, 40815, 322, 428, 2853, 11, 291, 362, 257, 29357, 22132, 13, 50510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12935617807749156, "compression_ratio": 1.618320610687023, "no_speech_prob": 1.69476574701094e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 173564, "start": 1738.8000000000002, "end": 1740.5200000000002, "text": " You took a priced risk, and you lost.", "tokens": [50523, 509, 1890, 257, 30349, 3148, 11, 293, 291, 2731, 13, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12935617807749156, "compression_ratio": 1.618320610687023, "no_speech_prob": 1.69476574701094e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 173564, "start": 1740.7, "end": 1746.5200000000002, "text": " But the author introduces a second type of failure, which is far more insidious, an ontological deficit.", "tokens": [50618, 583, 264, 3793, 31472, 257, 1150, 2010, 295, 7763, 11, 597, 307, 1400, 544, 1028, 327, 851, 11, 364, 6592, 4383, 22132, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12935617807749156, "compression_ratio": 1.618320610687023, "no_speech_prob": 1.69476574701094e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 173564, "start": 1746.96, "end": 1748.3200000000002, "text": " This isn't a calculated risk.", "tokens": [50931, 639, 1943, 380, 257, 15598, 3148, 13, 50999], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12935617807749156, "compression_ratio": 1.618320610687023, "no_speech_prob": 1.69476574701094e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 173564, "start": 1748.38, "end": 1749.8200000000002, "text": " This is a structural blindness.", "tokens": [51002, 639, 307, 257, 15067, 46101, 13, 51074], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12935617807749156, "compression_ratio": 1.618320610687023, "no_speech_prob": 1.69476574701094e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 173564, "start": 1750.3200000000002, "end": 1751.8200000000002, "text": " You didn't just throw away the data.", "tokens": [51099, 509, 994, 380, 445, 3507, 1314, 264, 1412, 13, 51174], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12935617807749156, "compression_ratio": 1.618320610687023, "no_speech_prob": 1.69476574701094e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 173564, "start": 1752.22, "end": 1756.7800000000002, "text": " You threw away the very vocabulary required to even notice that the data is missing.", "tokens": [51194, 509, 11918, 1314, 264, 588, 19864, 4739, 281, 754, 3449, 300, 264, 1412, 307, 5361, 13, 51422], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12935617807749156, "compression_ratio": 1.618320610687023, "no_speech_prob": 1.69476574701094e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 173564, "start": 1756.96, "end": 1758.0400000000002, "text": " Wait, can you elaborate on that?", "tokens": [51431, 3802, 11, 393, 291, 20945, 322, 300, 30, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12935617807749156, "compression_ratio": 1.618320610687023, "no_speech_prob": 1.69476574701094e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 175804, "start": 1758.04, "end": 1765.0, "text": " An ontological deficit means the system cannot, using its own internal logic, detect that a loss has occurred.", "tokens": [50365, 1107, 6592, 4383, 22132, 1355, 264, 1185, 2644, 11, 1228, 1080, 1065, 6920, 9952, 11, 5531, 300, 257, 4470, 575, 11068, 13, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13258719040175615, "compression_ratio": 1.4875, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130203947361087e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 175804, "start": 1765.58, "end": 1768.06, "text": " It is a blind spot protecting a blind spot.", "tokens": [50742, 467, 307, 257, 6865, 4008, 12316, 257, 6865, 4008, 13, 50866], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13258719040175615, "compression_ratio": 1.4875, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130203947361087e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 175804, "start": 1768.3999999999999, "end": 1769.62, "text": " Let me try to visualize this.", "tokens": [50883, 961, 385, 853, 281, 23273, 341, 13, 50944], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13258719040175615, "compression_ratio": 1.4875, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130203947361087e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 175804, "start": 1770.18, "end": 1772.92, "text": " A continuation deficit is throwing away the receipts.", "tokens": [50972, 316, 29357, 22132, 307, 10238, 1314, 264, 2268, 48908, 13, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13258719040175615, "compression_ratio": 1.4875, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130203947361087e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 177292, "start": 1772.92, "end": 1781.88, "text": " An ontological deficit is like a police department deciding, to save money on film, that they will only photograph crime scenes in black and white.", "tokens": [50365, 1107, 6592, 4383, 22132, 307, 411, 257, 3804, 5882, 17990, 11, 281, 3155, 1460, 322, 2007, 11, 300, 436, 486, 787, 8348, 7206, 8026, 294, 2211, 293, 2418, 13, 50813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11844884287012686, "compression_ratio": 1.579925650557621, "no_speech_prob": 1.2494615802063902e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 177292, "start": 1782.76, "end": 1788.9, "text": " Ten years later, a cold case detective reopens a file and asks, was the getaway car red or blue?", "tokens": [50857, 9380, 924, 1780, 11, 257, 3554, 1389, 25571, 28994, 694, 257, 3991, 293, 8962, 11, 390, 264, 483, 10318, 1032, 2182, 420, 3344, 30, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11844884287012686, "compression_ratio": 1.579925650557621, "no_speech_prob": 1.2494615802063902e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 177292, "start": 1789.26, "end": 1790.04, "text": " Oh, that's brilliant.", "tokens": [51182, 876, 11, 300, 311, 10248, 13, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11844884287012686, "compression_ratio": 1.579925650557621, "no_speech_prob": 1.2494615802063902e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 177292, "start": 1790.26, "end": 1793.4, "text": " And the tragedy is that the archive doesn't just lack the answer.", "tokens": [51232, 400, 264, 18563, 307, 300, 264, 23507, 1177, 380, 445, 5011, 264, 1867, 13, 51389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11844884287012686, "compression_ratio": 1.579925650557621, "no_speech_prob": 1.2494615802063902e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 177292, "start": 1793.66, "end": 1799.14, "text": " The storage medium itself structurally lacks the capacity to represent the concept of color.", "tokens": [51402, 440, 6725, 6399, 2564, 6594, 6512, 31132, 264, 6042, 281, 2906, 264, 3410, 295, 2017, 13, 51676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11844884287012686, "compression_ratio": 1.579925650557621, "no_speech_prob": 1.2494615802063902e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 179914, "start": 1799.14, "end": 1802.0200000000002, "text": " You can't even express the distinction between red and blue anymore.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 393, 380, 754, 5109, 264, 16844, 1296, 2182, 293, 3344, 3602, 13, 50509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11928829846081433, "compression_ratio": 1.6904761904761905, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764254031468976e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 179914, "start": 1802.46, "end": 1804.14, "text": " The information wasn't just lost.", "tokens": [50531, 440, 1589, 2067, 380, 445, 2731, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11928829846081433, "compression_ratio": 1.6904761904761905, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764254031468976e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 179914, "start": 1804.6200000000001, "end": 1807.92, "text": " The dimension of reality it occupied was annihilated.", "tokens": [50639, 440, 10139, 295, 4103, 309, 19629, 390, 40430, 45678, 13, 50804], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11928829846081433, "compression_ratio": 1.6904761904761905, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764254031468976e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 179914, "start": 1808.22, "end": 1813.0600000000002, "text": " Imagine if the legal system only accepted those black and white photos as valid evidence.", "tokens": [50819, 11739, 498, 264, 5089, 1185, 787, 9035, 729, 2211, 293, 2418, 5787, 382, 7363, 4467, 13, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11928829846081433, "compression_ratio": 1.6904761904761905, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764254031468976e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 179914, "start": 1813.3200000000002, "end": 1820.3200000000002, "text": " You would have an entire society structurally blind to color, making life or death decisions based on a corrupted compression of reality.", "tokens": [51074, 509, 576, 362, 364, 2302, 4086, 6594, 6512, 6865, 281, 2017, 11, 1455, 993, 420, 2966, 5327, 2361, 322, 257, 39480, 19355, 295, 4103, 13, 51424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11928829846081433, "compression_ratio": 1.6904761904761905, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764254031468976e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 179914, "start": 1820.7, "end": 1822.0800000000002, "text": " The system doesn't know it's blind.", "tokens": [51443, 440, 1185, 1177, 380, 458, 309, 311, 6865, 13, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11928829846081433, "compression_ratio": 1.6904761904761905, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764254031468976e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 179914, "start": 1822.48, "end": 1825.74, "text": " It believes the black and white photo is the absolute truth of the universe.", "tokens": [51532, 467, 12307, 264, 2211, 293, 2418, 5052, 307, 264, 8236, 3494, 295, 264, 6445, 13, 51695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11928829846081433, "compression_ratio": 1.6904761904761905, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764254031468976e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 182574, "start": 1825.74, "end": 1835.06, "text": " Have you ever cleaned out your garage, thrown away a random cable because you didn't know what it went to, and then six months later realized you threw away the power cord to your favorite speaker?", "tokens": [50365, 3560, 291, 1562, 16146, 484, 428, 14400, 11, 11732, 1314, 257, 4974, 8220, 570, 291, 994, 380, 458, 437, 309, 1437, 281, 11, 293, 550, 2309, 2493, 1780, 5334, 291, 11918, 1314, 264, 1347, 12250, 281, 428, 2954, 8145, 30, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13805593343881462, "compression_ratio": 1.4536082474226804, "no_speech_prob": 2.2453436679392702e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 182574, "start": 1835.82, "end": 1837.1200000000001, "text": " That's a continuation deficit.", "tokens": [50869, 663, 311, 257, 29357, 22132, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13805593343881462, "compression_ratio": 1.4536082474226804, "no_speech_prob": 2.2453436679392702e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 182574, "start": 1837.8, "end": 1841.18, "text": " You optimized for space, but failed the future query.", "tokens": [50968, 509, 26941, 337, 1901, 11, 457, 7612, 264, 2027, 14581, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13805593343881462, "compression_ratio": 1.4536082474226804, "no_speech_prob": 2.2453436679392702e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 184118, "start": 1841.18, "end": 1850.64, "text": " This framework history, compression, continuation, and ontological deficits, it suddenly explains so much more than software architecture.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 8388, 2503, 11, 19355, 11, 29357, 11, 293, 6592, 4383, 49616, 11, 309, 5800, 13948, 370, 709, 544, 813, 4722, 9482, 13, 50838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15999240562564038, "compression_ratio": 1.5027027027027027, "no_speech_prob": 2.370978196761242e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 184118, "start": 1851.7, "end": 1857.5, "text": " To prove this, Flixionet applies the triad to the real world through three stunning case studies.", "tokens": [50891, 1407, 7081, 341, 11, 3235, 970, 313, 302, 13165, 264, 1376, 345, 281, 264, 957, 1002, 807, 1045, 18550, 1389, 5313, 13, 51181], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15999240562564038, "compression_ratio": 1.5027027027027027, "no_speech_prob": 2.370978196761242e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 184118, "start": 1858.0, "end": 1860.66, "text": " The first compares Git to legal archives.", "tokens": [51206, 440, 700, 38334, 16939, 281, 5089, 25607, 13, 51339], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15999240562564038, "compression_ratio": 1.5027027027027027, "no_speech_prob": 2.370978196761242e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 186066, "start": 1860.66, "end": 1866.6200000000001, "text": " We celebrated Git earlier as the champion of unbounded history, but Flixion points out a crucial nuance.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 19366, 16939, 3071, 382, 264, 10971, 295, 517, 18767, 292, 2503, 11, 457, 3235, 970, 313, 2793, 484, 257, 11462, 42625, 13, 50663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10165351520885121, "compression_ratio": 1.667857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622667648070633e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 186066, "start": 1867.16, "end": 1870.66, "text": " Git actively, intentionally throws away massive amounts of history.", "tokens": [50690, 16939, 13022, 11, 22062, 19251, 1314, 5994, 11663, 295, 2503, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10165351520885121, "compression_ratio": 1.667857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622667648070633e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 186066, "start": 1871.22, "end": 1877.5400000000002, "text": " Git perfectly preserves the timeline of commits, but it explicitly discards the keystroke level editing history.", "tokens": [50893, 16939, 6239, 1183, 9054, 264, 12933, 295, 48311, 11, 457, 309, 20803, 2983, 2287, 264, 2141, 42706, 1496, 10000, 2503, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10165351520885121, "compression_ratio": 1.667857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622667648070633e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 186066, "start": 1877.66, "end": 1883.76, "text": " Yeah, it doesn't remember that I typed a sentence, deleted it, pasted around the room for ten minutes, retyped it, and then finally committed the file.", "tokens": [51215, 865, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 1604, 300, 286, 33941, 257, 8174, 11, 22981, 309, 11, 1791, 292, 926, 264, 1808, 337, 2064, 2077, 11, 319, 874, 3452, 309, 11, 293, 550, 2721, 7784, 264, 3991, 13, 51520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10165351520885121, "compression_ratio": 1.667857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622667648070633e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 186066, "start": 1884.0, "end": 1885.1200000000001, "text": " And why does it discard that?", "tokens": [51532, 400, 983, 775, 309, 31597, 300, 30, 51588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10165351520885121, "compression_ratio": 1.667857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622667648070633e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 188512, "start": 1885.12, "end": 1895.0, "text": " Because the feature continuation population for Git involves developers trying to find out when a bug was introduced or reverting a broken feature, keystrokes do not aid that continuation.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 264, 4111, 29357, 4415, 337, 16939, 11626, 8849, 1382, 281, 915, 484, 562, 257, 7426, 390, 7268, 420, 18438, 783, 257, 5463, 4111, 11, 2141, 27616, 5993, 360, 406, 9418, 300, 29357, 13, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12790091665167558, "compression_ratio": 1.6853932584269662, "no_speech_prob": 2.2624118290598405e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 188512, "start": 1895.4199999999998, "end": 1898.04, "text": " But a legal archive, an evidence room.", "tokens": [50880, 583, 257, 5089, 23507, 11, 364, 4467, 1808, 13, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12790091665167558, "compression_ratio": 1.6853932584269662, "no_speech_prob": 2.2624118290598405e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 188512, "start": 1898.2199999999998, "end": 1903.26, "text": " They retain signatures, biometric timestamps, and unbroken chain of custody logs.", "tokens": [51020, 814, 18340, 32322, 11, 3228, 29470, 49108, 23150, 11, 293, 517, 37947, 5021, 295, 26976, 20820, 13, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12790091665167558, "compression_ratio": 1.6853932584269662, "no_speech_prob": 2.2624118290598405e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 188512, "start": 1904.02, "end": 1911.1599999999999, "text": " Their future continuation is a hostile legal audit where proving exactly when and how a document was altered is the only thing that matters.", "tokens": [51310, 6710, 2027, 29357, 307, 257, 27312, 5089, 17748, 689, 27221, 2293, 562, 293, 577, 257, 4166, 390, 28783, 307, 264, 787, 551, 300, 7001, 13, 51667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12790091665167558, "compression_ratio": 1.6853932584269662, "no_speech_prob": 2.2624118290598405e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 191116, "start": 1911.16, "end": 1916.4, "text": " Two entirely different continuations demand two entirely different compressions of reality.", "tokens": [50365, 4453, 7696, 819, 2993, 763, 4733, 732, 7696, 819, 14778, 626, 295, 4103, 13, 50627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14452299417233935, "compression_ratio": 1.701067615658363, "no_speech_prob": 1.927927869432855e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 191116, "start": 1916.6200000000001, "end": 1918.98, "text": " The second case study moves from silicon to carbon.", "tokens": [50638, 440, 1150, 1389, 2979, 6067, 490, 22848, 281, 5954, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14452299417233935, "compression_ratio": 1.701067615658363, "no_speech_prob": 1.927927869432855e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 191116, "start": 1919.72, "end": 1924.8400000000001, "text": " It maps this exact computer science theory onto biological memory, the human brain.", "tokens": [50793, 467, 11317, 341, 1900, 3820, 3497, 5261, 3911, 13910, 4675, 11, 264, 1952, 3567, 13, 51049], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14452299417233935, "compression_ratio": 1.701067615658363, "no_speech_prob": 1.927927869432855e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 191116, "start": 1925.14, "end": 1928.22, "text": " This is where the trilogy elevates into sheer brilliance, honestly.", "tokens": [51064, 639, 307, 689, 264, 34030, 7701, 1024, 666, 23061, 8695, 6276, 11, 6095, 13, 51218], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14452299417233935, "compression_ratio": 1.701067615658363, "no_speech_prob": 1.927927869432855e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 191116, "start": 1928.66, "end": 1933.1000000000001, "text": " Flixion maps rate distortion optimization onto the biological process of systems consolidation.", "tokens": [51240, 3235, 970, 313, 11317, 3314, 28426, 19618, 3911, 264, 13910, 1399, 295, 3652, 39114, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14452299417233935, "compression_ratio": 1.701067615658363, "no_speech_prob": 1.927927869432855e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 191116, "start": 1933.76, "end": 1938.16, "text": " When you experience a novel event, the memory is initially encoded in the hippocampus.", "tokens": [51495, 1133, 291, 1752, 257, 7613, 2280, 11, 264, 4675, 307, 9105, 2058, 12340, 294, 264, 27745, 905, 1215, 301, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14452299417233935, "compression_ratio": 1.701067615658363, "no_speech_prob": 1.927927869432855e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 193816, "start": 1938.16, "end": 1945.22, "text": " It is incredibly rich in episodic detail, the exact temperature of the room, the smell of the air, the precise color of the shirt the person was wearing.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 6252, 4593, 294, 39200, 299, 2607, 11, 264, 1900, 4292, 295, 264, 1808, 11, 264, 4316, 295, 264, 1988, 11, 264, 13600, 2017, 295, 264, 8336, 264, 954, 390, 4769, 13, 50718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305176987607255, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.9888242528548483e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 193816, "start": 1945.6200000000001, "end": 1948.0600000000002, "text": " But this hippocampal storage is volatile, right?", "tokens": [50738, 583, 341, 27745, 905, 1215, 304, 6725, 307, 34377, 11, 558, 30, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305176987607255, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.9888242528548483e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 193816, "start": 1948.24, "end": 1948.44, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50869, 865, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305176987607255, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.9888242528548483e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 193816, "start": 1948.5800000000002, "end": 1950.1200000000001, "text": " And highly vulnerable to disruption.", "tokens": [50886, 400, 5405, 10955, 281, 28751, 13, 50963], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305176987607255, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.9888242528548483e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 193816, "start": 1950.4, "end": 1950.7, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50977, 1079, 13, 50992], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305176987607255, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.9888242528548483e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 193816, "start": 1951.24, "end": 1955.1200000000001, "text": " Over time, mostly while we sleep, that memory consolidates into the neocortex.", "tokens": [51019, 4886, 565, 11, 5240, 1339, 321, 2817, 11, 300, 4675, 19045, 1024, 666, 264, 408, 905, 36143, 13, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305176987607255, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.9888242528548483e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 193816, "start": 1955.68, "end": 1958.22, "text": " It becomes stable, but it undergoes massive compression.", "tokens": [51241, 467, 3643, 8351, 11, 457, 309, 26426, 279, 5994, 19355, 13, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305176987607255, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.9888242528548483e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 193816, "start": 1958.66, "end": 1959.5, "text": " It becomes schematic.", "tokens": [51390, 467, 3643, 44739, 13, 51432], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305176987607255, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.9888242528548483e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 193816, "start": 1959.66, "end": 1962.6200000000001, "text": " It loses that vivid episodic specificity.", "tokens": [51440, 467, 18293, 300, 23603, 39200, 299, 2685, 507, 13, 51588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305176987607255, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.9888242528548483e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 196262, "start": 1962.62, "end": 1969.0, "text": " So the brain is acting exactly like the bank server, collapsing 30-day transaction logs into a monthly summary.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 3567, 307, 6577, 2293, 411, 264, 3765, 7154, 11, 45339, 2217, 12, 810, 14425, 20820, 666, 257, 12878, 12691, 13, 50684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14626489722210428, "compression_ratio": 1.623728813559322, "no_speech_prob": 2.175260839509807e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 196262, "start": 1969.62, "end": 1973.7399999999998, "text": " The brain is aggressively throwing away data to optimize for the future.", "tokens": [50715, 440, 3567, 307, 32024, 10238, 1314, 1412, 281, 19719, 337, 264, 2027, 13, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14626489722210428, "compression_ratio": 1.623728813559322, "no_speech_prob": 2.175260839509807e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 196262, "start": 1974.12, "end": 1980.32, "text": " Flixion states the cognitive psychologist Endel Kolving here, specifically his concept of the enneagram and ecfori.", "tokens": [50940, 3235, 970, 313, 4368, 264, 15605, 29514, 6967, 338, 26137, 798, 510, 11, 4682, 702, 3410, 295, 264, 465, 716, 3914, 293, 11437, 2994, 72, 13, 51250], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14626489722210428, "compression_ratio": 1.623728813559322, "no_speech_prob": 2.175260839509807e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 196262, "start": 1980.6399999999999, "end": 1982.4199999999998, "text": " Let's define those because they are critical.", "tokens": [51266, 961, 311, 6964, 729, 570, 436, 366, 4924, 13, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14626489722210428, "compression_ratio": 1.623728813559322, "no_speech_prob": 2.175260839509807e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 196262, "start": 1982.6599999999999, "end": 1987.6999999999998, "text": " The enneagram is the physical, biochemical trace of a memory stored in the neural tissue.", "tokens": [51367, 440, 465, 716, 3914, 307, 264, 4001, 11, 12198, 34114, 13508, 295, 257, 4675, 12187, 294, 264, 18161, 12404, 13, 51619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14626489722210428, "compression_ratio": 1.623728813559322, "no_speech_prob": 2.175260839509807e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 196262, "start": 1988.5, "end": 1990.6599999999999, "text": " Ecfori is the active process of retrieval.", "tokens": [51659, 28993, 2994, 72, 307, 264, 4967, 1399, 295, 19817, 3337, 13, 51767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14626489722210428, "compression_ratio": 1.623728813559322, "no_speech_prob": 2.175260839509807e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 199066, "start": 1990.66, "end": 1998.38, "text": " It is the moment when a sensory cue in your present environment interacts with that stored enneagram to successfully reconstruct the memory.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 264, 1623, 562, 257, 27233, 22656, 294, 428, 1974, 2823, 43582, 365, 300, 12187, 465, 716, 3914, 281, 10727, 31499, 264, 4675, 13, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10825205249946658, "compression_ratio": 1.751700680272109, "no_speech_prob": 1.876083923629812e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 199066, "start": 1998.8000000000002, "end": 2004.94, "text": " Like smelling a specific brand of perfume on the street and suddenly being flooded with the memory of a childhood teacher.", "tokens": [50772, 1743, 35471, 257, 2685, 3360, 295, 28464, 322, 264, 4838, 293, 5800, 885, 31594, 365, 264, 4675, 295, 257, 9278, 5027, 13, 51079], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10825205249946658, "compression_ratio": 1.751700680272109, "no_speech_prob": 1.876083923629812e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 199066, "start": 2005.46, "end": 2006.6000000000001, "text": " The perfume is the cue.", "tokens": [51105, 440, 28464, 307, 264, 22656, 13, 51162], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10825205249946658, "compression_ratio": 1.751700680272109, "no_speech_prob": 1.876083923629812e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 199066, "start": 2007.0400000000002, "end": 2008.52, "text": " The reconstruction is the ecfori.", "tokens": [51184, 440, 31565, 307, 264, 11437, 2994, 72, 13, 51258], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10825205249946658, "compression_ratio": 1.751700680272109, "no_speech_prob": 1.876083923629812e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 199066, "start": 2008.6000000000001, "end": 2009.0600000000002, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51262, 7587, 13, 51285], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10825205249946658, "compression_ratio": 1.751700680272109, "no_speech_prob": 1.876083923629812e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 199066, "start": 2009.5, "end": 2014.24, "text": " What Tolving argued and what Flixion highlights is that the raw density of the enneagram doesn't matter.", "tokens": [51307, 708, 21402, 798, 20219, 293, 437, 3235, 970, 313, 14254, 307, 300, 264, 8936, 10305, 295, 264, 465, 716, 3914, 1177, 380, 1871, 13, 51544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10825205249946658, "compression_ratio": 1.751700680272109, "no_speech_prob": 1.876083923629812e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 199066, "start": 2014.74, "end": 2018.74, "text": " What matters is whether a future retrieval cue can successfully trigger ecfori.", "tokens": [51569, 708, 7001, 307, 1968, 257, 2027, 19817, 3337, 22656, 393, 10727, 7875, 11437, 2994, 72, 13, 51769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10825205249946658, "compression_ratio": 1.751700680272109, "no_speech_prob": 1.876083923629812e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 201874, "start": 2018.74, "end": 2027.66, "text": " If your cortex compresses a memory so aggressively that the daily cues you encounter can no longer reactivate it, you have suffered a biological continuation deficit.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 428, 33312, 14778, 279, 257, 4675, 370, 32024, 300, 264, 5212, 32192, 291, 8593, 393, 572, 2854, 4515, 592, 473, 309, 11, 291, 362, 12770, 257, 13910, 29357, 22132, 13, 50811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10404646223869876, "compression_ratio": 1.5380710659898478, "no_speech_prob": 2.7827742280633894e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 201874, "start": 2028.3, "end": 2033.1, "text": " Functionally, you have forgotten the event, even if the biochemical trace is still sitting in your skull.", "tokens": [50843, 11166, 882, 379, 11, 291, 362, 11832, 264, 2280, 11, 754, 498, 264, 12198, 34114, 13508, 307, 920, 3798, 294, 428, 11743, 13, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10404646223869876, "compression_ratio": 1.5380710659898478, "no_speech_prob": 2.7827742280633894e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 201874, "start": 2033.52, "end": 2035.06, "text": " The brain predicts the future.", "tokens": [51104, 440, 3567, 6069, 82, 264, 2027, 13, 51181], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10404646223869876, "compression_ratio": 1.5380710659898478, "no_speech_prob": 2.7827742280633894e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 203506, "start": 2035.06, "end": 2044.62, "text": " It throws away the color of the car that drove past you yesterday because its statistical model predicts you will only ever need to know the schematic fact that a car was present.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 19251, 1314, 264, 2017, 295, 264, 1032, 300, 13226, 1791, 291, 5186, 570, 1080, 22820, 2316, 6069, 82, 291, 486, 787, 1562, 643, 281, 458, 264, 44739, 1186, 300, 257, 1032, 390, 1974, 13, 50843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12316192660415382, "compression_ratio": 1.5170454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 2.012255596525736e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 203506, "start": 2045.28, "end": 2051.2599999999998, "text": " It optimizes for a specific pot, a specific probability distribution of future queries.", "tokens": [50876, 467, 5028, 5660, 337, 257, 2685, 1847, 11, 257, 2685, 8482, 7316, 295, 2027, 24109, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12316192660415382, "compression_ratio": 1.5170454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 2.012255596525736e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 205126, "start": 2051.26, "end": 2059.94, "text": " But if you end up witnessing a crime and the police ask you the color of the car, that biological compression suddenly becomes a massive liability.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 291, 917, 493, 39233, 257, 7206, 293, 264, 3804, 1029, 291, 264, 2017, 295, 264, 1032, 11, 300, 13910, 19355, 5800, 3643, 257, 5994, 25196, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11865213692906391, "compression_ratio": 1.6234817813765183, "no_speech_prob": 2.4089957459394462e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 205126, "start": 2060.1800000000003, "end": 2063.34, "text": " The brain assumed one future and a different one arrived.", "tokens": [50811, 440, 3567, 15895, 472, 2027, 293, 257, 819, 472, 6678, 13, 50969], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11865213692906391, "compression_ratio": 1.6234817813765183, "no_speech_prob": 2.4089957459394462e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 205126, "start": 2063.84, "end": 2069.0, "text": " Which brings us to the third and most controversial case study, the scientific method itself.", "tokens": [50994, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 2636, 293, 881, 17323, 1389, 2979, 11, 264, 8134, 3170, 2564, 13, 51252], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11865213692906391, "compression_ratio": 1.6234817813765183, "no_speech_prob": 2.4089957459394462e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 205126, "start": 2069.4, "end": 2074.6600000000003, "text": " Specifically, the reproducibility crisis that tore through empirical psychology over the last decade.", "tokens": [51272, 26058, 11, 264, 11408, 537, 39802, 5869, 300, 37341, 807, 31886, 15105, 670, 264, 1036, 10378, 13, 51535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11865213692906391, "compression_ratio": 1.6234817813765183, "no_speech_prob": 2.4089957459394462e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 207466, "start": 2074.66, "end": 2082.56, "text": " This blew my mind. Are you saying the crisis in science, all those famous studies that turned out to be fake or unreplicable, was just a data compression error?", "tokens": [50365, 639, 19075, 452, 1575, 13, 2014, 291, 1566, 264, 5869, 294, 3497, 11, 439, 729, 4618, 5313, 300, 3574, 484, 281, 312, 7592, 420, 20584, 4770, 712, 11, 390, 445, 257, 1412, 19355, 6713, 30, 50760], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11236680595620165, "compression_ratio": 1.5627118644067797, "no_speech_prob": 1.649050904509175e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 207466, "start": 2082.96, "end": 2087.46, "text": " Not a mistake, but the logical outcome of a specific retention policy.", "tokens": [50780, 1726, 257, 6146, 11, 457, 264, 14978, 9700, 295, 257, 2685, 22871, 3897, 13, 51005], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11236680595620165, "compression_ratio": 1.5627118644067797, "no_speech_prob": 1.649050904509175e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 207466, "start": 2088.46, "end": 2091.18, "text": " The Scientific Journal article is a technology of memory.", "tokens": [51055, 440, 47437, 16936, 7222, 307, 257, 2899, 295, 4675, 13, 51191], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11236680595620165, "compression_ratio": 1.5627118644067797, "no_speech_prob": 1.649050904509175e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 207466, "start": 2091.6, "end": 2094.92, "text": " It is a compression algorithm for months of chaotic lab work.", "tokens": [51212, 467, 307, 257, 19355, 9284, 337, 2493, 295, 27013, 2715, 589, 13, 51378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11236680595620165, "compression_ratio": 1.5627118644067797, "no_speech_prob": 1.649050904509175e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 207466, "start": 2095.42, "end": 2102.3199999999997, "text": " For decades, the academic incentive structures prioritized brevity, narrative elegance, and absolute novelty.", "tokens": [51403, 1171, 7878, 11, 264, 7778, 22346, 9227, 14846, 1602, 1403, 23110, 11, 9977, 14459, 719, 11, 293, 8236, 44805, 13, 51748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11236680595620165, "compression_ratio": 1.5627118644067797, "no_speech_prob": 1.649050904509175e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 210232, "start": 2102.32, "end": 2111.82, "text": " They did not prioritize continuation capacity, which, in science, means the ability of an independent lab to read the paper and replicate the experiment.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 630, 406, 25164, 29357, 6042, 11, 597, 11, 294, 3497, 11, 1355, 264, 3485, 295, 364, 6695, 2715, 281, 1401, 264, 3035, 293, 25356, 264, 5120, 13, 50840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06500593983397192, "compression_ratio": 1.7472527472527473, "no_speech_prob": 1.8255369004654964e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 210232, "start": 2112.06, "end": 2115.82, "text": " The researchers had to compress their method sections to fit page limits.", "tokens": [50852, 440, 10309, 632, 281, 14778, 641, 3170, 10863, 281, 3318, 3028, 10406, 13, 51040], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06500593983397192, "compression_ratio": 1.7472527472527473, "no_speech_prob": 1.8255369004654964e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 210232, "start": 2116.44, "end": 2125.2400000000002, "text": " They threw away the exact wording of the survey prompts, the specific ambient temperature of the testing room, the minor demographic quirks of the undergraduates they tested.", "tokens": [51071, 814, 11918, 1314, 264, 1900, 47602, 295, 264, 8984, 41095, 11, 264, 2685, 22997, 4292, 295, 264, 4997, 1808, 11, 264, 6696, 26331, 35645, 1694, 295, 264, 14295, 27710, 436, 8246, 13, 51511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06500593983397192, "compression_ratio": 1.7472527472527473, "no_speech_prob": 1.8255369004654964e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 210232, "start": 2125.6000000000004, "end": 2128.84, "text": " They published the photograph of the cake, but they threw away the recipe.", "tokens": [51529, 814, 6572, 264, 8348, 295, 264, 5908, 11, 457, 436, 11918, 1314, 264, 6782, 13, 51691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06500593983397192, "compression_ratio": 1.7472527472527473, "no_speech_prob": 1.8255369004654964e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 212884, "start": 2128.84, "end": 2136.98, "text": " And when a future researcher tried to execute the continuation, and they tried to replicate the study, they encountered a massive ontological deficit.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 562, 257, 2027, 21751, 3031, 281, 14483, 264, 29357, 11, 293, 436, 3031, 281, 25356, 264, 2979, 11, 436, 20381, 257, 5994, 6592, 4383, 22132, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07804725621197675, "compression_ratio": 1.6297872340425532, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983126280816329e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 212884, "start": 2137.52, "end": 2139.6800000000003, "text": " The essential causal distinctions were gone.", "tokens": [50799, 440, 7115, 38755, 1483, 49798, 645, 2780, 13, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07804725621197675, "compression_ratio": 1.6297872340425532, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983126280816329e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 212884, "start": 2139.92, "end": 2143.54, "text": " The original authors weren't necessarily acting in malicious bad faith.", "tokens": [50919, 440, 3380, 16552, 4999, 380, 4725, 6577, 294, 33496, 1578, 4522, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07804725621197675, "compression_ratio": 1.6297872340425532, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983126280816329e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 212884, "start": 2143.6600000000003, "end": 2149.26, "text": " They were simply optimizing their data retention for an academic system that rewarded publication over replication.", "tokens": [51106, 814, 645, 2935, 40425, 641, 1412, 22871, 337, 364, 7778, 1185, 300, 29105, 19953, 670, 39911, 13, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07804725621197675, "compression_ratio": 1.6297872340425532, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983126280816329e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 214926, "start": 2149.26, "end": 2165.94, "text": " The recent movement toward open data, pre-registration of hypotheses, and publishing raw data sets is essentially the scientific community waking up, realizing it had assumed the wrong distribution of future queries, and frantically adjusting its lambda dial to require less compression.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 5162, 3963, 7361, 1269, 1412, 11, 659, 12, 48933, 2405, 295, 49969, 11, 293, 17832, 8936, 1412, 6352, 307, 4476, 264, 8134, 1768, 20447, 493, 11, 16734, 309, 632, 15895, 264, 2085, 7316, 295, 2027, 24109, 11, 293, 431, 49505, 23559, 1080, 13607, 5502, 281, 3651, 1570, 19355, 13, 51199], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12156927017938524, "compression_ratio": 1.6644951140065147, "no_speech_prob": 2.0280335570610486e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 214926, "start": 2166.5, "end": 2168.88, "text": " It is a systemic correction of an ontological deficit.", "tokens": [51227, 467, 307, 257, 23789, 19984, 295, 364, 6592, 4383, 22132, 13, 51346], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12156927017938524, "compression_ratio": 1.6644951140065147, "no_speech_prob": 2.0280335570610486e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 214926, "start": 2169.28, "end": 2174.0200000000004, "text": " But this revelation leads us to the final, unsettling shift in flictions trilogy.", "tokens": [51366, 583, 341, 23456, 6689, 505, 281, 264, 2572, 11, 43964, 1688, 5513, 294, 932, 15607, 34030, 13, 51603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12156927017938524, "compression_ratio": 1.6644951140065147, "no_speech_prob": 2.0280335570610486e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 214926, "start": 2174.48, "end": 2178.86, "text": " The postscript of the third essay reveals the ultimate limit of all this elegant math.", "tokens": [51626, 440, 12300, 5944, 295, 264, 2636, 16238, 20893, 264, 9705, 4948, 295, 439, 341, 21117, 5221, 13, 51845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12156927017938524, "compression_ratio": 1.6644951140065147, "no_speech_prob": 2.0280335570610486e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 217886, "start": 2178.86, "end": 2190.48, "text": " If the entire value of our memories, whether it's digital code, biological synapses, or scientific journals, depends entirely on what the future is going to ask of them, who gets to decide what the future looks like?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 2302, 2158, 295, 527, 8495, 11, 1968, 309, 311, 4562, 3089, 11, 13910, 5451, 2382, 279, 11, 420, 8134, 29621, 11, 5946, 7696, 322, 437, 264, 2027, 307, 516, 281, 1029, 295, 552, 11, 567, 2170, 281, 4536, 437, 264, 2027, 1542, 411, 30, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11529539371358938, "compression_ratio": 1.6768707482993197, "no_speech_prob": 2.176103915119132e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 217886, "start": 2190.6400000000003, "end": 2192.1, "text": " This raises an important question.", "tokens": [50954, 639, 19658, 364, 1021, 1168, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11529539371358938, "compression_ratio": 1.6768707482993197, "no_speech_prob": 2.176103915119132e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 217886, "start": 2192.6200000000003, "end": 2199.7000000000003, "text": " The entire rate distortion framework relies on a variable called pi, the assumed probability distribution of future continuations.", "tokens": [51053, 440, 2302, 3314, 28426, 8388, 30910, 322, 257, 7006, 1219, 3895, 11, 264, 15895, 8482, 7316, 295, 2027, 2993, 763, 13, 51407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11529539371358938, "compression_ratio": 1.6768707482993197, "no_speech_prob": 2.176103915119132e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 217886, "start": 2200.2200000000003, "end": 2202.2200000000003, "text": " But pi is not a physical law.", "tokens": [51433, 583, 3895, 307, 406, 257, 4001, 2101, 13, 51533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11529539371358938, "compression_ratio": 1.6768707482993197, "no_speech_prob": 2.176103915119132e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 217886, "start": 2202.5, "end": 2203.3, "text": " It is a forecast.", "tokens": [51547, 467, 307, 257, 14330, 13, 51587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11529539371358938, "compression_ratio": 1.6768707482993197, "no_speech_prob": 2.176103915119132e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 217886, "start": 2203.82, "end": 2204.6, "text": " It is a guess.", "tokens": [51613, 467, 307, 257, 2041, 13, 51652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11529539371358938, "compression_ratio": 1.6768707482993197, "no_speech_prob": 2.176103915119132e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 217886, "start": 2204.84, "end": 2207.1400000000003, "text": " A piece of history isn't objectively important.", "tokens": [51664, 316, 2522, 295, 2503, 1943, 380, 46067, 1021, 13, 51779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11529539371358938, "compression_ratio": 1.6768707482993197, "no_speech_prob": 2.176103915119132e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 220714, "start": 2207.14, "end": 2211.64, "text": " The temperature of the room during a psychology experiment isn't inherently valuable.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 4292, 295, 264, 1808, 1830, 257, 15105, 5120, 1943, 380, 27993, 8263, 13, 50590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14419600168863933, "compression_ratio": 1.6640625, "no_speech_prob": 2.1931625352605844e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 220714, "start": 2212.02, "end": 2218.14, "text": " It only becomes relevant because some system or some human being values the continuation that depends on it.", "tokens": [50609, 467, 787, 3643, 7340, 570, 512, 1185, 420, 512, 1952, 885, 4190, 264, 29357, 300, 5946, 322, 309, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14419600168863933, "compression_ratio": 1.6640625, "no_speech_prob": 2.1931625352605844e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 220714, "start": 2218.42, "end": 2224.1, "text": " This shifts the entire problem away from computer science, away from thermodynamics, and into the realm of preference.", "tokens": [50929, 639, 19201, 264, 2302, 1154, 1314, 490, 3820, 3497, 11, 1314, 490, 8810, 35483, 11, 293, 666, 264, 15355, 295, 17502, 13, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14419600168863933, "compression_ratio": 1.6640625, "no_speech_prob": 2.1931625352605844e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 220714, "start": 2224.94, "end": 2228.02, "text": " Git's designers value the ability to revert bad code.", "tokens": [51255, 16939, 311, 16196, 2158, 264, 3485, 281, 319, 3281, 1578, 3089, 13, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14419600168863933, "compression_ratio": 1.6640625, "no_speech_prob": 2.1931625352605844e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 220714, "start": 2228.56, "end": 2231.3799999999997, "text": " Compliance officers value the ability to survive an audit.", "tokens": [51436, 33736, 6276, 9199, 2158, 264, 3485, 281, 7867, 364, 17748, 13, 51577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14419600168863933, "compression_ratio": 1.6640625, "no_speech_prob": 2.1931625352605844e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 223138, "start": 2231.38, "end": 2238.36, "text": " Evolution shaped the human brain to value physical survival and caloric efficiency over perfect photographic recall.", "tokens": [50365, 40800, 13475, 264, 1952, 3567, 281, 2158, 4001, 12559, 293, 2104, 16345, 10493, 670, 2176, 8348, 299, 9901, 13, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14303208434063455, "compression_ratio": 1.1958762886597938, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810628831828936e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 223836, "start": 2238.36, "end": 2246.6200000000003, "text": " So at the very bottom of the equations, beneath the C++ compilers, beneath the neural networks, it all just boils down to what we care about.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 412, 264, 588, 2767, 295, 264, 11787, 11, 17149, 264, 383, 25472, 715, 388, 433, 11, 17149, 264, 18161, 9590, 11, 309, 439, 445, 35049, 760, 281, 437, 321, 1127, 466, 13, 50778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10578655374461207, "compression_ratio": 1.6017316017316017, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524500068258567e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 223836, "start": 2246.76, "end": 2247.08, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50785, 1079, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10578655374461207, "compression_ratio": 1.6017316017316017, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524500068258567e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 223836, "start": 2247.56, "end": 2254.6200000000003, "text": " The mathematics of compression can tell you exactly how to optimally discard information, but they cannot tell you what you should value.", "tokens": [50825, 440, 18666, 295, 19355, 393, 980, 291, 2293, 577, 281, 5028, 379, 31597, 1589, 11, 457, 436, 2644, 980, 291, 437, 291, 820, 2158, 13, 51178], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10578655374461207, "compression_ratio": 1.6017316017316017, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524500068258567e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 223836, "start": 2255.4, "end": 2259.8, "text": " Choosing what to value is an estimation problem, and the target is constantly moving.", "tokens": [51217, 12366, 6110, 437, 281, 2158, 307, 364, 35701, 1154, 11, 293, 264, 3779, 307, 6460, 2684, 13, 51437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10578655374461207, "compression_ratio": 1.6017316017316017, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524500068258567e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 225980, "start": 2259.8, "end": 2269.32, "text": " If society decides tomorrow that individual privacy is fundamentally more important than algorithmic convenience, the pie distribution of the entire tech industry changes overnight.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 4086, 14898, 4153, 300, 2609, 11427, 307, 17879, 544, 1021, 813, 9284, 299, 19283, 11, 264, 1730, 7316, 295, 264, 2302, 7553, 3518, 2962, 13935, 13, 50841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15606313056134163, "compression_ratio": 1.4793814432989691, "no_speech_prob": 2.0923976527115196e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 225980, "start": 2270.0, "end": 2275.5, "text": " Suddenly, all their highly optimized compressed behavioral profiles become massive continuation deficits.", "tokens": [50875, 21194, 11, 439, 641, 5405, 26941, 30353, 19124, 23693, 1813, 5994, 29357, 49616, 13, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15606313056134163, "compression_ratio": 1.4793814432989691, "no_speech_prob": 2.0923976527115196e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 227550, "start": 2275.5, "end": 2280.22, "text": " Consider the implications as we hand more power to artificial intelligence.", "tokens": [50365, 17416, 264, 16602, 382, 321, 1011, 544, 1347, 281, 11677, 7599, 13, 50601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10411546744552314, "compression_ratio": 1.629251700680272, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173080669840134e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 227550, "start": 2281.02, "end": 2290.86, "text": " If an AI system is given the autonomy to choose its own pie found to predict what futures are valuable, it dictates what parts of our human history are worth retaining.", "tokens": [50641, 759, 364, 7318, 1185, 307, 2212, 264, 27278, 281, 2826, 1080, 1065, 1730, 1352, 281, 6069, 437, 26071, 366, 8263, 11, 309, 12569, 1024, 437, 3166, 295, 527, 1952, 2503, 366, 3163, 34936, 13, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10411546744552314, "compression_ratio": 1.629251700680272, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173080669840134e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 227550, "start": 2291.18, "end": 2292.44, "text": " Yeah, that's a chilling thought.", "tokens": [51149, 865, 11, 300, 311, 257, 31047, 1194, 13, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10411546744552314, "compression_ratio": 1.629251700680272, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173080669840134e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 227550, "start": 2292.44, "end": 2304.72, "text": " If an AI decides that a certain nuance of human emotion or cultural tradition has a near-zero probability of being useful for its optimized continuations, it will compress it away as statistical noise.", "tokens": [51212, 759, 364, 7318, 14898, 300, 257, 1629, 42625, 295, 1952, 8913, 420, 6988, 6994, 575, 257, 2651, 12, 32226, 8482, 295, 885, 4420, 337, 1080, 26941, 2993, 763, 11, 309, 486, 14778, 309, 1314, 382, 22820, 5658, 13, 51826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10411546744552314, "compression_ratio": 1.629251700680272, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173080669840134e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 230472, "start": 2304.72, "end": 2308.66, "text": " It would systematically create ontological deficits for humanity.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 576, 39531, 1884, 6592, 4383, 49616, 337, 10243, 13, 50562], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1299478049590209, "compression_ratio": 1.618421052631579, "no_speech_prob": 2.2191963978263063e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 230472, "start": 2309.1, "end": 2313.5, "text": " We would lose the very vocabulary needed to express what the machine discarded.", "tokens": [50584, 492, 576, 3624, 264, 588, 19864, 2978, 281, 5109, 437, 264, 3479, 45469, 13, 50804], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1299478049590209, "compression_ratio": 1.618421052631579, "no_speech_prob": 2.2191963978263063e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 230472, "start": 2314.3399999999997, "end": 2316.9399999999996, "text": " Retention is the ultimate expression of preference.", "tokens": [50846, 11495, 1251, 307, 264, 9705, 6114, 295, 17502, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1299478049590209, "compression_ratio": 1.618421052631579, "no_speech_prob": 2.2191963978263063e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 230472, "start": 2317.56, "end": 2322.18, "text": " When you choose what to remember, you are actively choosing what kind of future you are willing to inhabit.", "tokens": [51007, 1133, 291, 2826, 437, 281, 1604, 11, 291, 366, 13022, 10875, 437, 733, 295, 2027, 291, 366, 4950, 281, 21863, 13, 51238], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1299478049590209, "compression_ratio": 1.618421052631579, "no_speech_prob": 2.2191963978263063e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 230472, "start": 2322.66, "end": 2324.68, "text": " We have journeyed a massive distance today.", "tokens": [51262, 492, 362, 4671, 292, 257, 5994, 4560, 965, 13, 51363], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1299478049590209, "compression_ratio": 1.618421052631579, "no_speech_prob": 2.2191963978263063e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 230472, "start": 2324.8799999999997, "end": 2333.22, "text": " We started with the petty frustrations of compiling C++ code, uncovered the fundamental thermodynamic truths hidden in SpherePOP's primitives,", "tokens": [51373, 492, 1409, 365, 264, 39334, 7454, 12154, 295, 715, 4883, 383, 25472, 3089, 11, 37729, 264, 8088, 8810, 34988, 30079, 7633, 294, 318, 6605, 47, 12059, 311, 2886, 38970, 11, 51790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1299478049590209, "compression_ratio": 1.618421052631579, "no_speech_prob": 2.2191963978263063e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 233322, "start": 2333.22, "end": 2339.52, "text": " mapped the mathematics of compression onto the human brain, and finally arrived at the philosophy of human preference.", "tokens": [50365, 33318, 264, 18666, 295, 19355, 3911, 264, 1952, 3567, 11, 293, 2721, 6678, 412, 264, 10675, 295, 1952, 17502, 13, 50680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10765391648417771, "compression_ratio": 1.6977611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 2.117599932210945e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 233322, "start": 2339.52, "end": 2343.58, "text": " And we discovered that a compressed state is not the enemy of history.", "tokens": [50680, 400, 321, 6941, 300, 257, 30353, 1785, 307, 406, 264, 5945, 295, 2503, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10765391648417771, "compression_ratio": 1.6977611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 2.117599932210945e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 233322, "start": 2344.12, "end": 2349.52, "text": " It is simply history that has been optimized for a very specific, fiercely protected future.", "tokens": [50910, 467, 307, 2935, 2503, 300, 575, 668, 26941, 337, 257, 588, 2685, 11, 16334, 42879, 10594, 2027, 13, 51180], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10765391648417771, "compression_ratio": 1.6977611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 2.117599932210945e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 233322, "start": 2349.74, "end": 2353.66, "text": " And we saw that complexity in our tools is rarely essential.", "tokens": [51191, 400, 321, 1866, 300, 14024, 294, 527, 3873, 307, 13752, 7115, 13, 51387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10765391648417771, "compression_ratio": 1.6977611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 2.117599932210945e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 233322, "start": 2354.7999999999997, "end": 2361.9599999999996, "text": " Most often, it is just the unmanaged historical residue of systems that never learned how to forget gracefully.", "tokens": [51444, 4534, 2049, 11, 309, 307, 445, 264, 517, 1601, 2980, 8584, 34799, 295, 3652, 300, 1128, 3264, 577, 281, 2870, 10042, 2277, 13, 51802], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10765391648417771, "compression_ratio": 1.6977611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 2.117599932210945e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 236196, "start": 2361.96, "end": 2366.26, "text": " Think about the personal retention policies you execute every single day.", "tokens": [50365, 6557, 466, 264, 2973, 22871, 7657, 291, 14483, 633, 2167, 786, 13, 50580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11779815047534543, "compression_ratio": 1.6966966966966968, "no_speech_prob": 1.8470164633854758e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 236196, "start": 2366.38, "end": 2367.06, "text": " Oh, absolutely.", "tokens": [50586, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 50620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11779815047534543, "compression_ratio": 1.6966966966966968, "no_speech_prob": 1.8470164633854758e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 236196, "start": 2367.44, "end": 2370.56, "text": " When you pull out your phone to record a concert instead of just watching it.", "tokens": [50639, 1133, 291, 2235, 484, 428, 2593, 281, 2136, 257, 8543, 2602, 295, 445, 1976, 309, 13, 50795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11779815047534543, "compression_ratio": 1.6966966966966968, "no_speech_prob": 1.8470164633854758e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 236196, "start": 2370.8, "end": 2373.14, "text": " When you hold on to a bitter grudge against a friend.", "tokens": [50807, 1133, 291, 1797, 322, 281, 257, 13871, 677, 16032, 1970, 257, 1277, 13, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11779815047534543, "compression_ratio": 1.6966966966966968, "no_speech_prob": 1.8470164633854758e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 236196, "start": 2373.36, "end": 2376.7, "text": " Or when you quickly delete an old photo because it makes you cringe.", "tokens": [50935, 1610, 562, 291, 2661, 12097, 364, 1331, 5052, 570, 309, 1669, 291, 47081, 13, 51102], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11779815047534543, "compression_ratio": 1.6966966966966968, "no_speech_prob": 1.8470164633854758e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 236196, "start": 2377.16, "end": 2380.8, "text": " You are making a mathematical bet on what your future self will need to query.", "tokens": [51125, 509, 366, 1455, 257, 18894, 778, 322, 437, 428, 2027, 2698, 486, 643, 281, 14581, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11779815047534543, "compression_ratio": 1.6966966966966968, "no_speech_prob": 1.8470164633854758e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 236196, "start": 2381.4, "end": 2385.66, "text": " You are continually compressing the chaotic, high-fidelity history of your present life", "tokens": [51337, 509, 366, 22277, 14778, 278, 264, 27013, 11, 1090, 12, 69, 33343, 2503, 295, 428, 1974, 993, 51550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11779815047534543, "compression_ratio": 1.6966966966966968, "no_speech_prob": 1.8470164633854758e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 236196, "start": 2385.66, "end": 2388.7400000000002, "text": " into a tightly-bound state that you hope will serve you tomorrow.", "tokens": [51550, 666, 257, 21952, 12, 18767, 1785, 300, 291, 1454, 486, 4596, 291, 4153, 13, 51704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11779815047534543, "compression_ratio": 1.6966966966966968, "no_speech_prob": 1.8470164633854758e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 236196, "start": 2388.94, "end": 2390.6, "text": " You are constantly guessing your own pie.", "tokens": [51714, 509, 366, 6460, 17939, 428, 1065, 1730, 13, 51797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11779815047534543, "compression_ratio": 1.6966966966966968, "no_speech_prob": 1.8470164633854758e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 239060, "start": 2390.6, "end": 2396.16, "text": " The next time you make a choice to throw something away, whether it is a digital file, a box in", "tokens": [50365, 440, 958, 565, 291, 652, 257, 3922, 281, 3507, 746, 1314, 11, 1968, 309, 307, 257, 4562, 3991, 11, 257, 2424, 294, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10192298889160156, "compression_ratio": 1.5657370517928286, "no_speech_prob": 1.9356324269109