nd honestly,", "tokens": [51538, 428, 881, 7148, 14100, 11, 428, 6239, 48155, 589, 7555, 11, 293, 6095, 11, 51791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07891362288902545, "compression_ratio": 1.703448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 8.325314721467636e-13}, {"id": 6, "seek": 2852, "start": 28.52, "end": 32.64, "text": " the most advanced technologies on earth are silently turning into traps.", "tokens": [50365, 264, 881, 7339, 7943, 322, 4120, 366, 40087, 6246, 666, 24173, 13, 50571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09256325780817892, "compression_ratio": 1.6070287539936101, "no_speech_prob": 1.0943365354523782e-12}, {"id": 7, "seek": 2852, "start": 33.2, "end": 37.12, "text": " Yeah. We're exploring why things become fundamentally unrepairable and why that", "tokens": [50599, 865, 13, 492, 434, 12736, 983, 721, 1813, 17879, 517, 19919, 1246, 712, 293, 983, 300, 50795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09256325780817892, "compression_ratio": 1.6070287539936101, "no_speech_prob": 1.0943365354523782e-12}, {"id": 8, "seek": 2852, "start": 37.12, "end": 40.92, "text": " unrepairability isn't a mistake, but like a direct consequence of success.", "tokens": [50795, 517, 19919, 1246, 2310, 1943, 380, 257, 6146, 11, 457, 411, 257, 2047, 18326, 295, 2245, 13, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09256325780817892, "compression_ratio": 1.6070287539936101, "no_speech_prob": 1.0943365354523782e-12}, {"id": 9, "seek": 2852, "start": 41.08, "end": 46.68, "text": " Exactly. So welcome to a deep dive that will completely dismantle how you think about building", "tokens": [50993, 7587, 13, 407, 2928, 281, 257, 2452, 9192, 300, 486, 2584, 30506, 306, 577, 291, 519, 466, 2390, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09256325780817892, "compression_ratio": 1.6070287539936101, "no_speech_prob": 1.0943365354523782e-12}, {"id": 10, "seek": 2852, "start": 46.68, "end": 50.68, "text": " and maintaining the systems that run your world. It's a phenomenal paradox, really. I mean,", "tokens": [51273, 293, 14916, 264, 3652, 300, 1190, 428, 1002, 13, 467, 311, 257, 17778, 26221, 11, 534, 13, 286, 914, 11, 51473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09256325780817892, "compression_ratio": 1.6070287539936101, "no_speech_prob": 1.0943365354523782e-12}, {"id": 11, "seek": 2852, "start": 50.7, "end": 56.72, "text": " we spend our lives, our entire careers trying to compress messy reality into these clean", "tokens": [51474, 321, 3496, 527, 2909, 11, 527, 2302, 16409, 1382, 281, 14778, 16191, 4103, 666, 613, 2541, 51775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09256325780817892, "compression_ratio": 1.6070287539936101, "no_speech_prob": 1.0943365354523782e-12}, {"id": 12, "seek": 5672, "start": 56.72, "end": 61.86, "text": " functioning rules. Right. Like the perfect morning routine or a flawless piece of software.", "tokens": [50365, 18483, 4474, 13, 1779, 13, 1743, 264, 2176, 2446, 9927, 420, 257, 45693, 2522, 295, 4722, 13, 50622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11060296226950253, "compression_ratio": 1.5368852459016393, "no_speech_prob": 1.976782019325052e-12}, {"id": 13, "seek": 5672, "start": 62.28, "end": 67.64, "text": " Exactly. Or the ultimate corporate workflow. And when those things suddenly stop working and", "tokens": [50643, 7587, 13, 1610, 264, 9705, 10896, 20993, 13, 400, 562, 729, 721, 5800, 1590, 1364, 293, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11060296226950253, "compression_ratio": 1.5368852459016393, "no_speech_prob": 1.976782019325052e-12}, {"id": 14, "seek": 5672, "start": 67.64, "end": 71.5, "text": " we're just left staring at them completely helpless, we usually blame ourselves.", "tokens": [50911, 321, 434, 445, 1411, 18043, 412, 552, 2584, 27596, 11, 321, 2673, 10127, 4175, 13, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11060296226950253, "compression_ratio": 1.5368852459016393, "no_speech_prob": 1.976782019325052e-12}, {"id": 15, "seek": 5672, "start": 72.06, "end": 76.6, "text": " Yeah. We think, uh, we just didn't write good enough instructions or we didn't plan for", "tokens": [51132, 865, 13, 492, 519, 11, 2232, 11, 321, 445, 994, 380, 2464, 665, 1547, 9415, 420, 321, 994, 380, 1393, 337, 51359], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11060296226950253, "compression_ratio": 1.5368852459016393, "no_speech_prob": 1.976782019325052e-12}, {"id": 16, "seek": 5672, "start": 76.6, "end": 77.56, "text": " enough contingencies.", "tokens": [51359, 1547, 27820, 6464, 13, 51407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11060296226950253, "compression_ratio": 1.5368852459016393, "no_speech_prob": 1.976782019325052e-12}, {"id": 17, "seek": 7756, "start": 77.56, "end": 82.88, "text": " But the reality, as we're going to explore today, is that the moment you compress a history of trial", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 4103, 11, 382, 321, 434, 516, 281, 6839, 965, 11, 307, 300, 264, 1623, 291, 14778, 257, 2503, 295, 7308, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10078510519576399, "compression_ratio": 1.5302325581395348, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356307584383667e-12}, {"id": 18, "seek": 7756, "start": 82.88, "end": 88.7, "text": " and error into a perfectly efficient function, you are actively destroying the exact information", "tokens": [50631, 293, 6713, 666, 257, 6239, 7148, 2445, 11, 291, 366, 13022, 19926, 264, 1900, 1589, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10078510519576399, "compression_ratio": 1.5302325581395348, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356307584383667e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 7756, "start": 88.7, "end": 90.44, "text": " you will need to diagnose it later.", "tokens": [50922, 291, 486, 643, 281, 36238, 309, 1780, 13, 51009], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10078510519576399, "compression_ratio": 1.5302325581395348, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356307584383667e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 7756, "start": 90.68, "end": 95.76, "text": " So our source material for this exploration is this remarkable paper. It was published in July,", "tokens": [51021, 407, 527, 4009, 2527, 337, 341, 16197, 307, 341, 12802, 3035, 13, 467, 390, 6572, 294, 7370, 11, 51275], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10078510519576399, "compression_ratio": 1.5302325581395348, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356307584383667e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 9576, "start": 95.76, "end": 103.14, "text": " 2026, by Fliction, titled Diagnostic Coordinates and the Time of Repair. A correction to the", "tokens": [50365, 945, 10880, 11, 538, 3235, 4105, 11, 19841, 8789, 4535, 19634, 39620, 1024, 293, 264, 6161, 295, 3696, 1246, 13, 316, 19984, 281, 264, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19062003739383243, "compression_ratio": 1.49645390070922, "no_speech_prob": 1.694505755329978e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 9576, "start": 103.14, "end": 104.18, "text": " anti-alignment theorem.", "tokens": [50734, 6061, 12, 304, 41134, 20904, 13, 50786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19062003739383243, "compression_ratio": 1.49645390070922, "no_speech_prob": 1.694505755329978e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 9576, "start": 104.82000000000001, "end": 109.32000000000001, "text": " The terminology sounds incredibly academic, I know, but the mechanics they describe apply", "tokens": [50818, 440, 27575, 3263, 6252, 7778, 11, 286, 458, 11, 457, 264, 12939, 436, 6786, 3079, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19062003739383243, "compression_ratio": 1.49645390070922, "no_speech_prob": 1.694505755329978e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 9576, "start": 109.32000000000001, "end": 110.58000000000001, "text": " to literally everything.", "tokens": [51043, 281, 3736, 1203, 13, 51106], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19062003739383243, "compression_ratio": 1.49645390070922, "no_speech_prob": 1.694505755329978e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 9576, "start": 110.80000000000001, "end": 115.28, "text": " From like a grandmother's sourdough recipe to a multi-billion dollar satellite, right?", "tokens": [51117, 3358, 411, 257, 14317, 311, 11006, 67, 581, 6782, 281, 257, 4825, 12, 65, 11836, 7241, 16016, 11, 558, 30, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19062003739383243, "compression_ratio": 1.49645390070922, "no_speech_prob": 1.694505755329978e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 9576, "start": 115.28, "end": 119.86000000000001, "text": " Yep. All the way down to the physical memory cells inside the device you're using right now.", "tokens": [51341, 7010, 13, 1057, 264, 636, 760, 281, 264, 4001, 4675, 5438, 1854, 264, 4302, 291, 434, 1228, 558, 586, 13, 51570], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19062003739383243, "compression_ratio": 1.49645390070922, "no_speech_prob": 1.694505755329978e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 9576, "start": 119.94, "end": 120.56, "text": " It's wild.", "tokens": [51574, 467, 311, 4868, 13, 51605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19062003739383243, "compression_ratio": 1.49645390070922, "no_speech_prob": 1.694505755329978e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 12056, "start": 120.56, "end": 125.08, "text": " Our mission today is to uncover the hidden variables that dictate whether a broken system", "tokens": [50365, 2621, 4447, 965, 307, 281, 21694, 264, 7633, 9102, 300, 36071, 1968, 257, 5463, 1185, 50591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0873451154094097, "compression_ratio": 1.6497005988023952, "no_speech_prob": 1.2447841151938532e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 12056, "start": 125.08, "end": 128.5, "text": " can be saved or if it just has to be abandoned entirely.", "tokens": [50591, 393, 312, 6624, 420, 498, 309, 445, 575, 281, 312, 13732, 7696, 13, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0873451154094097, "compression_ratio": 1.6497005988023952, "no_speech_prob": 1.2447841151938532e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 12056, "start": 128.92000000000002, "end": 132.88, "text": " To really understand the correction this paper is making, though, we have to start by establishing", "tokens": [50783, 1407, 534, 1223, 264, 19984, 341, 3035, 307, 1455, 11, 1673, 11, 321, 362, 281, 722, 538, 22494, 50981], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0873451154094097, "compression_ratio": 1.6497005988023952, "no_speech_prob": 1.2447841151938532e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 12056, "start": 132.88, "end": 137.12, "text": " a baseline. We need to look at the original theorem that Fliction is responding to.", "tokens": [50981, 257, 20518, 13, 492, 643, 281, 574, 412, 264, 3380, 20904, 300, 3235, 4105, 307, 16670, 281, 13, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0873451154094097, "compression_ratio": 1.6497005988023952, "no_speech_prob": 1.2447841151938532e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 12056, "start": 137.28, "end": 138.88, "text": " Right. The anti-alignment theorem.", "tokens": [51201, 1779, 13, 440, 6061, 12, 304, 41134, 20904, 13, 51281], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0873451154094097, "compression_ratio": 1.6497005988023952, "no_speech_prob": 1.2447841151938532e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 12056, "start": 139.08, "end": 144.9, "text": " Exactly. This emerged from previous work focused on a concept called history before function.", "tokens": [51291, 7587, 13, 639, 20178, 490, 3894, 589, 5178, 322, 257, 3410, 1219, 2503, 949, 2445, 13, 51582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0873451154094097, "compression_ratio": 1.6497005988023952, "no_speech_prob": 1.2447841151938532e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 12056, "start": 144.9, "end": 149.82, "text": " Which basically means that every functional thing in our world, what the literature calls an", "tokens": [51582, 3013, 1936, 1355, 300, 633, 11745, 551, 294, 527, 1002, 11, 437, 264, 10394, 5498, 364, 51828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0873451154094097, "compression_ratio": 1.6497005988023952, "no_speech_prob": 1.2447841151938532e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 14982, "start": 149.82, "end": 152.9, "text": " operator, starts as this messy history of events.", "tokens": [50365, 12973, 11, 3719, 382, 341, 16191, 2503, 295, 3931, 13, 50519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13039098845587838, "compression_ratio": 1.6292134831460674, "no_speech_prob": 3.0436256813481943e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 14982, "start": 153.29999999999998, "end": 158.45999999999998, "text": " Right. Think of early civilizations figuring out agriculture. It's, you know, centuries", "tokens": [50539, 1779, 13, 6557, 295, 2440, 40749, 15213, 484, 14837, 13, 467, 311, 11, 291, 458, 11, 13926, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13039098845587838, "compression_ratio": 1.6292134831460674, "no_speech_prob": 3.0436256813481943e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 14982, "start": 158.45999999999998, "end": 165.26, "text": " of planting at the wrong time, using the wrong soil, crops dying, starving, trying again.", "tokens": [50797, 295, 20585, 412, 264, 2085, 565, 11, 1228, 264, 2085, 6704, 11, 16829, 8639, 11, 28420, 11, 1382, 797, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13039098845587838, "compression_ratio": 1.6292134831460674, "no_speech_prob": 3.0436256813481943e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 14982, "start": 165.38, "end": 167.2, "text": " There's a massive chaotic history.", "tokens": [51143, 821, 311, 257, 5994, 27013, 2503, 13, 51234], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13039098845587838, "compression_ratio": 1.6292134831460674, "no_speech_prob": 3.0436256813481943e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 14982, "start": 167.2, "end": 172.9, "text": " But eventually, they figure it out. They compress thousands of years of agonizing trial and error", "tokens": [51234, 583, 4728, 11, 436, 2573, 309, 484, 13, 814, 14778, 5383, 295, 924, 295, 623, 266, 3319, 7308, 293, 6713, 51519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13039098845587838, "compression_ratio": 1.6292134831460674, "no_speech_prob": 3.0436256813481943e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 14982, "start": 172.9, "end": 174.82, "text": " into a simple farmer's almanac.", "tokens": [51519, 666, 257, 2199, 17891, 311, 419, 1601, 326, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13039098845587838, "compression_ratio": 1.6292134831460674, "no_speech_prob": 3.0436256813481943e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 14982, "start": 175.0, "end": 177.24, "text": " Like plant the seeds after the last frost.", "tokens": [51624, 1743, 3709, 264, 9203, 934, 264, 1036, 19623, 13, 51736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13039098845587838, "compression_ratio": 1.6292134831460674, "no_speech_prob": 3.0436256813481943e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 17724, "start": 177.24, "end": 182.4, "text": " Exactly. That rule is the operator. It's incredibly efficient. You don't need to starve for three", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 663, 4978, 307, 264, 12973, 13, 467, 311, 6252, 7148, 13, 509, 500, 380, 643, 281, 46755, 337, 1045, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09817585192228619, "compression_ratio": 1.5980392156862746, "no_speech_prob": 1.427140740653532e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 17724, "start": 182.4, "end": 186.52, "text": " generations to know when to plant the wheat. You just read the rule and execute it.", "tokens": [50623, 10593, 281, 458, 562, 281, 3709, 264, 16691, 13, 509, 445, 1401, 264, 4978, 293, 14483, 309, 13, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09817585192228619, "compression_ratio": 1.5980392156862746, "no_speech_prob": 1.427140740653532e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 17724, "start": 186.68, "end": 190.94, "text": " And that compression is necessary, right? I mean, if you couldn't compress history into operators,", "tokens": [50837, 400, 300, 19355, 307, 4818, 11, 558, 30, 286, 914, 11, 498, 291, 2809, 380, 14778, 2503, 666, 19077, 11, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09817585192228619, "compression_ratio": 1.5980392156862746, "no_speech_prob": 1.427140740653532e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 17724, "start": 191.16, "end": 195.24, "text": " we'd have to relearn the laws of physics from scratch every single morning.", "tokens": [51061, 321, 1116, 362, 281, 2951, 1083, 264, 6064, 295, 10649, 490, 8459, 633, 2167, 2446, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09817585192228619, "compression_ratio": 1.5980392156862746, "no_speech_prob": 1.427140740653532e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 17724, "start": 195.46, "end": 201.38, "text": " We'd never get anything done. But the anti-alignment theorem takes this mathematically rigorous look", "tokens": [51276, 492, 1116, 1128, 483, 1340, 1096, 13, 583, 264, 6061, 12, 304, 41134, 20904, 2516, 341, 44003, 29882, 574, 51572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09817585192228619, "compression_ratio": 1.5980392156862746, "no_speech_prob": 1.427140740653532e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 17724, "start": 201.38, "end": 203.12, "text": " at that process of compression.", "tokens": [51572, 412, 300, 1399, 295, 19355, 13, 51659], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09817585192228619, "compression_ratio": 1.5980392156862746, "no_speech_prob": 1.427140740653532e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 20312, "start": 203.12, "end": 209.44, "text": " And it proves that the most efficient compression of a history into a function generically maximizes", "tokens": [50365, 400, 309, 25019, 300, 264, 881, 7148, 19355, 295, 257, 2503, 666, 257, 2445, 1337, 984, 5138, 5660, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12503651472238395, "compression_ratio": 1.549618320610687, "no_speech_prob": 1.2738381313312508e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 20312, "start": 209.44, "end": 211.70000000000002, "text": " a property called repair entropy.", "tokens": [50681, 257, 4707, 1219, 10535, 30867, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12503651472238395, "compression_ratio": 1.549618320610687, "no_speech_prob": 1.2738381313312508e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 20312, "start": 212.02, "end": 215.08, "text": " Yeah. Let's translate that. Let's make repair entropy tangible.", "tokens": [50810, 865, 13, 961, 311, 13799, 300, 13, 961, 311, 652, 10535, 30867, 27094, 13, 50963], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12503651472238395, "compression_ratio": 1.549618320610687, "no_speech_prob": 1.2738381313312508e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 20312, "start": 215.36, "end": 220.08, "text": " Okay. So, say I walk into my kitchen, I flip the light switch, and the light doesn't turn on.", "tokens": [50977, 1033, 13, 407, 11, 584, 286, 1792, 666, 452, 6525, 11, 286, 7929, 264, 1442, 3679, 11, 293, 264, 1442, 1177, 380, 1261, 322, 13, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12503651472238395, "compression_ratio": 1.549618320610687, "no_speech_prob": 1.2738381313312508e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 20312, "start": 220.46, "end": 222.52, "text": " I have a certain number of hypotheses, right?", "tokens": [51232, 286, 362, 257, 1629, 1230, 295, 49969, 11, 558, 30, 51335], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12503651472238395, "compression_ratio": 1.549618320610687, "no_speech_prob": 1.2738381313312508e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 20312, "start": 222.56, "end": 226.28, "text": " Sure. The bulb is dead, the breaker tripped, the wiring burned out.", "tokens": [51337, 4894, 13, 440, 21122, 307, 3116, 11, 264, 35375, 1376, 3320, 11, 264, 27520, 13490, 484, 13, 51523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12503651472238395, "compression_ratio": 1.549618320610687, "no_speech_prob": 1.2738381313312508e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 22628, "start": 226.28, "end": 231.68, "text": " All right. The whole city power grid is down. The log count of all those possible fault hypotheses,", "tokens": [50365, 1057, 558, 13, 440, 1379, 2307, 1347, 10748, 307, 760, 13, 440, 3565, 1207, 295, 439, 729, 1944, 7441, 49969, 11, 50635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11214794582790799, "compression_ratio": 1.5737704918032787, "no_speech_prob": 1.1067321104701877e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 22628, "start": 232.32, "end": 237.52, "text": " and my inability to distinguish between them based on just that one symptom, is my repair entropy.", "tokens": [50667, 293, 452, 33162, 281, 20206, 1296, 552, 2361, 322, 445, 300, 472, 29370, 11, 307, 452, 10535, 30867, 13, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11214794582790799, "compression_ratio": 1.5737704918032787, "no_speech_prob": 1.1067321104701877e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 22628, "start": 237.68, "end": 242.78, "text": " That is a perfect visualization. If your repair entropy is high, you are staring at this", "tokens": [50935, 663, 307, 257, 2176, 25801, 13, 759, 428, 10535, 30867, 307, 1090, 11, 291, 366, 18043, 412, 341, 51190], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11214794582790799, "compression_ratio": 1.5737704918032787, "no_speech_prob": 1.1067321104701877e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 22628, "start": 242.78, "end": 247.5, "text": " massive, undifferentiated list of potential causes for a single failure.", "tokens": [51190, 5994, 11, 674, 15790, 72, 770, 1329, 295, 3995, 7700, 337, 257, 2167, 7763, 13, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11214794582790799, "compression_ratio": 1.5737704918032787, "no_speech_prob": 1.1067321104701877e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 22628, "start": 247.66, "end": 248.64, "text": " You're basically blind.", "tokens": [51434, 509, 434, 1936, 6865, 13, 51483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11214794582790799, "compression_ratio": 1.5737704918032787, "no_speech_prob": 1.1067321104701877e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 24864, "start": 248.64, "end": 252.95999999999998, "text": " Completely blind. The anti-alignment theorem demonstrates that making an operator run", "tokens": [50365, 39978, 6865, 13, 440, 6061, 12, 304, 41134, 20904, 31034, 300, 1455, 364, 12973, 1190, 50581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12120837791293275, "compression_ratio": 1.68561872909699, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325085171892904e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 24864, "start": 252.95999999999998, "end": 257.74, "text": " perfectly means intentionally throwing away what it calls diagnostic surplus.", "tokens": [50581, 6239, 1355, 22062, 10238, 1314, 437, 309, 5498, 27897, 31019, 13, 50820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12120837791293275, "compression_ratio": 1.68561872909699, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325085171892904e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 24864, "start": 258.08, "end": 262.09999999999997, "text": " And diagnostic surplus is like all the extra context, the nuanced distinctions.", "tokens": [50837, 400, 27897, 31019, 307, 411, 439, 264, 2857, 4319, 11, 264, 45115, 1483, 49798, 13, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12120837791293275, "compression_ratio": 1.68561872909699, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325085171892904e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 24864, "start": 262.53999999999996, "end": 266.41999999999996, "text": " Yeah. All the failed experiments that were discarded because they weren't strictly necessary", "tokens": [51060, 865, 13, 1057, 264, 7612, 12050, 300, 645, 45469, 570, 436, 4999, 380, 20792, 4818, 51254], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12120837791293275, "compression_ratio": 1.68561872909699, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325085171892904e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 24864, "start": 266.41999999999996, "end": 268.84, "text": " for the final successful execution.", "tokens": [51254, 337, 264, 2572, 4406, 15058, 13, 51375], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12120837791293275, "compression_ratio": 1.68561872909699, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325085171892904e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 24864, "start": 269.21999999999997, "end": 271.74, "text": " I see this happen in corporate environments all the time, honestly.", "tokens": [51394, 286, 536, 341, 1051, 294, 10896, 12388, 439, 264, 565, 11, 6095, 13, 51520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12120837791293275, "compression_ratio": 1.68561872909699, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325085171892904e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 24864, "start": 271.96, "end": 276.56, "text": " A team spends six months building a complex marketing strategy.", "tokens": [51531, 316, 1469, 25620, 2309, 2493, 2390, 257, 3997, 6370, 5206, 13, 51761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12120837791293275, "compression_ratio": 1.68561872909699, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325085171892904e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 27656, "start": 276.56, "end": 280.2, "text": " Right. They debate a hundred approaches, run A-B tests.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 814, 7958, 257, 3262, 11587, 11, 1190, 316, 12, 33, 6921, 13, 50547], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0840296561901386, "compression_ratio": 1.5658362989323844, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553893893335835e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 27656, "start": 280.28000000000003, "end": 287.64, "text": " Exactly. And finally, they distill all that messy history into a pristine, one-page standard", "tokens": [50551, 7587, 13, 400, 2721, 11, 436, 42923, 439, 300, 16191, 2503, 666, 257, 582, 42745, 11, 472, 12, 15161, 3832, 50919], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0840296561901386, "compression_ratio": 1.5658362989323844, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553893893335835e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 27656, "start": 287.64, "end": 290.76, "text": " operating procedure. Step one, step two, step three.", "tokens": [50919, 7447, 10747, 13, 5470, 472, 11, 1823, 732, 11, 1823, 1045, 13, 51075], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0840296561901386, "compression_ratio": 1.5658362989323844, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553893893335835e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 27656, "start": 291.02, "end": 294.52, "text": " And then they delete the Slack channels and archive the brainstorming docs.", "tokens": [51088, 400, 550, 436, 12097, 264, 37211, 9235, 293, 23507, 264, 35245, 278, 45623, 13, 51263], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0840296561901386, "compression_ratio": 1.5658362989323844, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553893893335835e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 27656, "start": 294.62, "end": 300.18, "text": " Yeah. Because they want the new hires to just blindly follow the optimized SOP, they're", "tokens": [51268, 865, 13, 1436, 436, 528, 264, 777, 276, 3145, 281, 445, 47744, 1524, 264, 26941, 10621, 47, 11, 436, 434, 51546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0840296561901386, "compression_ratio": 1.5658362989323844, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553893893335835e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 27656, "start": 300.18, "end": 304.84000000000003, "text": " intentionally throwing away the diagnostic surplus to maximize efficiency.", "tokens": [51546, 22062, 10238, 1314, 264, 27897, 31019, 281, 19874, 10493, 13, 51779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0840296561901386, "compression_ratio": 1.5658362989323844, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553893893335835e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 30484, "start": 304.84, "end": 308.88, "text": " And by doing so, they guarantee that when the market shifts and step two stops generating", "tokens": [50365, 400, 538, 884, 370, 11, 436, 10815, 300, 562, 264, 2142, 19201, 293, 1823, 732, 10094, 17746, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06061260874678449, "compression_ratio": 1.691358024691358, "no_speech_prob": 2.158824768255796e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 30484, "start": 308.88, "end": 312.28, "text": " leads, the new hires will have absolutely no idea how to fix it.", "tokens": [50567, 6689, 11, 264, 777, 276, 3145, 486, 362, 3122, 572, 1558, 577, 281, 3191, 309, 13, 50737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06061260874678449, "compression_ratio": 1.691358024691358, "no_speech_prob": 2.158824768255796e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 30484, "start": 312.58, "end": 314.84, "text": " Execution and diagnosis are mathematically opposed.", "tokens": [50752, 17662, 1448, 293, 15217, 366, 44003, 8851, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06061260874678449, "compression_ratio": 1.691358024691358, "no_speech_prob": 2.158824768255796e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 30484, "start": 314.97999999999996, "end": 319.35999999999996, "text": " They really are. To be ruthlessly efficient at executing a function, a system must become", "tokens": [50872, 814, 534, 366, 13, 1407, 312, 38225, 12048, 7148, 412, 32368, 257, 2445, 11, 257, 1185, 1633, 1813, 51091], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06061260874678449, "compression_ratio": 1.691358024691358, "no_speech_prob": 2.158824768255796e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 30484, "start": 319.35999999999996, "end": 323.0, "text": " deeply impoverished at explaining why the function exists in the first place.", "tokens": [51091, 8760, 704, 3570, 4729, 412, 13468, 983, 264, 2445, 8198, 294, 264, 700, 1081, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06061260874678449, "compression_ratio": 1.691358024691358, "no_speech_prob": 2.158824768255796e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 30484, "start": 323.2, "end": 328.29999999999995, "text": " So the retained material that makes a system bloated and slow, that's the exact same material", "tokens": [51283, 407, 264, 33438, 2527, 300, 1669, 257, 1185, 1749, 770, 293, 2964, 11, 300, 311, 264, 1900, 912, 2527, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06061260874678449, "compression_ratio": 1.691358024691358, "no_speech_prob": 2.158824768255796e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 30484, "start": 328.29999999999995, "end": 332.62, "text": " that would let you cross off incorrect fault hypotheses when the system breaks.", "tokens": [51538, 300, 576, 718, 291, 3278, 766, 18424, 7441, 49969, 562, 264, 1185, 9857, 13, 51754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06061260874678449, "compression_ratio": 1.691358024691358, "no_speech_prob": 2.158824768255796e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 33262, "start": 332.62, "end": 338.08, "text": " Precisely. So the original theorem paints a pretty dark picture. It basically states that", "tokens": [50365, 48746, 736, 13, 407, 264, 3380, 20904, 28076, 257, 1238, 2877, 3036, 13, 467, 1936, 4368, 300, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08611589670181274, "compression_ratio": 1.5559701492537314, "no_speech_prob": 1.7411058489055775e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 33262, "start": 338.08, "end": 340.8, "text": " every efficient system is born with a fatal flaw.", "tokens": [50638, 633, 7148, 1185, 307, 4232, 365, 257, 24069, 13717, 13, 50774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08611589670181274, "compression_ratio": 1.5559701492537314, "no_speech_prob": 1.7411058489055775e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 33262, "start": 341.0, "end": 344.76, "text": " Just by virtue of being optimized, it's inherently hostile to being repaired.", "tokens": [50784, 1449, 538, 20816, 295, 885, 26941, 11, 309, 311, 27993, 27312, 281, 885, 36551, 13, 50972], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08611589670181274, "compression_ratio": 1.5559701492537314, "no_speech_prob": 1.7411058489055775e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 33262, "start": 345.04, "end": 350.64, "text": " Right. But this is where Flixian's new paper steps in and just completely upends the board.", "tokens": [50986, 1779, 13, 583, 341, 307, 689, 3235, 970, 952, 311, 777, 3035, 4439, 294, 293, 445, 2584, 493, 2581, 264, 3150, 13, 51266], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08611589670181274, "compression_ratio": 1.5559701492537314, "no_speech_prob": 1.7411058489055775e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 33262, "start": 350.76, "end": 355.98, "text": " Because if the original theorem is universally true, nothing complex would ever survive a single", "tokens": [51272, 1436, 498, 264, 3380, 20904, 307, 43995, 2074, 11, 1825, 3997, 576, 1562, 7867, 257, 2167, 51533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08611589670181274, "compression_ratio": 1.5559701492537314, "no_speech_prob": 1.7411058489055775e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 33262, "start": 355.98, "end": 356.42, "text": " breakdown.", "tokens": [51533, 18188, 13, 51555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08611589670181274, "compression_ratio": 1.5559701492537314, "no_speech_prob": 1.7411058489055775e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 35642, "start": 356.42, "end": 362.34000000000003, "text": " Exactly. Flixian looked at the math of the anti-alignment theorem and found a massive", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 3235, 970, 952, 2956, 412, 264, 5221, 295, 264, 6061, 12, 304, 41134, 20904, 293, 1352, 257, 5994, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09182480785334221, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.4750735315437478e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 35642, "start": 362.34000000000003, "end": 367.22, "text": " unexamined blind spot that warps our entire understanding of how systems fail.", "tokens": [50661, 11572, 335, 2001, 6865, 4008, 300, 1516, 1878, 527, 2302, 3701, 295, 577, 3652, 3061, 13, 50905], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09182480785334221, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.4750735315437478e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 35642, "start": 367.3, "end": 369.3, "text": " Okay, let's unpack this. What is the blind spot?", "tokens": [50909, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 26699, 341, 13, 708, 307, 264, 6865, 4008, 30, 51009], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09182480785334221, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.4750735315437478e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 35642, "start": 369.6, "end": 375.3, "text": " It's something Flixian calls the synchrony assumption. It's a subtle but devastating flaw in", "tokens": [51024, 467, 311, 746, 3235, 970, 952, 5498, 264, 19331, 88, 15302, 13, 467, 311, 257, 13743, 457, 21280, 13717, 294, 51309], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09182480785334221, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.4750735315437478e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 35642, "start": 375.3, "end": 377.56, "text": " how the previous literature applied the math.", "tokens": [51309, 577, 264, 3894, 10394, 6456, 264, 5221, 13, 51422], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09182480785334221, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.4750735315437478e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 35642, "start": 377.76, "end": 382.66, "text": " Well, the original theorem assumes that the information you possess at the exact moment you", "tokens": [51432, 1042, 11, 264, 3380, 20904, 37808, 300, 264, 1589, 291, 17490, 412, 264, 1900, 1623, 291, 51677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09182480785334221, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.4750735315437478e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 38266, "start": 382.66, "end": 388.5, "text": " finish compressing the system, the trace evaluated at compression time, is the exact same information", "tokens": [50365, 2413, 14778, 278, 264, 1185, 11, 264, 13508, 25509, 412, 19355, 565, 11, 307, 264, 1900, 912, 1589, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10113144874572753, "compression_ratio": 1.668, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356161217090381e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 38266, "start": 388.5, "end": 390.90000000000003, "text": " you will possess when you actually need to repair it.", "tokens": [50657, 291, 486, 17490, 562, 291, 767, 643, 281, 10535, 309, 13, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10113144874572753, "compression_ratio": 1.668, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356161217090381e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 38266, "start": 391.08000000000004, "end": 393.1, "text": " Wait, that makes no sense in the real world.", "tokens": [50786, 3802, 11, 300, 1669, 572, 2020, 294, 264, 957, 1002, 13, 50887], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10113144874572753, "compression_ratio": 1.668, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356161217090381e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 38266, "start": 393.20000000000005, "end": 394.02000000000004, "text": " No, it doesn't.", "tokens": [50892, 883, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 13, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10113144874572753, "compression_ratio": 1.668, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356161217090381e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 38266, "start": 394.24, "end": 401.14000000000004, "text": " That's like evaluating the usefulness of a car's repair manual strictly at the exact second the", "tokens": [50944, 663, 311, 411, 27479, 264, 4420, 1287, 295, 257, 1032, 311, 10535, 9688, 20792, 412, 264, 1900, 1150, 264, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10113144874572753, "compression_ratio": 1.668, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356161217090381e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 38266, "start": 401.14000000000004, "end": 405.90000000000003, "text": " car rolls off the assembly line in Detroit while the engineers who designed it are standing right", "tokens": [51289, 1032, 15767, 766, 264, 12103, 1622, 294, 20887, 1339, 264, 11955, 567, 4761, 309, 366, 4877, 558, 51527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10113144874572753, "compression_ratio": 1.668, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356161217090381e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 38266, "start": 405.90000000000003, "end": 406.16, "text": " there.", "tokens": [51527, 456, 13, 51540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10113144874572753, "compression_ratio": 1.668, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356161217090381e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 40616, "start": 406.16, "end": 411.12, "text": " It completely ignores what happens to that car and that manual when it breaks down on", "tokens": [50365, 467, 2584, 5335, 2706, 437, 2314, 281, 300, 1032, 293, 300, 9688, 562, 309, 9857, 760, 322, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041198798588344, "compression_ratio": 1.6920415224913494, "no_speech_prob": 1.7074184947840632e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 40616, "start": 411.12, "end": 413.68, "text": " a dirt road in a different country ten years later.", "tokens": [50613, 257, 11483, 3060, 294, 257, 819, 1941, 2064, 924, 1780, 13, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041198798588344, "compression_ratio": 1.6920415224913494, "no_speech_prob": 1.7074184947840632e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 40616, "start": 413.68, "end": 417.52000000000004, "text": " Right. So the theorem assumes we instantly break what we just built.", "tokens": [50741, 1779, 13, 407, 264, 20904, 37808, 321, 13518, 1821, 437, 321, 445, 3094, 13, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041198798588344, "compression_ratio": 1.6920415224913494, "no_speech_prob": 1.7074184947840632e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 40616, "start": 417.52000000000004, "end": 420.8, "text": " You've hit on the exact absurdity Flixian is highlighting.", "tokens": [50933, 509, 600, 2045, 322, 264, 1900, 19774, 507, 3235, 970, 952, 307, 26551, 13, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041198798588344, "compression_ratio": 1.6920415224913494, "no_speech_prob": 1.7074184947840632e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 40616, "start": 421.52000000000004, "end": 425.6, "text": " The synchrony assumption evaluates repairability strictly at the system's birth.", "tokens": [51133, 440, 19331, 88, 15302, 6133, 1024, 10535, 2310, 20792, 412, 264, 1185, 311, 3965, 13, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041198798588344, "compression_ratio": 1.6920415224913494, "no_speech_prob": 1.7074184947840632e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 40616, "start": 425.6, "end": 430.48, "text": " By mathematically treating the information at compression as identical to the information at", "tokens": [51337, 3146, 44003, 15083, 264, 1589, 412, 19355, 382, 14800, 281, 264, 1589, 412, 51581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041198798588344, "compression_ratio": 1.6920415224913494, "no_speech_prob": 1.7074184947840632e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 40616, "start": 430.48, "end": 433.92, "text": " repair, it locks the system's fate to its origin.", "tokens": [51581, 10535, 11, 309, 20703, 264, 1185, 311, 12738, 281, 1080, 4957, 13, 51753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041198798588344, "compression_ratio": 1.6920415224913494, "no_speech_prob": 1.7074184947840632e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 43392, "start": 433.92, "end": 439.38, "text": " Yeah, it assumes a system's capacity to be diagnosed is just a static, unchanging property", "tokens": [50365, 865, 11, 309, 37808, 257, 1185, 311, 6042, 281, 312, 16899, 307, 445, 257, 13437, 11, 517, 27123, 4707, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12398285335964626, "compression_ratio": 1.596551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496199379765429e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 43392, "start": 439.38, "end": 440.82, "text": " fits the moment it's created.", "tokens": [50638, 9001, 264, 1623, 309, 311, 2942, 13, 50710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12398285335964626, "compression_ratio": 1.596551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496199379765429e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 43392, "start": 441.48, "end": 447.38, "text": " And because the academic literature relied on that assumption for so long, it ended up dividing", "tokens": [50743, 400, 570, 264, 7778, 10394, 35463, 322, 300, 15302, 337, 370, 938, 11, 309, 4590, 493, 26764, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12398285335964626, "compression_ratio": 1.596551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496199379765429e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 43392, "start": 447.38, "end": 451.86, "text": " the entire world of systems into two incredibly rigid categories, right?", "tokens": [51038, 264, 2302, 1002, 295, 3652, 666, 732, 6252, 22195, 10479, 11, 558, 30, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12398285335964626, "compression_ratio": 1.596551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496199379765429e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 43392, "start": 451.98, "end": 458.32, "text": " Yes, the two-class picture. This dominated the field. On one side, you had history-first systems.", "tokens": [51268, 1079, 11, 264, 732, 12, 11665, 3036, 13, 639, 23755, 264, 2519, 13, 1282, 472, 1252, 11, 291, 632, 2503, 12, 29581, 3652, 13, 51585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12398285335964626, "compression_ratio": 1.596551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496199379765429e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 43392, "start": 458.46000000000004, "end": 462.3, "text": " Meaning systems that evolve organically through unrecorded trial and error.", "tokens": [51592, 19948, 3652, 300, 16693, 1798, 984, 807, 517, 38500, 292, 7308, 293, 6713, 13, 51784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12398285335964626, "compression_ratio": 1.596551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496199379765429e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 46230, "start": 462.3, "end": 469.1, "text": " Exactly. Biological adaptations, folk traditions, common law legal precedents, or, you know,", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 13007, 4383, 44465, 11, 15748, 15643, 11, 2689, 2101, 5089, 16969, 791, 11, 420, 11, 291, 458, 11, 50705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1678891991669277, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.714475891985423e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 46230, "start": 469.1, "end": 470.86, "text": " ancient shipbuilding techniques.", "tokens": [50705, 7832, 5374, 28126, 7512, 13, 50793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1678891991669277, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.714475891985423e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 46230, "start": 470.86, "end": 476.46000000000004, "text": " Because these systems are compressed purely for immediate survival and execution, they throw", "tokens": [50793, 1436, 613, 3652, 366, 30353, 17491, 337, 11629, 12559, 293, 15058, 11, 436, 3507, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1678891991669277, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.714475891985423e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 46230, "start": 476.46000000000004, "end": 478.54, "text": " away their diagnostic surplus immediately.", "tokens": [51073, 1314, 641, 27897, 31019, 4258, 13, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1678891991669277, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.714475891985423e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 46230, "start": 478.54, "end": 483.58000000000004, "text": " Right. The ancient shipbuilder knows the hole needs a specific shape so it doesn't capsize.", "tokens": [51177, 1779, 13, 440, 7832, 5374, 11516, 260, 3255, 264, 5458, 2203, 257, 2685, 3909, 370, 309, 1177, 380, 13855, 1125, 13, 51429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1678891991669277, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.714475891985423e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 46230, "start": 483.58000000000004, "end": 486.14, "text": " But they didn't write down the fluid dynamics equations.", "tokens": [51429, 583, 436, 994, 380, 2464, 760, 264, 9113, 15679, 11787, 13, 51557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1678891991669277, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.714475891985423e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 46230, "start": 486.14, "end": 488.38, "text": " They just know that if you shape it differently, you drown.", "tokens": [51557, 814, 445, 458, 300, 498, 291, 3909, 309, 7614, 11, 291, 20337, 13, 51669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1678891991669277, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.714475891985423e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 48838, "start": 488.38, "end": 494.06, "text": " Exactly. Under the synchrony assumption, history-first systems are viewed as inherently unrepairable", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 6974, 264, 19331, 88, 15302, 11, 2503, 12, 29581, 3652, 366, 19174, 382, 27993, 517, 19919, 1246, 712, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1416402023829771, "compression_ratio": 1.5622489959839359, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813176285240816e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 48838, "start": 494.06, "end": 494.62, "text": " from birth.", "tokens": [50649, 490, 3965, 13, 50677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1416402023829771, "compression_ratio": 1.5622489959839359, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813176285240816e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 48838, "start": 494.94, "end": 498.48, "text": " Because their trace at compression is already empty of diagnostic coordinates.", "tokens": [50693, 1436, 641, 13508, 412, 19355, 307, 1217, 6707, 295, 27897, 21056, 13, 50870], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1416402023829771, "compression_ratio": 1.5622489959839359, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813176285240816e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 48838, "start": 498.62, "end": 503.88, "text": " Yeah. Yeah. If the water density changes or the wood type changes, the shipbuilder doesn't", "tokens": [50877, 865, 13, 865, 13, 759, 264, 1281, 10305, 2962, 420, 264, 4576, 2010, 2962, 11, 264, 5374, 11516, 260, 1177, 380, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1416402023829771, "compression_ratio": 1.5622489959839359, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813176285240816e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 48838, "start": 503.88, "end": 508.94, "text": " have the underlying theory to diagnose why the new ships are sinking. The knowledge is purely", "tokens": [51140, 362, 264, 14217, 5261, 281, 36238, 983, 264, 777, 11434, 366, 28148, 13, 440, 3601, 307, 17491, 51393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1416402023829771, "compression_ratio": 1.5622489959839359, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813176285240816e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 48838, "start": 508.94, "end": 509.58, "text": " operational.", "tokens": [51393, 16607, 13, 51425], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1416402023829771, "compression_ratio": 1.5622489959839359, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813176285240816e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 50958, "start": 509.58, "end": 512.62, "text": " Okay. So that's the first class. History-first systems.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 407, 300, 311, 264, 700, 1508, 13, 12486, 12, 29581, 3652, 13, 50517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15017083426502265, "compression_ratio": 1.6277372262773722, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556634535591641e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 50958, "start": 512.62, "end": 513.5, "text": " Mm-hmm.", "tokens": [50517, 8266, 12, 10250, 13, 50561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15017083426502265, "compression_ratio": 1.6277372262773722, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556634535591641e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 50958, "start": 513.5, "end": 518.54, "text": " Basically born bad at being repaired. But then there's the second class, which the literature", "tokens": [50561, 8537, 4232, 1578, 412, 885, 36551, 13, 583, 550, 456, 311, 264, 1150, 1508, 11, 597, 264, 10394, 50813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15017083426502265, "compression_ratio": 1.6277372262773722, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556634535591641e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 50958, "start": 518.54, "end": 520.14, "text": " treated as the gold standard.", "tokens": [50813, 8668, 382, 264, 3821, 3832, 13, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15017083426502265, "compression_ratio": 1.6277372262773722, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556634535591641e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 50958, "start": 520.14, "end": 526.14, "text": " Theory-first systems. These are the engineered marvels of the modern world. Software architecture,", "tokens": [50893, 29009, 12, 29581, 3652, 13, 1981, 366, 264, 38648, 23893, 82, 295, 264, 4363, 1002, 13, 27428, 9482, 11, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15017083426502265, "compression_ratio": 1.6277372262773722, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556634535591641e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 50958, "start": 526.14, "end": 528.6999999999999, "text": " bridge designs, aerospace engineering.", "tokens": [51193, 7283, 11347, 11, 46817, 7043, 13, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15017083426502265, "compression_ratio": 1.6277372262773722, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556634535591641e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 50958, "start": 528.6999999999999, "end": 533.18, "text": " Because these systems don't emerge from blind trial and error, right? They're derived from explicit", "tokens": [51321, 1436, 613, 3652, 500, 380, 21511, 490, 6865, 7308, 293, 6713, 11, 558, 30, 814, 434, 18949, 490, 13691, 51545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15017083426502265, "compression_ratio": 1.6277372262773722, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556634535591641e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 50958, "start": 533.18, "end": 534.14, "text": " mathematical theory.", "tokens": [51545, 18894, 5261, 13, 51593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15017083426502265, "compression_ratio": 1.6277372262773722, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556634535591641e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 53414, "start": 534.14, "end": 539.26, "text": " Yeah. They come with blueprints, documented derivations, and formalized design constraints.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 814, 808, 365, 888, 23547, 47523, 11, 23007, 10151, 763, 11, 293, 9860, 1602, 1715, 18491, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08837315530487985, "compression_ratio": 1.7007874015748032, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487860339184368e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 53414, "start": 539.26, "end": 544.62, "text": " And because the derivation is written down as the system is built, the assumption was that the", "tokens": [50621, 400, 570, 264, 10151, 399, 307, 3720, 760, 382, 264, 1185, 307, 3094, 11, 264, 15302, 390, 300, 264, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08837315530487985, "compression_ratio": 1.7007874015748032, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487860339184368e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 53414, "start": 544.62, "end": 549.18, "text": " diagnostic surplus is never discarded. You wrote the blueprint, so you always have the blueprint.", "tokens": [50889, 27897, 31019, 307, 1128, 45469, 13, 509, 4114, 264, 35868, 11, 370, 291, 1009, 362, 264, 35868, 13, 51117], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08837315530487985, "compression_ratio": 1.7007874015748032, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487860339184368e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 53414, "start": 549.18, "end": 555.1, "text": " You know the exact load-bearing capacity of every steel beam, not because you broke 100 beams", "tokens": [51117, 509, 458, 264, 1900, 3677, 12, 650, 1921, 6042, 295, 633, 8269, 14269, 11, 406, 570, 291, 6902, 2319, 31040, 51413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08837315530487985, "compression_ratio": 1.7007874015748032, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487860339184368e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 53414, "start": 555.1, "end": 557.5, "text": " to test them, but because you calculated the physics.", "tokens": [51413, 281, 1500, 552, 11, 457, 570, 291, 15598, 264, 10649, 13, 51533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08837315530487985, "compression_ratio": 1.7007874015748032, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487860339184368e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 55750, "start": 557.5, "end": 563.34, "text": " So under the old two-class picture, theory-first systems were considered permanently repairable.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 833, 264, 1331, 732, 12, 11665, 3036, 11, 5261, 12, 29581, 3652, 645, 4888, 24042, 10535, 712, 13, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07519004691360343, "compression_ratio": 1.6048632218844985, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427257112042406e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 55750, "start": 563.34, "end": 567.82, "text": " Right. Because they were born with a robust set of diagnostic coordinates,", "tokens": [50657, 1779, 13, 1436, 436, 645, 4232, 365, 257, 13956, 992, 295, 27897, 21056, 11, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07519004691360343, "compression_ratio": 1.6048632218844985, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427257112042406e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 55750, "start": 567.82, "end": 571.42, "text": " the synchrony assumption dictated they would always possess those coordinates.", "tokens": [50881, 264, 19331, 88, 15302, 12569, 770, 436, 576, 1009, 17490, 729, 21056, 13, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07519004691360343, "compression_ratio": 1.6048632218844985, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427257112042406e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 55750, "start": 571.42, "end": 577.02, "text": " But Fliction points out that this is a complete fantasy. Origin alone does not predict outcome.", "tokens": [51061, 583, 3235, 4105, 2793, 484, 300, 341, 307, 257, 3566, 13861, 13, 45313, 3312, 775, 406, 6069, 9700, 13, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07519004691360343, "compression_ratio": 1.6048632218844985, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427257112042406e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 55750, "start": 577.02, "end": 581.58, "text": " Exactly. And I want to break down how Fliction actually proves this mathematically,", "tokens": [51341, 7587, 13, 400, 286, 528, 281, 1821, 760, 577, 3235, 4105, 767, 25019, 341, 44003, 11, 51569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07519004691360343, "compression_ratio": 1.6048632218844985, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427257112042406e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 55750, "start": 581.58, "end": 584.62, "text": " without getting bogged down in reading formulas like a textbook.", "tokens": [51569, 1553, 1242, 26132, 3004, 760, 294, 3760, 30546, 411, 257, 25591, 13, 51721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07519004691360343, "compression_ratio": 1.6048632218844985, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427257112042406e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 55750, "start": 584.62, "end": 586.54, "text": " Please, yes, keep it accessible.", "tokens": [51721, 2555, 11, 2086, 11, 1066, 309, 9515, 13, 51817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07519004691360343, "compression_ratio": 1.6048632218844985, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427257112042406e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 58654, "start": 586.54, "end": 589.66, "text": " The paper sets out to prove that losing information,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3035, 6352, 484, 281, 7081, 300, 7027, 1589, 11, 50521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06615442388197955, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.3621115913946555e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 58654, "start": 589.66, "end": 594.14, "text": " regardless of how your system was born, is the true driver of unrepairability.", "tokens": [50521, 10060, 295, 577, 428, 1185, 390, 4232, 11, 307, 264, 2074, 6787, 295, 517, 19919, 1246, 2310, 13, 50745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06615442388197955, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.3621115913946555e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 58654, "start": 594.6999999999999, "end": 598.6999999999999, "text": " The mechanism is actually quite intuitive once you strip away the symbols.", "tokens": [50773, 440, 7513, 307, 767, 1596, 21769, 1564, 291, 12828, 1314, 264, 16944, 13, 50973], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06615442388197955, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.3621115913946555e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 58654, "start": 598.6999999999999, "end": 602.6999999999999, "text": " Okay. Let's look at the relationship between the symptom you observe,", "tokens": [50973, 1033, 13, 961, 311, 574, 412, 264, 2480, 1296, 264, 29370, 291, 11441, 11, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06615442388197955, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.3621115913946555e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 58654, "start": 602.6999999999999, "end": 607.0999999999999, "text": " the trace of information you hold, and the resulting difficulty of the repair.", "tokens": [51173, 264, 13508, 295, 1589, 291, 1797, 11, 293, 264, 16505, 10360, 295, 264, 10535, 13, 51393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06615442388197955, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.3621115913946555e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 58654, "start": 607.0999999999999, "end": 612.62, "text": " Right. The paper proves that if you take your current pool of knowledge, your trace,", "tokens": [51393, 1779, 13, 440, 3035, 25019, 300, 498, 291, 747, 428, 2190, 7005, 295, 3601, 11, 428, 13508, 11, 51669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06615442388197955, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.3621115913946555e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 61262, "start": 612.62, "end": 618.46, "text": " and you delete even a single diagnostic coordinate, your repair difficulty fundamentally increases.", "tokens": [50365, 293, 291, 12097, 754, 257, 2167, 27897, 15670, 11, 428, 10535, 10360, 17879, 8637, 13, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12117166661504489, "compression_ratio": 1.5495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.927219018052484e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 61262, "start": 618.46, "end": 624.22, "text": " Wait. Let's define what a diagnostic coordinate actually is here. It's not like a GPS coordinate on a map.", "tokens": [50657, 3802, 13, 961, 311, 6964, 437, 257, 27897, 15670, 767, 307, 510, 13, 467, 311, 406, 411, 257, 19462, 15670, 322, 257, 4471, 13, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12117166661504489, "compression_ratio": 1.5495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.927219018052484e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 61262, "start": 624.22, "end": 630.14, "text": " No, no. It's a specific piece of retained information that allows you to distinguish between two different", "tokens": [50945, 883, 11, 572, 13, 467, 311, 257, 2685, 2522, 295, 33438, 1589, 300, 4045, 291, 281, 20206, 1296, 732, 819, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12117166661504489, "compression_ratio": 1.5495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.927219018052484e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 63014, "start": 630.14, "end": 633.26, "text": " possible histories that could have caused the failure.", "tokens": [50365, 1944, 30631, 300, 727, 362, 7008, 264, 7763, 13, 50521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515711545944214, "compression_ratio": 1.2307692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490828242202936e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 63014, "start": 633.26, "end": 639.1, "text": " Right. Think of a medical diagnosis. A patient comes in with a fever. That's the symptom.", "tokens": [50521, 1779, 13, 6557, 295, 257, 4625, 15217, 13, 316, 4537, 1487, 294, 365, 257, 18277, 13, 663, 311, 264, 29370, 13, 50813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515711545944214, "compression_ratio": 1.2307692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490828242202936e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 63910, "start": 639.1, "end": 643.66, "text": " The fever could be caused by a bacterial infection or a viral infection.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 18277, 727, 312, 7008, 538, 257, 35632, 11764, 420, 257, 16132, 11764, 13, 50593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10311451639447894, "compression_ratio": 1.6281407035175879, "no_speech_prob": 1.1643805494440662e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 63910, "start": 643.66, "end": 648.94, "text": " So the doctor orders a white blood cell count. That test result is a diagnostic coordinate.", "tokens": [50593, 407, 264, 4631, 9470, 257, 2418, 3390, 2815, 1207, 13, 663, 1500, 1874, 307, 257, 27897, 15670, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10311451639447894, "compression_ratio": 1.6281407035175879, "no_speech_prob": 1.1643805494440662e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 63910, "start": 648.94, "end": 654.62, "text": " Exactly. Its entire mathematical function is to draw a line between the bacterial history", "tokens": [50857, 7587, 13, 6953, 2302, 18894, 2445, 307, 281, 2642, 257, 1622, 1296, 264, 35632, 2503, 51141], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10311451639447894, "compression_ratio": 1.6281407035175879, "no_speech_prob": 1.1643805494440662e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 63910, "start": 654.62, "end": 658.38, "text": " and the viral history, allowing the doctor to eliminate one entirely.", "tokens": [51141, 293, 264, 16132, 2503, 11, 8293, 264, 4631, 281, 13819, 472, 7696, 13, 51329], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10311451639447894, "compression_ratio": 1.6281407035175879, "no_speech_prob": 1.1643805494440662e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 65838, "start": 658.38, "end": 663.74, "text": " So what Flickshen's math demonstrates is that if you lose that coordinate, like if the hospital", "tokens": [50365, 407, 437, 3235, 618, 2716, 268, 311, 5221, 31034, 307, 300, 498, 291, 3624, 300, 15670, 11, 411, 498, 264, 4530, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11285100533412053, "compression_ratio": 1.6058394160583942, "no_speech_prob": 1.4781934357110948e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 65838, "start": 663.74, "end": 668.3, "text": " loses the test result, your list of potential causes cannot possibly shrink.", "tokens": [50633, 18293, 264, 1500, 1874, 11, 428, 1329, 295, 3995, 7700, 2644, 6264, 23060, 13, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11285100533412053, "compression_ratio": 1.6058394160583942, "no_speech_prob": 1.4781934357110948e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 65838, "start": 668.3, "end": 673.26, "text": " Losing information can never rule out a false hypothesis. It can only merge distinct", "tokens": [50861, 441, 6110, 1589, 393, 1128, 4978, 484, 257, 7908, 17291, 13, 467, 393, 787, 22183, 10644, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11285100533412053, "compression_ratio": 1.6058394160583942, "no_speech_prob": 1.4781934357110948e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 65838, "start": 673.26, "end": 677.66, "text": " possibilities back together into a blurry, undifferentiated blob.", "tokens": [51109, 12178, 646, 1214, 666, 257, 37644, 11, 674, 15790, 72, 770, 46115, 13, 51329], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11285100533412053, "compression_ratio": 1.6058394160583942, "no_speech_prob": 1.4781934357110948e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 65838, "start": 677.66, "end": 681.98, "text": " You used to know it was a virus. Now you just know it's a virus or bacteria.", "tokens": [51329, 509, 1143, 281, 458, 309, 390, 257, 5752, 13, 823, 291, 445, 458, 309, 311, 257, 5752, 420, 11763, 13, 51545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11285100533412053, "compression_ratio": 1.6058394160583942, "no_speech_prob": 1.4781934357110948e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 65838, "start": 681.98, "end": 683.9, "text": " Your repair entropy strictly increases.", "tokens": [51545, 2260, 10535, 30867, 20792, 8637, 13, 51641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11285100533412053, "compression_ratio": 1.6058394160583942, "no_speech_prob": 1.4781934357110948e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 68390, "start": 683.9, "end": 689.74, "text": " And this brings us back to the flaw in the original theorem. The anti-alignment theorem wasn't wrong", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 5607, 505, 646, 281, 264, 13717, 294, 264, 3380, 20904, 13, 440, 6061, 12, 304, 41134, 20904, 2067, 380, 2085, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08604052460309371, "compression_ratio": 1.6115107913669064, "no_speech_prob": 1.455283268024521e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 68390, "start": 689.74, "end": 695.9, "text": " in its mechanics. It was just a special, highly constrained case where the repair happens to occur", "tokens": [50657, 294, 1080, 12939, 13, 467, 390, 445, 257, 2121, 11, 5405, 38901, 1389, 689, 264, 10535, 2314, 281, 5160, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08604052460309371, "compression_ratio": 1.6115107913669064, "no_speech_prob": 1.455283268024521e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 68390, "start": 695.9, "end": 700.78, "text": " immediately after the compression. Like a special law of physics that only applies inside a vacuum.", "tokens": [50965, 4258, 934, 264, 19355, 13, 1743, 257, 2121, 2101, 295, 10649, 300, 787, 13165, 1854, 257, 14224, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08604052460309371, "compression_ratio": 1.6115107913669064, "no_speech_prob": 1.455283268024521e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 68390, "start": 700.78, "end": 705.66, "text": " Exactly. But we don't live in a vacuum. We live in a world governed by time.", "tokens": [51209, 7587, 13, 583, 321, 500, 380, 1621, 294, 257, 14224, 13, 492, 1621, 294, 257, 1002, 35529, 538, 565, 13, 51453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08604052460309371, "compression_ratio": 1.6115107913669064, "no_speech_prob": 1.455283268024521e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 68390, "start": 705.66, "end": 709.9, "text": " Time is the ultimate variable that tears origin and availability apart.", "tokens": [51453, 6161, 307, 264, 9705, 7006, 300, 10462, 4957, 293, 17945, 4936, 13, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08604052460309371, "compression_ratio": 1.6115107913669064, "no_speech_prob": 1.455283268024521e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 70990, "start": 709.9, "end": 715.26, "text": " And to prove this, Flickshen introduces four specific real-world case studies throughout the paper.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 281, 7081, 341, 11, 3235, 618, 2716, 268, 31472, 1451, 2685, 957, 12, 13217, 1389, 5313, 3710, 264, 3035, 13, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08514877634310941, "compression_ratio": 1.6245847176079735, "no_speech_prob": 2.044495432326765e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 70990, "start": 715.26, "end": 720.4599999999999, "text": " These cases are designed to show exactly how systems actually fail when you drop the", "tokens": [50633, 1981, 3331, 366, 4761, 281, 855, 2293, 577, 3652, 767, 3061, 562, 291, 3270, 264, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08514877634310941, "compression_ratio": 1.6245847176079735, "no_speech_prob": 2.044495432326765e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 70990, "start": 720.4599999999999, "end": 724.22, "text": " synchrony assumption and introduce the friction of reality.", "tokens": [50893, 19331, 88, 15302, 293, 5366, 264, 17710, 295, 4103, 13, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08514877634310941, "compression_ratio": 1.6245847176079735, "no_speech_prob": 2.044495432326765e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 70990, "start": 724.22, "end": 730.22, "text": " Let's dive into case one, which represents the ultimate history-first system, the altitude recipe.", "tokens": [51081, 961, 311, 9192, 666, 1389, 472, 11, 597, 8855, 264, 9705, 2503, 12, 29581, 1185, 11, 264, 24003, 6782, 13, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08514877634310941, "compression_ratio": 1.6245847176079735, "no_speech_prob": 2.044495432326765e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 70990, "start": 730.22, "end": 735.74, "text": " Imagine a deeply treasured family bread recipe. It's been passed down for generations,", "tokens": [51381, 11739, 257, 8760, 12985, 67, 1605, 5961, 6782, 13, 467, 311, 668, 4678, 760, 337, 10593, 11, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08514877634310941, "compression_ratio": 1.6245847176079735, "no_speech_prob": 2.044495432326765e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 70990, "start": 735.74, "end": 739.5799999999999, "text": " refined over decades of baking in a specific seaside town.", "tokens": [51657, 26201, 670, 7878, 295, 12102, 294, 257, 2685, 22535, 482, 3954, 13, 51849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08514877634310941, "compression_ratio": 1.6245847176079735, "no_speech_prob": 2.044495432326765e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 73958, "start": 739.58, "end": 744.5400000000001, "text": " The grandmother who perfected it didn't use thermometers or humidity sensors. She used her senses.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 14317, 567, 2176, 292, 309, 994, 380, 764, 8810, 34675, 420, 24751, 14840, 13, 1240, 1143, 720, 17057, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08703859992649245, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 1.920572858735148e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 73958, "start": 744.5400000000001, "end": 749.1, "text": " Right. She adjusted the flour based on how the dough felt on a rainy day versus a dry day.", "tokens": [50613, 1779, 13, 1240, 19871, 264, 7693, 2361, 322, 577, 264, 7984, 2762, 322, 257, 27181, 786, 5717, 257, 4016, 786, 13, 50841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08703859992649245, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 1.920572858735148e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 73958, "start": 749.1, "end": 753.5, "text": " Over time, all of that incredibly complex environmental interaction", "tokens": [50841, 4886, 565, 11, 439, 295, 300, 6252, 3997, 8303, 9285, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08703859992649245, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 1.920572858735148e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 73958, "start": 753.5, "end": 757.26, "text": " was compressed into a rigid, operationally optimal operator.", "tokens": [51061, 390, 30353, 666, 257, 22195, 11, 6916, 379, 16252, 12973, 13, 51249], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08703859992649245, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 1.920572858735148e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 73958, "start": 758.14, "end": 765.34, "text": " Mix these exact ratios, knead for 10 minutes, bake it 350 degrees for 40 minutes.", "tokens": [51293, 12769, 613, 1900, 32435, 11, 28602, 337, 1266, 2077, 11, 16562, 309, 18065, 5310, 337, 3356, 2077, 13, 51653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08703859992649245, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 1.920572858735148e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 76534, "start": 765.34, "end": 770.0600000000001, "text": " It is a flawless execution engine. If you follow those instructions in that seaside town,", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 45693, 15058, 2848, 13, 759, 291, 1524, 729, 9415, 294, 300, 22535, 482, 3954, 11, 50601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07129738781903242, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 2.253947896380115e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 76534, "start": 770.0600000000001, "end": 774.94, "text": " you get perfect bread every single time. It has absorbed the history of its environment beautifully.", "tokens": [50601, 291, 483, 2176, 5961, 633, 2167, 565, 13, 467, 575, 20799, 264, 2503, 295, 1080, 2823, 16525, 13, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07129738781903242, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 2.253947896380115e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 76534, "start": 774.94, "end": 779.98, "text": " But then, the great grandchild inherits the recipe, moves to a cabin in Denver,", "tokens": [50845, 583, 550, 11, 264, 869, 2697, 15129, 9484, 1208, 264, 6782, 11, 6067, 281, 257, 9401, 294, 26270, 11, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07129738781903242, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 2.253947896380115e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 76534, "start": 779.98, "end": 783.1, "text": " Colorado at high altitude, and tries to bake the bread.", "tokens": [51097, 15786, 412, 1090, 24003, 11, 293, 9898, 281, 16562, 264, 5961, 13, 51253], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07129738781903242, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 2.253947896380115e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 76534, "start": 783.1, "end": 787.02, "text": " And it is a disaster. The dough overproofs, the structure collapses,", "tokens": [51253, 400, 309, 307, 257, 11293, 13, 440, 7984, 670, 15690, 82, 11, 264, 3877, 48765, 11, 51449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07129738781903242, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 2.253947896380115e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 76534, "start": 787.02, "end": 790.86, "text": " the crust burns while the inside remains raw. The operator has failed.", "tokens": [51449, 264, 18156, 22684, 1339, 264, 1854, 7023, 8936, 13, 440, 12973, 575, 7612, 13, 51641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07129738781903242, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 2.253947896380115e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 79086, "start": 790.86, "end": 793.74, "text": " But the true tragedy isn't the failure, is it?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 2074, 18563, 1943, 380, 264, 7763, 11, 307, 309, 30, 50509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1181695318629599, "compression_ratio": 1.6135593220338984, "no_speech_prob": 2.0837973273984955e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 79086, "start": 793.74, "end": 797.1800000000001, "text": " No, it is the complete diagnostic paralysis that follows.", "tokens": [50509, 883, 11, 309, 307, 264, 3566, 27897, 49507, 300, 10002, 13, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1181695318629599, "compression_ratio": 1.6135593220338984, "no_speech_prob": 2.0837973273984955e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 79086, "start": 797.1800000000001, "end": 801.74, "text": " Let's put ourselves in the kitchen with that baker in Denver. They pull the flat ruined bread out", "tokens": [50681, 961, 311, 829, 4175, 294, 264, 6525, 365, 300, 48148, 294, 26270, 13, 814, 2235, 264, 4962, 17013, 5961, 484, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1181695318629599, "compression_ratio": 1.6135593220338984, "no_speech_prob": 2.0837973273984955e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 79086, "start": 801.74, "end": 805.74, "text": " of the oven. They look at the recipe card. What are their fault hypotheses?", "tokens": [50909, 295, 264, 9090, 13, 814, 574, 412, 264, 6782, 2920, 13, 708, 366, 641, 7441, 49969, 30, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1181695318629599, "compression_ratio": 1.6135593220338984, "no_speech_prob": 2.0837973273984955e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 79086, "start": 805.74, "end": 810.62, "text": " Did I measure the flour wrong? Was the yeast expired? Did I knead it too long? Is my oven temperature", "tokens": [51109, 2589, 286, 3481, 264, 7693, 2085, 30, 3027, 264, 21629, 36587, 30, 2589, 286, 28602, 309, 886, 938, 30, 1119, 452, 9090, 4292, 51353], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1181695318629599, "compression_ratio": 1.6135593220338984, "no_speech_prob": 2.0837973273984955e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 79086, "start": 810.62, "end": 816.0600000000001, "text": " inaccurate? They could spend weeks tweaking those variables. Buy new yeast, calibrate the oven,", "tokens": [51353, 46443, 30, 814, 727, 3496, 3259, 6986, 2456, 729, 9102, 13, 19146, 777, 21629, 11, 21583, 4404, 264, 9090, 11, 51625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1181695318629599, "compression_ratio": 1.6135593220338984, "no_speech_prob": 2.0837973273984955e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 81606, "start": 816.06, "end": 821.26, "text": " knead for 11 minutes instead of 10. But none of those vertical adjustments will fix the problem,", "tokens": [50365, 28602, 337, 2975, 2077, 2602, 295, 1266, 13, 583, 6022, 295, 729, 9429, 18624, 486, 3191, 264, 1154, 11, 50625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05727331709153581, "compression_ratio": 1.7079037800687284, "no_speech_prob": 2.004888009082828e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 81606, "start": 821.26, "end": 826.4599999999999, "text": " because the problem is atmospheric pressure and the boiling point of water. The ambient pressure", "tokens": [50625, 570, 264, 1154, 307, 28854, 3321, 293, 264, 16208, 935, 295, 1281, 13, 440, 22997, 3321, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05727331709153581, "compression_ratio": 1.7079037800687284, "no_speech_prob": 2.004888009082828e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 81606, "start": 826.4599999999999, "end": 832.6999999999999, "text": " in Denver is lower, which means water evaporates faster, drying out the dough and altering the yeast", "tokens": [50885, 294, 26270, 307, 3126, 11, 597, 1355, 1281, 26315, 1024, 4663, 11, 22709, 484, 264, 7984, 293, 11337, 278, 264, 21629, 51197], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05727331709153581, "compression_ratio": 1.7079037800687284, "no_speech_prob": 2.004888009082828e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 81606, "start": 832.6999999999999, "end": 838.78, "text": " fermentation rate. But the concept of atmospheric pressure does not exist anywhere on that recipe", "tokens": [51197, 43161, 3314, 13, 583, 264, 3410, 295, 28854, 3321, 775, 406, 2514, 4992, 322, 300, 6782, 51501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05727331709153581, "compression_ratio": 1.7079037800687284, "no_speech_prob": 2.004888009082828e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 81606, "start": 838.78, "end": 844.54, "text": " card. The diagnostic coordinates that would distinguish a sea level success from a high altitude failure", "tokens": [51501, 2920, 13, 440, 27897, 21056, 300, 576, 20206, 257, 4158, 1496, 2245, 490, 257, 1090, 24003, 7763, 51789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05727331709153581, "compression_ratio": 1.7079037800687284, "no_speech_prob": 2.004888009082828e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 84454, "start": 844.54, "end": 849.5, "text": " were never retained. The grandmother didn't need to retain them because she never left sea level.", "tokens": [50365, 645, 1128, 33438, 13, 440, 14317, 994, 380, 643, 281, 18340, 552, 570, 750, 1128, 1411, 4158, 1496, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05356620238707946, "compression_ratio": 1.6864686468646866, "no_speech_prob": 2.2451478610269193e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 84454, "start": 849.5, "end": 855.18, "text": " So in this specific case, the synchrony assumption actually holds true. The trace at repair time in", "tokens": [50613, 407, 294, 341, 2685, 1389, 11, 264, 19331, 88, 15302, 767, 9190, 2074, 13, 440, 13508, 412, 10535, 565, 294, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05356620238707946, "compression_ratio": 1.6864686468646866, "no_speech_prob": 2.2451478610269193e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 84454, "start": 855.18, "end": 860.4599999999999, "text": " Denver is exactly as impoverished as the trace at compression time when the recipe was written down.", "tokens": [50897, 26270, 307, 2293, 382, 704, 3570, 4729, 382, 264, 13508, 412, 19355, 565, 562, 264, 6782, 390, 3720, 760, 13, 51161], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05356620238707946, "compression_ratio": 1.6864686468646866, "no_speech_prob": 2.2451478610269193e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 84454, "start": 861.02, "end": 866.9399999999999, "text": " It was born perfectly optimized for its niche and inherently blind to anything outside of it. The altitude", "tokens": [51189, 467, 390, 4232, 6239, 26941, 337, 1080, 19956, 293, 27993, 6865, 281, 1340, 2380, 295, 309, 13, 440, 24003, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05356620238707946, "compression_ratio": 1.6864686468646866, "no_speech_prob": 2.2451478610269193e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 84454, "start": 866.9399999999999, "end": 873.5, "text": " recipe is the classic failure mode of a history-first system. It lacks the vocabulary to describe its own", "tokens": [51485, 6782, 307, 264, 7230, 7763, 4391, 295, 257, 2503, 12, 29581, 1185, 13, 467, 31132, 264, 19864, 281, 6786, 1080, 1065, 51813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05356620238707946, "compression_ratio": 1.6864686468646866, "no_speech_prob": 2.2451478610269193e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 87350, "start": 873.5, "end": 879.82, "text": " failure. But the genius affliction paper is how it contrasts this with case two, which dismantles the", "tokens": [50365, 7763, 13, 583, 264, 14017, 2096, 75, 4105, 3035, 307, 577, 309, 8712, 82, 341, 365, 1389, 732, 11, 597, 30506, 904, 264, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13218199412027995, "compression_ratio": 1.5627376425855513, "no_speech_prob": 1.927619522335e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 87350, "start": 879.82, "end": 885.42, "text": " illusion of the theory-first system. We move from the grandmother's kitchen to a highly engineered", "tokens": [50681, 18854, 295, 264, 5261, 12, 29581, 1185, 13, 492, 1286, 490, 264, 14317, 311, 6525, 281, 257, 5405, 38648, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13218199412027995, "compression_ratio": 1.5627376425855513, "no_speech_prob": 1.927619522335e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 87350, "start": 885.42, "end": 893.26, "text": " corporate environment. The legacy code base. This is the exact opposite origin story. Imagine a massive", "tokens": [50961, 10896, 2823, 13, 440, 11711, 3089, 3096, 13, 639, 307, 264, 1900, 6182, 4957, 1657, 13, 11739, 257, 5994, 51353], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13218199412027995, "compression_ratio": 1.5627376425855513, "no_speech_prob": 1.927619522335e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 87350, "start": 893.26, "end": 900.78, "text": " software platform powering a financial institution built by elite architects. Theory-first in every sense.", "tokens": [51353, 4722, 3663, 1347, 278, 257, 4669, 7818, 3094, 538, 17801, 30491, 13, 29009, 12, 29581, 294, 633, 2020, 13, 51729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13218199412027995, "compression_ratio": 1.5627376425855513, "no_speech_prob": 1.927619522335e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 90078, "start": 900.78, "end": 906.54, "text": " Every algorithm has a mathematical proof. Every magic constant, those specific numbers hard-coded in", "tokens": [50365, 2048, 9284, 575, 257, 18894, 8177, 13, 2048, 5585, 5754, 11, 729, 2685, 3547, 1152, 12, 66, 12340, 294, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06827193855220436, "compression_ratio": 1.6042296072507554, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549703451939179e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 90078, "start": 906.54, "end": 913.3399999999999, "text": " to govern load balancing or timeout limits, is backed by a 50-page design doc. Explaining exactly why that", "tokens": [50653, 281, 1980, 3677, 22495, 420, 565, 346, 10406, 11, 307, 20391, 538, 257, 2625, 12, 15161, 1715, 3211, 13, 12514, 3686, 2293, 983, 300, 50993], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06827193855220436, "compression_ratio": 1.6042296072507554, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549703451939179e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 90078, "start": 913.3399999999999, "end": 918.78, "text": " specific value was chosen based on hardware constraints and network latency. At the moment of its birth,", "tokens": [50993, 2685, 2158, 390, 8614, 2361, 322, 8837, 18491, 293, 3209, 27043, 13, 1711, 264, 1623, 295, 1080, 3965, 11, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06827193855220436, "compression_ratio": 1.6042296072507554, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549703451939179e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 90078, "start": 918.78, "end": 923.66, "text": " its diagnostic availability is absolute. If you ask the lead engineer a question, they could pull up the", "tokens": [51265, 1080, 27897, 17945, 307, 8236, 13, 759, 291, 1029, 264, 1477, 11403, 257, 1168, 11, 436, 727, 2235, 493, 264, 51509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06827193855220436, "compression_ratio": 1.6042296072507554, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549703451939179e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 90078, "start": 923.66, "end": 928.78, "text": " derivation and tell you exactly why it's structured that way. The synchrony assumption looks at that code base at", "tokens": [51509, 10151, 399, 293, 980, 291, 2293, 983, 309, 311, 18519, 300, 636, 13, 440, 19331, 88, 15302, 1542, 412, 300, 3089, 3096, 412, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06827193855220436, "compression_ratio": 1.6042296072507554, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549703451939179e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 92878, "start": 928.78, "end": 934.86, "text": " birth and declares it permanently repairable. But then real life happens. Three years pass. The lead", "tokens": [50365, 3965, 293, 979, 19415, 309, 24042, 10535, 712, 13, 583, 550, 957, 993, 2314, 13, 6244, 924, 1320, 13, 440, 1477, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.048817074817159904, "compression_ratio": 1.553030303030303, "no_speech_prob": 3.504480126231835e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 92878, "start": 934.86, "end": 939.98, "text": " architect gets poached by a competitor. The secondary engineers are moved to a different project. The", "tokens": [50669, 6331, 2170, 714, 15095, 538, 257, 27266, 13, 440, 11396, 11955, 366, 4259, 281, 257, 819, 1716, 13, 440, 50925], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.048817074817159904, "compression_ratio": 1.553030303030303, "no_speech_prob": 3.504480126231835e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 92878, "start": 939.98, "end": 946.06, "text": " server infrastructure is subtly upgraded. Late one night, there's an outage. A junior developer applies", "tokens": [50925, 7154, 6896, 307, 7257, 356, 24133, 13, 31220, 472, 1818, 11, 456, 311, 364, 484, 609, 13, 316, 16195, 10754, 13165, 51229], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.048817074817159904, "compression_ratio": 1.553030303030303, "no_speech_prob": 3.504480126231835e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 92878, "start": 946.06, "end": 951.8199999999999, "text": " an undocumented hotfix just to get the system back online, promising to write down the reasoning later.", "tokens": [51229, 364, 40472, 2368, 69, 970, 445, 281, 483, 264, 1185, 646, 2950, 11, 20257, 281, 2464, 760, 264, 21577, 1780, 13, 51517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.048817074817159904, "compression_ratio": 1.553030303030303, "no_speech_prob": 3.504480126231835e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 95182, "start": 951.82, "end": 957.9000000000001, "text": " But they never do. Exactly. Fliction introduces a concept here called transmission decay.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 436, 1128, 360, 13, 7587, 13, 3235, 4105, 31472, 257, 3410, 510, 1219, 11574, 21039, 13, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0850863961612477, "compression_ratio": 1.5805084745762712, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827685942078952e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 95182, "start": 957.9000000000001, "end": 964.62, "text": " The operator itself, the running code, has not changed one bit. It's still executing the exact", "tokens": [50669, 440, 12973, 2564, 11, 264, 2614, 3089, 11, 575, 406, 3105, 472, 857, 13, 467, 311, 920, 32368, 264, 1900, 51005], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0850863961612477, "compression_ratio": 1.5805084745762712, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827685942078952e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 95182, "start": 964.62, "end": 969.5, "text": " same logic it did on day one. The system is functioning. But the diagnostic coordinates,", "tokens": [51005, 912, 9952, 309, 630, 322, 786, 472, 13, 440, 1185, 307, 18483, 13, 583, 264, 27897, 21056, 11, 51249], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0850863961612477, "compression_ratio": 1.5805084745762712, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827685942078952e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 95182, "start": 969.5, "end": 975.34, "text": " the derivations, the institutional memory, the why behind the what are evaporating. And eventually,", "tokens": [51249, 264, 10151, 763, 11, 264, 18391, 4675, 11, 264, 983, 2261, 264, 437, 366, 26315, 990, 13, 400, 4728, 11, 51541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0850863961612477, "compression_ratio": 1.5805084745762712, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827685942078952e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 97534, "start": 975.34, "end": 980.5400000000001, "text": " five years down the line, a new team of engineers inherits the system. They look at the code,", "tokens": [50365, 1732, 924, 760, 264, 1622, 11, 257, 777, 1469, 295, 11955, 9484, 1208, 264, 1185, 13, 814, 574, 412, 264, 3089, 11, 50625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06215876561624033, "compression_ratio": 1.697594501718213, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179267769966034e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 97534, "start": 980.5400000000001, "end": 985.26, "text": " they see a magic constant, and they realize that if they change that number, the entire financial", "tokens": [50625, 436, 536, 257, 5585, 5754, 11, 293, 436, 4325, 300, 498, 436, 1319, 300, 1230, 11, 264, 2302, 4669, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06215876561624033, "compression_ratio": 1.697594501718213, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179267769966034e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 97534, "start": 985.26, "end": 991.1, "text": " platform crashes. But nobody in the building and no document in the wiki can explain what that number", "tokens": [50861, 3663, 28642, 13, 583, 5079, 294, 264, 2390, 293, 572, 4166, 294, 264, 261, 9850, 393, 2903, 437, 300, 1230, 51153], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06215876561624033, "compression_ratio": 1.697594501718213, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179267769966034e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 97534, "start": 991.1, "end": 996.3000000000001, "text": " represents. What's fascinating is that the legacy code base has arrived at the exact same state", "tokens": [51153, 8855, 13, 708, 311, 10343, 307, 300, 264, 11711, 3089, 3096, 575, 6678, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 1785, 51413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06215876561624033, "compression_ratio": 1.697594501718213, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179267769966034e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 97534, "start": 996.3000000000001, "end": 1001.98, "text": " of diagnostic paralysis as the altitude recipe, but through a completely different mechanism. The recipe", "tokens": [51413, 295, 27897, 49507, 382, 264, 24003, 6782, 11, 457, 807, 257, 2584, 819, 7513, 13, 440, 6782, 51697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06215876561624033, "compression_ratio": 1.697594501718213, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179267769966034e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 100198, "start": 1001.98, "end": 1007.5, "text": " never had the coordinates. The code base had them, but lost them to time. The origin of the system", "tokens": [50365, 1128, 632, 264, 21056, 13, 440, 3089, 3096, 632, 552, 11, 457, 2731, 552, 281, 565, 13, 440, 4957, 295, 264, 1185, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.048784540333879106, "compression_ratio": 1.7604166666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158157068608346e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 100198, "start": 1007.5, "end": 1012.3000000000001, "text": " provided absolutely no protection against the friction of reality. And fliction goes further than just", "tokens": [50641, 5649, 3122, 572, 6334, 1970, 264, 17710, 295, 4103, 13, 400, 932, 4105, 1709, 3052, 813, 445, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.048784540333879106, "compression_ratio": 1.7604166666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158157068608346e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 100198, "start": 1012.3000000000001, "end": 1018.7, "text": " describing this. They map out the mathematical inevitability of it. They use a standard exponential", "tokens": [50881, 16141, 341, 13, 814, 4471, 484, 264, 18894, 14481, 2310, 295, 309, 13, 814, 764, 257, 3832, 21510, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.048784540333879106, "compression_ratio": 1.7604166666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158157068608346e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 100198, "start": 1018.7, "end": 1024.7, "text": " decay model to show that if there is even the slightest positive rate of decay, if your company", "tokens": [51201, 21039, 2316, 281, 855, 300, 498, 456, 307, 754, 264, 41040, 3353, 3314, 295, 21039, 11, 498, 428, 2237, 51501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.048784540333879106, "compression_ratio": 1.7604166666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158157068608346e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 100198, "start": 1024.7, "end": 1031.5, "text": " experiences even a tiny fraction of staff turnover, no initial advantage will save you. The math is brutal in", "tokens": [51501, 5235, 754, 257, 5870, 14135, 295, 3525, 37137, 11, 572, 5883, 5002, 486, 3155, 291, 13, 440, 5221, 307, 17878, 294, 51841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.048784540333879106, "compression_ratio": 1.7604166666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158157068608346e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 103150, "start": 1031.5, "end": 1038.14, "text": " its clarity. It proves that unbounded decay guarantees a complete collapse of repairability. You can build", "tokens": [50365, 1080, 16992, 13, 467, 25019, 300, 517, 18767, 292, 21039, 32567, 257, 3566, 15584, 295, 10535, 2310, 13, 509, 393, 1322, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.056037257202958636, "compression_ratio": 1.6111111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.9047595532090122e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 103150, "start": 1038.14, "end": 1043.9, "text": " the most robust, beautifully documented architecture in the history of engineering. But if you do not", "tokens": [50697, 264, 881, 13956, 11, 16525, 23007, 9482, 294, 264, 2503, 295, 7043, 13, 583, 498, 291, 360, 406, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.056037257202958636, "compression_ratio": 1.6111111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.9047595532090122e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 103150, "start": 1043.9, "end": 1049.66, "text": " actively fight the decay of institutional knowledge, you will eventually be staring at a magic constant", "tokens": [50985, 13022, 2092, 264, 21039, 295, 18391, 3601, 11, 291, 486, 4728, 312, 18043, 412, 257, 5585, 5754, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.056037257202958636, "compression_ratio": 1.6111111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.9047595532090122e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 103150, "start": 1049.66, "end": 1055.58, "text": " you don't understand, feeling just as helpless as the Bader in Denver. This is a profound shift in how we", "tokens": [51273, 291, 500, 380, 1223, 11, 2633, 445, 382, 27596, 382, 264, 363, 8312, 294, 26270, 13, 639, 307, 257, 14382, 5513, 294, 577, 321, 51569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.056037257202958636, "compression_ratio": 1.6111111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.9047595532090122e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 103150, "start": 1055.58, "end": 1060.38, "text": " should think about building things. We focus so much on the launch, we celebrate the release of the new", "tokens": [51569, 820, 519, 466, 2390, 721, 13, 492, 1879, 370, 709, 322, 264, 4025, 11, 321, 8098, 264, 4374, 295, 264, 777, 51809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.056037257202958636, "compression_ratio": 1.6111111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.9047595532090122e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 106038, "start": 1060.38, "end": 1066.5400000000002, "text": " software, the new corporate strategy. But fliction is showing us that the origin is irrelevant if the", "tokens": [50365, 4722, 11, 264, 777, 10896, 5206, 13, 583, 932, 4105, 307, 4099, 505, 300, 264, 4957, 307, 28682, 498, 264, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08511559736161005, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 2.2801606523042972e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 106038, "start": 1066.5400000000002, "end": 1072.7800000000002, "text": " transmission over time isn't secured. To truly isolate this phenomenon, the paper proposes a brilliant", "tokens": [50673, 11574, 670, 565, 1943, 380, 22905, 13, 1407, 4908, 25660, 341, 14029, 11, 264, 3035, 2365, 4201, 257, 10248, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08511559736161005, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 2.2801606523042972e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 106038, "start": 1072.7800000000002, "end": 1079.0200000000002, "text": " unrun experiment. A thought experiment designed to completely sever origin from availability. They suggest", "tokens": [50985, 517, 12997, 5120, 13, 316, 1194, 5120, 4761, 281, 2584, 2802, 4957, 490, 17945, 13, 814, 3402, 51297], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08511559736161005, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 2.2801606523042972e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 106038, "start": 1079.0200000000002, "end": 1087.18, "text": " taking a pristine, perfectly functioning theory first component. An engineered artifact with a complete,", "tokens": [51297, 1940, 257, 582, 42745, 11, 6239, 18483, 5261, 700, 6542, 13, 1107, 38648, 34806, 365, 257, 3566, 11, 51705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08511559736161005, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 2.2801606523042972e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 108718, "start": 1087.18, "end": 1093.42, "text": " flawless design derivation. Okay, we have our perfect artifact. Now deliberately strip away all the", "tokens": [50365, 45693, 1715, 10151, 399, 13, 1033, 11, 321, 362, 527, 2176, 34806, 13, 823, 23506, 12828, 1314, 439, 264, 50677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07272900234569203, "compression_ratio": 1.583011583011583, "no_speech_prob": 2.2975664339813795e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 108718, "start": 1093.42, "end": 1098.8600000000001, "text": " documentation, delete the comments in the source code, shred the blueprints, wipe the memories of the", "tokens": [50677, 14333, 11, 12097, 264, 3053, 294, 264, 4009, 3089, 11, 21567, 264, 888, 23547, 47523, 11, 14082, 264, 8495, 295, 264, 50949], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07272900234569203, "compression_ratio": 1.583011583011583, "no_speech_prob": 2.2975664339813795e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 108718, "start": 1098.8600000000001, "end": 1105.26, "text": " engineers. But leave the physical artifact itself completely untouched and operational. You are holding the", "tokens": [50949, 11955, 13, 583, 1856, 264, 4001, 34806, 2564, 2584, 1701, 36740, 293, 16607, 13, 509, 366, 5061, 264, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07272900234569203, "compression_ratio": 1.583011583011583, "no_speech_prob": 2.2975664339813795e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 108718, "start": 1105.26, "end": 1111.9, "text": " origin fixed. It is undeniably a theory first system, but you have artificially induced catastrophic", "tokens": [51269, 4957, 6806, 13, 467, 307, 674, 15711, 1188, 257, 5261, 700, 1185, 11, 457, 291, 362, 39905, 2270, 33991, 34915, 51601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07272900234569203, "compression_ratio": 1.583011583011583, "no_speech_prob": 2.2975664339813795e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 111190, "start": 1111.9, "end": 1118.8600000000001, "text": " transmission decay instantly. You've ripped the diagnostic coordinates away. Infliction argues that if you", "tokens": [50365, 11574, 21039, 13518, 13, 509, 600, 22780, 264, 27897, 21056, 1314, 13, 682, 3423, 4105, 38218, 300, 498, 291, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05631850747501149, "compression_ratio": 1.7216494845360826, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878979767695479e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 111190, "start": 1118.8600000000001, "end": 1123.66, "text": " hand that stripped artifact to a mechanic, their ability to diagnose and repair it when it breaks", "tokens": [50713, 1011, 300, 33221, 34806, 281, 257, 23860, 11, 641, 3485, 281, 36238, 293, 10535, 309, 562, 309, 9857, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05631850747501149, "compression_ratio": 1.7216494845360826, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878979767695479e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 111190, "start": 1123.66, "end": 1128.14, "text": " will immediately plummet to match the failure profile of the altitude recipe. The origin of the", "tokens": [50953, 486, 4258, 25854, 5537, 281, 2995, 264, 7763, 7964, 295, 264, 24003, 6782, 13, 440, 4957, 295, 264, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05631850747501149, "compression_ratio": 1.7216494845360826, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878979767695479e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 111190, "start": 1128.14, "end": 1133.66, "text": " system offers zero residual diagnostic power if the coordinates are missing at the exact moment repair", "tokens": [51177, 1185, 7736, 4018, 27980, 27897, 1347, 498, 264, 21056, 366, 5361, 412, 264, 1900, 1623, 10535, 51453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05631850747501149, "compression_ratio": 1.7216494845360826, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878979767695479e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 111190, "start": 1133.66, "end": 1138.8600000000001, "text": " is attempted. The true governing variable is not how the system was born, but what information is", "tokens": [51453, 307, 18997, 13, 440, 2074, 30054, 7006, 307, 406, 577, 264, 1185, 390, 4232, 11, 457, 437, 1589, 307, 51713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05631850747501149, "compression_ratio": 1.7216494845360826, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878979767695479e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 113886, "start": 1138.86, "end": 1143.5, "text": " physically present at the time of the breakdown. I want to pause here and look at an incredibly powerful", "tokens": [50365, 9762, 1974, 412, 264, 565, 295, 264, 18188, 13, 286, 528, 281, 10465, 510, 293, 574, 412, 364, 6252, 4005, 50597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05658956195997155, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 2.564047932307467e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 113886, "start": 1143.5, "end": 1150.78, "text": " visual analogy that the paper places in its appendix, but which I think belongs right here in the core of", "tokens": [50597, 5056, 21663, 300, 264, 3035, 3190, 294, 1080, 34116, 970, 11, 457, 597, 286, 519, 12953, 558, 510, 294, 264, 4965, 295, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05658956195997155, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 2.564047932307467e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 113886, "start": 1150.78, "end": 1157.34, "text": " our discussion. Oh, the coarsening partitions concept. Yes, it perfectly illustrates what transmission decay", "tokens": [50961, 527, 5017, 13, 876, 11, 264, 598, 685, 4559, 644, 2451, 3410, 13, 1079, 11, 309, 6239, 41718, 437, 11574, 21039, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05658956195997155, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 2.564047932307467e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 113886, "start": 1157.34, "end": 1164.06, "text": " actually feels like inside a system. The appendix uses this mathematical concept to map out how coordinates", "tokens": [51289, 767, 3417, 411, 1854, 257, 1185, 13, 440, 34116, 970, 4960, 341, 18894, 3410, 281, 4471, 484, 577, 21056, 51625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05658956195997155, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 2.564047932307467e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 116406, "start": 1164.06, "end": 1169.82, "text": " carve up the space of possibilities. Imagine every possible way your software could have been built,", "tokens": [50365, 33832, 493, 264, 1901, 295, 12178, 13, 11739, 633, 1944, 636, 428, 4722, 727, 362, 668, 3094, 11, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07999399546030406, "compression_ratio": 1.757679180887372, "no_speech_prob": 2.4083211553477257e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 116406, "start": 1169.82, "end": 1176.1399999999999, "text": " and every possible way it could fail, as a giant solid block of marble. When you write the code and", "tokens": [50653, 293, 633, 1944, 636, 309, 727, 3061, 11, 382, 257, 7410, 5100, 3461, 295, 26844, 13, 1133, 291, 2464, 264, 3089, 293, 50969], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07999399546030406, "compression_ratio": 1.757679180887372, "no_speech_prob": 2.4083211553477257e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 116406, "start": 1176.1399999999999, "end": 1181.1799999999998, "text": " create a diagnostic coordinate, say, you write a comment explaining that a specific function handles server", "tokens": [50969, 1884, 257, 27897, 15670, 11, 584, 11, 291, 2464, 257, 2871, 13468, 300, 257, 2685, 2445, 18722, 7154, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07999399546030406, "compression_ratio": 1.757679180887372, "no_speech_prob": 2.4083211553477257e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 116406, "start": 1181.1799999999998, "end": 1186.46, "text": " timeouts, you're essentially taking a chisel and slicing that block of marble into two distinct pieces.", "tokens": [51221, 565, 7711, 11, 291, 434, 4476, 1940, 257, 417, 39711, 293, 46586, 300, 3461, 295, 26844, 666, 732, 10644, 3755, 13, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07999399546030406, "compression_ratio": 1.757679180887372, "no_speech_prob": 2.4083211553477257e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 116406, "start": 1186.46, "end": 1191.58, "text": " You have the timeout failure piece and the everything else piece. Exactly. The mathematical term is an", "tokens": [51485, 509, 362, 264, 565, 346, 7763, 2522, 293, 264, 1203, 1646, 2522, 13, 7587, 13, 440, 18894, 1433, 307, 364, 51741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07999399546030406, "compression_ratio": 1.757679180887372, "no_speech_prob": 2.4083211553477257e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 119158, "start": 1191.58, "end": 1197.74, "text": " induced partition. Every coordinate you retain slices the block further. A highly repairable,", "tokens": [50365, 33991, 24808, 13, 2048, 15670, 291, 18340, 19793, 264, 3461, 3052, 13, 316, 5405, 10535, 712, 11, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07112911201658703, "compression_ratio": 1.5703125, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968976559120444e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 119158, "start": 1197.74, "end": 1203.26, "text": " deeply documented system is a block of marble that has been sliced into millions of tiny, specific,", "tokens": [50673, 8760, 23007, 1185, 307, 257, 3461, 295, 26844, 300, 575, 668, 27098, 666, 6803, 295, 5870, 11, 2685, 11, 50949], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07112911201658703, "compression_ratio": 1.5703125, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968976559120444e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 119158, "start": 1203.26, "end": 1209.5, "text": " distinct cubes. When a failure occurs, you use the symptoms to immediately pinpoint exactly which tiny", "tokens": [50949, 10644, 25415, 13, 1133, 257, 7763, 11843, 11, 291, 764, 264, 8332, 281, 4258, 40837, 2293, 597, 5870, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07112911201658703, "compression_ratio": 1.5703125, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968976559120444e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 119158, "start": 1209.5, "end": 1215.4199999999998, "text": " cube you are standing in. You know exactly what went wrong. But what happens when transmission decay sets", "tokens": [51261, 13728, 291, 366, 4877, 294, 13, 509, 458, 2293, 437, 1437, 2085, 13, 583, 437, 2314, 562, 11574, 21039, 6352, 51557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07112911201658703, "compression_ratio": 1.5703125, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968976559120444e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 121542, "start": 1215.42, "end": 1220.78, "text": " in? What happens when the engineer who wrote that comment leaves the company and the documentation is", "tokens": [50365, 294, 30, 708, 2314, 562, 264, 11403, 567, 4114, 300, 2871, 5510, 264, 2237, 293, 264, 14333, 307, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08883116556250531, "compression_ratio": 1.583011583011583, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779816910268084e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 121542, "start": 1220.78, "end": 1227.02, "text": " lost? The slices disappear. The tiny cubes begin to merge back together into larger indistinguishable", "tokens": [50633, 2731, 30, 440, 19793, 11596, 13, 440, 5870, 25415, 1841, 281, 22183, 646, 1214, 666, 4833, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 712, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08883116556250531, "compression_ratio": 1.583011583011583, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779816910268084e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 121542, "start": 1227.02, "end": 1233.1000000000001, "text": " blocks. This is what the paper formally defines as coarsening. I visualize it like taking a crystal", "tokens": [50945, 8474, 13, 639, 307, 437, 264, 3035, 25983, 23122, 382, 598, 685, 4559, 13, 286, 23273, 309, 411, 1940, 257, 13662, 51249], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08883116556250531, "compression_ratio": 1.583011583011583, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779816910268084e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 121542, "start": 1233.1000000000001, "end": 1240.0600000000002, "text": " clear high definition photograph and slowly turning it into a pixelated 8-bit image. Every time you lose a", "tokens": [51249, 1850, 1090, 7123, 8348, 293, 5692, 6246, 309, 666, 257, 19261, 770, 1649, 12, 5260, 3256, 13, 2048, 565, 291, 3624, 257, 51597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08883116556250531, "compression_ratio": 1.583011583011583, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779816910268084e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 124006, "start": 1240.06, "end": 1245.5, "text": " piece of institutional memory, the pixels get bigger. The distinct edge between a server timeout and a", "tokens": [50365, 2522, 295, 18391, 4675, 11, 264, 18668, 483, 3801, 13, 440, 10644, 4691, 1296, 257, 7154, 565, 346, 293, 257, 50637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0471209726835552, "compression_ratio": 1.6719745222929936, "no_speech_prob": 2.1760971930656625e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 124006, "start": 1245.5, "end": 1251.6599999999999, "text": " database lock disappears into a single blurry square. Eventually, if decay goes unchecked, the pixels", "tokens": [50637, 8149, 4017, 25527, 666, 257, 2167, 37644, 3732, 13, 17586, 11, 498, 21039, 1709, 46672, 292, 11, 264, 18668, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0471209726835552, "compression_ratio": 1.6719745222929936, "no_speech_prob": 2.1760971930656625e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 124006, "start": 1251.6599999999999, "end": 1256.94, "text": " become so massive that you can't even tell if you are looking at a picture of a dog or a cat. You have", "tokens": [50945, 1813, 370, 5994, 300, 291, 393, 380, 754, 980, 498, 291, 366, 1237, 412, 257, 3036, 295, 257, 3000, 420, 257, 3857, 13, 509, 362, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0471209726835552, "compression_ratio": 1.6719745222929936, "no_speech_prob": 2.1760971930656625e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 124006, "start": 1256.94, "end": 1262.86, "text": " completely lost the resolution required to diagnose the image. That pixelation is the physical manifestation", "tokens": [51209, 2584, 2731, 264, 8669, 4739, 281, 36238, 264, 3256, 13, 663, 19261, 399, 307, 264, 4001, 29550, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0471209726835552, "compression_ratio": 1.6719745222929936, "no_speech_prob": 2.1760971930656625e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 124006, "start": 1262.86, "end": 1268.62, "text": " of repair entropy increasing. You are losing the ability to make distinctions. And the tragedy of the legacy", "tokens": [51505, 295, 10535, 30867, 5662, 13, 509, 366, 7027, 264, 3485, 281, 652, 1483, 49798, 13, 400, 264, 18563, 295, 264, 11711, 51793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0471209726835552, "compression_ratio": 1.6719745222929936, "no_speech_prob": 2.1760971930656625e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 126862, "start": 1268.62, "end": 1274.54, "text": " codebase is that the software is still running perfectly while the image pixelates. The execution", "tokens": [50365, 3089, 17429, 307, 300, 264, 4722, 307, 920, 2614, 6239, 1339, 264, 3256, 19261, 1024, 13, 440, 15058, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0707630736104558, "compression_ratio": 1.6451612903225807, "no_speech_prob": 1.7338193597851714e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 126862, "start": 1274.54, "end": 1280.6999999999998, "text": " is flawless, but the diagnostic resolution is quietly degrading in the background. Until the day it", "tokens": [50661, 307, 45693, 11, 457, 264, 27897, 8669, 307, 19141, 24740, 278, 294, 264, 3678, 13, 9088, 264, 786, 309, 50969], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0707630736104558, "compression_ratio": 1.6451612903225807, "no_speech_prob": 1.7338193597851714e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 126862, "start": 1280.6999999999998, "end": 1288.1399999999999, "text": " crashes and you are left staring at a single massive blurry pixel with no idea where to even begin. So we", "tokens": [50969, 28642, 293, 291, 366, 1411, 18043, 412, 257, 2167, 5994, 37644, 19261, 365, 572, 1558, 689, 281, 754, 1841, 13, 407, 321, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0707630736104558, "compression_ratio": 1.6451612903225807, "no_speech_prob": 1.7338193597851714e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 126862, "start": 1288.1399999999999, "end": 1293.9799999999998, "text": " have explored the history-first recipe that never had the coordinates and the theory-first codebase that", "tokens": [51341, 362, 24016, 264, 2503, 12, 29581, 6782, 300, 1128, 632, 264, 21056, 293, 264, 5261, 12, 29581, 3089, 17429, 300, 51633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0707630736104558, "compression_ratio": 1.6451612903225807, "no_speech_prob": 1.7338193597851714e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 129398, "start": 1293.98, "end": 1299.9, "text": " lost them to time. In both cases, the failure results in a silent absence of knowledge. You know", "tokens": [50365, 2731, 552, 281, 565, 13, 682, 1293, 3331, 11, 264, 7763, 3542, 294, 257, 12784, 17145, 295, 3601, 13, 509, 458, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047111388175719, "compression_ratio": 1.6411042944785277, "no_speech_prob": 2.3347983702654007e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 129398, "start": 1299.9, "end": 1305.1, "text": " the system is broken, the bread is flat, the server is down, but you just don't know what to do. But", "tokens": [50661, 264, 1185, 307, 5463, 11, 264, 5961, 307, 4962, 11, 264, 7154, 307, 760, 11, 457, 291, 445, 500, 380, 458, 437, 281, 360, 13, 583, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047111388175719, "compression_ratio": 1.6411042944785277, "no_speech_prob": 2.3347983702654007e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 129398, "start": 1305.1, "end": 1311.1, "text": " Fliction introduces a third scenario that is arguably far more dangerous than simple ignorance. What happens", "tokens": [50921, 3235, 4105, 31472, 257, 2636, 9005, 300, 307, 26771, 1400, 544, 5795, 813, 2199, 25390, 13, 708, 2314, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047111388175719, "compression_ratio": 1.6411042944785277, "no_speech_prob": 2.3347983702654007e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 129398, "start": 1311.1, "end": 1316.8600000000001, "text": " if you don't lose the coordinates? What if you preserve your high-resolution image perfectly, with absolutely no", "tokens": [51221, 498, 291, 500, 380, 3624, 264, 21056, 30, 708, 498, 291, 15665, 428, 1090, 12, 495, 3386, 3256, 6239, 11, 365, 3122, 572, 51509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047111388175719, "compression_ratio": 1.6411042944785277, "no_speech_prob": 2.3347983702654007e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 129398, "start": 1316.8600000000001, "end": 1323.74, "text": " decay, but the reality you are looking at fundamentally changes? This brings us to section 3. Scope failure and the", "tokens": [51509, 21039, 11, 457, 264, 4103, 291, 366, 1237, 412, 17879, 2962, 30, 639, 5607, 505, 281, 3541, 805, 13, 2747, 1114, 7763, 293, 264, 51853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047111388175719, "compression_ratio": 1.6411042944785277, "no_speech_prob": 2.3347983702654007e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 132374, "start": 1323.74, "end": 1328.54, "text": " danger of the confident error. To understand this, we have to look at the boundary between what a", "tokens": [50365, 4330, 295, 264, 6679, 6713, 13, 1407, 1223, 341, 11, 321, 362, 281, 574, 412, 264, 12866, 1296, 437, 257, 50605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06571388244628906, "compression_ratio": 1.7342657342657342, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321956365280334e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 132374, "start": 1328.54, "end": 1333.74, "text": " system is designed to handle and what reality actually throws at it. The paper introduces a", "tokens": [50605, 1185, 307, 4761, 281, 4813, 293, 437, 4103, 767, 19251, 412, 309, 13, 440, 3035, 31472, 257, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06571388244628906, "compression_ratio": 1.7342657342657342, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321956365280334e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 132374, "start": 1333.74, "end": 1339.74, "text": " critical distinction between two types of sufficiency, operational sufficiency and scoped diagnostic", "tokens": [50865, 4924, 16844, 1296, 732, 3467, 295, 459, 49086, 11, 16607, 459, 49086, 293, 795, 27277, 27897, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06571388244628906, "compression_ratio": 1.7342657342657342, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321956365280334e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 132374, "start": 1339.74, "end": 1345.98, "text": " sufficiency. To make operational sufficiency concrete, Fliction borrows an analogy from Jay Wilson,", "tokens": [51165, 459, 49086, 13, 1407, 652, 16607, 459, 49086, 9859, 11, 3235, 4105, 14828, 28251, 364, 21663, 490, 11146, 15388, 11, 51477], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06571388244628906, "compression_ratio": 1.7342657342657342, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321956365280334e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 132374, "start": 1345.98, "end": 1352.14, "text": " a philosopher of science who focuses on the emergence of ordinary objects. Imagine a standard macroscopic", "tokens": [51477, 257, 29805, 295, 3497, 567, 16109, 322, 264, 36211, 295, 10547, 6565, 13, 11739, 257, 3832, 7912, 38006, 299, 51785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06571388244628906, "compression_ratio": 1.7342657342657342, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321956365280334e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 135214, "start": 1352.14, "end": 1357.18, "text": " description of a wooden chair. You measure its height, its weight, the density of the wood,", "tokens": [50365, 3855, 295, 257, 14744, 6090, 13, 509, 3481, 1080, 6681, 11, 1080, 3364, 11, 264, 10305, 295, 264, 4576, 11, 50617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.059347586198286575, "compression_ratio": 1.8527131782945736, "no_speech_prob": 1.883262643054273e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 135214, "start": 1357.18, "end": 1362.94, "text": " its geometric dimensions. You have a very accurate, high-resolution description of a chair. Now,", "tokens": [50617, 1080, 33246, 12819, 13, 509, 362, 257, 588, 8559, 11, 1090, 12, 495, 3386, 3855, 295, 257, 6090, 13, 823, 11, 50905], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.059347586198286575, "compression_ratio": 1.8527131782945736, "no_speech_prob": 1.883262643054273e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 135214, "start": 1362.94, "end": 1367.3400000000001, "text": " take that macroscopic description of the chair and try to plug it into the equations of quantum", "tokens": [50905, 747, 300, 7912, 38006, 299, 3855, 295, 264, 6090, 293, 853, 281, 5452, 309, 666, 264, 11787, 295, 13018, 51125], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.059347586198286575, "compression_ratio": 1.8527131782945736, "no_speech_prob": 1.883262643054273e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 135214, "start": 1367.3400000000001, "end": 1373.0200000000002, "text": " mechanics to predict its subatomic behavior. The math simply won't run. The equations of quantum", "tokens": [51125, 12939, 281, 6069, 1080, 1422, 267, 21401, 5223, 13, 440, 5221, 2935, 1582, 380, 1190, 13, 440, 11787, 295, 13018, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.059347586198286575, "compression_ratio": 1.8527131782945736, "no_speech_prob": 1.883262643054273e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 135214, "start": 1373.0200000000002, "end": 1379.26, "text": " mechanics require variables, spin states, wave functions, particle positions, that a macroscopic", "tokens": [51409, 12939, 3651, 9102, 11, 6060, 4368, 11, 5772, 6828, 11, 12359, 8432, 11, 300, 257, 7912, 38006, 299, 51721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.059347586198286575, "compression_ratio": 1.8527131782945736, "no_speech_prob": 1.883262643054273e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 137926, "start": 1379.26, "end": 1385.9, "text": " description of wood fundamentally does not possess. It is a profound mismatch of vocabulary. The system", "tokens": [50365, 3855, 295, 4576, 17879, 775, 406, 17490, 13, 467, 307, 257, 14382, 23220, 852, 295, 19864, 13, 440, 1185, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06058936066679902, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.681575126540047e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 137926, "start": 1385.9, "end": 1392.22, "text": " refuses to process the input. That is operational insufficiency. The coordinate set is so completely", "tokens": [50697, 33222, 281, 1399, 264, 4846, 13, 663, 307, 16607, 1028, 1245, 42081, 13, 440, 15670, 992, 307, 370, 2584, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06058936066679902, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.681575126540047e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 137926, "start": 1392.22, "end": 1398.3, "text": " inadequate for the dynamics being evaluated that the entire process halts. And as a user, this is", "tokens": [51013, 42107, 337, 264, 15679, 885, 25509, 300, 264, 2302, 1399, 7523, 1373, 13, 400, 382, 257, 4195, 11, 341, 307, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06058936066679902, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.681575126540047e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 137926, "start": 1398.3, "end": 1404.7, "text": " actually a safe failure mode. It's loud. It's like a computer throwing a fatal syntax error and refusing to", "tokens": [51317, 767, 257, 3273, 7763, 4391, 13, 467, 311, 6588, 13, 467, 311, 411, 257, 3820, 10238, 257, 24069, 28431, 6713, 293, 37289, 281, 51637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06058936066679902, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.681575126540047e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 140470, "start": 1404.7, "end": 1410.78, "text": " compile. The system stops, throws its hands up, and says, I cannot process reality with the tools you gave", "tokens": [50365, 31413, 13, 440, 1185, 10094, 11, 19251, 1080, 2377, 493, 11, 293, 1619, 11, 286, 2644, 1399, 4103, 365, 264, 3873, 291, 2729, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06490097697983441, "compression_ratio": 1.6557377049180328, "no_speech_prob": 2.5736704434287105e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 140470, "start": 1410.78, "end": 1415.18, "text": " me. You know instantly that your model is broken. Affliction is far more concerned with the second", "tokens": [50669, 385, 13, 509, 458, 13518, 300, 428, 2316, 307, 5463, 13, 12840, 75, 4105, 307, 1400, 544, 5922, 365, 264, 1150, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06490097697983441, "compression_ratio": 1.6557377049180328, "no_speech_prob": 2.5736704434287105e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 140470, "start": 1415.18, "end": 1420.8600000000001, "text": " type of failure, scoped diagnostic sufficiency. What happens when the system doesn't throw an error?", "tokens": [50889, 2010, 295, 7763, 11, 795, 27277, 27897, 459, 49086, 13, 708, 2314, 562, 264, 1185, 1177, 380, 3507, 364, 6713, 30, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06490097697983441, "compression_ratio": 1.6557377049180328, "no_speech_prob": 2.5736704434287105e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 140470, "start": 1420.8600000000001, "end": 1425.02, "text": " What happens when it encounters a reality it wasn't designed for, but instead of stopping,", "tokens": [51173, 708, 2314, 562, 309, 26310, 257, 4103, 309, 2067, 380, 4761, 337, 11, 457, 2602, 295, 12767, 11, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06490097697983441, "compression_ratio": 1.6557377049180328, "no_speech_prob": 2.5736704434287105e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 140470, "start": 1425.02, "end": 1431.82, "text": " it confidently evaluates the wrong data and proceeds as if everything is fine? This leads us to case three,", "tokens": [51381, 309, 41956, 6133, 1024, 264, 2085, 1412, 293, 32280, 382, 498, 1203, 307, 2489, 30, 639, 6689, 505, 281, 1389, 1045, 11, 51721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06490097697983441, "compression_ratio": 1.6557377049180328, "no_speech_prob": 2.5736704434287105e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 143182, "start": 1431.82, "end": 1437.5, "text": " the Hamming decoder. This is a real, physical system used in computer engineering, and it perfectly", "tokens": [50365, 264, 8234, 2810, 979, 19866, 13, 639, 307, 257, 957, 11, 4001, 1185, 1143, 294, 3820, 7043, 11, 293, 309, 6239, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06150395653464578, "compression_ratio": 1.6915254237288135, "no_speech_prob": 3.4233618544099453e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 143182, "start": 1437.5, "end": 1442.86, "text": " illustrates the terror of the confident error. A Hamming code is a type of error correcting memory.", "tokens": [50649, 41718, 264, 8127, 295, 264, 6679, 6713, 13, 316, 8234, 2810, 3089, 307, 257, 2010, 295, 6713, 47032, 4675, 13, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06150395653464578, "compression_ratio": 1.6915254237288135, "no_speech_prob": 3.4233618544099453e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 143182, "start": 1442.86, "end": 1447.98, "text": " We are specifically looking at the Hamming 7-4 code. Without getting lost in binary matrices,", "tokens": [50917, 492, 366, 4682, 1237, 412, 264, 8234, 2810, 1614, 12, 19, 3089, 13, 9129, 1242, 2731, 294, 17434, 32284, 11, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06150395653464578, "compression_ratio": 1.6915254237288135, "no_speech_prob": 3.4233618544099453e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 143182, "start": 1447.98, "end": 1454.3799999999999, "text": " the fundamental mechanism is this. Every time a computer saves a chunk of data, the Hamming algorithm", "tokens": [51173, 264, 8088, 7513, 307, 341, 13, 2048, 565, 257, 3820, 19155, 257, 16635, 295, 1412, 11, 264, 8234, 2810, 9284, 51493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06150395653464578, "compression_ratio": 1.6915254237288135, "no_speech_prob": 3.4233618544099453e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 143182, "start": 1454.3799999999999, "end": 1460.62, "text": " calculates and stores exactly three extra bits of information called syndrome bits. These syndrome bits", "tokens": [51493, 4322, 1024, 293, 9512, 2293, 1045, 2857, 9239, 295, 1589, 1219, 19371, 9239, 13, 1981, 19371, 9239, 51805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06150395653464578, "compression_ratio": 1.6915254237288135, "no_speech_prob": 3.4233618544099453e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 146062, "start": 1460.62, "end": 1466.54, "text": " are the pure embodiment of diagnostic coordinates. They are specifically designed for one purpose,", "tokens": [50365, 366, 264, 6075, 28935, 2328, 295, 27897, 21056, 13, 814, 366, 4682, 4761, 337, 472, 4334, 11, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07032176186056698, "compression_ratio": 1.6861924686192469, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722157954533133e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 146062, "start": 1466.54, "end": 1471.82, "text": " to monitor the fault space the engineers anticipated. The engineers designed this system under the", "tokens": [50661, 281, 6002, 264, 7441, 1901, 264, 11955, 23267, 13, 440, 11955, 4761, 341, 1185, 833, 264, 50925], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07032176186056698, "compression_ratio": 1.6861924686192469, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722157954533133e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 146062, "start": 1471.82, "end": 1478.2199999999998, "text": " assumption that the most common error in a computer's memory is a single bit randomly flipping from a zero", "tokens": [50925, 15302, 300, 264, 881, 2689, 6713, 294, 257, 3820, 311, 4675, 307, 257, 2167, 857, 16979, 26886, 490, 257, 4018, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07032176186056698, "compression_ratio": 1.6861924686192469, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722157954533133e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 146062, "start": 1478.2199999999998, "end": 1485.34, "text": " to a one, maybe caused by a cosmic ray hitting the microchip. We call that anticipated fault space", "tokens": [51245, 281, 257, 472, 11, 1310, 7008, 538, 257, 27614, 18592, 8850, 264, 4532, 339, 647, 13, 492, 818, 300, 23267, 7441, 1901, 51601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07032176186056698, "compression_ratio": 1.6861924686192469, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722157954533133e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 148534, "start": 1485.34, "end": 1491.26, "text": " eDesign. And within eDesign, the Hamming decoder is an absolute miracle of efficiency. If a single", "tokens": [50365, 308, 29543, 788, 13, 400, 1951, 308, 29543, 788, 11, 264, 8234, 2810, 979, 19866, 307, 364, 8236, 14660, 295, 10493, 13, 759, 257, 2167, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04922574457496104, "compression_ratio": 1.606177606177606, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756220535043333e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 148534, "start": 1491.26, "end": 1497.5, "text": " bit flips anywhere in the data, the decoder looks at its three syndrome bits, runs a quick calculation,", "tokens": [50661, 857, 40249, 4992, 294, 264, 1412, 11, 264, 979, 19866, 1542, 412, 1080, 1045, 19371, 9239, 11, 6676, 257, 1702, 17108, 11, 50973], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04922574457496104, "compression_ratio": 1.606177606177606, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756220535043333e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 148534, "start": 1497.5, "end": 1502.78, "text": " and points a laser directly at the corrupted bit. It flips it back, repairs the data, and the computer", "tokens": [50973, 293, 2793, 257, 12530, 3838, 412, 264, 39480, 857, 13, 467, 40249, 309, 646, 11, 28823, 264, 1412, 11, 293, 264, 3820, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04922574457496104, "compression_ratio": 1.606177606177606, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756220535043333e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 148534, "start": 1502.78, "end": 1509.02, "text": " keeps running flawlessly. Its diagnostic availability is 100% within its designated scope. But the universe is", "tokens": [51237, 5965, 2614, 13717, 12048, 13, 6953, 27897, 17945, 307, 2319, 4, 1951, 1080, 21688, 11923, 13, 583, 264, 6445, 307, 51549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04922574457496104, "compression_ratio": 1.606177606177606, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756220535043333e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 150902, "start": 1509.02, "end": 1514.94, "text": " not bound by the engineer's design document. Reality contains an infinite fault space, which the paper", "tokens": [50365, 406, 5472, 538, 264, 11403, 311, 1715, 4166, 13, 33822, 8306, 364, 13785, 7441, 1901, 11, 597, 264, 3035, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12674538294474283, "compression_ratio": 1.5848375451263539, "no_speech_prob": 2.371571038509157e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 150902, "start": 1514.94, "end": 1521.98, "text": " calls eActual. What happens when reality introduces an error that is outside of eDesign? What happens if that", "tokens": [50661, 5498, 308, 30338, 901, 13, 708, 2314, 562, 4103, 31472, 364, 6713, 300, 307, 2380, 295, 308, 29543, 788, 30, 708, 2314, 498, 300, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12674538294474283, "compression_ratio": 1.5848375451263539, "no_speech_prob": 2.371571038509157e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 150902, "start": 1521.98, "end": 1528.3799999999999, "text": " cosmic ray hits the microchip at just the wrong angle, and two bits flip simultaneously? This is the crux of a", "tokens": [51013, 27614, 18592, 8664, 264, 4532, 339, 647, 412, 445, 264, 2085, 5802, 11, 293, 732, 9239, 7929, 16561, 30, 639, 307, 264, 5140, 87, 295, 257, 51333], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12674538294474283, "compression_ratio": 1.5848375451263539, "no_speech_prob": 2.371571038509157e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 150902, "start": 1528.3799999999999, "end": 1535.02, "text": " confident error. When a double bit error occurs, the Hamming decoder does not experience operational insufficiency.", "tokens": [51333, 6679, 6713, 13, 1133, 257, 3834, 857, 6713, 11843, 11, 264, 8234, 2810, 979, 19866, 775, 406, 1752, 16607, 1028, 1245, 42081, 13, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12674538294474283, "compression_ratio": 1.5848375451263539, "no_speech_prob": 2.371571038509157e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 153502, "start": 1535.02, "end": 1541.02, "text": " It doesn't look at the data, like the quantum equation looking at the wooden chair. It doesn't throw a fatal error", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1177, 380, 574, 412, 264, 1412, 11, 411, 264, 13018, 5367, 1237, 412, 264, 14744, 6090, 13, 467, 1177, 380, 3507, 257, 24069, 6713, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1287606622754913, "compression_ratio": 1.709090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.610611600685874e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 153502, "start": 1541.02, "end": 1547.02, "text": " and alert the system that something impossible has happened. Because it only speaks the language of single bit errors.", "tokens": [50665, 293, 9615, 264, 1185, 300, 746, 6243, 575, 2011, 13, 1436, 309, 787, 10789, 264, 2856, 295, 2167, 857, 13603, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1287606622754913, "compression_ratio": 1.709090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.610611600685874e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 153502, "start": 1547.02, "end": 1555.02, "text": " Exactly. It evaluates the corrupted data using its three syndrome bits. Because of how the binary math overlaps,", "tokens": [50965, 7587, 13, 467, 6133, 1024, 264, 39480, 1412, 1228, 1080, 1045, 19371, 9239, 13, 1436, 295, 577, 264, 17434, 5221, 15986, 2382, 11, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1287606622754913, "compression_ratio": 1.709090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.610611600685874e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 153502, "start": 1555.02, "end": 1561.02, "text": " the calculation for a double bit error will inevitably produce a syndrome that perfectly matches the mathematical signature", "tokens": [51365, 264, 17108, 337, 257, 3834, 857, 6713, 486, 28171, 5258, 257, 19371, 300, 6239, 10676, 264, 18894, 13397, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1287606622754913, "compression_ratio": 1.709090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.610611600685874e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 156102, "start": 1561.02, "end": 1568.06, "text": " of some random innocent single bit error. So the decoder looks at a catastrophic double failure,", "tokens": [50365, 295, 512, 4974, 13171, 2167, 857, 6713, 13, 407, 264, 979, 19866, 1542, 412, 257, 34915, 3834, 7763, 11, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09081274339522438, "compression_ratio": 1.639344262295082, "no_speech_prob": 2.0756805562544e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 156102, "start": 1568.7, "end": 1573.5, "text": " mathematically hallucinates that it's a simple single failure, targets a completely innocent piece", "tokens": [50749, 44003, 35212, 259, 1024, 300, 309, 311, 257, 2199, 2167, 7763, 11, 12911, 257, 2584, 13171, 2522, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09081274339522438, "compression_ratio": 1.639344262295082, "no_speech_prob": 2.0756805562544e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 156102, "start": 1573.5, "end": 1579.5, "text": " of data, and fixes it. It actively miscorrects the data. And the most terrifying part is that once it", "tokens": [50989, 295, 1412, 11, 293, 32539, 309, 13, 467, 13022, 3346, 19558, 2554, 82, 264, 1412, 13, 400, 264, 881, 18106, 644, 307, 300, 1564, 309, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09081274339522438, "compression_ratio": 1.639344262295082, "no_speech_prob": 2.0756805562544e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 156102, "start": 1579.5, "end": 1585.02, "text": " applies the wrong fix, the resulting output perfectly satisfies every single internal parity check the", "tokens": [51289, 13165, 264, 2085, 3191, 11, 264, 16505, 5598, 6239, 44271, 633, 2167, 6920, 44747, 1520, 264, 51565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09081274339522438, "compression_ratio": 1.639344262295082, "no_speech_prob": 2.0756805562544e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 158502, "start": 1585.02, "end": 1591.9, "text": " system is capable of running. To the system, it looks like a textbook. Flawless repair. It logs a success.", "tokens": [50365, 1185, 307, 8189, 295, 2614, 13, 1407, 264, 1185, 11, 309, 1542, 411, 257, 25591, 13, 479, 5901, 1832, 10535, 13, 467, 20820, 257, 2245, 13, 50709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07426183919111888, "compression_ratio": 1.6758893280632412, "no_speech_prob": 1.4102923473133244e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 158502, "start": 1591.9, "end": 1597.26, "text": " It congratulates itself. It is perfectly maintained. Its coordinates haven't decayed at all. But it is", "tokens": [50709, 467, 9774, 26192, 2564, 13, 467, 307, 6239, 17578, 13, 6953, 21056, 2378, 380, 21039, 292, 412, 439, 13, 583, 309, 307, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07426183919111888, "compression_ratio": 1.6758893280632412, "no_speech_prob": 1.4102923473133244e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 158502, "start": 1597.26, "end": 1604.06, "text": " diagnostically blind to its own boundaries. It is silently corrupting the core data while reporting that all", "tokens": [50977, 43215, 984, 6865, 281, 1080, 1065, 13180, 13, 467, 307, 40087, 17366, 278, 264, 4965, 1412, 1339, 10031, 300, 439, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07426183919111888, "compression_ratio": 1.6758893280632412, "no_speech_prob": 1.4102923473133244e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 158502, "start": 1604.06, "end": 1610.3, "text": " systems are nominal. The danger of scope diagnostic sufficiency is that a perfectly maintained system can", "tokens": [51317, 3652, 366, 41641, 13, 440, 4330, 295, 11923, 27897, 459, 49086, 307, 300, 257, 6239, 17578, 1185, 393, 51629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07426183919111888, "compression_ratio": 1.6758893280632412, "no_speech_prob": 1.4102923473133244e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 161030, "start": 1610.3, "end": 1616.22, "text": " become a liability the moment the environment shifts. When the baker fails in Denver, they at", "tokens": [50365, 1813, 257, 25196, 264, 1623, 264, 2823, 19201, 13, 1133, 264, 48148, 18199, 294, 26270, 11, 436, 412, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07805830499400264, "compression_ratio": 1.6694915254237288, "no_speech_prob": 2.315540337596844e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 161030, "start": 1616.22, "end": 1622.1399999999999, "text": " least know the bread is flat. When legacy code base crashes, the engineers know the server is down.", "tokens": [50661, 1935, 458, 264, 5961, 307, 4962, 13, 1133, 11711, 3089, 3096, 28642, 11, 264, 11955, 458, 264, 7154, 307, 760, 13, 50957], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07805830499400264, "compression_ratio": 1.6694915254237288, "no_speech_prob": 2.315540337596844e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 161030, "start": 1622.7, "end": 1628.7, "text": " Ignorance is painful, but it is obvious. The Hamming decoder, facing an out of scope fault,", "tokens": [50985, 24754, 284, 719, 307, 11697, 11, 457, 309, 307, 6322, 13, 440, 8234, 2810, 979, 19866, 11, 7170, 364, 484, 295, 11923, 7441, 11, 51285], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07805830499400264, "compression_ratio": 1.6694915254237288, "no_speech_prob": 2.315540337596844e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 161030, "start": 1628.7, "end": 1634.46, "text": " is experiencing something far worse than ignorance. It is experiencing the illusion of knowledge. If you are", "tokens": [51285, 307, 11139, 746, 1400, 5324, 813, 25390, 13, 467, 307, 11139, 264, 18854, 295, 3601, 13, 759, 291, 366, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07805830499400264, "compression_ratio": 1.6694915254237288, "no_speech_prob": 2.315540337596844e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 163446, "start": 1634.46, "end": 1639.3400000000001, "text": " listening to this, I want you to project this dynamic onto your own life and your own work.", "tokens": [50365, 4764, 281, 341, 11, 286, 528, 291, 281, 1716, 341, 8546, 3911, 428, 1065, 993, 293, 428, 1065, 589, 13, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07294460000662968, "compression_ratio": 1.6611842105263157, "no_speech_prob": 2.1760804963522062e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 163446, "start": 1639.3400000000001, "end": 1644.3, "text": " We build Hamming decoders all the time. Think about the algorithms that govern our social media feeds", "tokens": [50609, 492, 1322, 8234, 2810, 979, 378, 433, 439, 264, 565, 13, 6557, 466, 264, 14642, 300, 1980, 527, 2093, 3021, 23712, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07294460000662968, "compression_ratio": 1.6611842105263157, "no_speech_prob": 2.1760804963522062e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 163446, "start": 1644.3, "end": 1649.66, "text": " or the KPI dashboards you use to run your business. Those dashboards are built on a specific set of", "tokens": [50857, 420, 264, 591, 31701, 8240, 17228, 291, 764, 281, 1190, 428, 1606, 13, 3950, 8240, 17228, 366, 3094, 322, 257, 2685, 992, 295, 51125], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07294460000662968, "compression_ratio": 1.6611842105263157, "no_speech_prob": 2.1760804963522062e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 163446, "start": 1649.66, "end": 1655.18, "text": " diagnostic coordinates, click-through rates, retention metrics, engagement scores. They were perfectly", "tokens": [51125, 27897, 21056, 11, 2052, 12, 11529, 6846, 11, 22871, 16367, 11, 8742, 13444, 13, 814, 645, 6239, 51401], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07294460000662968, "compression_ratio": 1.6611842105263157, "no_speech_prob": 2.1760804963522062e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 163446, "start": 1655.18, "end": 1661.1000000000001, "text": " calibrated to diagnose the business environment as it existed three years ago, your e-design. But the market", "tokens": [51401, 21583, 5468, 281, 36238, 264, 1606, 2823, 382, 309, 13135, 1045, 924, 2057, 11, 428, 308, 12, 14792, 788, 13, 583, 264, 2142, 51697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07294460000662968, "compression_ratio": 1.6611842105263157, "no_speech_prob": 2.1760804963522062e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 166110, "start": 1661.1, "end": 1667.8999999999999, "text": " shifts. Consumer behavior changes. A new technology disrupts the baseline. Your actual environment,", "tokens": [50365, 19201, 13, 39494, 5223, 2962, 13, 316, 777, 2899, 14124, 82, 264, 20518, 13, 2260, 3539, 2823, 11, 50705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07735205142297477, "compression_ratio": 1.6130136986301369, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427689287015768e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 166110, "start": 1667.8999999999999, "end": 1673.1799999999998, "text": " e-actual, has mutated. But your dashboard doesn't throw an error message. It doesn't tell you that", "tokens": [50705, 308, 12, 578, 901, 11, 575, 5839, 770, 13, 583, 428, 18342, 1177, 380, 3507, 364, 6713, 3636, 13, 467, 1177, 380, 980, 291, 300, 50969], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07735205142297477, "compression_ratio": 1.6130136986301369, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427689287015768e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 166110, "start": 1673.1799999999998, "end": 1678.6999999999998, "text": " its foundational assumptions are no longer valid. It just keeps spitting out beautiful high-resolution", "tokens": [50969, 1080, 32195, 17695, 366, 572, 2854, 7363, 13, 467, 445, 5965, 637, 2414, 484, 2238, 1090, 12, 495, 3386, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07735205142297477, "compression_ratio": 1.6130136986301369, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427689287015768e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 166110, "start": 1678.6999999999998, "end": 1685.8999999999999, "text": " charts. And when sales drop, the dashboard confidently diagnoses the problem based on its outdated vocabulary.", "tokens": [51245, 17767, 13, 400, 562, 5763, 3270, 11, 264, 18342, 41956, 7234, 4201, 264, 1154, 2361, 322, 1080, 36313, 19864, 13, 51605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07735205142297477, "compression_ratio": 1.6130136986301369, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427689287015768e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 166110, "start": 1685.8999999999999, "end": 1689.1799999999998, "text": " It tells you to spend more money on a specific ad channel,", "tokens": [51605, 467, 5112, 291, 281, 3496, 544, 1460, 322, 257, 2685, 614, 2269, 11, 51769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07735205142297477, "compression_ratio": 1.6130136986301369, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427689287015768e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 168918, "start": 1689.18, "end": 1694.54, "text": " or to tweak a specific product feature. And because the data looks flawless, you make perfectly", "tokens": [50365, 420, 281, 29879, 257, 2685, 1674, 4111, 13, 400, 570, 264, 1412, 1542, 45693, 11, 291, 652, 6239, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07446805820908657, "compression_ratio": 1.5471698113207548, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656563703118746e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 168918, "start": 1694.54, "end": 1699.9, "text": " logical, data-driven decisions that actively drive your business off a cliff.", "tokens": [50633, 14978, 11, 1412, 12, 25456, 5327, 300, 13022, 3332, 428, 1606, 766, 257, 22316, 13, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07446805820908657, "compression_ratio": 1.5471698113207548, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656563703118746e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 168918, "start": 1699.9, "end": 1703.74, "text": " You are experiencing a confident error on a massive scale.", "tokens": [50901, 509, 366, 11139, 257, 6679, 6713, 322, 257, 5994, 4373, 13, 51093], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07446805820908657, "compression_ratio": 1.5471698113207548, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656563703118746e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 168918, "start": 1703.74, "end": 1709.02, "text": " This leads to a fascinating philosophical point Fliction makes regarding diagnostic autonomy,", "tokens": [51093, 639, 6689, 281, 257, 10343, 25066, 935, 3235, 4105, 1669, 8595, 27897, 27278, 11, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07446805820908657, "compression_ratio": 1.5471698113207548, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656563703118746e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 168918, "start": 1709.02, "end": 1714.3, "text": " which again draws on Jay Wilson's work, specifically the concept of weak emergence.", "tokens": [51357, 597, 797, 20045, 322, 11146, 15388, 311, 589, 11, 4682, 264, 3410, 295, 5336, 36211, 13, 51621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07446805820908657, "compression_ratio": 1.5471698113207548, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656563703118746e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 171430, "start": 1714.3, "end": 1718.78, "text": " There is a natural human instinct, when confronted with the terror of the confident error,", "tokens": [50365, 821, 307, 257, 3303, 1952, 16556, 11, 562, 31257, 365, 264, 8127, 295, 264, 6679, 6713, 11, 50589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07591898464462132, "compression_ratio": 1.667870036101083, "no_speech_prob": 2.793695396546836e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 171430, "start": 1718.78, "end": 1723.58, "text": " to hoard information. We think, if the system missed the double-bit error because it only had", "tokens": [50589, 281, 45940, 1589, 13, 492, 519, 11, 498, 264, 1185, 6721, 264, 3834, 12, 5260, 6713, 570, 309, 787, 632, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07591898464462132, "compression_ratio": 1.667870036101083, "no_speech_prob": 2.793695396546836e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 171430, "start": 1723.58, "end": 1727.8999999999999, "text": " three syndrome bits, we should redesign the system to record every single state change,", "tokens": [50829, 1045, 19371, 9239, 11, 321, 820, 39853, 264, 1185, 281, 2136, 633, 2167, 1785, 1319, 11, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07591898464462132, "compression_ratio": 1.667870036101083, "no_speech_prob": 2.793695396546836e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 171430, "start": 1727.8999999999999, "end": 1732.86, "text": " every microsecond of history, forever. We assume that infinite retention equals infinite", "tokens": [51045, 633, 3123, 37841, 18882, 295, 2503, 11, 5680, 13, 492, 6552, 300, 13785, 22871, 6915, 13785, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07591898464462132, "compression_ratio": 1.667870036101083, "no_speech_prob": 2.793695396546836e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 171430, "start": 1732.86, "end": 1739.02, "text": " repairability. The ultimate big data fallacy. If we just track everything, we'll never be surprised.", "tokens": [51293, 10535, 2310, 13, 440, 9705, 955, 1412, 2100, 2551, 13, 759, 321, 445, 2837, 1203, 11, 321, 603, 1128, 312, 6100, 13, 51601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07591898464462132, "compression_ratio": 1.667870036101083, "no_speech_prob": 2.793695396546836e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 173902, "start": 1739.02, "end": 1745.34, "text": " But weak emergence proves mathematically that this is a computationally impossible and functionally", "tokens": [50365, 583, 5336, 36211, 25019, 44003, 300, 341, 307, 257, 24903, 379, 6243, 293, 2445, 379, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10485929534548805, "compression_ratio": 1.626984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760858972773463e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 173902, "start": 1745.34, "end": 1751.74, "text": " useless goal. A system does not need to retain every detail of its history. It only needs to retain the", "tokens": [50681, 14115, 3387, 13, 316, 1185, 775, 406, 643, 281, 18340, 633, 2607, 295, 1080, 2503, 13, 467, 787, 2203, 281, 18340, 264, 51001], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10485929534548805, "compression_ratio": 1.626984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760858972773463e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 173902, "start": 1751.74, "end": 1757.58, "text": " specific autonomous distinctions that discriminate faults in the environment it actually inhabits.", "tokens": [51001, 2685, 23797, 1483, 49798, 300, 47833, 36090, 294, 264, 2823, 309, 767, 16934, 1208, 13, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10485929534548805, "compression_ratio": 1.626984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760858972773463e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 173902, "start": 1757.58, "end": 1763.98, "text": " So if your computer is buried in a lead-lined bunker where double-bit errors physically cannot occur due to", "tokens": [51293, 407, 498, 428, 3820, 307, 14101, 294, 257, 1477, 12, 13564, 39579, 689, 3834, 12, 5260, 13603, 9762, 2644, 5160, 3462, 281, 51613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10485929534548805, "compression_ratio": 1.626984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760858972773463e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 176398, "start": 1763.98, "end": 1769.66, "text": " radiation shielding, those three syndrome bits are genuinely perfectly sufficient.", "tokens": [50365, 12420, 10257, 278, 11, 729, 1045, 19371, 9239, 366, 17839, 6239, 11563, 13, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08163335063669941, "compression_ratio": 1.6426116838487972, "no_speech_prob": 1.466480365960865e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 176398, "start": 1769.66, "end": 1775.02, "text": " Adding a trillion gigabytes of historical log data wouldn't increase your repairability by a single", "tokens": [50649, 31204, 257, 18723, 42741, 295, 8584, 3565, 1412, 2759, 380, 3488, 428, 10535, 2310, 538, 257, 2167, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08163335063669941, "compression_ratio": 1.6426116838487972, "no_speech_prob": 1.466480365960865e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 176398, "start": 1775.02, "end": 1779.82, "text": " percentage point. It would just add noise. It adds descriptive fidelity to the history, but", "tokens": [50917, 9668, 935, 13, 467, 576, 445, 909, 5658, 13, 467, 10860, 42585, 46404, 281, 264, 2503, 11, 457, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08163335063669941, "compression_ratio": 1.6426116838487972, "no_speech_prob": 1.466480365960865e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 176398, "start": 1779.82, "end": 1785.58, "text": " zero diagnostic value to the repair. The goal of a good system isn't maximal data hoarding. It is", "tokens": [51157, 4018, 27897, 2158, 281, 264, 10535, 13, 440, 3387, 295, 257, 665, 1185, 1943, 380, 49336, 1412, 45940, 278, 13, 467, 307, 51445], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08163335063669941, "compression_ratio": 1.6426116838487972, "no_speech_prob": 1.466480365960865e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 176398, "start": 1785.58, "end": 1790.6200000000001, "text": " perfectly scoped sufficiency. Exactly. You need the precise coordinates that separate the faults you will", "tokens": [51445, 6239, 795, 27277, 459, 49086, 13, 7587, 13, 509, 643, 264, 13600, 21056, 300, 4994, 264, 36090, 291, 486, 51697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08163335063669941, "compression_ratio": 1.6426116838487972, "no_speech_prob": 1.466480365960865e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 179062, "start": 1790.62, "end": 1795.1799999999998, "text": " actually encounter. But the question remains, what happens when you finally realize your scope has", "tokens": [50365, 767, 8593, 13, 583, 264, 1168, 7023, 11, 437, 2314, 562, 291, 2721, 4325, 428, 11923, 575, 50593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08637808894251918, "compression_ratio": 1.6336633663366336, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485619072457603e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 179062, "start": 1795.1799999999998, "end": 1800.78, "text": " failed? What happens when you catch the hemming decoder actively corrupting the data? Or when the baker", "tokens": [50593, 7612, 30, 708, 2314, 562, 291, 3745, 264, 415, 2174, 278, 979, 19866, 13022, 17366, 278, 264, 1412, 30, 1610, 562, 264, 48148, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08637808894251918, "compression_ratio": 1.6336633663366336, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485619072457603e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 179062, "start": 1800.78, "end": 1806.06, "text": " finally accepts that adjusting the yeast won't fix the altitude problem? How do you actually go about", "tokens": [50873, 2721, 33538, 300, 23559, 264, 21629, 1582, 380, 3191, 264, 24003, 1154, 30, 1012, 360, 291, 767, 352, 466, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08637808894251918, "compression_ratio": 1.6336633663366336, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485619072457603e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 179062, "start": 1806.06, "end": 1812.54, "text": " fixing a system that lacks the vocabulary to describe its own failure? This brings us to Section 4,", "tokens": [51137, 19442, 257, 1185, 300, 31132, 264, 19864, 281, 6786, 1080, 1065, 7763, 30, 639, 5607, 505, 281, 21804, 1017, 11, 51461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08637808894251918, "compression_ratio": 1.6336633663366336, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485619072457603e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 179062, "start": 1813.1, "end": 1819.1799999999998, "text": " Vertical vs. Horizontal Repair. The paper divides the act of repair into two fundamentally", "tokens": [51489, 21044, 804, 12041, 13, 42141, 896, 304, 3696, 1246, 13, 440, 3035, 41347, 264, 605, 295, 10535, 666, 732, 17879, 51793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08637808894251918, "compression_ratio": 1.6336633663366336, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485619072457603e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 181918, "start": 1819.18, "end": 1824.7, "text": " different types of cognitive and mathematical labor. Let's start with vertical repair, which is", "tokens": [50365, 819, 3467, 295, 15605, 293, 18894, 5938, 13, 961, 311, 722, 365, 9429, 10535, 11, 597, 307, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06958949565887451, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.694504454287371e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 181918, "start": 1824.7, "end": 1829.42, "text": " essentially the comfort zone of engineering. It means doing more of the same. Let's use the", "tokens": [50641, 4476, 264, 3400, 6668, 295, 7043, 13, 467, 1355, 884, 544, 295, 264, 912, 13, 961, 311, 764, 264, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06958949565887451, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.694504454287371e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 181918, "start": 1829.42, "end": 1835.42, "text": " hamming decoder to illustrate vertical repair. When computer engineers originally realized that double", "tokens": [50877, 36600, 278, 979, 19866, 281, 23221, 9429, 10535, 13, 1133, 3820, 11955, 7993, 5334, 300, 3834, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06958949565887451, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.694504454287371e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 181918, "start": 1835.42, "end": 1841.02, "text": " bit errors were a catastrophic problem, they didn't throw out the entire concept of binary math and", "tokens": [51177, 857, 13603, 645, 257, 34915, 1154, 11, 436, 994, 380, 3507, 484, 264, 2302, 3410, 295, 17434, 5221, 293, 51457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06958949565887451, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.694504454287371e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 181918, "start": 1841.02, "end": 1845.26, "text": " syndrome bits. They stayed within the existing representational scheme. They just extended it.", "tokens": [51457, 19371, 9239, 13, 814, 9181, 1951, 264, 6741, 2906, 1478, 12232, 13, 814, 445, 10913, 309, 13, 51669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06958949565887451, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.694504454287371e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 184526, "start": 1845.26, "end": 1851.02, "text": " They added one extra bit to the end of the string, an overall parity bit. Yes. By adding that single", "tokens": [50365, 814, 3869, 472, 2857, 857, 281, 264, 917, 295, 264, 6798, 11, 364, 4787, 44747, 857, 13, 1079, 13, 3146, 5127, 300, 2167, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0710643148913826, "compression_ratio": 1.6374501992031874, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439429228996664e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 184526, "start": 1851.02, "end": 1858.54, "text": " bit, they engaged in vertical repair. They created a new standard called SCCD, Single Error Correction,", "tokens": [50653, 857, 11, 436, 8237, 294, 9429, 10535, 13, 814, 2942, 257, 777, 3832, 1219, 9028, 16508, 11, 31248, 3300, 2874, 3925, 11417, 11, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0710643148913826, "compression_ratio": 1.6374501992031874, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439429228996664e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 184526, "start": 1858.54, "end": 1863.82, "text": " Double Error Detection. They expanded the diagnostic power of the system without inventing a new language.", "tokens": [51029, 16633, 3300, 2874, 4237, 10183, 13, 814, 14342, 264, 27897, 1347, 295, 264, 1185, 1553, 7962, 278, 257, 777, 2856, 13, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0710643148913826, "compression_ratio": 1.6374501992031874, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439429228996664e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 184526, "start": 1863.82, "end": 1870.3, "text": " Now, when a double bit error occurs, the system evaluates the extended string and essentially says,", "tokens": [51293, 823, 11, 562, 257, 3834, 857, 6713, 11843, 11, 264, 1185, 6133, 1024, 264, 10913, 6798, 293, 4476, 1619, 11, 51617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0710643148913826, "compression_ratio": 1.6374501992031874, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439429228996664e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 187030, "start": 1870.3, "end": 1876.86, "text": " I see a 2-bit error. I don't have enough resolution to fix it, but I possess the vocabulary to recognize it.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 536, 257, 568, 12, 5260, 6713, 13, 286, 500, 380, 362, 1547, 8669, 281, 3191, 309, 11, 457, 286, 17490, 264, 19864, 281, 5521, 309, 13, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06526999945168967, "compression_ratio": 1.5783132530120483, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810568116507277e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 187030, "start": 1877.58, "end": 1883.5, "text": " I refuse to certify this data as safe. I am throwing an error. They cured the confident error", "tokens": [50729, 286, 16791, 281, 5351, 2505, 341, 1412, 382, 3273, 13, 286, 669, 10238, 364, 6713, 13, 814, 29617, 264, 6679, 6713, 51025], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06526999945168967, "compression_ratio": 1.5783132530120483, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810568116507277e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 187030, "start": 1883.5, "end": 1889.18, "text": " by climbing higher on the existing lattice of possibilities. Vertical repair is powerful,", "tokens": [51025, 538, 14780, 2946, 322, 264, 6741, 34011, 295, 12178, 13, 21044, 804, 10535, 307, 4005, 11, 51309], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06526999945168967, "compression_ratio": 1.5783132530120483, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810568116507277e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 187030, "start": 1889.18, "end": 1895.4199999999998, "text": " but it is bounded. It encompasses things like recovering lost documentation for the legacy code base", "tokens": [51309, 457, 309, 307, 37498, 13, 467, 49866, 721, 411, 29180, 2731, 14333, 337, 264, 11711, 3089, 3096, 51621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06526999945168967, "compression_ratio": 1.5783132530120483, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810568116507277e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 189542, "start": 1895.42, "end": 1900.7, "text": " or adding a parity bit. You are manipulating the existing vocabulary to cover a slightly larger", "tokens": [50365, 420, 5127, 257, 44747, 857, 13, 509, 366, 40805, 264, 6741, 19864, 281, 2060, 257, 4748, 4833, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06349896934797179, "compression_ratio": 1.7429577464788732, "no_speech_prob": 2.686646911886914e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 189542, "start": 1900.7, "end": 1905.8200000000002, "text": " fault space, but horizontal repair is entirely different and it is vastly more difficult. To", "tokens": [50629, 7441, 1901, 11, 457, 12750, 10535, 307, 7696, 819, 293, 309, 307, 41426, 544, 2252, 13, 1407, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06349896934797179, "compression_ratio": 1.7429577464788732, "no_speech_prob": 2.686646911886914e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 189542, "start": 1905.8200000000002, "end": 1911.1000000000001, "text": " understand horizontal repair, we have to go back to the cabin in Denver. The baker is staring at the", "tokens": [50885, 1223, 12750, 10535, 11, 321, 362, 281, 352, 646, 281, 264, 9401, 294, 26270, 13, 440, 48148, 307, 18043, 412, 264, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06349896934797179, "compression_ratio": 1.7429577464788732, "no_speech_prob": 2.686646911886914e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 189542, "start": 1911.1000000000001, "end": 1916.8600000000001, "text": " flatbread. They have exhausted all vertical repairs. They've tweaked the flour ratios. They've changed the", "tokens": [51149, 4962, 31051, 13, 814, 362, 17992, 439, 9429, 28823, 13, 814, 600, 6986, 7301, 264, 7693, 32435, 13, 814, 600, 3105, 264, 51437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06349896934797179, "compression_ratio": 1.7429577464788732, "no_speech_prob": 2.686646911886914e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 189542, "start": 1916.8600000000001, "end": 1921.66, "text": " oven temperature. They've bought new yeast. They have explored every possible combination of their", "tokens": [51437, 9090, 4292, 13, 814, 600, 4243, 777, 21629, 13, 814, 362, 24016, 633, 1944, 6562, 295, 641, 51677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06349896934797179, "compression_ratio": 1.7429577464788732, "no_speech_prob": 2.686646911886914e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 192166, "start": 1921.66, "end": 1927.26, "text": " existing vocabulary and nothing works. How do they solve the problem? They cannot solve it from within", "tokens": [50365, 6741, 19864, 293, 1825, 1985, 13, 1012, 360, 436, 5039, 264, 1154, 30, 814, 2644, 5039, 309, 490, 1951, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0516990490679471, "compression_ratio": 1.6366666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420038052305523e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 192166, "start": 1927.26, "end": 1933.74, "text": " the recipe. To successfully diagnose the altitude failure, the baker has to undergo a fundamental", "tokens": [50645, 264, 6782, 13, 1407, 10727, 36238, 264, 24003, 7763, 11, 264, 48148, 575, 281, 26426, 257, 8088, 50969], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0516990490679471, "compression_ratio": 1.6366666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420038052305523e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 192166, "start": 1933.74, "end": 1938.8600000000001, "text": " cognitive shift. They must introduce concepts that did not exist in the grandmother's universe.", "tokens": [50969, 15605, 5513, 13, 814, 1633, 5366, 10392, 300, 630, 406, 2514, 294, 264, 14317, 311, 6445, 13, 51225], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0516990490679471, "compression_ratio": 1.6366666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420038052305523e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 192166, "start": 1938.8600000000001, "end": 1944.94, "text": " Whaling point, atmosphere pressure, evaporation rate. And as the paper proves in its mathematical", "tokens": [51225, 506, 4270, 935, 11, 8018, 3321, 11, 1073, 569, 9357, 3314, 13, 400, 382, 264, 3035, 25019, 294, 1080, 18894, 51529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0516990490679471, "compression_ratio": 1.6366666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420038052305523e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 192166, "start": 1944.94, "end": 1951.18, "text": " breakdown, this is not a recovery of lost data. This is the crucial distinction. The baker isn't", "tokens": [51529, 18188, 11, 341, 307, 406, 257, 8597, 295, 2731, 1412, 13, 639, 307, 264, 11462, 16844, 13, 440, 48148, 1943, 380, 51841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0516990490679471, "compression_ratio": 1.6366666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420038052305523e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 195118, "start": 1951.18, "end": 1955.18, "text": " remembering something the grandmother forgot to write down. The grandmother didn't know what", "tokens": [50365, 20719, 746, 264, 14317, 5298, 281, 2464, 760, 13, 440, 14317, 994, 380, 458, 437, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06329604621245483, "compression_ratio": 1.7040816326530612, "no_speech_prob": 2.0280209803158478e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 195118, "start": 1955.18, "end": 1961.3400000000001, "text": " atmospheric pressure was either, and she didn't need to. The baker is inventing an entirely new ontology.", "tokens": [50565, 28854, 3321, 390, 2139, 11, 293, 750, 994, 380, 643, 281, 13, 440, 48148, 307, 7962, 278, 364, 7696, 777, 6592, 1793, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06329604621245483, "compression_ratio": 1.7040816326530612, "no_speech_prob": 2.0280209803158478e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 195118, "start": 1961.3400000000001, "end": 1966.8600000000001, "text": " They are completely re-describing the fault space itself. They are jumping to an entirely new set of", "tokens": [50873, 814, 366, 2584, 319, 12, 14792, 39541, 264, 7441, 1901, 2564, 13, 814, 366, 11233, 281, 364, 7696, 777, 992, 295, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06329604621245483, "compression_ratio": 1.7040816326530612, "no_speech_prob": 2.0280209803158478e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 195118, "start": 1966.8600000000001, "end": 1972.54, "text": " framework assumptions. Horizontal repair requires introducing a coordinate type that was fundamentally", "tokens": [51149, 8388, 17695, 13, 42141, 896, 304, 10535, 7029, 15424, 257, 15670, 2010, 300, 390, 17879, 51433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06329604621245483, "compression_ratio": 1.7040816326530612, "no_speech_prob": 2.0280209803158478e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 195118, "start": 1972.54, "end": 1978.0600000000002, "text": " unrepresentable in the original vocabulary. You cannot map out the physics of high-altitude baking", "tokens": [51433, 517, 19919, 11662, 712, 294, 264, 3380, 19864, 13, 509, 2644, 4471, 484, 264, 10649, 295, 1090, 12, 3198, 4377, 12102, 51709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06329604621245483, "compression_ratio": 1.7040816326530612, "no_speech_prob": 2.0280209803158478e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 197806, "start": 1978.06, "end": 1983.82, "text": " using only the language of cups of flour and minutes in the oven. But consider the philosophical weight of", "tokens": [50365, 1228, 787, 264, 2856, 295, 13381, 295, 7693, 293, 2077, 294, 264, 9090, 13, 583, 1949, 264, 25066, 3364, 295, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06537113303229922, "compression_ratio": 1.57421875, "no_speech_prob": 2.201405507537557e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 197806, "start": 1983.82, "end": 1989.1799999999998, "text": " that. To engage in horizontal repair, you have to look at your current understanding of the world,", "tokens": [50653, 300, 13, 1407, 4683, 294, 12750, 10535, 11, 291, 362, 281, 574, 412, 428, 2190, 3701, 295, 264, 1002, 11, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06537113303229922, "compression_ratio": 1.57421875, "no_speech_prob": 2.201405507537557e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 197806, "start": 1989.1799999999998, "end": 1994.22, "text": " acknowledge that it is mathematically inadequate to describe the reality you are experiencing,", "tokens": [50921, 10692, 300, 309, 307, 44003, 42107, 281, 6786, 264, 4103, 291, 366, 11139, 11, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06537113303229922, "compression_ratio": 1.57421875, "no_speech_prob": 2.201405507537557e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 197806, "start": 1994.22, "end": 1999.5, "text": " and somehow invent a concept you didn't previously know existed. It's like a society that believes the", "tokens": [51173, 293, 6063, 7962, 257, 3410, 291, 994, 380, 8046, 458, 13135, 13, 467, 311, 411, 257, 4086, 300, 12307, 264, 51437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06537113303229922, "compression_ratio": 1.57421875, "no_speech_prob": 2.201405507537557e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 199950, "start": 1999.5, "end": 2006.54, "text": " world is a flat 2D map trying to understand why airplanes disappear over the horizon. You can't", "tokens": [50365, 1002, 307, 257, 4962, 568, 35, 4471, 1382, 281, 1223, 983, 32947, 11596, 670, 264, 18046, 13, 509, 393, 380, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08112092018127441, "compression_ratio": 1.596774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 2.3709688726225586e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 199950, "start": 2006.54, "end": 2011.82, "text": " just draw more lines on the map. You have to invent the z-axis. You have to invent a globe. And that is", "tokens": [50717, 445, 2642, 544, 3876, 322, 264, 4471, 13, 509, 362, 281, 7962, 264, 710, 12, 24633, 13, 509, 362, 281, 7962, 257, 15371, 13, 400, 300, 307, 50981], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08112092018127441, "compression_ratio": 1.596774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 2.3709688726225586e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 199950, "start": 2011.82, "end": 2017.9, "text": " exactly why affliction leaves the formalization of horizontal repair as an open frontier in the paper.", "tokens": [50981, 2293, 983, 2096, 75, 4105, 5510, 264, 9860, 2144, 295, 12750, 10535, 382, 364, 1269, 35853, 294, 264, 3035, 13, 51285], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08112092018127441, "compression_ratio": 1.596774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 2.3709688726225586e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 199950, "start": 2018.78, "end": 2023.98, "text": " The entire mathematical framework of diagnostic coordinates is built on tracking distinctions", "tokens": [51329, 440, 2302, 18894, 8388, 295, 27897, 21056, 307, 3094, 322, 11603, 1483, 49798, 51589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08112092018127441, "compression_ratio": 1.596774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 2.3709688726225586e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 202398, "start": 2023.98, "end": 2029.26, "text": " within a known set of possibilities. How do you mathematically model the sudden expansion of the", "tokens": [50365, 1951, 257, 2570, 992, 295, 12178, 13, 1012, 360, 291, 44003, 2316, 264, 3990, 11260, 295, 264, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07259633899789995, "compression_ratio": 1.6612903225806452, "no_speech_prob": 1.3993211971097264e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 202398, "start": 2029.26, "end": 2035.1, "text": " possibility space itself? How do you formalize a paradigm shift? The math becomes exponentially more", "tokens": [50629, 7959, 1901, 2564, 30, 1012, 360, 291, 9860, 1125, 257, 24709, 5513, 30, 440, 5221, 3643, 37330, 544, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07259633899789995, "compression_ratio": 1.6612903225806452, "no_speech_prob": 1.3993211971097264e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 202398, "start": 2035.1, "end": 2041.1, "text": " complex. Infliction admits that entirely new formal machinery will be needed to map it out. Okay, let's", "tokens": [50921, 3997, 13, 682, 3423, 4105, 46682, 300, 7696, 777, 9860, 27302, 486, 312, 2978, 281, 4471, 309, 484, 13, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07259633899789995, "compression_ratio": 1.6612903225806452, "no_speech_prob": 1.3993211971097264e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 202398, "start": 2041.1, "end": 2046.78, "text": " pull back and look at the terrifying landscape we've just traversed. We've seen history-first systems that", "tokens": [51221, 2235, 646, 293, 574, 412, 264, 18106, 9661, 321, 600, 445, 23149, 292, 13, 492, 600, 1612, 2503, 12, 29581, 3652, 300, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07259633899789995, "compression_ratio": 1.6612903225806452, "no_speech_prob": 1.3993211971097264e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 202398, "start": 2046.78, "end": 2052.46, "text": " never had the vocabulary to survive outside their niche. We've seen theory-first systems passively wrought", "tokens": [51505, 1128, 632, 264, 19864, 281, 7867, 2380, 641, 19956, 13, 492, 600, 1612, 5261, 12, 29581, 3652, 1320, 3413, 928, 930, 51789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07259633899789995, "compression_ratio": 1.6612903225806452, "no_speech_prob": 1.3993211971097264e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 205246, "start": 2052.46, "end": 2057.7400000000002, "text": " away into magic constants due to transmission decay. We've seen perfectly maintained systems", "tokens": [50365, 1314, 666, 5585, 35870, 3462, 281, 11574, 21039, 13, 492, 600, 1612, 6239, 17578, 3652, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.047152664603256594, "compression_ratio": 1.6015936254980079, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111144094862253e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 205246, "start": 2057.7400000000002, "end": 2063.42, "text": " confidently lie to us because the world changed beneath their feet. And we've seen that fixing these", "tokens": [50629, 41956, 4544, 281, 505, 570, 264, 1002, 3105, 17149, 641, 3521, 13, 400, 321, 600, 1612, 300, 19442, 613, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.047152664603256594, "compression_ratio": 1.6015936254980079, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111144094862253e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 205246, "start": 2063.42, "end": 2070.54, "text": " profound scope failures requires inventing entirely new dimensions of reality. It feels like entropy has", "tokens": [50913, 14382, 11923, 20774, 7029, 7962, 278, 7696, 777, 12819, 295, 4103, 13, 467, 3417, 411, 30867, 575, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.047152664603256594, "compression_ratio": 1.6015936254980079, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111144094862253e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 205246, "start": 2070.54, "end": 2077.26, "text": " all the cards. Is decay just the inevitable tragic end state of all complex systems? If the paper ended", "tokens": [51269, 439, 264, 5632, 13, 1119, 21039, 445, 264, 21451, 20385, 917, 1785, 295, 439, 3997, 3652, 30, 759, 264, 3035, 4590, 51605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.047152664603256594, "compression_ratio": 1.6015936254980079, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111144094862253e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 207726, "start": 2077.26, "end": 2083.6600000000003, "text": " there, it would be a purely pessimistic read. But Flixian introduces a fourth and final case study to", "tokens": [50365, 456, 11, 309, 576, 312, 257, 17491, 37399, 3142, 1401, 13, 583, 3235, 970, 952, 31472, 257, 6409, 293, 2572, 1389, 2979, 281, 50685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07097053527832031, "compression_ratio": 1.5300751879699248, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281916999886682e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 207726, "start": 2083.6600000000003, "end": 2089.6600000000003, "text": " prove that decay, while inevitable, does not have to be terminal. It requires us to look at the very", "tokens": [50685, 7081, 300, 21039, 11, 1339, 21451, 11, 775, 406, 362, 281, 312, 14709, 13, 467, 7029, 505, 281, 574, 412, 264, 588, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07097053527832031, "compression_ratio": 1.5300751879699248, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281916999886682e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 207726, "start": 2089.6600000000003, "end": 2095.34, "text": " foundation of modern computing. Case four, the DRAM cell. Dynamic random access memory. This is the", "tokens": [50985, 7030, 295, 4363, 15866, 13, 17791, 1451, 11, 264, 12118, 2865, 2815, 13, 45440, 4974, 2105, 4675, 13, 639, 307, 264, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07097053527832031, "compression_ratio": 1.5300751879699248, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281916999886682e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 207726, "start": 2095.34, "end": 2100.38, "text": " physical hardware that is actively holding this very conversation in the memory of the listener's device", "tokens": [51269, 4001, 8837, 300, 307, 13022, 5061, 341, 588, 3761, 294, 264, 4675, 295, 264, 31569, 311, 4302, 51521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07097053527832031, "compression_ratio": 1.5300751879699248, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281916999886682e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 210038, "start": 2100.38, "end": 2105.82, "text": " right now. Yes. A DRAM cell is incredibly simple at a physical level. It stores a single bit of", "tokens": [50365, 558, 586, 13, 1079, 13, 316, 12118, 2865, 2815, 307, 6252, 2199, 412, 257, 4001, 1496, 13, 467, 9512, 257, 2167, 857, 295, 50637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0547246975941701, "compression_ratio": 1.6411960132890366, "no_speech_prob": 2.5233636794658176e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 210038, "start": 2105.82, "end": 2111.82, "text": " information, a one or zero, as an electrical charge held on a microscopic capacitor. But physics is", "tokens": [50637, 1589, 11, 257, 472, 420, 4018, 11, 382, 364, 12147, 4602, 5167, 322, 257, 47897, 29372, 13, 583, 10649, 307, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0547246975941701, "compression_ratio": 1.6411960132890366, "no_speech_prob": 2.5233636794658176e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 210038, "start": 2111.82, "end": 2116.46, "text": " relentless. The moment you push that electrical charge onto the capacitor, it begins to leak away.", "tokens": [50937, 46136, 13, 440, 1623, 291, 2944, 300, 12147, 4602, 3911, 264, 29372, 11, 309, 7338, 281, 17143, 1314, 13, 51169], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0547246975941701, "compression_ratio": 1.6411960132890366, "no_speech_prob": 2.5233636794658176e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 210038, "start": 2116.46, "end": 2122.78, "text": " The voltage drops, governed by a strict exponential decay curve. It is experiencing the exact same", "tokens": [51169, 440, 8352, 11438, 11, 35529, 538, 257, 10910, 21510, 21039, 7605, 13, 467, 307, 11139, 264, 1900, 912, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0547246975941701, "compression_ratio": 1.6411960132890366, "no_speech_prob": 2.5233636794658176e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 210038, "start": 2122.78, "end": 2128.78, "text": " physical reality as the legacy code base. Left alone, the charge will bleed out into the surrounding", "tokens": [51485, 4001, 4103, 382, 264, 11711, 3089, 3096, 13, 16405, 3312, 11, 264, 4602, 486, 28385, 484, 666, 264, 11498, 51785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0547246975941701, "compression_ratio": 1.6411960132890366, "no_speech_prob": 2.5233636794658176e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 212878, "start": 2128.78, "end": 2134.94, "text": " silicon. The voltage will drop to zero and the data will be lost forever. Entropy is pulling it toward", "tokens": [50365, 22848, 13, 440, 8352, 486, 3270, 281, 4018, 293, 264, 1412, 486, 312, 2731, 5680, 13, 3951, 27514, 307, 8407, 309, 7361, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05569045733561558, "compression_ratio": 1.6879194630872483, "no_speech_prob": 1.489249262104364e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 212878, "start": 2134.94, "end": 2141.02, "text": " oblivion. But the DRAM cell doesn't die. And it doesn't survive because it was perfectly documented", "tokens": [50673, 47039, 313, 13, 583, 264, 12118, 2865, 2815, 1177, 380, 978, 13, 400, 309, 1177, 380, 7867, 570, 309, 390, 6239, 23007, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05569045733561558, "compression_ratio": 1.6879194630872483, "no_speech_prob": 1.489249262104364e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 212878, "start": 2141.02, "end": 2145.9, "text": " or because it has an incredibly robust initial compression. It survives because it utilizes an", "tokens": [50977, 420, 570, 309, 575, 364, 6252, 13956, 5883, 19355, 13, 467, 46231, 570, 309, 4976, 5660, 364, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05569045733561558, "compression_ratio": 1.6879194630872483, "no_speech_prob": 1.489249262104364e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 212878, "start": 2145.9, "end": 2151.82, "text": " active, scheduled, relentless process called the refresh cycle. This is the genius of the architecture.", "tokens": [51221, 4967, 11, 15678, 11, 46136, 1399, 1219, 264, 15134, 6586, 13, 639, 307, 264, 14017, 295, 264, 9482, 13, 51517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05569045733561558, "compression_ratio": 1.6879194630872483, "no_speech_prob": 1.489249262104364e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 212878, "start": 2151.82, "end": 2157.5, "text": " The computer knows the physics of the decay. It knows that there is a critical threshold called Vmin,", "tokens": [51517, 440, 3820, 3255, 264, 10649, 295, 264, 21039, 13, 467, 3255, 300, 456, 307, 257, 4924, 14678, 1219, 691, 2367, 11, 51801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05569045733561558, "compression_ratio": 1.6879194630872483, "no_speech_prob": 1.489249262104364e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 215750, "start": 2157.5, "end": 2161.66, "text": " the minimum distinguishable voltage. If the charge drops below Vmin,", "tokens": [50365, 264, 7285, 20206, 712, 8352, 13, 759, 264, 4602, 11438, 2507, 691, 2367, 11, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0665308961244387, "compression_ratio": 1.6763636363636363, "no_speech_prob": 2.117074310997724e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 215750, "start": 2161.66, "end": 2166.78, "text": " the computer can no longer tell if it's looking at a faded one or just background static. The", "tokens": [50573, 264, 3820, 393, 572, 2854, 980, 498, 309, 311, 1237, 412, 257, 36352, 472, 420, 445, 3678, 13437, 13, 440, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0665308961244387, "compression_ratio": 1.6763636363636363, "no_speech_prob": 2.117074310997724e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 215750, "start": 2166.78, "end": 2172.22, "text": " pixelation has become too severe. So before the voltage can ever hit Vmin, the computer sends a", "tokens": [50829, 19261, 399, 575, 1813, 886, 8922, 13, 407, 949, 264, 8352, 393, 1562, 2045, 691, 2367, 11, 264, 3820, 14790, 257, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0665308961244387, "compression_ratio": 1.6763636363636363, "no_speech_prob": 2.117074310997724e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 215750, "start": 2172.22, "end": 2178.06, "text": " command. It physically reads the fading degraded charge, interprets it while the resolution is still", "tokens": [51101, 5622, 13, 467, 9762, 15700, 264, 38644, 24740, 292, 4602, 11, 17489, 1373, 309, 1339, 264, 8669, 307, 920, 51393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0665308961244387, "compression_ratio": 1.6763636363636363, "no_speech_prob": 2.117074310997724e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 215750, "start": 2178.06, "end": 2184.14, "text": " just barely high enough, and then actively rewrites that same data back into the cell at full maximum", "tokens": [51393, 445, 10268, 1090, 1547, 11, 293, 550, 13022, 319, 86, 30931, 300, 912, 1412, 646, 666, 264, 2815, 412, 1577, 6674, 51697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0665308961244387, "compression_ratio": 1.6763636363636363, "no_speech_prob": 2.117074310997724e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 218414, "start": 2184.14, "end": 2189.2599999999998, "text": " voltage. It catches the signal right as it's fading into noise and shouts it back into existence. And", "tokens": [50365, 8352, 13, 467, 25496, 264, 6358, 558, 382, 309, 311, 38644, 666, 5658, 293, 402, 7711, 309, 646, 666, 9123, 13, 400, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04907076934288288, "compression_ratio": 1.6188524590163935, "no_speech_prob": 1.560289983153218e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 218414, "start": 2189.2599999999998, "end": 2194.46, "text": " it does this thousands of times a second. The mathematical proof for this establishes that as", "tokens": [50621, 309, 775, 341, 5383, 295, 1413, 257, 1150, 13, 440, 18894, 8177, 337, 341, 8327, 279, 300, 382, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04907076934288288, "compression_ratio": 1.6188524590163935, "no_speech_prob": 1.560289983153218e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 218414, "start": 2194.46, "end": 2199.74, "text": " long as the interval between those refresh cycles is strictly shorter than the time it takes for the", "tokens": [50881, 938, 382, 264, 15035, 1296, 729, 15134, 17796, 307, 20792, 11639, 813, 264, 565, 309, 2516, 337, 264, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04907076934288288, "compression_ratio": 1.6188524590163935, "no_speech_prob": 1.560289983153218e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 218414, "start": 2199.74, "end": 2206.22, "text": " exponential decay to hit Vmin, the readability condition of the system is maintained indefinitely.", "tokens": [51145, 21510, 21039, 281, 2045, 691, 2367, 11, 264, 1401, 2310, 4188, 295, 264, 1185, 307, 17578, 24162, 10925, 13, 51469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04907076934288288, "compression_ratio": 1.6188524590163935, "no_speech_prob": 1.560289983153218e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 220622, "start": 2206.22, "end": 2211.58, "text": " You can hold a fragile, leaky electrical charge perfectly stable forever, not by building a", "tokens": [50365, 509, 393, 1797, 257, 23847, 11, 476, 15681, 12147, 4602, 6239, 8351, 5680, 11, 406, 538, 2390, 257, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06875369401104682, "compression_ratio": 1.619672131147541, "no_speech_prob": 1.72117994769877e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 220622, "start": 2211.58, "end": 2217.8199999999997, "text": " better capacitor, but by actively fighting the decay. Consider the massive philosophical implications", "tokens": [50633, 1101, 29372, 11, 457, 538, 13022, 5237, 264, 21039, 13, 17416, 264, 5994, 25066, 16602, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06875369401104682, "compression_ratio": 1.619672131147541, "no_speech_prob": 1.72117994769877e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 220622, "start": 2217.8199999999997, "end": 2223.58, "text": " this has for human systems. We tend to view repairability as a static property. We think of", "tokens": [50945, 341, 575, 337, 1952, 3652, 13, 492, 3928, 281, 1910, 10535, 2310, 382, 257, 13437, 4707, 13, 492, 519, 295, 51233], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06875369401104682, "compression_ratio": 1.619672131147541, "no_speech_prob": 1.72117994769877e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 220622, "start": 2223.58, "end": 2228.7, "text": " a corporate culture or a marriage or a code base as something we build once. We write the employee", "tokens": [51233, 257, 10896, 3713, 420, 257, 7194, 420, 257, 3089, 3096, 382, 746, 321, 1322, 1564, 13, 492, 2464, 264, 10738, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06875369401104682, "compression_ratio": 1.619672131147541, "no_speech_prob": 1.72117994769877e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 220622, "start": 2228.7, "end": 2234.9399999999996, "text": " handbook, we say our vows, we publish the code, and we expect it to just stand there defying gravity. But the", "tokens": [51489, 1011, 2939, 11, 321, 584, 527, 371, 1509, 11, 321, 11374, 264, 3089, 11, 293, 321, 2066, 309, 281, 445, 1463, 456, 1060, 1840, 12110, 13, 583, 264, 51801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06875369401104682, "compression_ratio": 1.619672131147541, "no_speech_prob": 1.72117994769877e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 223494, "start": 2234.94, "end": 2240.86, "text": " DRAM cell proves that diagnostic availability is not a static quantity. It is an active state that", "tokens": [50365, 12118, 2865, 2815, 25019, 300, 27897, 17945, 307, 406, 257, 13437, 11275, 13, 467, 307, 364, 4967, 1785, 300, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052952832645840116, "compression_ratio": 1.583596214511041, "no_speech_prob": 1.93517380939201e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 223494, "start": 2240.86, "end": 2246.14, "text": " requires continuous, deliberate reinvestment. For human organizations, memory and understanding are", "tokens": [50661, 7029, 10957, 11, 30515, 6561, 5571, 518, 13, 1171, 1952, 6150, 11, 4675, 293, 3701, 366, 50925], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052952832645840116, "compression_ratio": 1.583596214511041, "no_speech_prob": 1.93517380939201e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 223494, "start": 2246.14, "end": 2251.9, "text": " just leaky capacitors. Institutional knowledge evaporates. The why behind the processes degrades", "tokens": [50925, 445, 476, 15681, 4637, 9862, 13, 2730, 41859, 3601, 26315, 1024, 13, 440, 983, 2261, 264, 7555, 368, 22626, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052952832645840116, "compression_ratio": 1.583596214511041, "no_speech_prob": 1.93517380939201e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 223494, "start": 2251.9, "end": 2257.42, "text": " into background noise. If you want your team's processes to survive, you cannot just write a brilliant", "tokens": [51213, 666, 3678, 5658, 13, 759, 291, 528, 428, 1469, 311, 7555, 281, 7867, 11, 291, 2644, 445, 2464, 257, 10248, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052952832645840116, "compression_ratio": 1.583596214511041, "no_speech_prob": 1.93517380939201e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 223494, "start": 2257.42, "end": 2263.1, "text": " manifesto on day one and walk away. You have to establish a refresh rate. You have to actively schedule", "tokens": [51489, 10067, 78, 322, 786, 472, 293, 1792, 1314, 13, 509, 362, 281, 8327, 257, 15134, 3314, 13, 509, 362, 281, 13022, 7567, 51773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052952832645840116, "compression_ratio": 1.583596214511041, "no_speech_prob": 1.93517380939201e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 226310, "start": 2263.1, "end": 2268.7, "text": " moments where you pull the team together and say, let's read the fading charge of our institutional", "tokens": [50365, 6065, 689, 291, 2235, 264, 1469, 1214, 293, 584, 11, 718, 311, 1401, 264, 38644, 4602, 295, 527, 18391, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0653602641561757, "compression_ratio": 1.643312101910828, "no_speech_prob": 1.721189597098105e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 226310, "start": 2268.7, "end": 2273.9, "text": " memory. Why do we perform step three this way? Oh, right, because of that catastrophic client failure", "tokens": [50645, 4675, 13, 1545, 360, 321, 2042, 1823, 1045, 341, 636, 30, 876, 11, 558, 11, 570, 295, 300, 34915, 6423, 7763, 50905], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0653602641561757, "compression_ratio": 1.643312101910828, "no_speech_prob": 1.721189597098105e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 226310, "start": 2273.9, "end": 2278.7799999999997, "text": " three years ago. You take that faded memory and you rewrite it to full strength in the minds of your", "tokens": [50905, 1045, 924, 2057, 13, 509, 747, 300, 36352, 4675, 293, 291, 28132, 309, 281, 1577, 3800, 294, 264, 9634, 295, 428, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0653602641561757, "compression_ratio": 1.643312101910828, "no_speech_prob": 1.721189597098105e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 226310, "start": 2278.7799999999997, "end": 2284.38, "text": " current team. If you don't schedule that refresh cycle, the physics of human forgetting guarantees that", "tokens": [51149, 2190, 1469, 13, 759, 291, 500, 380, 7567, 300, 15134, 6586, 11, 264, 10649, 295, 1952, 25428, 32567, 300, 51429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0653602641561757, "compression_ratio": 1.643312101910828, "no_speech_prob": 1.721189597098105e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 226310, "start": 2284.38, "end": 2290.38, "text": " you will eventually hit human. The reason for the process will become indistinguishable from the daily grind,", "tokens": [51429, 291, 486, 4728, 2045, 1952, 13, 440, 1778, 337, 264, 1399, 486, 1813, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 712, 490, 264, 5212, 16700, 11, 51729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0653602641561757, "compression_ratio": 1.643312101910828, "no_speech_prob": 1.721189597098105e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 229038, "start": 2290.38, "end": 2296.2200000000003, "text": " and you will be left with a company run by magic constants where nobody knows why anything happens,", "tokens": [50365, 293, 291, 486, 312, 1411, 365, 257, 2237, 1190, 538, 5585, 35870, 689, 5079, 3255, 983, 1340, 2314, 11, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08896236858148684, "compression_ratio": 1.52734375, "no_speech_prob": 1.410305249319177e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 229038, "start": 2296.2200000000003, "end": 2301.42, "text": " but everyone is terrified to change it. The origin of your culture doesn't matter if you aren't", "tokens": [50657, 457, 1518, 307, 23051, 281, 1319, 309, 13, 440, 4957, 295, 428, 3713, 1177, 380, 1871, 498, 291, 3212, 380, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08896236858148684, "compression_ratio": 1.52734375, "no_speech_prob": 1.410305249319177e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 229038, "start": 2301.42, "end": 2307.1, "text": " actively regenerating its coordinates. So how does Fliction synthesize this incredible journey?", "tokens": [50917, 13022, 26358, 990, 1080, 21056, 13, 407, 577, 775, 3235, 4105, 26617, 1125, 341, 4651, 4671, 30, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08896236858148684, "compression_ratio": 1.52734375, "no_speech_prob": 1.410305249319177e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 229038, "start": 2307.9, "end": 2314.3, "text": " We have a grandmother's seaside recipe, a rotting corporate code base, a blind but confident binary", "tokens": [51241, 492, 362, 257, 14317, 311, 22535, 482, 6782, 11, 257, 4297, 783, 10896, 3089, 3096, 11, 257, 6865, 457, 6679, 17434, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08896236858148684, "compression_ratio": 1.52734375, "no_speech_prob": 1.410305249319177e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 231430, "start": 2314.3, "end": 2320.94, "text": " decoder, and a physically leaking microscopic capacitor. How do these wildly disparate realities", "tokens": [50365, 979, 19866, 11, 293, 257, 9762, 32856, 47897, 29372, 13, 1012, 360, 613, 34731, 14548, 473, 27785, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05690425017784382, "compression_ratio": 1.588, "no_speech_prob": 2.124889890778303e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 231430, "start": 2321.42, "end": 2326.78, "text": " coalesce into a single theory of repair? In the final section of the paper, Fliction brings all these", "tokens": [50721, 598, 4229, 384, 666, 257, 2167, 5261, 295, 10535, 30, 682, 264, 2572, 3541, 295, 264, 3035, 11, 3235, 4105, 5607, 439, 613, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05690425017784382, "compression_ratio": 1.588, "no_speech_prob": 2.124889890778303e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 231430, "start": 2326.78, "end": 2331.5, "text": " threads together, but they do it with a remarkable degree of scientific humility. They propose an", "tokens": [50989, 19314, 1214, 11, 457, 436, 360, 309, 365, 257, 12802, 4314, 295, 8134, 27106, 13, 814, 17421, 364, 51225], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05690425017784382, "compression_ratio": 1.588, "no_speech_prob": 2.124889890778303e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 231430, "start": 2331.5, "end": 2337.98, "text": " unresolved equation. The paper establishes unequivocally that diagnostic availability represented by", "tokens": [51225, 517, 495, 29110, 5367, 13, 440, 3035, 8327, 279, 2251, 358, 592, 905, 379, 300, 27897, 17945, 10379, 538, 51549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05690425017784382, "compression_ratio": 1.588, "no_speech_prob": 2.124889890778303e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 233798, "start": 2337.98, "end": 2344.3, "text": " D is dependent on three fundamental pillars. First, there is C, the representable vocabulary.", "tokens": [50365, 413, 307, 12334, 322, 1045, 8088, 26729, 13, 2386, 11, 456, 307, 383, 11, 264, 2906, 712, 19864, 13, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0667513814465753, "compression_ratio": 1.6209677419354838, "no_speech_prob": 1.9054571288867894e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 233798, "start": 2345.18, "end": 2350.7, "text": " Do you have the words, the concepts, the dimensions required to describe the failure? Are you trying", "tokens": [50725, 1144, 291, 362, 264, 2283, 11, 264, 10392, 11, 264, 12819, 4739, 281, 6786, 264, 7763, 30, 2014, 291, 1382, 51001], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0667513814465753, "compression_ratio": 1.6209677419354838, "no_speech_prob": 1.9054571288867894e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 233798, "start": 2350.7, "end": 2357.1, "text": " to diagnose an atmospheric pressure problem with a flower and water vocabulary? Second, there is A,", "tokens": [51001, 281, 36238, 364, 28854, 3321, 1154, 365, 257, 8617, 293, 1281, 19864, 30, 5736, 11, 456, 307, 316, 11, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0667513814465753, "compression_ratio": 1.6209677419354838, "no_speech_prob": 1.9054571288867894e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 233798, "start": 2357.1, "end": 2363.5, "text": " temporal availability. Has the vocabulary survived the passage of time? Did the documentation decay? Is the", "tokens": [51321, 30881, 17945, 13, 8646, 264, 19864, 14433, 264, 11497, 295, 565, 30, 2589, 264, 14333, 21039, 30, 1119, 264, 51641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0667513814465753, "compression_ratio": 1.6209677419354838, "no_speech_prob": 1.9054571288867894e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 236350, "start": 2363.5, "end": 2369.42, "text": " refresh cycle fast enough to catch the fading charge before it hits Vmin? And third, there is E, the fault", "tokens": [50365, 15134, 6586, 2370, 1547, 281, 3745, 264, 38644, 4602, 949, 309, 8664, 691, 2367, 30, 400, 2636, 11, 456, 307, 462, 11, 264, 7441, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07634274464733196, "compression_ratio": 1.588679245283019, "no_speech_prob": 2.5245365693760125e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 236350, "start": 2369.42, "end": 2374.62, "text": " space. What is the actual physical reality the system is colliding with? Are you facing a single-bit", "tokens": [50661, 1901, 13, 708, 307, 264, 3539, 4001, 4103, 264, 1185, 307, 1263, 2819, 365, 30, 2014, 291, 7170, 257, 2167, 12, 5260, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07634274464733196, "compression_ratio": 1.588679245283019, "no_speech_prob": 2.5245365693760125e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 236350, "start": 2374.62, "end": 2380.78, "text": " error you designed for, or a double-bit error that will trigger a confident misdiagnosis? Vocabulary, time,", "tokens": [50921, 6713, 291, 4761, 337, 11, 420, 257, 3834, 12, 5260, 6713, 300, 486, 7875, 257, 6679, 3346, 4504, 4535, 8211, 30, 8993, 19189, 11, 565, 11, 51229], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07634274464733196, "compression_ratio": 1.588679245283019, "no_speech_prob": 2.5245365693760125e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 236350, "start": 2380.78, "end": 2387.82, "text": " and environment. C, A, and E. But Fliction resists the urge to simply slap these three variables together", "tokens": [51229, 293, 2823, 13, 383, 11, 316, 11, 293, 462, 13, 583, 3235, 4105, 725, 1751, 264, 19029, 281, 2935, 21075, 613, 1045, 9102, 1214, 51581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07634274464733196, "compression_ratio": 1.588679245283019, "no_speech_prob": 2.5245365693760125e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 238782, "start": 2387.82, "end": 2393.6600000000003, "text": " into a neat, easily digestible multiplication formula. They explicitly state that assuming these", "tokens": [50365, 666, 257, 10654, 11, 3612, 13884, 964, 27290, 8513, 13, 814, 20803, 1785, 300, 11926, 613, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06516295450705069, "compression_ratio": 1.6387096774193548, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733457489595763e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 238782, "start": 2393.6600000000003, "end": 2398.38, "text": " factors just multiply together implies a mathematical structure that has not been proven. It's a fascinating", "tokens": [50657, 6771, 445, 12972, 1214, 18779, 257, 18894, 3877, 300, 575, 406, 668, 12785, 13, 467, 311, 257, 10343, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06516295450705069, "compression_ratio": 1.6387096774193548, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733457489595763e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 238782, "start": 2398.38, "end": 2405.7400000000002, "text": " cliffhanger. They are basically asking, does your vocabulary act as an absolute hard ceiling on your", "tokens": [50893, 22316, 71, 3176, 13, 814, 366, 1936, 3365, 11, 775, 428, 19864, 605, 382, 364, 8236, 1152, 13655, 322, 428, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06516295450705069, "compression_ratio": 1.6387096774193548, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733457489595763e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 238782, "start": 2405.7400000000002, "end": 2411.9, "text": " repairability? If you don't possess the concept of a z-axis, is your ability to diagnose a 3D problem", "tokens": [51261, 10535, 2310, 30, 759, 291, 500, 380, 17490, 264, 3410, 295, 257, 710, 12, 24633, 11, 307, 428, 3485, 281, 36238, 257, 805, 35, 1154, 51569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06516295450705069, "compression_ratio": 1.6387096774193548, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733457489595763e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 238782, "start": 2411.9, "end": 2417.42, "text": " mathematically locked at absolute zero, regardless of how much time you spend or how perfectly your", "tokens": [51569, 44003, 9376, 412, 8236, 4018, 11, 10060, 295, 577, 709, 565, 291, 3496, 420, 577, 6239, 428, 51845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06516295450705069, "compression_ratio": 1.6387096774193548, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733457489595763e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 241742, "start": 2417.42, "end": 2423.26, "text": " existing 2D map is maintained? Or do these variables interact in far more complex non-linear ways?", "tokens": [50365, 6741, 568, 35, 4471, 307, 17578, 30, 1610, 360, 613, 9102, 4648, 294, 1400, 544, 3997, 2107, 12, 28263, 2098, 30, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07409062293859628, "compression_ratio": 1.5723270440251573, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493920386798864e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 241742, "start": 2423.26, "end": 2428.62, "text": " Does a highly volatile environment force a system to artificially accelerate its refresh cycles,", "tokens": [50657, 4402, 257, 5405, 34377, 2823, 3464, 257, 1185, 281, 39905, 2270, 21341, 1080, 15134, 17796, 11, 50925], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07409062293859628, "compression_ratio": 1.5723270440251573, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493920386798864e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 241742, "start": 2428.62, "end": 2433.98, "text": " fundamentally altering its temporal availability? Fliction maps the territory but leaves the exact", "tokens": [50925, 17879, 11337, 278, 1080, 30881, 17945, 30, 3235, 4105, 11317, 264, 11360, 457, 5510, 264, 1900, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07409062293859628, "compression_ratio": 1.5723270440251573, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493920386798864e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 241742, "start": 2433.98, "end": 2438.94, "text": " topography of that dependency function as the great open challenge for future researchers. This has", "tokens": [51193, 1192, 5820, 295, 300, 33621, 2445, 382, 264, 869, 1269, 3430, 337, 2027, 10309, 13, 639, 575, 51441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07409062293859628, "compression_ratio": 1.5723270440251573, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493920386798864e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 241742, "start": 2438.94, "end": 2444.54, "text": " been an absolutely staggering reevaluation of how we build and fix our world. Let's trace the arc of what", "tokens": [51441, 668, 364, 3122, 42974, 43060, 46504, 295, 577, 321, 1322, 293, 3191, 527, 1002, 13, 961, 311, 13508, 264, 10346, 295, 437, 51721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07409062293859628, "compression_ratio": 1.5723270440251573, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493920386798864e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 244454, "start": 2444.54, "end": 2450.14, "text": " we've uncovered. We began with the bleak premise of the anti-alignment theorem, that the very act of", "tokens": [50365, 321, 600, 37729, 13, 492, 4283, 365, 264, 5408, 514, 22045, 295, 264, 6061, 12, 304, 41134, 20904, 11, 300, 264, 588, 605, 295, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05477577707041865, "compression_ratio": 1.6833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.7827995983942255e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 244454, "start": 2450.14, "end": 2456.3, "text": " optimizing a system for perfect execution necessitates the destruction of its repairability. But we", "tokens": [50645, 40425, 257, 1185, 337, 2176, 15058, 2688, 30035, 264, 13563, 295, 1080, 10535, 2310, 13, 583, 321, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05477577707041865, "compression_ratio": 1.6833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.7827995983942255e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 244454, "start": 2456.3, "end": 2462.7799999999997, "text": " discovered that this grim outlook relies on the synchrony assumption, a fallacy that falsely equates the", "tokens": [50953, 6941, 300, 341, 36010, 26650, 30910, 322, 264, 19331, 88, 15302, 11, 257, 2100, 2551, 300, 16720, 736, 1267, 1024, 264, 51277], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05477577707041865, "compression_ratio": 1.6833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.7827995983942255e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 244454, "start": 2462.7799999999997, "end": 2468.06, "text": " moment of a system's birth with the moment of its eventual failure. By shattering that assumption,", "tokens": [51277, 1623, 295, 257, 1185, 311, 3965, 365, 264, 1623, 295, 1080, 33160, 7763, 13, 3146, 402, 14849, 300, 15302, 11, 51541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05477577707041865, "compression_ratio": 1.6833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.7827995983942255e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 246806, "start": 2468.06, "end": 2473.74, "text": " we revealed the hidden mechanisms that govern true resilience. We saw how history-first systems,", "tokens": [50365, 321, 9599, 264, 7633, 15902, 300, 1980, 2074, 19980, 13, 492, 1866, 577, 2503, 12, 29581, 3652, 11, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06587878704071044, "compression_ratio": 1.711340206185567, "no_speech_prob": 3.699143422131179e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 246806, "start": 2473.74, "end": 2479.02, "text": " like the altitude recipe, are born perfectly optimized but inherently blind to the world outside", "tokens": [50649, 411, 264, 24003, 6782, 11, 366, 4232, 6239, 26941, 457, 27993, 6865, 281, 264, 1002, 2380, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06587878704071044, "compression_ratio": 1.711340206185567, "no_speech_prob": 3.699143422131179e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 246806, "start": 2479.02, "end": 2485.42, "text": " their niche. We watched the illusion of theory-first systems shatter as perfect architectural derivation", "tokens": [50913, 641, 19956, 13, 492, 6337, 264, 18854, 295, 5261, 12, 29581, 3652, 402, 1161, 382, 2176, 26621, 10151, 399, 51233], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06587878704071044, "compression_ratio": 1.711340206185567, "no_speech_prob": 3.699143422131179e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 246806, "start": 2485.42, "end": 2491.82, "text": " passively decays into incomprehensible magic constants. We explored the terrifying reality of", "tokens": [51233, 1320, 3413, 979, 3772, 666, 14036, 40128, 30633, 5585, 35870, 13, 492, 24016, 264, 18106, 4103, 295, 51553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06587878704071044, "compression_ratio": 1.711340206185567, "no_speech_prob": 3.699143422131179e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 246806, "start": 2491.82, "end": 2496.86, "text": " operational scope failure, where a system like the Hamming decoder maintains perfect internal logic while", "tokens": [51553, 16607, 11923, 7763, 11, 689, 257, 1185, 411, 264, 8234, 2810, 979, 19866, 33385, 2176, 6920, 9952, 1339, 51805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06587878704071044, "compression_ratio": 1.711340206185567, "no_speech_prob": 3.699143422131179e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 249686, "start": 2496.86, "end": 2501.98, "text": " confidently corrupting reality because it lacks the vocabulary to recognize an out-of-scope fault.", "tokens": [50365, 41956, 17366, 278, 4103, 570, 309, 31132, 264, 19864, 281, 5521, 364, 484, 12, 2670, 12, 4417, 1114, 7441, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08034807551990855, "compression_ratio": 1.6241830065359477, "no_speech_prob": 2.4562129673916244e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 249686, "start": 2501.98, "end": 2506.7000000000003, "text": " And finally, we found a blueprint for survival in the microscopic architecture of the DRAM cell,", "tokens": [50621, 400, 2721, 11, 321, 1352, 257, 35868, 337, 12559, 294, 264, 47897, 9482, 295, 264, 12118, 2865, 2815, 11, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08034807551990855, "compression_ratio": 1.6241830065359477, "no_speech_prob": 2.4562129673916244e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 249686, "start": 2506.7000000000003, "end": 2512.38, "text": " proving that the inevitable 