_speech_prob": 2.475094565065894e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 85104, "start": 873.68, "end": 879.28, "text": " exists in a vacuum it does not tell you how to select it especially when there is chaos and uncertainty", "tokens": [51497, 8198, 294, 257, 14224, 309, 775, 406, 980, 291, 577, 281, 3048, 309, 2318, 562, 456, 307, 14158, 293, 15697, 51777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.029003438495454333, "compression_ratio": 1.7430555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 2.475094565065894e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 87928, "start": 879.28, "end": 885.8399999999999, "text": " to handle the rogue wave we have to introduce the adversary the adversary and the captain this is", "tokens": [50365, 281, 4813, 264, 39100, 5772, 321, 362, 281, 5366, 264, 48222, 264, 48222, 293, 264, 14871, 341, 307, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05388888819464322, "compression_ratio": 1.8296296296296297, "no_speech_prob": 2.0842687385030922e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 87928, "start": 885.8399999999999, "end": 891.52, "text": " such a great framing in the text the text argues that a ship's captain who only knows that a safe", "tokens": [50693, 1270, 257, 869, 28971, 294, 264, 2487, 264, 2487, 38218, 300, 257, 5374, 311, 14871, 567, 787, 3255, 300, 257, 3273, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05388888819464322, "compression_ratio": 1.8296296296296297, "no_speech_prob": 2.0842687385030922e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 87928, "start": 891.52, "end": 897.12, "text": " route exists hasn't actually done her job not at all if i am on a ship and the captain gets on the", "tokens": [50977, 7955, 8198, 6132, 380, 767, 1096, 720, 1691, 406, 412, 439, 498, 741, 669, 322, 257, 5374, 293, 264, 14871, 2170, 322, 264, 51257], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05388888819464322, "compression_ratio": 1.8296296296296297, "no_speech_prob": 2.0842687385030922e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 87928, "start": 897.12, "end": 902.72, "text": " loudspeaker and says folks there's a route that works if the sea remains perfectly flat and the wind", "tokens": [51257, 6588, 7053, 4003, 293, 1619, 4024, 456, 311, 257, 7955, 300, 1985, 498, 264, 4158, 7023, 6239, 4962, 293, 264, 2468, 51537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05388888819464322, "compression_ratio": 1.8296296296296297, "no_speech_prob": 2.0842687385030922e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 87928, "start": 902.72, "end": 908.4, "text": " never ever changes i am immediately looking for a life raft yeah you'd want to get off that boat a", "tokens": [51537, 1128, 1562, 2962, 741, 669, 4258, 1237, 337, 257, 993, 43863, 1338, 291, 1116, 528, 281, 483, 766, 300, 6582, 257, 51821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05388888819464322, "compression_ratio": 1.8296296296296297, "no_speech_prob": 2.0842687385030922e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 90840, "start": 908.4, "end": 913.92, "text": " competent captain plots the route that survives the absolute worst weather the season could throw", "tokens": [50365, 29998, 14871, 28609, 264, 7955, 300, 46231, 264, 8236, 5855, 5503, 264, 3196, 727, 3507, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060325733338943636, "compression_ratio": 1.857677902621723, "no_speech_prob": 2.15515799650845e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 90840, "start": 913.92, "end": 918.64, "text": " at them this marks the crucial transition in the math from the question of mere existence to the", "tokens": [50641, 412, 552, 341, 10640, 264, 11462, 6034, 294, 264, 5221, 490, 264, 1168, 295, 8401, 9123, 281, 264, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060325733338943636, "compression_ratio": 1.857677902621723, "no_speech_prob": 2.15515799650845e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 90840, "start": 918.64, "end": 925.68, "text": " question of selection when a complex system has multiple viable paths when the mathematical map", "tokens": [50877, 1168, 295, 9450, 562, 257, 3997, 1185, 575, 3866, 22024, 14518, 562, 264, 18894, 4471, 51229], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060325733338943636, "compression_ratio": 1.857677902621723, "no_speech_prob": 2.15515799650845e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 90840, "start": 925.68, "end": 930.88, "text": " gives you several choices that all theoretically keep you on the seawall how do you pick the best one", "tokens": [51229, 2709, 291, 2940, 7994, 300, 439, 29400, 1066, 291, 322, 264, 369, 1607, 336, 577, 360, 291, 1888, 264, 1151, 472, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060325733338943636, "compression_ratio": 1.857677902621723, "no_speech_prob": 2.15515799650845e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 90840, "start": 930.88, "end": 937.68, "text": " to solve this fliction introduces aubin's concept of guaranteed valuation guaranteed valuation yeah you", "tokens": [51489, 281, 5039, 341, 932, 4105, 31472, 257, 836, 259, 311, 3410, 295, 18031, 38546, 18031, 38546, 1338, 291, 51829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060325733338943636, "compression_ratio": 1.857677902621723, "no_speech_prob": 2.15515799650845e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 93768, "start": 937.68, "end": 942.8, "text": " mathematically split the future into two parts the part the system controls which is the menu of", "tokens": [50365, 44003, 7472, 264, 2027, 666, 732, 3166, 264, 644, 264, 1185, 9003, 597, 307, 264, 6510, 295, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.035580530595243645, "compression_ratio": 1.801762114537445, "no_speech_prob": 2.6193242453481647e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 93768, "start": 942.8, "end": 948.88, "text": " allotments or feedbacks and the part it absolutely does not control which are the adversaries perturbations", "tokens": [50621, 439, 310, 1117, 420, 5824, 82, 293, 264, 644, 309, 3122, 775, 406, 1969, 597, 366, 264, 17641, 4889, 40468, 763, 50925], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.035580530595243645, "compression_ratio": 1.801762114537445, "no_speech_prob": 2.6193242453481647e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 93768, "start": 948.88, "end": 954.8, "text": " the gusts of wind the gusts of wind the rogue waves so you're basically setting up a game theory", "tokens": [50925, 264, 9679, 82, 295, 2468, 264, 9679, 82, 295, 2468, 264, 39100, 9417, 370, 291, 434, 1936, 3287, 493, 257, 1216, 5261, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.035580530595243645, "compression_ratio": 1.801762114537445, "no_speech_prob": 2.6193242453481647e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 93768, "start": 954.8, "end": 963.04, "text": " scenario against the universe itself yes formally it is a controlled dynamical game and the objective is to", "tokens": [51221, 9005, 1970, 264, 6445, 2564, 2086, 25983, 309, 307, 257, 10164, 5999, 804, 1216, 293, 264, 10024, 307, 281, 51633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.035580530595243645, "compression_ratio": 1.801762114537445, "no_speech_prob": 2.6193242453481647e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 96304, "start": 963.04, "end": 968.4, "text": " select the control feedback that guarantees the best possible outcome against the absolute worst", "tokens": [50365, 3048, 264, 1969, 5824, 300, 32567, 264, 1151, 1944, 9700, 1970, 264, 8236, 5855, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05244115868000069, "compression_ratio": 1.8333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283646724045257e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 96304, "start": 968.4, "end": 973.92, "text": " possible sequence of perturbations the adversary can throw at you the text has a concrete mathematical", "tokens": [50633, 1944, 8310, 295, 40468, 763, 264, 48222, 393, 3507, 412, 291, 264, 2487, 575, 257, 9859, 18894, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05244115868000069, "compression_ratio": 1.8333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283646724045257e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 96304, "start": 973.92, "end": 978.3199999999999, "text": " example of this that really clarified the difference between viable and robust for me the steering", "tokens": [50909, 1365, 295, 341, 300, 534, 47605, 264, 2649, 1296, 22024, 293, 13956, 337, 385, 264, 14823, 51129], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05244115868000069, "compression_ratio": 1.8333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283646724045257e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 96304, "start": 978.3199999999999, "end": 984.0, "text": " example yes imagine you have a simple system just a point on a number line and your entire goal is", "tokens": [51129, 1365, 2086, 3811, 291, 362, 257, 2199, 1185, 445, 257, 935, 322, 257, 1230, 1622, 293, 428, 2302, 3387, 307, 51413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05244115868000069, "compression_ratio": 1.8333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283646724045257e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 96304, "start": 984.0, "end": 989.8399999999999, "text": " to steer to zero you have two different control systems like two steering wheels okay lay them out the first", "tokens": [51413, 281, 30814, 281, 4018, 291, 362, 732, 819, 1969, 3652, 411, 732, 14823, 10046, 1392, 2360, 552, 484, 264, 700, 51705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05244115868000069, "compression_ratio": 1.8333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283646724045257e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 98984, "start": 989.84, "end": 996.24, "text": " one just pushes constantly towards zero if you are at a positive number it pushes negative with a force", "tokens": [50365, 472, 445, 21020, 6460, 3030, 4018, 498, 291, 366, 412, 257, 3353, 1230, 309, 21020, 3671, 365, 257, 3464, 50685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03944231455142681, "compression_ratio": 1.8464285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 3.196751023615274e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 98984, "start": 996.24, "end": 1002.08, "text": " of one if you're negative it pushes positive with a force of one just a constant push simple enough the", "tokens": [50685, 295, 472, 498, 291, 434, 3671, 309, 21020, 3353, 365, 257, 3464, 295, 472, 445, 257, 5754, 2944, 2199, 1547, 264, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03944231455142681, "compression_ratio": 1.8464285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 3.196751023615274e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 98984, "start": 1002.08, "end": 1008.24, "text": " second steering wheel uses what the text calls a sliding mode convention let's break down why these two", "tokens": [50977, 1150, 14823, 5589, 4960, 437, 264, 2487, 5498, 257, 21169, 4391, 10286, 718, 311, 1821, 760, 983, 613, 732, 51285], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03944231455142681, "compression_ratio": 1.8464285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 3.196751023615274e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 98984, "start": 1008.24, "end": 1014.64, "text": " steering wheels yield completely different futures because technically without an adversaire both of these", "tokens": [51285, 14823, 10046, 11257, 2584, 819, 26071, 570, 12120, 1553, 364, 17641, 9020, 1293, 295, 613, 51605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03944231455142681, "compression_ratio": 1.8464285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 3.196751023615274e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 98984, "start": 1014.64, "end": 1019.76, "text": " feedbacks are perfectly viable right if you just leave them alone they'll both eventually get your", "tokens": [51605, 5824, 82, 366, 6239, 22024, 558, 498, 291, 445, 1856, 552, 3312, 436, 603, 1293, 4728, 483, 428, 51861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03944231455142681, "compression_ratio": 1.8464285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 3.196751023615274e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 101976, "start": 1019.76, "end": 1025.28, "text": " point to zero but let's introduce our adversary let's say the adversary can introduce a small", "tokens": [50365, 935, 281, 4018, 457, 718, 311, 5366, 527, 48222, 718, 311, 584, 264, 48222, 393, 5366, 257, 1359, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.053399500093962014, "compression_ratio": 1.96875, "no_speech_prob": 2.201410278027116e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 101976, "start": 1025.28, "end": 1031.68, "text": " unpredictable perturbation they can push the system with a force of a little 0.5 in any direction", "tokens": [50641, 31160, 40468, 399, 436, 393, 2944, 264, 1185, 365, 257, 3464, 295, 257, 707, 1958, 13, 20, 294, 604, 3513, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.053399500093962014, "compression_ratio": 1.96875, "no_speech_prob