5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.1377816007060448e-12}, {"id": 2, "seek": 0, "start": 11.9, "end": 12.780000000000001, "text": " Right, like a container.", "tokens": [50960, 1779, 11, 411, 257, 10129, 13, 51004], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0931801023937407, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.1377816007060448e-12}, {"id": 3, "seek": 0, "start": 13.02, "end": 20.06, "text": " Exactly. We imagine ourselves standing at the threshold, holding a flashlight, you know, and just stepping forward into the dark.", "tokens": [51016, 7587, 13, 492, 3811, 4175, 4877, 412, 264, 14678, 11, 5061, 257, 30835, 11, 291, 458, 11, 293, 445, 16821, 2128, 666, 264, 2877, 13, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0931801023937407, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.1377816007060448e-12}, {"id": 4, "seek": 0, "start": 20.16, "end": 25.16, "text": " And the underlying assumption there is that the future is just, it's a place that already exists.", "tokens": [51373, 400, 264, 14217, 15302, 456, 307, 300, 264, 2027, 307, 445, 11, 309, 311, 257, 1081, 300, 1217, 8198, 13, 51623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0931801023937407, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.1377816007060448e-12}, {"id": 5, "seek": 0, "start": 25.32, "end": 27.34, "text": " Yeah, waiting for us to stumble into it.", "tokens": [51631, 865, 11, 3806, 337, 505, 281, 41302, 666, 309, 13, 51732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0931801023937407, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.1377816007060448e-12}, {"id": 6, "seek": 2734, "start": 27.34, "end": 30.82, "text": " Waiting to be illuminated or mapped out. We just have to navigate it.", "tokens": [50365, 37291, 281, 312, 48577, 420, 33318, 484, 13, 492, 445, 362, 281, 12350, 309, 13, 50539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10354548052322766, "compression_ratio": 1.6331168831168832, "no_speech_prob": 7.148916333042654e-13}, {"id": 7, "seek": 2734, "start": 30.9, "end": 38.4, "text": " But we're doing a deep dive today into a new working draft from July 2026, and it completely shatters that container metaphor.", "tokens": [50543, 583, 321, 434, 884, 257, 2452, 9192, 965, 666, 257, 777, 1364, 11206, 490, 7370, 945, 10880, 11, 293, 309, 2584, 402, 37690, 300, 10129, 19157, 13, 50918], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10354548052322766, "compression_ratio": 1.6331168831168832, "no_speech_prob": 7.148916333042654e-13}, {"id": 8, "seek": 2734, "start": 38.62, "end": 42.96, "text": " It really does. It's called generative continuation geometry by an author named Flixing.", "tokens": [50929, 467, 534, 775, 13, 467, 311, 1219, 1337, 1166, 29357, 18426, 538, 364, 3793, 4926, 3235, 970, 278, 13, 51146], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10354548052322766, "compression_ratio": 1.6331168831168832, "no_speech_prob": 7.148916333042654e-13}, {"id": 9, "seek": 2734, "start": 43.16, "end": 45.82, "text": " And it argues that the future is not a place we just walk into.", "tokens": [51156, 400, 309, 38218, 300, 264, 2027, 307, 406, 257, 1081, 321, 445, 1792, 666, 13, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10354548052322766, "compression_ratio": 1.6331168831168832, "no_speech_prob": 7.148916333042654e-13}, {"id": 10, "seek": 2734, "start": 45.9, "end": 50.379999999999995, "text": " It's a structure that is generated, compressed, and measured step by step.", "tokens": [51293, 467, 311, 257, 3877, 300, 307, 10833, 11, 30353, 11, 293, 12690, 1823, 538, 1823, 13, 51517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10354548052322766, "compression_ratio": 1.6331168831168832, "no_speech_prob": 7.148916333042654e-13}, {"id": 11, "seek": 2734, "start": 50.760000000000005, "end": 53.879999999999995, "text": " So the mission for you listening today, our third person in this conversation,", "tokens": [51536, 407, 264, 4447, 337, 291, 4764, 965, 11, 527, 2636, 954, 294, 341, 3761, 11, 51692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10354548052322766, "compression_ratio": 1.6331168831168832, "no_speech_prob": 7.148916333042654e-13}, {"id": 12, "seek": 5388, "start": 53.88, "end": 58.14, "text": " is to understand how we stop measuring the future and start, well, growing it.", "tokens": [50365, 307, 281, 1223, 577, 321, 1590, 13389, 264, 2027, 293, 722, 11, 731, 11, 4194, 309, 13, 50578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09983033719270126, "compression_ratio": 1.592920353982301, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051516027124844e-12}, {"id": 13, "seek": 5388, "start": 58.28, "end": 63.2, "text": " Growing it, yeah. That transition from measuring to growing is, I mean, it's the hinge of the entire document.", "tokens": [50585, 32569, 309, 11, 1338, 13, 663, 6034, 490, 13389, 281, 4194, 307, 11, 286, 914, 11, 309, 311, 264, 28822, 295, 264, 2302, 4166, 13, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09983033719270126, "compression_ratio": 1.592920353982301, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051516027124844e-12}, {"id": 14, "seek": 5388, "start": 63.56, "end": 69.98, "text": " And I want to promise you, the listener, right up front, we are going to be looking at some heavy concepts today.", "tokens": [50849, 400, 286, 528, 281, 6228, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 11, 558, 493, 1868, 11, 321, 366, 516, 281, 312, 1237, 412, 512, 4676, 10392, 965, 13, 51170], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09983033719270126, "compression_ratio": 1.592920353982301, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051516027124844e-12}, {"id": 15, "seek": 5388, "start": 70.32000000000001, "end": 73.66, "text": " Things like Lipschitz constants and Hausdorff distances.", "tokens": [51187, 9514, 411, 441, 2600, 339, 6862, 35870, 293, 22725, 67, 284, 602, 22182, 13, 51354], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09983033719270126, "compression_ratio": 1.592920353982301, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051516027124844e-12}, {"id": 16, "seek": 7366, "start": 73.66, "end": 77.84, "text": " But we are absolutely stripping away the jargon.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 321, 366, 3122, 3575, 3759, 1314, 264, 15181, 10660, 13, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1496622297498915, "compression_ratio": 1.5537459283387622, "no_speech_prob": 1.30942815184526e-12}, {"id": 17, "seek": 7366, "start": 77.97999999999999, "end": 81.1, "text": " We're going for pure, mind-expanding, aha moments.", "tokens": [50581, 492, 434, 516, 337, 6075, 11, 1575, 12, 15952, 42389, 11, 47340, 6065, 13, 50737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1496622297498915, "compression_ratio": 1.5537459283387622, "no_speech_prob": 1.30942815184526e-12}, {"id": 18, "seek": 7366, "start": 81.2, "end": 81.88, "text": " No, absolutely.", "tokens": [50742, 883, 11, 3122, 13, 50776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1496622297498915, "compression_ratio": 1.5537459283387622, "no_speech_prob": 1.30942815184526e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 7366, "start": 82.14, "end": 85.03999999999999, "text": " I mean, if you look at earlier geometric frameworks,", "tokens": [50789, 286, 914, 11, 498, 291, 574, 412, 3071, 33246, 29834, 11, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1496622297498915, "compression_ratio": 1.5537459283387622, "no_speech_prob": 1.30942815184526e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 7366, "start": 85.56, "end": 90.66, "text": " mathematicians would look at a system, say, a pendulum or an economy or even a chess game,", "tokens": [50960, 32811, 2567, 576, 574, 412, 257, 1185, 11, 584, 11, 257, 44103, 420, 364, 5010, 420, 754, 257, 24122, 1216, 11, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1496622297498915, "compression_ratio": 1.5537459283387622, "no_speech_prob": 1.30942815184526e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 7366, "start": 90.74, "end": 93.3, "text": " and ask, like, how much room does this state have?", "tokens": [51219, 293, 1029, 11, 411, 11, 577, 709, 1808, 775, 341, 1785, 362, 30, 51347], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1496622297498915, "compression_ratio": 1.5537459283387622, "no_speech_prob": 1.30942815184526e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 7366, "start": 93.4, "end": 93.75999999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51352, 1779, 13, 51370], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1496622297498915, "compression_ratio": 1.5537459283387622, "no_speech_prob": 1.30942815184526e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 7366, "start": 94.17999999999999, "end": 96.17999999999999, "text": " How far apart are two possible futures?", "tokens": [51391, 1012, 1400, 4936, 366, 732, 1944, 26071, 30, 51491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1496622297498915, "compression_ratio": 1.5537459283387622, "no_speech_prob": 1.30942815184526e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 7366, "start": 96.78, "end": 98.96, "text": " If I make a slight change to the chessboard right now,", "tokens": [51521, 759, 286, 652, 257, 4036, 1319, 281, 264, 24122, 3787, 558, 586, 11, 51630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1496622297498915, "compression_ratio": 1.5537459283387622, "no_speech_prob": 1.30942815184526e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 7366, "start": 99.08, "end": 102.8, "text": " how wildly do the outcomes diverge, say, 10 moves down the line?", "tokens": [51636, 577, 34731, 360, 264, 10070, 18558, 432, 11, 584, 11, 1266, 6067, 760, 264, 1622, 30, 51822], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1496622297498915, "compression_ratio": 1.5537459283387622, "no_speech_prob": 1.30942815184526e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 10280, "start": 102.8, "end": 104.0, "text": " It's very measurement-focused.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 588, 13160, 12, 44062, 13, 50425], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14307995998498166, "compression_ratio": 1.6411042944785277, "no_speech_prob": 1.478334381993518e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 10280, "start": 104.25999999999999, "end": 107.42, "text": " Right. It takes the space of all possible futures as a given.", "tokens": [50438, 1779, 13, 467, 2516, 264, 1901, 295, 439, 1944, 26071, 382, 257, 2212, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14307995998498166, "compression_ratio": 1.6411042944785277, "no_speech_prob": 1.478334381993518e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 10280, "start": 107.78, "end": 109.06, "text": " It treats time as a geography.", "tokens": [50614, 467, 19566, 565, 382, 257, 26695, 13, 50678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14307995998498166, "compression_ratio": 1.6411042944785277, "no_speech_prob": 1.478334381993518e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 10280, "start": 109.24, "end": 112.75999999999999, "text": " Like the flashlight in the dark room, we're just measuring the dimensions of the room.", "tokens": [50687, 1743, 264, 30835, 294, 264, 2877, 1808, 11, 321, 434, 445, 13389, 264, 12819, 295, 264, 1808, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14307995998498166, "compression_ratio": 1.6411042944785277, "no_speech_prob": 1.478334381993518e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 10280, "start": 113.0, "end": 118.64, "text": " But Fliction proposes that the room doesn't even exist until the specific rules of the system build it.", "tokens": [50875, 583, 3235, 4105, 2365, 4201, 300, 264, 1808, 1177, 380, 754, 2514, 1826, 264, 2685, 4474, 295, 264, 1185, 1322, 309, 13, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14307995998498166, "compression_ratio": 1.6411042944785277, "no_speech_prob": 1.478334381993518e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 10280, "start": 118.74, "end": 123.94, "text": " Exactly. And to illustrate this, the draft introduces this concept called continuation attractors.", "tokens": [51162, 7587, 13, 400, 281, 23221, 341, 11, 264, 11206, 31472, 341, 3410, 1219, 29357, 5049, 830, 13, 51422], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14307995998498166, "compression_ratio": 1.6411042944785277, "no_speech_prob": 1.478334381993518e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 10280, "start": 124.14, "end": 128.44, "text": " And it contrasts it with a really great biological analogy, the growth of a fern.", "tokens": [51432, 400, 309, 8712, 82, 309, 365, 257, 534, 869, 13910, 21663, 11, 264, 4599, 295, 257, 283, 1248, 13, 51647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14307995998498166, "compression_ratio": 1.6411042944785277, "no_speech_prob": 1.478334381993518e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 10280, "start": 128.82, "end": 130.66, "text": " The fern analogy was so helpful for me.", "tokens": [51666, 440, 283, 1248, 21663, 390, 370, 4961, 337, 385, 13, 51758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14307995998498166, "compression_ratio": 1.6411042944785277, "no_speech_prob": 1.478334381993518e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 13066, "start": 130.66, "end": 138.9, "text": " Because if you want to digitally store a highly detailed image of a fern, you run into a massive data problem, right?", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 498, 291, 528, 281, 36938, 3531, 257, 5405, 9942, 3256, 295, 257, 283, 1248, 11, 291, 1190, 666, 257, 5994, 1412, 1154, 11, 558, 30, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12985665639241536, "compression_ratio": 1.525, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012615716542e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 13066, "start": 139.12, "end": 146.96, "text": " Massive. Because storing the exact spatial coordinates of every single stem, every leaflet, every sub-leaflet,", "tokens": [50788, 10482, 488, 13, 1436, 26085, 264, 1900, 23598, 21056, 295, 633, 2167, 12312, 11, 633, 10871, 2631, 11, 633, 1422, 12, 306, 2792, 2631, 11, 51180], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12985665639241536, "compression_ratio": 1.525, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012615716542e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 13066, "start": 147.26, "end": 149.16, "text": " it requires an enormous amount of memory.", "tokens": [51195, 309, 7029, 364, 11322, 2372, 295, 4675, 13, 51290], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12985665639241536, "compression_ratio": 1.525, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012615716542e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 13066, "start": 149.4, "end": 151.04, "text": " The complexity is just staggering.", "tokens": [51302, 440, 14024, 307, 445, 42974, 13, 51384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12985665639241536, "compression_ratio": 1.525, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012615716542e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 15104, "start": 151.04, "end": 159.84, "text": " But if you look closely at a fern, one little pinna, like a leaflet off the main stem, is basically just a smaller version of the whole fern.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 291, 574, 8185, 412, 257, 283, 1248, 11, 472, 707, 5447, 629, 11, 411, 257, 10871, 2631, 766, 264, 2135, 12312, 11, 307, 1936, 445, 257, 4356, 3037, 295, 264, 1379, 283, 1248, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09101040022713798, "compression_ratio": 1.657439446366782, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428750941778868e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 15104, "start": 160.04, "end": 163.54, "text": " Right. And a pineal on that leaflet is a smaller fern again. It's fractal.", "tokens": [50815, 1779, 13, 400, 257, 15113, 304, 322, 300, 10871, 2631, 307, 257, 4356, 283, 1248, 797, 13, 467, 311, 17948, 304, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09101040022713798, "compression_ratio": 1.657439446366782, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428750941778868e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 15104, "start": 163.68, "end": 165.6, "text": " Yes. It has self-similarity.", "tokens": [50997, 1079, 13, 467, 575, 2698, 12, 30937, 2202, 507, 13, 51093], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09101040022713798, "compression_ratio": 1.657439446366782, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428750941778868e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 15104, "start": 165.85999999999999, "end": 165.98, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [51106, 12753, 13, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09101040022713798, "compression_ratio": 1.657439446366782, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428750941778868e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 15104, "start": 166.0, "end": 168.7, "text": " Which means you don't actually need to store the shape.", "tokens": [51113, 3013, 1355, 291, 500, 380, 767, 643, 281, 3531, 264, 3909, 13, 51248], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09101040022713798, "compression_ratio": 1.657439446366782, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428750941778868e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 15104, "start": 168.84, "end": 171.57999999999998, "text": " No. You only need to store a very small set of growth rules.", "tokens": [51255, 883, 13, 509, 787, 643, 281, 3531, 257, 588, 1359, 992, 295, 4599, 4474, 13, 51392], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09101040022713798, "compression_ratio": 1.657439446366782, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428750941778868e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 15104, "start": 171.88, "end": 176.42, "text": " You apply those rules to a starting point, take the output, and feed it back into the rules.", "tokens": [51407, 509, 3079, 729, 4474, 281, 257, 2891, 935, 11, 747, 264, 5598, 11, 293, 3154, 309, 646, 666, 264, 4474, 13, 51634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09101040022713798, "compression_ratio": 1.657439446366782, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428750941778868e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 15104, "start": 176.5, "end": 177.1, "text": " Over and over.", "tokens": [51638, 4886, 293, 670, 13, 51668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09101040022713798, "compression_ratio": 1.657439446366782, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428750941778868e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 17710, "start": 177.1, "end": 181.12, "text": " Exactly. The shape isn't sitting in a digital container waiting to be loaded.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 440, 3909, 1943, 380, 3798, 294, 257, 4562, 10129, 3806, 281, 312, 13210, 13, 50566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12638557979038784, "compression_ratio": 1.5804195804195804, "no_speech_prob": 1.1465736129631643e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 17710, "start": 181.54, "end": 185.54, "text": " It is dynamically generated by the recursive application of an operator.", "tokens": [50587, 467, 307, 43492, 10833, 538, 264, 20560, 488, 3861, 295, 364, 12973, 13, 50787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12638557979038784, "compression_ratio": 1.5804195804195804, "no_speech_prob": 1.1465736129631643e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 17710, "start": 185.85999999999999, "end": 191.95999999999998, "text": " And the distinction the author draws here between true generation and mere accumulation is, it's vital,", "tokens": [50803, 400, 264, 16844, 264, 3793, 20045, 510, 1296, 2074, 5125, 293, 8401, 35647, 307, 11, 309, 311, 11707, 11, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12638557979038784, "compression_ratio": 1.5804195804195804, "no_speech_prob": 1.1465736129631643e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 17710, "start": 192.45999999999998, "end": 196.0, "text": " they reference Stuart Kaufman's concept of the adjacent possible.", "tokens": [51133, 436, 6408, 36236, 44590, 1601, 311, 3410, 295, 264, 24441, 1944, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12638557979038784, "compression_ratio": 1.5804195804195804, "no_speech_prob": 1.1465736129631643e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 17710, "start": 196.16, "end": 197.2, "text": " Yeah, that's a key contrast.", "tokens": [51318, 865, 11, 300, 311, 257, 2141, 8712, 13, 51370], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12638557979038784, "compression_ratio": 1.5804195804195804, "no_speech_prob": 1.1465736129631643e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 17710, "start": 197.38, "end": 203.07999999999998, "text": " Because in Kaufman's model, you look at your current state, find everything you can reach in one step,", "tokens": [51379, 1436, 294, 44590, 1601, 311, 2316, 11, 291, 574, 412, 428, 2190, 1785, 11, 915, 1203, 291, 393, 2524, 294, 472, 1823, 11, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12638557979038784, "compression_ratio": 1.5804195804195804, "no_speech_prob": 1.1465736129631643e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 20308, "start": 203.08, "end": 207.52, "text": " and you just add it to your territory. Then you look at that new border, find everything you can read", "tokens": [50365, 293, 291, 445, 909, 309, 281, 428, 11360, 13, 1396, 291, 574, 412, 300, 777, 7838, 11, 915, 1203, 291, 393, 1401, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06731324929457444, "compression_ratio": 1.160919540229885, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080571982838744e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 20752, "start": 207.52, "end": 208.86, "text": " from there and add that.", "tokens": [50365, 490, 456, 293, 909, 300, 13, 50432], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14918336001309482, "compression_ratio": 1.681159420289855, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980715015184721e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 20752, "start": 208.86, "end": 215.3, "text": " It resembles a puddle spreading outward on pavement. The space of possibilities just keeps unioning with", "tokens": [50432, 467, 34433, 257, 14166, 2285, 15232, 26914, 322, 38305, 13, 440, 1901, 295, 12178, 445, 5965, 11671, 278, 365, 50754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14918336001309482, "compression_ratio": 1.681159420289855, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980715015184721e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 20752, "start": 215.3, "end": 218.42000000000002, "text": " its adjacent possibilities. It grows monotonically.", "tokens": [50754, 1080, 24441, 12178, 13, 467, 13156, 1108, 27794, 984, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14918336001309482, "compression_ratio": 1.681159420289855, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980715015184721e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 20752, "start": 218.56, "end": 218.78, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50917, 1779, 13, 50928], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14918336001309482, "compression_ratio": 1.681159420289855, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980715015184721e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 20752, "start": 219.20000000000002, "end": 224.82000000000002, "text": " And assuming the universe isn't strictly finite, that puddle just spreads without bound. It never settles.", "tokens": [50949, 400, 11926, 264, 6445, 1943, 380, 20792, 19362, 11, 300, 14166, 2285, 445, 25728, 1553, 5472, 13, 467, 1128, 5584, 904, 13, 51230], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14918336001309482, "compression_ratio": 1.681159420289855, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980715015184721e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 20752, "start": 224.98000000000002, "end": 231.10000000000002, "text": " It never forms a coherent, self-similar structure. Fliction is mathematically strict about the spreading", "tokens": [51238, 467, 1128, 6422, 257, 36239, 11, 2698, 12, 30937, 2202, 3877, 13, 3235, 4105, 307, 44003, 10910, 466, 264, 15232, 51544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14918336001309482, "compression_ratio": 1.681159420289855, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980715015184721e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 20752, "start": 231.10000000000002, "end": 234.88, "text": " outward. Endlessly is accumulation. It's just piling things up.", "tokens": [51544, 26914, 13, 6967, 12048, 307, 35647, 13, 467, 311, 445, 280, 4883, 721, 493, 13, 51733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14918336001309482, "compression_ratio": 1.681159420289855, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980715015184721e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 23488, "start": 234.88, "end": 236.9, "text": " True generation requires something else.", "tokens": [50365, 13587, 5125, 7029, 746, 1646, 13, 50466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09077960566470497, "compression_ratio": 1.6777408637873754, "no_speech_prob": 2.1009173133829107e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 23488, "start": 237.01999999999998, "end": 239.64, "text": " Yeah. It requires a mechanism that forces convergence.", "tokens": [50472, 865, 13, 467, 7029, 257, 7513, 300, 5874, 32181, 13, 50603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09077960566470497, "compression_ratio": 1.6777408637873754, "no_speech_prob": 2.1009173133829107e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 23488, "start": 239.96, "end": 243.18, "text": " And I'll admit, I found myself struggling with that convergence part at first.", "tokens": [50619, 400, 286, 603, 9796, 11, 286, 1352, 2059, 9314, 365, 300, 32181, 644, 412, 700, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09077960566470497, "compression_ratio": 1.6777408637873754, "no_speech_prob": 2.1009173133829107e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 23488, "start": 243.44, "end": 249.07999999999998, "text": " Because if we are endlessly applying rules, you know, feeding the output back into the machine over", "tokens": [50793, 1436, 498, 321, 366, 44920, 9275, 4474, 11, 291, 458, 11, 12919, 264, 5598, 646, 666, 264, 3479, 670, 51075], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09077960566470497, "compression_ratio": 1.6777408637873754, "no_speech_prob": 2.1009173133829107e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 23488, "start": 249.07999999999998, "end": 253.14, "text": " and over, my intuition is that the math should just explode into infinity.", "tokens": [51075, 293, 670, 11, 452, 24002, 307, 300, 264, 5221, 820, 445, 21411, 666, 13202, 13, 51278], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09077960566470497, "compression_ratio": 1.6777408637873754, "no_speech_prob": 2.1009173133829107e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 23488, "start": 253.51999999999998, "end": 256.24, "text": " Sure. Because piling things up makes sense. It just gets bigger.", "tokens": [51297, 4894, 13, 1436, 280, 4883, 721, 493, 1669, 2020, 13, 467, 445, 2170, 3801, 13, 51433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09077960566470497, "compression_ratio": 1.6777408637873754, "no_speech_prob": 2.1009173133829107e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 23488, "start": 256.68, "end": 262.26, "text": " Right. But generating a highly specific, intricate shape requires the math to settle down.", "tokens": [51455, 1779, 13, 583, 17746, 257, 5405, 2685, 11, 38015, 3909, 7029, 264, 5221, 281, 11852, 760, 13, 51734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09077960566470497, "compression_ratio": 1.6777408637873754, "no_speech_prob": 2.1009173133829107e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 26226, "start": 262.26, "end": 265.08, "text": " It requires, like, a gravitational pull.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 7029, 11, 411, 11, 257, 28538, 2235, 13, 50506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13560249984905284, "compression_ratio": 1.6452991452991452, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144881434699721e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 26226, "start": 265.28, "end": 270.44, "text": " And that gravitational pull is provided by a specific type of mathematical rule called a contraction.", "tokens": [50516, 400, 300, 28538, 2235, 307, 5649, 538, 257, 2685, 2010, 295, 18894, 4978, 1219, 257, 37372, 13, 50774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13560249984905284, "compression_ratio": 1.6452991452991452, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144881434699721e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 26226, "start": 271.06, "end": 273.74, "text": " And this works through something called the Hutchinson operator.", "tokens": [50805, 400, 341, 1985, 807, 746, 1219, 264, 48499, 14321, 12973, 13, 50939], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13560249984905284, "compression_ratio": 1.6452991452991452, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144881434699721e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 26226, "start": 273.94, "end": 275.68, "text": " Okay. Break down a contraction for us.", "tokens": [50949, 1033, 13, 16925, 760, 257, 37372, 337, 505, 13, 51036], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13560249984905284, "compression_ratio": 1.6452991452991452, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144881434699721e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 26226, "start": 276.03999999999996, "end": 280.62, "text": " So, a contraction is a rule that strictly reduces the distance between points.", "tokens": [51054, 407, 11, 257, 37372, 307, 257, 4978, 300, 20792, 18081, 264, 4560, 1296, 2793, 13, 51283], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13560249984905284, "compression_ratio": 1.6452991452991452, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144881434699721e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 26226, "start": 281.08, "end": 283.62, "text": " Imagine laying a map of your city on a table.", "tokens": [51306, 11739, 14903, 257, 4471, 295, 428, 2307, 322, 257, 3199, 13, 51433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13560249984905284, "compression_ratio": 1.6452991452991452, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144881434699721e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 26226, "start": 283.7, "end": 284.44, "text": " Okay. Got it.", "tokens": [51437, 1033, 13, 5803, 309, 13, 51474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13560249984905284, "compression_ratio": 1.6452991452991452, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144881434699721e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 28444, "start": 284.44, "end": 292.4, "text": " Now, imagine a specialized scanner that duplicates that map, shrinks it down to half its size, and drops it back onto the original map.", "tokens": [50365, 823, 11, 3811, 257, 19813, 30211, 300, 17154, 1024, 300, 4471, 11, 9884, 16431, 309, 760, 281, 1922, 1080, 2744, 11, 293, 11438, 309, 646, 3911, 264, 3380, 4471, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13050045533613724, "compression_ratio": 1.7235772357723578, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428754194385386e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 28444, "start": 292.74, "end": 298.44, "text": " So, if I pick any two coffee shops on the original map, the distance between them might be, say, two miles.", "tokens": [50780, 407, 11, 498, 286, 1888, 604, 732, 4982, 14457, 322, 264, 3380, 4471, 11, 264, 4560, 1296, 552, 1062, 312, 11, 584, 11, 732, 6193, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13050045533613724, "compression_ratio": 1.7235772357723578, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428754194385386e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 28444, "start": 298.7, "end": 300.16, "text": " But on the shrunken copy...", "tokens": [51078, 583, 322, 264, 9884, 39071, 5055, 485, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13050045533613724, "compression_ratio": 1.7235772357723578, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428754194385386e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 28444, "start": 300.16, "end": 303.5, "text": " The distance between those exact same two coffee shops is now one mile.", "tokens": [51151, 440, 4560, 1296, 729, 1900, 912, 732, 4982, 14457, 307, 586, 472, 12620, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13050045533613724, "compression_ratio": 1.7235772357723578, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428754194385386e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 28444, "start": 303.72, "end": 304.18, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51329, 3153, 13, 51352], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13050045533613724, "compression_ratio": 1.7235772357723578, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428754194385386e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 28444, "start": 304.62, "end": 304.86, "text": " Right?", "tokens": [51374, 1779, 30, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13050045533613724, "compression_ratio": 1.7235772357723578, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428754194385386e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 28444, "start": 305.18, "end": 308.1, "text": " The distance has been multiplied by a factor strictly less than one.", "tokens": [51402, 440, 4560, 575, 668, 17207, 538, 257, 5952, 20792, 1570, 813, 472, 13, 51548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13050045533613724, "compression_ratio": 1.7235772357723578, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428754194385386e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 30810, "start": 308.1, "end": 309.96000000000004, "text": " That is the definition of a contraction.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 264, 7123, 295, 257, 37372, 13, 50458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15486753211831147, "compression_ratio": 1.651851851851852, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160372093646734e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 30810, "start": 310.42, "end": 312.3, "text": " The rules aren't just creating new points.", "tokens": [50481, 440, 4474, 3212, 380, 445, 4084, 777, 2793, 13, 50575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15486753211831147, "compression_ratio": 1.651851851851852, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160372093646734e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 30810, "start": 312.70000000000005, "end": 314.56, "text": " They are actively compressing the space.", "tokens": [50595, 814, 366, 13022, 14778, 278, 264, 1901, 13, 50688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15486753211831147, "compression_ratio": 1.651851851851852, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160372093646734e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 30810, "start": 315.1, "end": 321.68, "text": " And to measure that compression across entirely different weird shapes, the author uses the Hausdorff distance.", "tokens": [50715, 400, 281, 3481, 300, 19355, 2108, 7696, 819, 3657, 10854, 11, 264, 3793, 4960, 264, 22725, 67, 284, 602, 4560, 13, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15486753211831147, "compression_ratio": 1.651851851851852, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160372093646734e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 30810, "start": 322.74, "end": 326.06, "text": " I know I promise no jargon, but this one is cool.", "tokens": [51097, 286, 458, 286, 6228, 572, 15181, 10660, 11, 457, 341, 472, 307, 1627, 13, 51263], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15486753211831147, "compression_ratio": 1.651851851851852, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160372093646734e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 30810, "start": 326.54, "end": 335.36, "text": " If we want to move past the intuition and into the actual rigorous geometry, we have to understand how Hausdorff measures the gap between two complex features.", "tokens": [51287, 759, 321, 528, 281, 1286, 1791, 264, 24002, 293, 666, 264, 3539, 29882, 18426, 11, 321, 362, 281, 1223, 577, 22725, 67, 284, 602, 8000, 264, 7417, 1296, 732, 3997, 4122, 13, 51728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15486753211831147, "compression_ratio": 1.651851851851852, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160372093646734e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 33536, "start": 335.36, "end": 342.1, "text": " Yeah, the Hausdorff distance is brilliant because it handles asymmetrical, messy shapes perfectly.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 11, 264, 22725, 67, 284, 602, 4560, 307, 10248, 570, 309, 18722, 37277, 32283, 11, 16191, 10854, 6239, 13, 50702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12779511500449076, "compression_ratio": 1.7692307692307692, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594543463695373e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 33536, "start": 342.88, "end": 346.52000000000004, "text": " If you have shape A and shape B, you don't just measure the distance between their centers.", "tokens": [50741, 759, 291, 362, 3909, 316, 293, 3909, 363, 11, 291, 500, 380, 445, 3481, 264, 4560, 1296, 641, 10898, 13, 50923], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12779511500449076, "compression_ratio": 1.7692307692307692, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594543463695373e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 33536, "start": 346.86, "end": 348.16, "text": " Because that wouldn't tell you much.", "tokens": [50940, 1436, 300, 2759, 380, 980, 291, 709, 13, 51005], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12779511500449076, "compression_ratio": 1.7692307692307692, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594543463695373e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 33536, "start": 348.18, "end": 348.38, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51006, 1779, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12779511500449076, "compression_ratio": 1.7692307692307692, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594543463695373e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 33536, "start": 348.68, "end": 350.24, "text": " You find the worst case scenario.", "tokens": [51031, 509, 915, 264, 5855, 1389, 9005, 13, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12779511500449076, "compression_ratio": 1.7692307692307692, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594543463695373e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 33536, "start": 350.90000000000003, "end": 355.66, "text": " You imagine a point in shape A that is as far away as possible from any part of shape B.", "tokens": [51142, 509, 3811, 257, 935, 294, 3909, 316, 300, 307, 382, 1400, 1314, 382, 1944, 490, 604, 644, 295, 3909, 363, 13, 51380], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12779511500449076, "compression_ratio": 1.7692307692307692, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594543463695373e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 33536, "start": 356.08000000000004, "end": 357.5, "text": " And you calculate that distance.", "tokens": [51401, 400, 291, 8873, 300, 4560, 13, 51472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12779511500449076, "compression_ratio": 1.7692307692307692, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594543463695373e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 33536, "start": 357.6, "end": 357.84000000000003, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51477, 1033, 13, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12779511500449076, "compression_ratio": 1.7692307692307692, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594543463695373e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 33536, "start": 358.0, "end": 359.26, "text": " Then you do the exact reverse.", "tokens": [51497, 1396, 291, 360, 264, 1900, 9943, 13, 51560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12779511500449076, "compression_ratio": 1.7692307692307692, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594543463695373e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 33536, "start": 359.38, "end": 359.58000000000004, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51566, 865, 13, 51576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12779511500449076, "compression_ratio": 1.7692307692307692, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594543463695373e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 33536, "start": 359.72, "end": 362.82, "text": " You find the point in shape B that is farthest from any part of shape A.", "tokens": [51583, 509, 915, 264, 935, 294, 3909, 363, 300, 307, 1400, 36356, 490, 604, 644, 295, 3909, 316, 13, 51738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12779511500449076, "compression_ratio": 1.7692307692307692, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594543463695373e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 36282, "start": 362.82, "end": 366.98, "text": " And the larger of those two worst case distances becomes your official Hausdorff distance.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 4833, 295, 729, 732, 5855, 1389, 22182, 3643, 428, 4783, 22725, 67, 284, 602, 4560, 13, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15005675149620126, "compression_ratio": 1.6538461538461537, "no_speech_prob": 1.169367662597065e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 36282, "start": 367.24, "end": 367.68, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50586, 7587, 13, 50608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15005675149620126, "compression_ratio": 1.6538461538461537, "no_speech_prob": 1.169367662597065e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 36282, "start": 368.12, "end": 374.06, "text": " It guarantees that no matter where you are in shape A, you are at most that distance away from shape B, and vice versa.", "tokens": [50630, 467, 32567, 300, 572, 1871, 689, 291, 366, 294, 3909, 316, 11, 291, 366, 412, 881, 300, 4560, 1314, 490, 3909, 363, 11, 293, 11964, 25650, 13, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15005675149620126, "compression_ratio": 1.6538461538461537, "no_speech_prob": 1.169367662597065e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 36282, "start": 374.38, "end": 377.6, "text": " It is a definitive metric for how well two futures overlap.", "tokens": [50943, 467, 307, 257, 28152, 20678, 337, 577, 731, 732, 26071, 19959, 13, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15005675149620126, "compression_ratio": 1.6538461538461537, "no_speech_prob": 1.169367662597065e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 36282, "start": 377.6, "end": 378.08, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51104, 1033, 13, 51128], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15005675149620126, "compression_ratio": 1.6538461538461537, "no_speech_prob": 1.169367662597065e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 36282, "start": 378.3, "end": 387.08, "text": " So, armed with the Hausdorff distance to measure the space and contractions to shrink the space, Flixian invokes the Banach fixed point theorem.", "tokens": [51139, 407, 11, 16297, 365, 264, 22725, 67, 284, 602, 4560, 281, 3481, 264, 1901, 293, 4364, 626, 281, 23060, 264, 1901, 11, 3235, 970, 952, 1048, 8606, 264, 13850, 608, 6806, 935, 20904, 13, 51578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15005675149620126, "compression_ratio": 1.6538461538461537, "no_speech_prob": 1.169367662597065e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 38708, "start": 387.08, "end": 387.47999999999996, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 50385], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15511817262883773, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612899428169014e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 38708, "start": 387.65999999999997, "end": 393.84, "text": " And this requires the space of all possible shapes to be complete, meaning there are no missing pieces.", "tokens": [50394, 400, 341, 7029, 264, 1901, 295, 439, 1944, 10854, 281, 312, 3566, 11, 3620, 456, 366, 572, 5361, 3755, 13, 50703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15511817262883773, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612899428169014e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 38708, "start": 393.97999999999996, "end": 394.18, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50710, 1779, 13, 50720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15511817262883773, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612899428169014e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 38708, "start": 394.35999999999996, "end": 395.47999999999996, "text": " No mathematical potholes.", "tokens": [50729, 883, 18894, 280, 900, 7456, 13, 50785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15511817262883773, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612899428169014e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 38708, "start": 395.59999999999997, "end": 396.06, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50791, 7587, 13, 50814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15511817262883773, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612899428169014e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 38708, "start": 396.35999999999996, "end": 396.58, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50829, 865, 13, 50840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15511817262883773, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612899428169014e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 38708, "start": 396.68, "end": 404.86, "text": " In a complete metric space, if you have a sequence of shapes that keep getting closer and closer together, meaning their Hausdorff distances are shrinking towards zero,", "tokens": [50845, 682, 257, 3566, 20678, 1901, 11, 498, 291, 362, 257, 8310, 295, 10854, 300, 1066, 1242, 4966, 293, 4966, 1214, 11, 3620, 641, 22725, 67, 284, 602, 22182, 366, 41684, 3030, 4018, 11, 51254], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15511817262883773, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612899428169014e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 38708, "start": 405.91999999999996, "end": 409.02, "text": " they won't suddenly vanish or fall through a hole in the mathematics.", "tokens": [51307, 436, 1582, 380, 5800, 43584, 420, 2100, 807, 257, 5458, 294, 264, 18666, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15511817262883773, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612899428169014e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 38708, "start": 409.41999999999996, "end": 413.36, "text": " They're guaranteed to land on a concrete, mathematically real limit.", "tokens": [51482, 814, 434, 18031, 281, 2117, 322, 257, 9859, 11, 44003, 957, 4948, 13, 51679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15511817262883773, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612899428169014e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 41336, "start": 413.36, "end": 416.56, "text": " And the continuation attractor theorem builds directly on that.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 29357, 5049, 284, 20904, 15182, 3838, 322, 300, 13, 50525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13029016494750978, "compression_ratio": 1.6564885496183206, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813168695825609e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 41336, "start": 416.56, "end": 427.02000000000004, "text": " If our growth rules are contractions and our space is complete, applying those rules repeatedly will inevitably drag any starting shape toward one single unique geometric limit.", "tokens": [50525, 759, 527, 4599, 4474, 366, 4364, 626, 293, 527, 1901, 307, 3566, 11, 9275, 729, 4474, 18227, 486, 28171, 5286, 604, 2891, 3909, 7361, 472, 2167, 3845, 33246, 4948, 13, 51048], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13029016494750978, "compression_ratio": 1.6564885496183206, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813168695825609e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 41336, "start": 427.34000000000003, "end": 427.96000000000004, "text": " The attractor.", "tokens": [51064, 440, 5049, 284, 13, 51095], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13029016494750978, "compression_ratio": 1.6564885496183206, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813168695825609e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 41336, "start": 428.28000000000003, "end": 432.08000000000004, "text": " It doesn't matter if your starting shape was a square, a circle, or just a random scribble.", "tokens": [51111, 467, 1177, 380, 1871, 498, 428, 2891, 3909, 390, 257, 3732, 11, 257, 6329, 11, 420, 445, 257, 4974, 39435, 638, 13, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13029016494750978, "compression_ratio": 1.6564885496183206, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813168695825609e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 41336, "start": 432.42, "end": 436.28000000000003, "text": " The contracting rules will pull it relentlessly until it forms the fern.", "tokens": [51318, 440, 36095, 4474, 486, 2235, 309, 34045, 12048, 1826, 309, 6422, 264, 283, 1248, 13, 51511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13029016494750978, "compression_ratio": 1.6564885496183206, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813168695825609e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 41336, "start": 436.36, "end": 437.06, "text": " That's wild.", "tokens": [51515, 663, 311, 4868, 13, 51550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13029016494750978, "compression_ratio": 1.6564885496183206, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813168695825609e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 43706, "start": 437.06, "end": 444.76, "text": " And once it hits that final shape, applying the rules one more time just gives you the exact same shape back, it has achieved perfect self-similarity.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 1564, 309, 8664, 300, 2572, 3909, 11, 9275, 264, 4474, 472, 544, 565, 445, 2709, 291, 264, 1900, 912, 3909, 646, 11, 309, 575, 11042, 2176, 2698, 12, 30937, 2202, 507, 13, 50750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12597518131650728, "compression_ratio": 1.517094017094017, "no_speech_prob": 1.90517653736455e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 43706, "start": 445.08, "end": 454.04, "text": " Okay, let's make this concrete because the draft provides a stunningly stark example of this called the two refusals, which generates the cantor set.", "tokens": [50766, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 652, 341, 9859, 570, 264, 11206, 6417, 257, 18550, 356, 17417, 1365, 295, 341, 1219, 264, 732, 1895, 301, 1124, 11, 597, 23815, 264, 11223, 284, 992, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12597518131650728, "compression_ratio": 1.517094017094017, "no_speech_prob": 1.90517653736455e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 43706, "start": 454.44, "end": 456.4, "text": " Let's walk through the physical mechanics of it.", "tokens": [51234, 961, 311, 1792, 807, 264, 4001, 12939, 295, 309, 13, 51332], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12597518131650728, "compression_ratio": 1.517094017094017, "no_speech_prob": 1.90517653736455e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 43706, "start": 456.5, "end": 456.72, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [51337, 4894, 13, 51348], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12597518131650728, "compression_ratio": 1.517094017094017, "no_speech_prob": 1.90517653736455e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 45672, "start": 456.72, "end": 462.64000000000004, "text": " We take a solid line segment, like a continuous piece of string stretching from zero to one.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 747, 257, 5100, 1622, 9469, 11, 411, 257, 10957, 2522, 295, 6798, 19632, 490, 4018, 281, 472, 13, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13566039265065954, "compression_ratio": 1.9370370370370371, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759212933039393e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 45672, "start": 463.02000000000004, "end": 465.1, "text": " Our first rule dictates a refusal.", "tokens": [50680, 2621, 700, 4978, 12569, 1024, 257, 48948, 13, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13566039265065954, "compression_ratio": 1.9370370370370371, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759212933039393e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 45672, "start": 465.74, "end": 469.98, "text": " We have to locate the middle third of that string, cut it out, and discard it.", "tokens": [50816, 492, 362, 281, 22370, 264, 2808, 2636, 295, 300, 6798, 11, 1723, 309, 484, 11, 293, 31597, 309, 13, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13566039265065954, "compression_ratio": 1.9370370370370371, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759212933039393e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 45672, "start": 470.22, "end": 474.42, "text": " So you are left with two shorter pieces of string, one on the left, one on the right.", "tokens": [51040, 407, 291, 366, 1411, 365, 732, 11639, 3755, 295, 6798, 11, 472, 322, 264, 1411, 11, 472, 322, 264, 558, 13, 51250], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13566039265065954, "compression_ratio": 1.9370370370370371, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759212933039393e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 45672, "start": 474.54, "end": 474.8, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51256, 1779, 13, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13566039265065954, "compression_ratio": 1.9370370370370371, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759212933039393e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 45672, "start": 474.90000000000003, "end": 479.14000000000004, "text": " And our second rule is just to apply the first rule again to whatever survived.", "tokens": [51274, 400, 527, 1150, 4978, 307, 445, 281, 3079, 264, 700, 4978, 797, 281, 2035, 14433, 13, 51486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13566039265065954, "compression_ratio": 1.9370370370370371, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759212933039393e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 45672, "start": 479.46000000000004, "end": 481.88000000000005, "text": " We take the left string, cut out its middle third.", "tokens": [51502, 492, 747, 264, 1411, 6798, 11, 1723, 484, 1080, 2808, 2636, 13, 51623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13566039265065954, "compression_ratio": 1.9370370370370371, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759212933039393e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 45672, "start": 482.0, "end": 483.88000000000005, "text": " We take the right string, cut out its middle third.", "tokens": [51629, 492, 747, 264, 558, 6798, 11, 1723, 484, 1080, 2808, 2636, 13, 51723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13566039265065954, "compression_ratio": 1.9370370370370371, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759212933039393e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 45672, "start": 484.02000000000004, "end": 486.14000000000004, "text": " So now we have four even shorter pieces.", "tokens": [51730, 407, 586, 321, 362, 1451, 754, 11639, 3755, 13, 51836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13566039265065954, "compression_ratio": 1.9370370370370371, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759212933039393e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 48614, "start": 486.14, "end": 486.78, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1678141997410701, "compression_ratio": 1.62109375, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077911350707464e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 48614, "start": 487.24, "end": 490.94, "text": " And we repeat this recursive refusal out to infinity.", "tokens": [50420, 400, 321, 7149, 341, 20560, 488, 48948, 484, 281, 13202, 13, 50605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1678141997410701, "compression_ratio": 1.62109375, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077911350707464e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 48614, "start": 491.18, "end": 494.06, "text": " And the mathematics of what remains at the limit of infinity is profound.", "tokens": [50617, 400, 264, 18666, 295, 437, 7023, 412, 264, 4948, 295, 13202, 307, 14382, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1678141997410701, "compression_ratio": 1.62109375, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077911350707464e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 48614, "start": 495.02, "end": 501.4, "text": " You are left with an uncountable number of points, yet the total length of all those points combined is precisely zero.", "tokens": [50809, 509, 366, 1411, 365, 364, 6219, 792, 712, 1230, 295, 2793, 11, 1939, 264, 3217, 4641, 295, 439, 729, 2793, 9354, 307, 13402, 4018, 13, 51128], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1678141997410701, "compression_ratio": 1.62109375, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077911350707464e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 48614, "start": 501.78, "end": 503.56, "text": " It is a nowhere dense dust.", "tokens": [51147, 467, 307, 257, 11159, 18011, 8634, 13, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1678141997410701, "compression_ratio": 1.62109375, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077911350707464e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 48614, "start": 503.88, "end": 505.21999999999997, "text": " A nowhere dense dust.", "tokens": [51252, 316, 11159, 18011, 8634, 13, 51319], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1678141997410701, "compression_ratio": 1.62109375, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077911350707464e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 48614, "start": 505.74, "end": 509.59999999999997, "text": " It's a highly complex, infinitely detailed future geometry.", "tokens": [51345, 467, 311, 257, 5405, 3997, 11, 36227, 9942, 2027, 18426, 13, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1678141997410701, "compression_ratio": 1.62109375, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077911350707464e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 48614, "start": 510.2, "end": 512.8199999999999, "text": " But it wasn't accumulated by a spreading puddle.", "tokens": [51568, 583, 309, 2067, 380, 31346, 538, 257, 15232, 14166, 2285, 13, 51699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1678141997410701, "compression_ratio": 1.62109375, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077911350707464e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 51282, "start": 512.82, "end": 517.5400000000001, "text": " It was entirely determined by two really simple contraction rules.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 390, 7696, 9540, 538, 732, 534, 2199, 37372, 4474, 13, 50601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2181219418843587, "compression_ratio": 0.9705882352941176, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617333594218242e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 51754, "start": 517.54, "end": 522.5999999999999, "text": " The instruction set is microscopic, but the resulting reality is infinitely deep.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 10951, 992, 307, 47897, 11, 457, 264, 16505, 4103, 307, 36227, 2452, 13, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14227533340454102, "compression_ratio": 1.6179245283018868, "no_speech_prob": 1.790190174918993e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 51754, "start": 523.16, "end": 525.7199999999999, "text": " This completely reframes the scale of analysis.", "tokens": [50646, 639, 2584, 13334, 1632, 264, 4373, 295, 5215, 13, 50774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14227533340454102, "compression_ratio": 1.6179245283018868, "no_speech_prob": 1.790190174918993e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 51754, "start": 526.18, "end": 526.76, "text": " How so?", "tokens": [50797, 1012, 370, 30, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14227533340454102, "compression_ratio": 1.6179245283018868, "no_speech_prob": 1.790190174918993e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 51754, "start": 526.88, "end": 533.48, "text": " Well, the natural unit of study for a complex system is no longer the vast, overwhelming space of the future itself.", "tokens": [50832, 1042, 11, 264, 3303, 4985, 295, 2979, 337, 257, 3997, 1185, 307, 572, 2854, 264, 8369, 11, 13373, 1901, 295, 264, 2027, 2564, 13, 51162], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14227533340454102, "compression_ratio": 1.6179245283018868, "no_speech_prob": 1.790190174918993e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 51754, "start": 534.18, "end": 538.4599999999999, "text": " The natural unit of study becomes the small set of contracting operations that built it.", "tokens": [51197, 440, 3303, 4985, 295, 2979, 3643, 264, 1359, 992, 295, 36095, 7705, 300, 3094, 309, 13, 51411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14227533340454102, "compression_ratio": 1.6179245283018868, "no_speech_prob": 1.790190174918993e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 53846, "start": 538.46, "end": 544.22, "text": " And for you listening, applying this to human behavior shifts the paradigm of how we view our personal trajectories.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 337, 291, 4764, 11, 9275, 341, 281, 1952, 5223, 19201, 264, 24709, 295, 577, 321, 1910, 527, 2973, 18257, 2083, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12700042416972498, "compression_ratio": 1.4444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037886722471752e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 53846, "start": 544.5400000000001, "end": 547.5600000000001, "text": " We so often view our lives as that spreading puddle, right?", "tokens": [50669, 492, 370, 2049, 1910, 527, 2909, 382, 300, 15232, 14166, 2285, 11, 558, 30, 50820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12700042416972498, "compression_ratio": 1.4444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037886722471752e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 53846, "start": 547.6800000000001, "end": 552.38, "text": " A massive accumulation of random events just expanding endlessly into the dark room.", "tokens": [50826, 316, 5994, 35647, 295, 4974, 3931, 445, 14702, 44920, 666, 264, 2877, 1808, 13, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12700042416972498, "compression_ratio": 1.4444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037886722471752e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 53846, "start": 552.52, "end": 552.82, "text": " Absolutely.", "tokens": [51068, 7021, 13, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12700042416972498, "compression_ratio": 1.4444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037886722471752e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 55282, "start": 552.82, "end": 558.44, "text": " But the math of the continuation attractor suggests our futures are actually generated by our personal contractions.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 5221, 295, 264, 29357, 5049, 284, 13409, 527, 26071, 366, 767, 10833, 538, 527, 2973, 4364, 626, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11967207590738932, "compression_ratio": 1.707395498392283, "no_speech_prob": 2.262755737988953e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 55282, "start": 558.5200000000001, "end": 561.98, "text": " Like, if you have a strict rule where you always read for 20 minutes before bed,", "tokens": [50650, 1743, 11, 498, 291, 362, 257, 10910, 4978, 689, 291, 1009, 1401, 337, 945, 2077, 949, 2901, 11, 50823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11967207590738932, "compression_ratio": 1.707395498392283, "no_speech_prob": 2.262755737988953e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 55282, "start": 562.0600000000001, "end": 566.98, "text": " or a rule where you never check your phone during a conversation, those aren't just isolated events adding up.", "tokens": [50827, 420, 257, 4978, 689, 291, 1128, 1520, 428, 2593, 1830, 257, 3761, 11, 729, 3212, 380, 445, 14621, 3931, 5127, 493, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11967207590738932, "compression_ratio": 1.707395498392283, "no_speech_prob": 2.262755737988953e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 55282, "start": 567.3000000000001, "end": 568.1800000000001, "text": " No, they're operators.", "tokens": [51089, 883, 11, 436, 434, 19077, 13, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11967207590738932, "compression_ratio": 1.707395498392283, "no_speech_prob": 2.262755737988953e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 55282, "start": 568.5600000000001, "end": 576.82, "text": " If those rules act as true contractions, if they consistently pull your behavior toward a specific center and away from random drift,", "tokens": [51152, 759, 729, 4474, 605, 382, 2074, 4364, 626, 11, 498, 436, 14961, 2235, 428, 5223, 7361, 257, 2685, 3056, 293, 1314, 490, 4974, 19699, 11, 51565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11967207590738932, "compression_ratio": 1.707395498392283, "no_speech_prob": 2.262755737988953e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 55282, "start": 577.44, "end": 580.36, "text": " they generate a very specific geometric limit.", "tokens": [51596, 436, 8460, 257, 588, 2685, 33246, 4948, 13, 51742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11967207590738932, "compression_ratio": 1.707395498392283, "no_speech_prob": 2.262755737988953e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 55282, "start": 580.5, "end": 581.74, "text": " A behavioral fern.", "tokens": [51749, 316, 19124, 283, 1248, 13, 51811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11967207590738932, "compression_ratio": 1.707395498392283, "no_speech_prob": 2.262755737988953e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 58174, "start": 581.74, "end": 584.28, "text": " Yes. Apply daily to their own output.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 25264, 5212, 281, 641, 1065, 5598, 13, 50492], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14097165631818342, "compression_ratio": 1.6517241379310346, "no_speech_prob": 1.5737262838363963e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 58174, "start": 584.6800000000001, "end": 588.86, "text": " Those tiny rules generate the precise, fractal shape of your future.", "tokens": [50512, 3950, 5870, 4474, 8460, 264, 13600, 11, 17948, 304, 3909, 295, 428, 2027, 13, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14097165631818342, "compression_ratio": 1.6517241379310346, "no_speech_prob": 1.5737262838363963e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 58174, "start": 589.28, "end": 591.58, "text": " You aren't walking into a pre-existing tomorrow.", "tokens": [50742, 509, 3212, 380, 4494, 666, 257, 659, 12, 36447, 4153, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14097165631818342, "compression_ratio": 1.6517241379310346, "no_speech_prob": 1.5737262838363963e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 58174, "start": 592.0600000000001, "end": 596.8, "text": " You are rendering a cantor set in real time through the rules you refuse to break.", "tokens": [50881, 509, 366, 22407, 257, 11223, 284, 992, 294, 957, 565, 807, 264, 4474, 291, 16791, 281, 1821, 13, 51118], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14097165631818342, "compression_ratio": 1.6517241379310346, "no_speech_prob": 1.5737262838363963e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 58174, "start": 597.12, "end": 600.78, "text": " That structural generation covers the first major phase of the draft.", "tokens": [51134, 663, 15067, 5125, 10538, 264, 700, 2563, 5574, 295, 264, 11206, 13, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14097165631818342, "compression_ratio": 1.6517241379310346, "no_speech_prob": 1.5737262838363963e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 58174, "start": 601.3, "end": 604.6, "text": " But moving into the second phase, the author flips the perspective entirely.", "tokens": [51343, 583, 2684, 666, 264, 1150, 5574, 11, 264, 3793, 40249, 264, 4585, 7696, 13, 51508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14097165631818342, "compression_ratio": 1.6517241379310346, "no_speech_prob": 1.5737262838363963e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 58174, "start": 605.0600000000001, "end": 609.78, "text": " We transition from examining how futures branch out and grow to how they merge back together.", "tokens": [51531, 492, 6034, 490, 34662, 577, 26071, 9819, 484, 293, 1852, 281, 577, 436, 22183, 646, 1214, 13, 51767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14097165631818342, "compression_ratio": 1.6517241379310346, "no_speech_prob": 1.5737262838363963e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 60978, "start": 609.78, "end": 612.48, "text": " Right. The author introduces continuation quotients.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 440, 3793, 31472, 29357, 9641, 2448, 13, 50500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17619558590561596, "compression_ratio": 1.55, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488084769034073e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 60978, "start": 612.88, "end": 616.0, "text": " We move from the creation of detail to the destruction of distinction.", "tokens": [50520, 492, 1286, 490, 264, 8016, 295, 2607, 281, 264, 13563, 295, 16844, 13, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17619558590561596, "compression_ratio": 1.55, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488084769034073e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 60978, "start": 616.64, "end": 622.8399999999999, "text": " The draft examines what happens when two entirely different histories produce the exact same reachable future.", "tokens": [50708, 440, 11206, 1139, 1652, 437, 2314, 562, 732, 7696, 819, 30631, 5258, 264, 1900, 912, 2524, 712, 2027, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17619558590561596, "compression_ratio": 1.55, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488084769034073e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 60978, "start": 623.06, "end": 625.0799999999999, "text": " And the physical analogy here is just perfect.", "tokens": [51029, 400, 264, 4001, 21663, 510, 307, 445, 2176, 13, 51130], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17619558590561596, "compression_ratio": 1.55, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488084769034073e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 60978, "start": 625.3199999999999, "end": 626.76, "text": " Picture two distinct rivers.", "tokens": [51142, 35730, 732, 10644, 18361, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17619558590561596, "compression_ratio": 1.55, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488084769034073e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 62676, "start": 626.76, "end": 631.3, "text": " One originates from, like, glacial melt on the frozen north face of a mountain range.", "tokens": [50365, 1485, 4957, 1024, 490, 11, 411, 11, 1563, 25980, 10083, 322, 264, 12496, 6830, 1851, 295, 257, 6937, 3613, 13, 50592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13631202114952934, "compression_ratio": 1.4712041884816753, "no_speech_prob": 1.97292594587839e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 62676, "start": 631.3, "end": 635.24, "text": " It carves through hard granite, dropping down steep, violent waterfalls.", "tokens": [50592, 467, 1032, 977, 807, 1152, 9370, 642, 11, 13601, 760, 16841, 11, 11867, 1281, 18542, 13, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13631202114952934, "compression_ratio": 1.4712041884816753, "no_speech_prob": 1.97292594587839e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 62676, "start": 635.58, "end": 643.0, "text": " And the other river starts in a warm subterranean spring on the lush south side, meandering lazily through soft limestone.", "tokens": [50806, 400, 264, 661, 6810, 3719, 294, 257, 4561, 1422, 391, 24584, 5587, 322, 264, 49729, 7377, 1252, 11, 385, 474, 1794, 19320, 953, 807, 2787, 2364, 19098, 13, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13631202114952934, "compression_ratio": 1.4712041884816753, "no_speech_prob": 1.97292594587839e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 64300, "start": 643.0, "end": 647.94, "text": " So their histories, their compositions, their energetic states are completely, entirely different.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 641, 30631, 11, 641, 43401, 11, 641, 24935, 4368, 366, 2584, 11, 7696, 819, 13, 50612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20225956326439268, "compression_ratio": 1.641255605381166, "no_speech_prob": 3.068702410236046e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 64300, "start": 648.12, "end": 649.08, "text": " Entirely different.", "tokens": [50621, 3951, 621, 356, 819, 13, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20225956326439268, "compression_ratio": 1.641255605381166, "no_speech_prob": 3.068702410236046e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 64300, "start": 649.46, "end": 652.74, "text": " But eventually, geography forces them to a confluence.", "tokens": [50688, 583, 4728, 11, 26695, 5874, 552, 281, 257, 1497, 40432, 13, 50852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20225956326439268, "compression_ratio": 1.641255605381166, "no_speech_prob": 3.068702410236046e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 64300, "start": 653.02, "end": 656.38, "text": " They merge into a single massive waterway.", "tokens": [50866, 814, 22183, 666, 257, 2167, 5994, 1281, 676, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20225956326439268, "compression_ratio": 1.641255605381166, "no_speech_prob": 3.068702410236046e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 64300, "start": 657.12, "end": 661.6, "text": " From the perspective of a boat launched a mile downstream of that confluence,", "tokens": [51071, 3358, 264, 4585, 295, 257, 6582, 8730, 257, 12620, 30621, 295, 300, 1497, 40432, 11, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20225956326439268, "compression_ratio": 1.641255605381166, "no_speech_prob": 3.068702410236046e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 64300, "start": 661.82, "end": 666.08, "text": " the origin of the water beneath the hull is fundamentally inaccessible.", "tokens": [51306, 264, 4957, 295, 264, 1281, 17149, 264, 32335, 307, 17879, 33230, 780, 964, 13, 51519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20225956326439268, "compression_ratio": 1.641255605381166, "no_speech_prob": 3.068702410236046e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 66608, "start": 666.08, "end": 670.7, "text": " And it's not simply that the information is obscured or difficult to measure.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 309, 311, 406, 2935, 300, 264, 1589, 307, 22082, 3831, 420, 2252, 281, 3481, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10818737243937555, "compression_ratio": 1.784452296819788, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947691080376748e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 66608, "start": 671.14, "end": 675.7800000000001, "text": " It is mathematically irrelevant to any physical interaction the boat will experience moving forward.", "tokens": [50618, 467, 307, 44003, 28682, 281, 604, 4001, 9285, 264, 6582, 486, 1752, 2684, 2128, 13, 50850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10818737243937555, "compression_ratio": 1.784452296819788, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947691080376748e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 66608, "start": 676.2800000000001, "end": 679.7800000000001, "text": " The history of the water has no bearing on the future trajectory of the boat.", "tokens": [50875, 440, 2503, 295, 264, 1281, 575, 572, 17350, 322, 264, 2027, 21512, 295, 264, 6582, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10818737243937555, "compression_ratio": 1.784452296819788, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947691080376748e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 66608, "start": 679.94, "end": 680.1600000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51058, 1779, 13, 51069], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10818737243937555, "compression_ratio": 1.784452296819788, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947691080376748e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 66608, "start": 680.5600000000001, "end": 685.94, "text": " And to formalize this merging, fliction defines an equivalence relation called a continuation quotient.", "tokens": [51089, 400, 281, 9860, 1125, 341, 44559, 11, 932, 4105, 23122, 364, 9052, 655, 9721, 1219, 257, 29357, 9641, 1196, 13, 51358], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10818737243937555, "compression_ratio": 1.784452296819788, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947691080376748e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 66608, "start": 686.64, "end": 688.72, "text": " Two different histories are mathematically equivalent.", "tokens": [51393, 4453, 819, 30631, 366, 44003, 10344, 13, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10818737243937555, "compression_ratio": 1.784452296819788, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947691080376748e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 66608, "start": 688.88, "end": 692.76, "text": " They are placed into the same quotient if their continuation spaces are identical.", "tokens": [51505, 814, 366, 7074, 666, 264, 912, 9641, 1196, 498, 641, 29357, 7673, 366, 14800, 13, 51699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10818737243937555, "compression_ratio": 1.784452296819788, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947691080376748e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 69276, "start": 692.76, "end": 699.52, "text": " And a continuation space is the formal set of all possible futures a system can reach within a specific time horizon.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 257, 29357, 1901, 307, 264, 9860, 992, 295, 439, 1944, 26071, 257, 1185, 393, 2524, 1951, 257, 2685, 565, 18046, 13, 50703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11371649982773255, "compression_ratio": 1.7734375, "no_speech_prob": 2.108827652433365e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 69276, "start": 699.8, "end": 703.9399999999999, "text": " So if history A allows you to eventually reach states X, Y, and Z,", "tokens": [50717, 407, 498, 2503, 316, 4045, 291, 281, 4728, 2524, 4368, 1783, 11, 398, 11, 293, 1176, 11, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11371649982773255, "compression_ratio": 1.7734375, "no_speech_prob": 2.108827652433365e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 69276, "start": 704.5, "end": 708.56, "text": " and history B allows you to eventually reach those exact same states X, Y, and Z,", "tokens": [50952, 293, 2503, 363, 4045, 291, 281, 4728, 2524, 729, 1900, 912, 4368, 1783, 11, 398, 11, 293, 1176, 11, 51155], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11371649982773255, "compression_ratio": 1.7734375, "no_speech_prob": 2.108827652433365e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 69276, "start": 709.24, "end": 714.54, "text": " then under this geometric framework, history A and history B are identical.", "tokens": [51189, 550, 833, 341, 33246, 8388, 11, 2503, 316, 293, 2503, 363, 366, 14800, 13, 51454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11371649982773255, "compression_ratio": 1.7734375, "no_speech_prob": 2.108827652433365e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 69276, "start": 714.8, "end": 717.38, "text": " See, my initial reaction to this was really defensive.", "tokens": [51467, 3008, 11, 452, 5883, 5480, 281, 341, 390, 534, 16468, 13, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11371649982773255, "compression_ratio": 1.7734375, "no_speech_prob": 2.108827652433365e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 69276, "start": 717.9, "end": 720.84, "text": " Because our histories feel intrinsically valuable to us.", "tokens": [51622, 1436, 527, 30631, 841, 28621, 984, 8263, 281, 505, 13, 51769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11371649982773255, "compression_ratio": 1.7734375, "no_speech_prob": 2.108827652433365e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 72084, "start": 720.84, "end": 727.7800000000001, "text": " The idea that two radically different paths could be deemed mathematically identical just because they arrive at the same waiting room,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1558, 300, 732, 35508, 819, 14518, 727, 312, 27637, 44003, 14800, 445, 570, 436, 8881, 412, 264, 912, 3806, 1808, 11, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.158887829891471, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 2.3620944610003303e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 72084, "start": 728.38, "end": 729.9200000000001, "text": " it feels like an erasure of the past.", "tokens": [50742, 309, 3417, 411, 364, 1189, 2508, 295, 264, 1791, 13, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.158887829891471, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 2.3620944610003303e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 72084, "start": 730.1, "end": 731.6800000000001, "text": " And that discomfort is totally natural.", "tokens": [50828, 400, 300, 28552, 307, 3879, 3303, 13, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.158887829891471, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 2.3620944610003303e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 72084, "start": 731.9, "end": 731.96, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50918, 865, 13, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.158887829891471, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 2.3620944610003303e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 72084, "start": 732.32, "end": 739.2800000000001, "text": " But the author relies on a property called time-homogenous dynamics to prove a really important structural lemma.", "tokens": [50939, 583, 264, 3793, 30910, 322, 257, 4707, 1219, 565, 12, 71, 298, 45519, 15679, 281, 7081, 257, 534, 1021, 15067, 7495, 1696, 13, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.158887829891471, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 2.3620944610003303e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 72084, "start": 739.62, "end": 741.6600000000001, "text": " Under these conditions, collisions are permanent.", "tokens": [51304, 6974, 613, 4487, 11, 46537, 366, 10996, 13, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.158887829891471, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 2.3620944610003303e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 74166, "start": 741.66, "end": 748.3399999999999, "text": " Meaning, if two states have the exact same immediate one-step future, they will share every subsequent future forever.", "tokens": [50365, 19948, 11, 498, 732, 4368, 362, 264, 1900, 912, 11629, 472, 12, 16792, 2027, 11, 436, 486, 2073, 633, 19962, 2027, 5680, 13, 50699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10648345947265625, "compression_ratio": 1.7182130584192439, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360748235666916e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 74166, "start": 748.4599999999999, "end": 752.14, "text": " Because the rules governing the system don't arbitrarily change based on the clock.", "tokens": [50705, 1436, 264, 4474, 30054, 264, 1185, 500, 380, 19071, 3289, 1319, 2361, 322, 264, 7830, 13, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10648345947265625, "compression_ratio": 1.7182130584192439, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360748235666916e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 74166, "start": 752.4599999999999, "end": 757.0799999999999, "text": " If state A and state B both transition into state C at the next tick of the clock,", "tokens": [50905, 759, 1785, 316, 293, 1785, 363, 1293, 6034, 666, 1785, 383, 412, 264, 958, 5204, 295, 264, 7830, 11, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10648345947265625, "compression_ratio": 1.7182130584192439, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360748235666916e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 74166, "start": 757.36, "end": 761.12, "text": " they are now both sitting in state C, subject to the exact same homogenous rules.", "tokens": [51150, 436, 366, 586, 1293, 3798, 294, 1785, 383, 11, 3983, 281, 264, 1900, 912, 3655, 45519, 4474, 13, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10648345947265625, "compression_ratio": 1.7182130584192439, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360748235666916e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 74166, "start": 761.26, "end": 766.02, "text": " There is literally nothing left in the mechanics of the universe to distinguish them moving forward.", "tokens": [51345, 821, 307, 3736, 1825, 1411, 294, 264, 12939, 295, 264, 6445, 281, 20206, 552, 2684, 2128, 13, 51583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10648345947265625, "compression_ratio": 1.7182130584192439, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360748235666916e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 74166, "start": 766.4, "end": 768.06, "text": " The collision cannot be undone.", "tokens": [51602, 440, 24644, 2644, 312, 674, 546, 13, 51685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10648345947265625, "compression_ratio": 1.7182130584192439, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360748235666916e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 76806, "start": 768.06, "end": 774.0, "text": " To ground this in engineering, because the math gets pretty abstract, the draft dissects a traffic light system.", "tokens": [50365, 1407, 2727, 341, 294, 7043, 11, 570, 264, 5221, 2170, 1238, 12649, 11, 264, 11206, 48332, 82, 257, 6419, 1442, 1185, 13, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12924874062631644, "compression_ratio": 1.5848375451263539, "no_speech_prob": 2.4086843630755084e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 76806, "start": 774.38, "end": 778.3599999999999, "text": " And it's a beautifully contained example of mechanical memory and reachable futures.", "tokens": [50681, 400, 309, 311, 257, 16525, 16212, 1365, 295, 12070, 4675, 293, 2524, 712, 26071, 13, 50880], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12924874062631644, "compression_ratio": 1.5848375451263539, "no_speech_prob": 2.4086843630755084e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 76806, "start": 778.6199999999999, "end": 779.1999999999999, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [50893, 467, 534, 307, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12924874062631644, "compression_ratio": 1.5848375451263539, "no_speech_prob": 2.4086843630755084e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 76806, "start": 779.2399999999999, "end": 783.18, "text": " Imagine an intersection controlled by a light with four distinct phases.", "tokens": [50924, 11739, 364, 15236, 10164, 538, 257, 1442, 365, 1451, 10644, 18764, 13, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12924874062631644, "compression_ratio": 1.5848375451263539, "no_speech_prob": 2.4086843630755084e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 76806, "start": 783.9, "end": 788.1199999999999, "text": " Phase 0 is a red light for cars, opening the crosswalk for pedestrians.", "tokens": [51157, 24432, 1958, 307, 257, 2182, 1442, 337, 5163, 11, 5193, 264, 3278, 12490, 337, 48339, 13, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12924874062631644, "compression_ratio": 1.5848375451263539, "no_speech_prob": 2.4086843630755084e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 76806, "start": 788.9399999999999, "end": 793.06, "text": " Phases 1, 2, and 3 cycle through various green and yellow lights for the vehicles.", "tokens": [51409, 2623, 1957, 502, 11, 568, 11, 293, 805, 6586, 807, 3683, 3092, 293, 5566, 5811, 337, 264, 8948, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12924874062631644, "compression_ratio": 1.5848375451263539, "no_speech_prob": 2.4086843630755084e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 79306, "start": 793.06, "end": 795.88, "text": " And alongside the phase, the system maintains a request bit.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 12385, 264, 5574, 11, 264, 1185, 33385, 257, 5308, 857, 13, 50506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14277305603027343, "compression_ratio": 1.7102473498233215, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149010076572546e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 79306, "start": 796.28, "end": 798.64, "text": " It's a mechanical memory state of either 0 or 1.", "tokens": [50526, 467, 311, 257, 12070, 4675, 1785, 295, 2139, 1958, 420, 502, 13, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14277305603027343, "compression_ratio": 1.7102473498233215, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149010076572546e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 79306, "start": 799.26, "end": 801.26, "text": " This bit tracks pedestrian intent.", "tokens": [50675, 639, 857, 10218, 33947, 8446, 13, 50775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14277305603027343, "compression_ratio": 1.7102473498233215, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149010076572546e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 79306, "start": 801.68, "end": 804.4, "text": " If someone pushes the crossing button, the bit flips to 1.", "tokens": [50796, 759, 1580, 21020, 264, 14712, 2960, 11, 264, 857, 40249, 281, 502, 13, 50932], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14277305603027343, "compression_ratio": 1.7102473498233215, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149010076572546e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 79306, "start": 804.64, "end": 806.8199999999999, "text": " If no one is waiting, it remains 0.", "tokens": [50944, 759, 572, 472, 307, 3806, 11, 309, 7023, 1958, 13, 51053], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14277305603027343, "compression_ratio": 1.7102473498233215, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149010076572546e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 79306, "start": 807.28, "end": 811.88, "text": " So, an engineer writing the software for this controller has to make a highly specific decision.", "tokens": [51076, 407, 11, 364, 11403, 3579, 264, 4722, 337, 341, 10561, 575, 281, 652, 257, 5405, 2685, 3537, 13, 51306], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14277305603027343, "compression_ratio": 1.7102473498233215, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149010076572546e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 79306, "start": 812.5, "end": 815.9, "text": " When exactly should the system clear that request bit back to 0?", "tokens": [51337, 1133, 2293, 820, 264, 1185, 1850, 300, 5308, 857, 646, 281, 1958, 30, 51507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14277305603027343, "compression_ratio": 1.7102473498233215, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149010076572546e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 79306, "start": 816.28, "end": 820.38, "text": " When should the machine mathematically forget that a pedestrian pushed the button?", "tokens": [51526, 1133, 820, 264, 3479, 44003, 2870, 300, 257, 33947, 9152, 264, 2960, 30, 51731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14277305603027343, "compression_ratio": 1.7102473498233215, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149010076572546e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 82038, "start": 820.38, "end": 825.8, "text": " And the draft contrasts two designs to illustrate the power of continuation quotients.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 11206, 8712, 82, 732, 11347, 281, 23221, 264, 1347, 295, 29357, 9641, 2448, 13, 50636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15551312764485678, "compression_ratio": 1.6349809885931559, "no_speech_prob": 1.87591023444178e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 82038, "start": 826.62, "end": 828.62, "text": " The first is mathematically exact.", "tokens": [50677, 440, 700, 307, 44003, 1900, 13, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15551312764485678, "compression_ratio": 1.6349809885931559, "no_speech_prob": 1.87591023444178e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 82038, "start": 829.3, "end": 834.34, "text": " The rule states, clear the request bit unconditionally upon arrival at phase 0.", "tokens": [50811, 440, 4978, 4368, 11, 1850, 264, 5308, 857, 34959, 15899, 3564, 18365, 412, 5574, 1958, 13, 51063], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15551312764485678, "compression_ratio": 1.6349809885931559, "no_speech_prob": 1.87591023444178e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 82038, "start": 834.66, "end": 837.1, "text": " Okay, let's track the futures of that exact design.", "tokens": [51079, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 2837, 264, 26071, 295, 300, 1900, 1715, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15551312764485678, "compression_ratio": 1.6349809885931559, "no_speech_prob": 1.87591023444178e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 82038, "start": 837.88, "end": 841.28, "text": " The light is currently at phase 3, the final yellow light before red.", "tokens": [51240, 440, 1442, 307, 4362, 412, 5574, 805, 11, 264, 2572, 5566, 1442, 949, 2182, 13, 51410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15551312764485678, "compression_ratio": 1.6349809885931559, "no_speech_prob": 1.87591023444178e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 82038, "start": 841.82, "end": 845.4, "text": " A pedestrian has pushed the button, so the request bit is holding a 1.", "tokens": [51437, 316, 33947, 575, 9152, 264, 2960, 11, 370, 264, 5308, 857, 307, 5061, 257, 502, 13, 51616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15551312764485678, "compression_ratio": 1.6349809885931559, "no_speech_prob": 1.87591023444178e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 82038, "start": 845.78, "end": 846.1, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51635, 1779, 13, 51651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15551312764485678, "compression_ratio": 1.6349809885931559, "no_speech_prob": 1.87591023444178e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 82038, "start": 846.34, "end": 847.78, "text": " We will call that history A.", "tokens": [51663, 492, 486, 818, 300, 2503, 316, 13, 51735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15551312764485678, "compression_ratio": 1.6349809885931559, "no_speech_prob": 1.87591023444178e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 84778, "start": 847.78, "end": 852.92, "text": " Now, consider history B. The light is at phase 3, but the request bit is 0.", "tokens": [50365, 823, 11, 1949, 2503, 363, 13, 440, 1442, 307, 412, 5574, 805, 11, 457, 264, 5308, 857, 307, 1958, 13, 50622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13139000273587412, "compression_ratio": 1.6791044776119404, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485582209583739e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 84778, "start": 853.18, "end": 854.0799999999999, "text": " No one pushed the button.", "tokens": [50635, 883, 472, 9152, 264, 2960, 13, 50680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13139000273587412, "compression_ratio": 1.6791044776119404, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485582209583739e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 84778, "start": 854.4399999999999, "end": 859.02, "text": " Under the exact design, the transition from phase 3 dictates that the light moves to phase 0.", "tokens": [50698, 6974, 264, 1900, 1715, 11, 264, 6034, 490, 5574, 805, 12569, 1024, 300, 264, 1442, 6067, 281, 5574, 1958, 13, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13139000273587412, "compression_ratio": 1.6791044776119404, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485582209583739e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 84778, "start": 859.24, "end": 863.14, "text": " The moment it arrives at phase 0, the software forcibly sets the bit to 0", "tokens": [50938, 440, 1623, 309, 20116, 412, 5574, 1958, 11, 264, 4722, 337, 537, 25021, 6352, 264, 857, 281, 1958, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13139000273587412, "compression_ratio": 1.6791044776119404, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485582209583739e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 84778, "start": 863.14, "end": 866.36, "text": " because the crosswalk is now open and the pedestrian is being served.", "tokens": [51133, 570, 264, 3278, 12490, 307, 586, 1269, 293, 264, 33947, 307, 885, 7584, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13139000273587412, "compression_ratio": 1.6791044776119404, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485582209583739e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 84778, "start": 866.62, "end": 868.88, "text": " Notice what happened to the continuation spaces there.", "tokens": [51307, 13428, 437, 2011, 281, 264, 29357, 7673, 456, 13, 51420], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13139000273587412, "compression_ratio": 1.6791044776119404, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485582209583739e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 84778, "start": 869.62, "end": 872.4599999999999, "text": " History A and history B had completely different pasts.", "tokens": [51457, 12486, 316, 293, 2503, 363, 632, 2584, 819, 1791, 82, 13, 51599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13139000273587412, "compression_ratio": 1.6791044776119404, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485582209583739e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 87246, "start": 872.46, "end": 874.76, "text": " One had waiting pedestrian, one did not.", "tokens": [50365, 1485, 632, 3806, 33947, 11, 472, 630, 406, 13, 50480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17605200966635903, "compression_ratio": 1.5867768595041323, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691630495655919e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 87246, "start": 875.08, "end": 877.4200000000001, "text": " But their one-step future is completely identical.", "tokens": [50496, 583, 641, 472, 12, 16792, 2027, 307, 2584, 14800, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17605200966635903, "compression_ratio": 1.5867768595041323, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691630495655919e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 87246, "start": 877.98, "end": 880.0400000000001, "text": " They both arrive at phase 0 with a cleared bit.", "tokens": [50641, 814, 1293, 8881, 412, 5574, 1958, 365, 257, 19725, 857, 13, 50744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17605200966635903, "compression_ratio": 1.5867768595041323, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691630495655919e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 87246, "start": 880.2, "end": 880.52, "text": " Ah.", "tokens": [50752, 2438, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17605200966635903, "compression_ratio": 1.5867768595041323, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691630495655919e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 87246, "start": 881.2800000000001, "end": 882.6, "text": " The reverse hit the confluence.", "tokens": [50806, 440, 9943, 2045, 264, 1497, 40432, 13, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17605200966635903, "compression_ratio": 1.5867768595041323, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691630495655919e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 87246, "start": 883.26, "end": 887.6600000000001, "text": " The system correctly recognized that the past history of the button push during phase 3", "tokens": [50905, 440, 1185, 8944, 9823, 300, 264, 1791, 2503, 295, 264, 2960, 2944, 1830, 5574, 805, 51125], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17605200966635903, "compression_ratio": 1.5867768595041323, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691630495655919e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 87246, "start": 887.6600000000001, "end": 892.36, "text": " is now mathematically irrelevant because the pedestrian is currently walking across the street.", "tokens": [51125, 307, 586, 44003, 28682, 570, 264, 33947, 307, 4362, 4494, 2108, 264, 4838, 13, 51360], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17605200966635903, "compression_ratio": 1.5867768595041323, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691630495655919e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 87246, "start": 892.86, "end": 893.86, "text": " It merged the histories.", "tokens": [51385, 467, 36427, 264, 30631, 13, 51435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17605200966635903, "compression_ratio": 1.5867768595041323, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691630495655919e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 89386, "start": 893.86, "end": 896.5, "text": " Fliction calls this design exactness.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 5498, 341, 1715, 1900, 1287, 13, 50497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15696454756330736, "compression_ratio": 1.643939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281822674297675e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 89386, "start": 897.1, "end": 902.12, "text": " The mechanical memory of the system perfectly aligns with the actual geometry of its reachable futures.", "tokens": [50527, 440, 12070, 4675, 295, 264, 1185, 6239, 7975, 82, 365, 264, 3539, 18426, 295, 1080, 2524, 712, 26071, 13, 50778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15696454756330736, "compression_ratio": 1.643939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281822674297675e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 89386, "start": 902.62, "end": 910.34, "text": " But the true power of this framework reveals itself when we examine what happens when an engineer fails to achieve design exactness.", "tokens": [50803, 583, 264, 2074, 1347, 295, 341, 8388, 20893, 2564, 562, 321, 17496, 437, 2314, 562, 364, 11403, 18199, 281, 4584, 1715, 1900, 1287, 13, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15696454756330736, "compression_ratio": 1.643939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281822674297675e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 89386, "start": 910.7, "end": 912.98, "text": " This moves us into the third phase of the draft.", "tokens": [51207, 639, 6067, 505, 666, 264, 2636, 5574, 295, 264, 11206, 13, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15696454756330736, "compression_ratio": 1.643939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281822674297675e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 89386, "start": 913.58, "end": 915.58, "text": " Distinction loss under quotients.", "tokens": [51351, 9840, 12987, 4470, 833, 9641, 2448, 13, 51451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15696454756330736, "compression_ratio": 1.643939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281822674297675e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 89386, "start": 915.84, "end": 916.12, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51464, 1779, 13, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15696454756330736, "compression_ratio": 1.643939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281822674297675e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 89386, "start": 916.22, "end": 920.54, "text": " Like, what is the mathematical penalty for forcing a merge too early?", "tokens": [51483, 1743, 11, 437, 307, 264, 18894, 16263, 337, 19030, 257, 22183, 886, 2440, 30, 51699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15696454756330736, "compression_ratio": 1.643939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281822674297675e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 92054, "start": 920.54, "end": 921.14, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50395], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12602454616177466, "compression_ratio": 1.7725752508361203, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234845499202288e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 92054, "start": 921.9399999999999, "end": 927.24, "text": " If the continuation quotient is the perfect merge, an inexact quotient is a destructive merge.", "tokens": [50435, 759, 264, 29357, 9641, 1196, 307, 264, 2176, 22183, 11, 364, 29961, 578, 9641, 1196, 307, 257, 26960, 22183, 13, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12602454616177466, "compression_ratio": 1.7725752508361203, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234845499202288e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 92054, "start": 927.9599999999999, "end": 930.38, "text": " And the text uses a library catalog to illustrate this.", "tokens": [50736, 400, 264, 2487, 4960, 257, 6405, 19746, 281, 23221, 341, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12602454616177466, "compression_ratio": 1.7725752508361203, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234845499202288e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 92054, "start": 930.4599999999999, "end": 931.64, "text": " A catalog is a quotient, right?", "tokens": [50861, 316, 19746, 307, 257, 9641, 1196, 11, 558, 30, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12602454616177466, "compression_ratio": 1.7725752508361203, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234845499202288e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 92054, "start": 931.7199999999999, "end": 937.12, "text": " It takes a thousand-page physical object and compresses it into a title, an author, and a Dewey decimal number.", "tokens": [50924, 467, 2516, 257, 4714, 12, 15161, 4001, 2657, 293, 14778, 279, 309, 666, 257, 4876, 11, 364, 3793, 11, 293, 257, 1346, 826, 88, 26601, 1230, 13, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12602454616177466, "compression_ratio": 1.7725752508361203, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234845499202288e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 92054, "start": 937.36, "end": 944.56, "text": " And a perfectly designed catalog loses no information that a patron actually requires to make a decision about retrieving the book.", "tokens": [51206, 400, 257, 6239, 4761, 19746, 18293, 572, 1589, 300, 257, 21843, 767, 7029, 281, 652, 257, 3537, 466, 19817, 798, 264, 1446, 13, 51566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12602454616177466, "compression_ratio": 1.7725752508361203, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234845499202288e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 92054, "start": 944.7199999999999, "end": 949.5999999999999, "text": " But imagine a poorly designed catalog that only allows two categories for the entire building.", "tokens": [51574, 583, 3811, 257, 22271, 4761, 19746, 300, 787, 4045, 732, 10479, 337, 264, 2302, 2390, 13, 51818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12602454616177466, "compression_ratio": 1.7725752508361203, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234845499202288e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 94960, "start": 949.6, "end": 951.26, "text": " Fiction and nonfiction.", "tokens": [50365, 479, 4105, 293, 2107, 32041, 13, 50448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14564129314591398, "compression_ratio": 1.6724137931034482, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815765360028712e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 94960, "start": 951.38, "end": 952.64, "text": " Oh, that would be a nightmare.", "tokens": [50454, 876, 11, 300, 576, 312, 257, 18724, 13, 50517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14564129314591398, "compression_ratio": 1.6724137931034482, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815765360028712e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 94960, "start": 953.02, "end": 953.24, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50536, 1779, 13, 50547], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14564129314591398, "compression_ratio": 1.6724137931034482, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815765360028712e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 94960, "start": 953.82, "end": 965.4200000000001, "text": " You are taking a deeply personal, harrowing memoir about surviving a war and a dense academic textbook on cellular biology and forcing them into the exact same mathematical fiber.", "tokens": [50576, 509, 366, 1940, 257, 8760, 2973, 11, 2233, 1892, 278, 38306, 466, 24948, 257, 1516, 293, 257, 18011, 7778, 25591, 322, 29267, 14956, 293, 19030, 552, 666, 264, 1900, 912, 18894, 12874, 13, 51156], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14564129314591398, "compression_ratio": 1.6724137931034482, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815765360028712e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 94960, "start": 966.1800000000001, "end": 967.94, "text": " You haven't lied, they are both nonfiction.", "tokens": [51194, 509, 2378, 380, 20101, 11, 436, 366, 1293, 2107, 32041, 13, 51282], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14564129314591398, "compression_ratio": 1.6724137931034482, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815765360028712e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 94960, "start": 968.5600000000001, "end": 972.66, "text": " But you have destroyed distinctions that dictate entirely different futures for the patron.", "tokens": [51313, 583, 291, 362, 8937, 1483, 49798, 300, 36071, 7696, 819, 26071, 337, 264, 21843, 13, 51518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14564129314591398, "compression_ratio": 1.6724137931034482, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815765360028712e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 94960, "start": 972.84, "end": 978.52, "text": " Because if I need to study for a biology exam, merging those two books into one category fails me entirely.", "tokens": [51527, 1436, 498, 286, 643, 281, 2979, 337, 257, 14956, 1139, 11, 44559, 729, 732, 3642, 666, 472, 7719, 18199, 385, 7696, 13, 51811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14564129314591398, "compression_ratio": 1.6724137931034482, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815765360028712e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 97852, "start": 978.52, "end": 982.1, "text": " And the critical contribution of this chapter is quantifying that failure.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 4924, 13150, 295, 341, 7187, 307, 4426, 5489, 300, 7763, 13, 50544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11285687375951696, "compression_ratio": 1.6418439716312057, "no_speech_prob": 1.501250295951606e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 97852, "start": 983.04, "end": 986.8, "text": " How much information is destroyed when a system forces a false merge?", "tokens": [50591, 1012, 709, 1589, 307, 8937, 562, 257, 1185, 5874, 257, 7908, 22183, 30, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11285687375951696, "compression_ratio": 1.6418439716312057, "no_speech_prob": 1.501250295951606e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 97852, "start": 987.48, "end": 989.68, "text": " The draft provides a strict formula for this.", "tokens": [50813, 440, 11206, 6417, 257, 10910, 8513, 337, 341, 13, 50923], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11285687375951696, "compression_ratio": 1.6418439716312057, "no_speech_prob": 1.501250295951606e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 97852, "start": 990.18, "end": 997.56, "text": " The loss at any given fiber is the base two logarithm of the number of distinct continuation spaces that are forced into that single fiber.", "tokens": [50948, 440, 4470, 412, 604, 2212, 12874, 307, 264, 3096, 732, 41473, 32674, 295, 264, 1230, 295, 10644, 29357, 7673, 300, 366, 7579, 666, 300, 2167, 12874, 13, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11285687375951696, "compression_ratio": 1.6418439716312057, "no_speech_prob": 1.501250295951606e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 97852, "start": 997.8, "end": 999.74, "text": " Okay, let's break down the mechanics of that formula.", "tokens": [51329, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 1821, 760, 264, 12939, 295, 300, 8513, 13, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11285687375951696, "compression_ratio": 1.6418439716312057, "no_speech_prob": 1.501250295951606e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 97852, "start": 1000.0799999999999, "end": 1000.34, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [51443, 4894, 13, 51456], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11285687375951696, "compression_ratio": 1.6418439716312057, "no_speech_prob": 1.501250295951606e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 97852, "start": 1000.6999999999999, "end": 1003.66, "text": " We look at the single bin, we shove things into our nonfiction category.", "tokens": [51474, 492, 574, 412, 264, 2167, 5171, 11, 321, 35648, 721, 666, 527, 2107, 32041, 7719, 13, 51622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11285687375951696, "compression_ratio": 1.6418439716312057, "no_speech_prob": 1.501250295951606e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 100366, "start": 1003.66, "end": 1009.3, "text": " We count how many genuinely different futures or distinct continuation spaces we threw in there.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 1207, 577, 867, 17839, 819, 26071, 420, 10644, 29357, 7673, 321, 11918, 294, 456, 13, 50647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.151689574832008, "compression_ratio": 1.7353951890034365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977475840786795e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 100366, "start": 1010.0, "end": 1014.88, "text": " If we threw in textbooks, memoirs, cookbooks, and travel guides, that's four distinct futures.", "tokens": [50682, 759, 321, 11918, 294, 33587, 11, 38306, 82, 11, 2543, 15170, 11, 293, 3147, 17007, 11, 300, 311, 1451, 10644, 26071, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.151689574832008, "compression_ratio": 1.7353951890034365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977475840786795e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 100366, "start": 1015.1, "end": 1017.1999999999999, "text": " We take the base two logarithm of four.", "tokens": [50937, 492, 747, 264, 3096, 732, 41473, 32674, 295, 1451, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.151689574832008, "compression_ratio": 1.7353951890034365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977475840786795e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 100366, "start": 1017.36, "end": 1018.04, "text": " Which is two.", "tokens": [51050, 3013, 307, 732, 13, 51084], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.151689574832008, "compression_ratio": 1.7353951890034365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977475840786795e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 100366, "start": 1018.16, "end": 1019.9399999999999, "text": " Exactly two bits of information lost.", "tokens": [51090, 7587, 732, 9239, 295, 1589, 2731, 13, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.151689574832008, "compression_ratio": 1.7353951890034365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977475840786795e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 100366, "start": 1020.06, "end": 1020.28, "text": " Uh-huh.", "tokens": [51185, 4019, 12, 18710, 13, 51196], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.151689574832008, "compression_ratio": 1.7353951890034365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977475840786795e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 100366, "start": 1020.52, "end": 1024.8799999999999, "text": " The logarithm scales the count of futures into a precise measure of destroyed data.", "tokens": [51208, 440, 41473, 32674, 17408, 264, 1207, 295, 26071, 666, 257, 13600, 3481, 295, 8937, 1412, 13, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.151689574832008, "compression_ratio": 1.7353951890034365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977475840786795e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 100366, "start": 1025.3999999999999, "end": 1030.82, "text": " If the catalog is perfectly designed, every item in a bin points to only one shared future.", "tokens": [51452, 759, 264, 19746, 307, 6239, 4761, 11, 633, 3174, 294, 257, 5171, 2793, 281, 787, 472, 5507, 2027, 13, 51723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.151689574832008, "compression_ratio": 1.7353951890034365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977475840786795e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 100366, "start": 1031.44, "end": 1033.2, "text": " The number of distinct spaces is one.", "tokens": [51754, 440, 1230, 295, 10644, 7673, 307, 472, 13, 51842], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.151689574832008, "compression_ratio": 1.7353951890034365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977475840786795e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 103320, "start": 1033.2, "end": 1035.38, "text": " And the logarithm of one is zero.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 41473, 32674, 295, 472, 307, 4018, 13, 50474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12644490702398892, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622656806048909e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 103320, "start": 1035.8400000000001, "end": 1036.42, "text": " Zero loss.", "tokens": [50497, 17182, 4470, 13, 50526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12644490702398892, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622656806048909e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 103320, "start": 1036.52, "end": 1037.0800000000002, "text": " Zero loss.", "tokens": [50531, 17182, 4470, 13, 50559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12644490702398892, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622656806048909e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 103320, "start": 1037.52, "end": 1041.2, "text": " That realization fundamentally shifted how I viewed these systems.", "tokens": [50581, 663, 25138, 17879, 18892, 577, 286, 19174, 613, 3652, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12644490702398892, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622656806048909e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 103320, "start": 1042.0, "end": 1048.74, "text": " The continuation quotient, the perfect merging of the rivers, is actually the ultimate lossless compression algorithm.", "tokens": [50805, 440, 29357, 9641, 1196, 11, 264, 2176, 44559, 295, 264, 18361, 11, 307, 767, 264, 9705, 4470, 1832, 19355, 9284, 13, 51142], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12644490702398892, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622656806048909e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 103320, "start": 1049.3600000000001, "end": 1056.6000000000001, "text": " It is the absolute coarsest summary of a history you can possibly create without losing a single pixel of resolution regarding the future.", "tokens": [51173, 467, 307, 264, 8236, 598, 685, 377, 12691, 295, 257, 2503, 291, 393, 6264, 1884, 1553, 7027, 257, 2167, 19261, 295, 8669, 8595, 264, 2027, 13, 51535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12644490702398892, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622656806048909e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 103320, "start": 1056.78, "end": 1057.7, "text": " That's a great way to put it.", "tokens": [51544, 663, 311, 257, 869, 636, 281, 829, 309, 13, 51590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12644490702398892, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622656806048909e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 103320, "start": 1057.76, "end": 1062.04, "text": " It strips away every irrelevant detail of the past while perfectly preserving the map of tomorrow.", "tokens": [51593, 467, 19842, 1314, 633, 28682, 2607, 295, 264, 1791, 1339, 6239, 33173, 264, 4471, 295, 4153, 13, 51807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12644490702398892, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622656806048909e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 106204, "start": 1062.04, "end": 1070.2, "text": " In theorem 3.1 in the text, mathematically proves that the true continuation quotient is the unique courses quotient with zero loss.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 20904, 805, 13, 16, 294, 264, 2487, 11, 44003, 25019, 300, 264, 2074, 29357, 9641, 1196, 307, 264, 3845, 7712, 9641, 1196, 365, 4018, 4470, 13, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12021296075049867, "compression_ratio": 1.4657534246575343, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622690416316256e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 106204, "start": 1070.68, "end": 1074.72, "text": " Any attempt to compress the system further will result in strictly positive loss.", "tokens": [50797, 2639, 5217, 281, 14778, 264, 1185, 3052, 486, 1874, 294, 20792, 3353, 4470, 13, 50999], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12021296075049867, "compression_ratio": 1.4657534246575343, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622690416316256e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 107472, "start": 1074.72, "end": 1081.24, "text": " So to see that positive loss in action, we return to the traffic light and look at the flawed alternative design.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 281, 536, 300, 3353, 4470, 294, 3069, 11, 321, 2736, 281, 264, 6419, 1442, 293, 574, 412, 264, 38823, 8535, 1715, 13, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1525736302137375, "compression_ratio": 1.5810055865921788, "no_speech_prob": 2.3164246128887234e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 107472, "start": 1082.08, "end": 1085.46, "text": " The exact design cleared the bit upon arrival at the red light.", "tokens": [50733, 440, 1900, 1715, 19725, 264, 857, 3564, 18365, 412, 264, 2182, 1442, 13, 50902], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1525736302137375, "compression_ratio": 1.5810055865921788, "no_speech_prob": 2.3164246128887234e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 107472, "start": 1085.82, "end": 1091.42, "text": " But the flawed rule states, clear the request bit whenever the system is currently sitting at phase zero.", "tokens": [50920, 583, 264, 38823, 4978, 4368, 11, 1850, 264, 5308, 857, 5699, 264, 1185, 307, 4362, 3798, 412, 5574, 4018, 13, 51200], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1525736302137375, "compression_ratio": 1.5810055865921788, "no_speech_prob": 2.3164246128887234e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 109142, "start": 1091.42, "end": 1093.8200000000002, "text": " Superficially, it sounds identical, doesn't it?", "tokens": [50365, 4548, 1786, 2270, 11, 309, 3263, 14800, 11, 1177, 380, 309, 30, 50485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17098193523312402, "compression_ratio": 1.7639484978540771, "no_speech_prob": 2.3074025329306025e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 109142, "start": 1093.94, "end": 1095.6000000000001, "text": " If the light is red, clear the bit.", "tokens": [50491, 759, 264, 1442, 307, 2182, 11, 1850, 264, 857, 13, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17098193523312402, "compression_ratio": 1.7639484978540771, "no_speech_prob": 2.3074025329306025e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 109142, "start": 1096.0, "end": 1098.64, "text": " But the geometry of the futures tells a very different story.", "tokens": [50594, 583, 264, 18426, 295, 264, 26071, 5112, 257, 588, 819, 1657, 13, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17098193523312402, "compression_ratio": 1.7639484978540771, "no_speech_prob": 2.3074025329306025e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 109142, "start": 1098.94, "end": 1101.14, "text": " So imagine the light is already resting at phase zero.", "tokens": [50741, 407, 3811, 264, 1442, 307, 1217, 21221, 412, 5574, 4018, 13, 50851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17098193523312402, "compression_ratio": 1.7639484978540771, "no_speech_prob": 2.3074025329306025e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 109142, "start": 1101.5, "end": 1102.54, "text": " The crosswalk is open.", "tokens": [50869, 440, 3278, 12490, 307, 1269, 13, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17098193523312402, "compression_ratio": 1.7639484978540771, "no_speech_prob": 2.3074025329306025e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 109142, "start": 1102.9, "end": 1104.98, "text": " A pedestrian runs up late and hits the button.", "tokens": [50939, 316, 33947, 6676, 493, 3469, 293, 8664, 264, 2960, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17098193523312402, "compression_ratio": 1.7639484978540771, "no_speech_prob": 2.3074025329306025e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 109142, "start": 1105.38, "end": 1106.46, "text": " The bit flips to one.", "tokens": [51063, 440, 857, 40249, 281, 472, 13, 51117], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17098193523312402, "compression_ratio": 1.7639484978540771, "no_speech_prob": 2.3074025329306025e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 109142, "start": 1106.8200000000002, "end": 1107.7, "text": " That is state A.", "tokens": [51135, 663, 307, 1785, 316, 13, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17098193523312402, "compression_ratio": 1.7639484978540771, "no_speech_prob": 2.3074025329306025e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 109142, "start": 1108.1200000000001, "end": 1111.5, "text": " Now imagine the light is resting at phase zero and no one is there.", "tokens": [51200, 823, 3811, 264, 1442, 307, 21221, 412, 5574, 4018, 293, 572, 472, 307, 456, 13, 51369], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17098193523312402, "compression_ratio": 1.7639484978540771, "no_speech_prob": 2.3074025329306025e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 109142, "start": 1111.7, "end": 1112.78, "text": " The bit is zero.", "tokens": [51379, 440, 857, 307, 4018, 13, 51433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17098193523312402, "compression_ratio": 1.7639484978540771, "no_speech_prob": 2.3074025329306025e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 109142, "start": 1113.1200000000001, "end": 1114.0, "text": " That is state B.", "tokens": [51450, 663, 307, 1785, 363, 13, 51494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17098193523312402, "compression_ratio": 1.7639484978540771, "no_speech_prob": 2.3074025329306025e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 111400, "start": 1114.32, "end": 1118.08, "text": " Under the flawed design, the software evaluates its current state.", "tokens": [50381, 6974, 264, 38823, 1715, 11, 264, 4722, 6133, 1024, 1080, 2190, 1785, 13, 50569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16293937887921428, "compression_ratio": 1.7623762376237624, "no_speech_prob": 1.519314622028256e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 111400, "start": 1118.48, "end": 1119.72, "text": " It sees it is at phase zero.", "tokens": [50589, 467, 8194, 309, 307, 412, 5574, 4018, 13, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16293937887921428, "compression_ratio": 1.7623762376237624, "no_speech_prob": 1.519314622028256e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 111400, "start": 1120.12, "end": 1121.5, "text": " The rule demands it clear the bit.", "tokens": [50671, 440, 4978, 15107, 309, 1850, 264, 857, 13, 50740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16293937887921428, "compression_ratio": 1.7623762376237624, "no_speech_prob": 1.519314622028256e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 111400, "start": 1121.88, "end": 1124.12, "text": " It forcibly changes state A into state B.", "tokens": [50759, 467, 337, 537, 25021, 2962, 1785, 316, 666, 1785, 363, 13, 50871], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16293937887921428, "compression_ratio": 1.7623762376237624, "no_speech_prob": 1.519314622028256e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 111400, "start": 1124.3, "end": 1124.84, "text": " It merges them.", "tokens": [50880, 467, 3551, 2880, 552, 13, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16293937887921428, "compression_ratio": 1.7623762376237624, "no_speech_prob": 1.519314622028256e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 111400, "start": 1125.18, "end": 1128.58, "text": " But those two states absolutely do not share the same one-step future.", "tokens": [50924, 583, 729, 732, 4368, 3122, 360, 406, 2073, 264, 912, 472, 12, 16792, 2027, 13, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16293937887921428, "compression_ratio": 1.7623762376237624, "no_speech_prob": 1.519314622028256e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 111400, "start": 1128.78, "end": 1129.32, "text": " No, they don't.", "tokens": [51104, 883, 11, 436, 500, 380, 13, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16293937887921428, "compression_ratio": 1.7623762376237624, "no_speech_prob": 1.519314622028256e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 111400, "start": 1129.32, "end": 1133.56, "text": " The light is about to transition out of phase zero into the green light for cars.", "tokens": [51131, 440, 1442, 307, 466, 281, 6034, 484, 295, 5574, 4018, 666, 264, 3092, 1442, 337, 5163, 13, 51343], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16293937887921428, "compression_ratio": 1.7623762376237624, "no_speech_prob": 1.519314622028256e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 111400, "start": 1133.88, "end": 1134.38, "text": " Phase one.", "tokens": [51359, 24432, 472, 13, 51384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16293937887921428, "compression_ratio": 1.7623762376237624, "no_speech_prob": 1.519314622028256e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 111400, "start": 1135.08, "end": 1139.44, "text": " If no one pushed the button, you know, state B, the light should just cycle normally.", "tokens": [51419, 759, 572, 472, 9152, 264, 2960, 11, 291, 458, 11, 1785, 363, 11, 264, 1442, 820, 445, 6586, 5646, 13, 51637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16293937887921428, "compression_ratio": 1.7623762376237624, "no_speech_prob": 1.519314622028256e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 111400, "start": 1139.56, "end": 1142.98, "text": " But if someone just ran up and hit the button while the light was red, state A,", "tokens": [51643, 583, 498, 1580, 445, 5872, 493, 293, 2045, 264, 2960, 1339, 264, 1442, 390, 2182, 11, 1785, 316, 11, 51814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16293937887921428, "compression_ratio": 1.7623762376237624, "no_speech_prob": 1.519314622028256e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 114298, "start": 1142.98, "end": 1147.82, "text": " the system must remember that intent so it can prioritize the crosswalk on the next cycle.", "tokens": [50365, 264, 1185, 1633, 1604, 300, 8446, 370, 309, 393, 25164, 264, 3278, 12490, 322, 264, 958, 6586, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305462646484375, "compression_ratio": 1.6524822695035462, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983079660122912e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 114298, "start": 1148.26, "end": 1150.42, "text": " By clearing the bit while sitting at the red light,", "tokens": [50629, 3146, 23937, 264, 857, 1339, 3798, 412, 264, 2182, 1442, 11, 50737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305462646484375, "compression_ratio": 1.6524822695035462, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983079660122912e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 114298, "start": 1151.0, "end": 1154.6, "text": " the system effectively deleted the existence of the late-arriving pedestrian.", "tokens": [50766, 264, 1185, 8659, 22981, 264, 9123, 295, 264, 3469, 12, 289, 470, 798, 33947, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305462646484375, "compression_ratio": 1.6524822695035462, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983079660122912e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 114298, "start": 1155.54, "end": 1159.28, "text": " It merged two states that possess genuinely different continuation spaces.", "tokens": [50993, 467, 3551, 3004, 732, 4368, 300, 17490, 17839, 819, 29357, 7673, 13, 51180], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305462646484375, "compression_ratio": 1.6524822695035462, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983079660122912e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 114298, "start": 1160.06, "end": 1166.1, "text": " A controller looking even one horizon ahead desperately needs to distinguish between those two states.", "tokens": [51219, 316, 10561, 1237, 754, 472, 18046, 2286, 23726, 2203, 281, 20206, 1296, 729, 732, 4368, 13, 51521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305462646484375, "compression_ratio": 1.6524822695035462, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983079660122912e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 114298, "start": 1166.2, "end": 1169.74, "text": " And we can calculate the exact cost of that bad engineering, right?", "tokens": [51526, 400, 321, 393, 8873, 264, 1900, 2063, 295, 300, 1578, 7043, 11, 558, 30, 51703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305462646484375, "compression_ratio": 1.6524822695035462, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983079660122912e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 116974, "start": 1169.74, "end": 1173.18, "text": " We force two distinct continuation spaces into a single state.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 3464, 732, 10644, 29357, 7673, 666, 257, 2167, 1785, 13, 50537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15311447561603703, "compression_ratio": 1.5480769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858799733495244e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 116974, "start": 1173.46, "end": 1176.44, "text": " The formula demands the base two logarithm of two.", "tokens": [50551, 440, 8513, 15107, 264, 3096, 732, 41473, 32674, 295, 732, 13, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15311447561603703, "compression_ratio": 1.5480769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858799733495244e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 116974, "start": 1176.7, "end": 1177.76, "text": " Which is exactly one.", "tokens": [50713, 3013, 307, 2293, 472, 13, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15311447561603703, "compression_ratio": 1.5480769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858799733495244e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 116974, "start": 1178.16, "end": 1182.44, "text": " The mathematics prove that this specific, seemingly minor software design error", "tokens": [50786, 440, 18666, 7081, 300, 341, 2685, 11, 18709, 6696, 4722, 1715, 6713, 51000], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15311447561603703, "compression_ratio": 1.5480769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858799733495244e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 116974, "start": 1182.44, "end": 1185.38, "text": " caused precisely one bit of information loss.", "tokens": [51000, 7008, 13402, 472, 857, 295, 1589, 4470, 13, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15311447561603703, "compression_ratio": 1.5480769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858799733495244e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 116974, "start": 1185.8, "end": 1188.88, "text": " It's a beautifully rigorous way to measure systemic badness.", "tokens": [51168, 467, 311, 257, 16525, 29882, 636, 281, 3481, 23789, 1578, 1287, 13, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15311447561603703, "compression_ratio": 1.5480769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858799733495244e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 118888, "start": 1188.88, "end": 1195.8200000000002, "text": " And the draft takes this a step further by introducing eventual periodicity and the concept of the deadline.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 11206, 2516, 341, 257, 1823, 3052, 538, 15424, 33160, 27790, 507, 293, 264, 3410, 295, 264, 20615, 13, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14710920507257635, "compression_ratio": 1.6057692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735352474136044e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 118888, "start": 1196.24, "end": 1200.1000000000001, "text": " Because the request bit in that traffic system isn't universally redundant,", "tokens": [50733, 1436, 264, 5308, 857, 294, 300, 6419, 1185, 1943, 380, 43995, 40997, 11, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14710920507257635, "compression_ratio": 1.6057692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735352474136044e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 118888, "start": 1200.5200000000002, "end": 1202.38, "text": " but it isn't universally essential either.", "tokens": [50947, 457, 309, 1943, 380, 43995, 7115, 2139, 13, 51040], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14710920507257635, "compression_ratio": 1.6057692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735352474136044e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 118888, "start": 1202.8200000000002, "end": 1205.24, "text": " It operates on a strict expiration schedule.", "tokens": [51062, 467, 22577, 322, 257, 10910, 39657, 7567, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14710920507257635, "compression_ratio": 1.6057692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735352474136044e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 118888, "start": 1205.6000000000001, "end": 1205.8000000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51201, 1779, 13, 51211], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14710920507257635, "compression_ratio": 1.6057692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735352474136044e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 118888, "start": 1205.98, "end": 1208.8000000000002, "text": " The traffic light operates on a rigid four-step cycle.", "tokens": [51220, 440, 6419, 1442, 22577, 322, 257, 22195, 1451, 12, 16792, 6586, 13, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14710920507257635, "compression_ratio": 1.6057692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735352474136044e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 120880, "start": 1208.8, "end": 1223.7, "text": " So, if the light is currently at phase one, the green light,", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 498, 264, 1442, 307, 4362, 412, 5574, 472, 11, 264, 3092, 1442, 11, 51110], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11835971332731701, "compression_ratio": 1.7563451776649746, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404782926024206e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 120880, "start": 1223.86, "end": 1227.52, "text": " the system inherently knows that in exactly three steps it will hit phase zero.", "tokens": [51118, 264, 1185, 27993, 3255, 300, 294, 2293, 1045, 4439, 309, 486, 2045, 5574, 4018, 13, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11835971332731701, "compression_ratio": 1.7563451776649746, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404782926024206e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 120880, "start": 1227.72, "end": 1229.86, "text": " And at phase zero, the bit will be cleared unconditionally.", "tokens": [51311, 400, 412, 5574, 4018, 11, 264, 857, 486, 312, 19725, 34959, 15899, 13, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11835971332731701, "compression_ratio": 1.7563451776649746, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404782926024206e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 120880, "start": 1230.5, "end": 1234.6399999999999, "text": " Therefore, the question of whether the bit is currently holding a one or zero at phase one", "tokens": [51450, 7504, 11, 264, 1168, 295, 1968, 264, 857, 307, 4362, 5061, 257, 472, 420, 4018, 412, 5574, 472, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11835971332731701, "compression_ratio": 1.7563451776649746, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404782926024206e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 120880, "start": 1234.6399999999999, "end": 1237.4199999999998, "text": " will categorically not matter three horizons from now.", "tokens": [51657, 486, 19250, 984, 406, 1871, 1045, 7937, 892, 490, 586, 13, 51796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11835971332731701, "compression_ratio": 1.7563451776649746, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404782926024206e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 123742, "start": 1237.42, "end": 1241.48, "text": " The system's own structural periodicity answers the question on a delay.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1185, 311, 1065, 15067, 27790, 507, 6338, 264, 1168, 322, 257, 8577, 13, 50568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12574041539972478, "compression_ratio": 1.6589403973509933, "no_speech_prob": 1.920635742461152e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 123742, "start": 1242.14, "end": 1243.6200000000001, "text": " The memory naturally expires.", "tokens": [50601, 440, 4675, 8195, 1278, 3145, 13, 50675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12574041539972478, "compression_ratio": 1.6589403973509933, "no_speech_prob": 1.920635742461152e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 123742, "start": 1244.04, "end": 1248.44, "text": " And the exact design of the traffic light clears the bit at the absolute earliest possible moment", "tokens": [50696, 400, 264, 1900, 1715, 295, 264, 6419, 1442, 47033, 264, 857, 412, 264, 8236, 20573, 1944, 1623, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12574041539972478, "compression_ratio": 1.6589403973509933, "no_speech_prob": 1.920635742461152e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 123742, "start": 1248.44, "end": 1253.02, "text": " after it stops mattering, which simultaneously happens to be the latest possible moment", "tokens": [50916, 934, 309, 10094, 1871, 278, 11, 597, 16561, 2314, 281, 312, 264, 6792, 1944, 1623, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12574041539972478, "compression_ratio": 1.6589403973509933, "no_speech_prob": 1.920635742461152e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 123742, "start": 1253.02, "end": 1256.2, "text": " where failing to clear it would result in an observable failure.", "tokens": [51145, 689, 18223, 281, 1850, 309, 576, 1874, 294, 364, 9951, 712, 7763, 13, 51304], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12574041539972478, "compression_ratio": 1.6589403973509933, "no_speech_prob": 1.920635742461152e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 123742, "start": 1256.4, "end": 1258.6000000000001, "text": " It perfectly rides the boundary of necessity.", "tokens": [51314, 467, 6239, 20773, 264, 12866, 295, 24217, 13, 51424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12574041539972478, "compression_ratio": 1.6589403973509933, "no_speech_prob": 1.920635742461152e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 123742, "start": 1258.96, "end": 1262.96, "text": " Translating this deadline concept to cognitive load is fascinating.", "tokens": [51442, 6531, 75, 990, 341, 20615, 3410, 281, 15605, 3677, 307, 10343, 13, 51642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12574041539972478, "compression_ratio": 1.6589403973509933, "no_speech_prob": 1.920635742461152e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 123742, "start": 1263.5, "end": 1265.68, "text": " We all carry mental request bits.", "tokens": [51669, 492, 439, 3985, 4973, 5308, 9239, 13, 51778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12574041539972478, "compression_ratio": 1.6589403973509933, "no_speech_prob": 1.920635742461152e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 126568, "start": 1265.68, "end": 1266.92, "text": " We track details.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 2837, 4365, 13, 50427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13064947668111548, "compression_ratio": 1.6482758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 2.7936956133872703e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 126568, "start": 1267.1000000000001, "end": 1270.3400000000001, "text": " We agonize over past decisions and maintain distinctions in our memory.", "tokens": [50436, 492, 623, 266, 1125, 670, 1791, 5327, 293, 6909, 1483, 49798, 294, 527, 4675, 13, 50598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13064947668111548, "compression_ratio": 1.6482758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 2.7936956133872703e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 126568, "start": 1270.8200000000002, "end": 1275.9, "text": " We spend massive amounts of cognitive energy differentiating between choice A and choice B.", "tokens": [50622, 492, 3496, 5994, 11663, 295, 15605, 2281, 27372, 990, 1296, 3922, 316, 293, 3922, 363, 13, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13064947668111548, "compression_ratio": 1.6482758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 2.7936956133872703e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 126568, "start": 1276.02, "end": 1276.8, "text": " Oh, constantly.", "tokens": [50882, 876, 11, 6460, 13, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13064947668111548, "compression_ratio": 1.6482758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 2.7936956133872703e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 126568, "start": 1277.04, "end": 1281.18, "text": " But if the larger system we are operating with in our workplace dynamics, our family routines,", "tokens": [50933, 583, 498, 264, 4833, 1185, 321, 366, 7447, 365, 294, 527, 15328, 15679, 11, 527, 1605, 33827, 11, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13064947668111548, "compression_ratio": 1.6482758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 2.7936956133872703e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 126568, "start": 1281.8200000000002, "end": 1286.78, "text": " the macroeconomic cycle is structurally guaranteed to resolve that distinction anyway in a few horizons.", "tokens": [51172, 264, 18887, 68, 31646, 6586, 307, 6594, 6512, 18031, 281, 14151, 300, 16844, 4033, 294, 257, 1326, 7937, 892, 13, 51420], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13064947668111548, "compression_ratio": 1.6482758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 2.7936956133872703e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 126568, "start": 1287.02, "end": 1290.96, "text": " We are actively maintaining memory that has already lost its continuation value.", "tokens": [51432, 492, 366, 13022, 14916, 4675, 300, 575, 1217, 2731, 1080, 29357, 2158, 13, 51629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13064947668111548, "compression_ratio": 1.6482758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 2.7936956133872703e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 129096, "start": 1290.96, "end": 1299.52, "text": " We endure a high cognitive carrying cost to preserve distinctions that the underlying mathematics of our lives have already scheduled for deletion.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 24732, 257, 1090, 15605, 9792, 2063, 281, 15665, 1483, 49798, 300, 264, 14217, 18666, 295, 527, 2909, 362, 1217, 15678, 337, 1103, 302, 313, 13, 50793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10991723362992449, "compression_ratio": 1.5895196506550218, "no_speech_prob": 3.2159741449738766e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 129096, "start": 1300.18, "end": 1305.98, "text": " The universe has already merged the rivers, but we are still rowing against the current, insisting the water is different.", "tokens": [50826, 440, 6445, 575, 1217, 36427, 264, 18361, 11, 457, 321, 366, 920, 5386, 278, 1970, 264, 2190, 11, 13466, 278, 264, 1281, 307, 819, 13, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10991723362992449, "compression_ratio": 1.5895196506550218, "no_speech_prob": 3.2159741449738766e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 129096, "start": 1306.18, "end": 1309.6200000000001, "text": " We are voluntarily paying that one-bit loss of mental energy.", "tokens": [51126, 492, 366, 41782, 6229, 300, 472, 12, 5260, 4470, 295, 4973, 2281, 13, 51298], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10991723362992449, "compression_ratio": 1.5895196506550218, "no_speech_prob": 3.2159741449738766e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 129096, "start": 1309.94, "end": 1311.54, "text": " It's an exhausting way to live.", "tokens": [51314, 467, 311, 364, 34076, 636, 281, 1621, 13, 51394], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10991723362992449, "compression_ratio": 1.5895196506550218, "no_speech_prob": 3.2159741449738766e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 131154, "start": 1311.54, "end": 1318.72, "text": " Which brings us to what I consider the absolute masterstroke of this draft, phase four, the grand unification.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 437, 286, 1949, 264, 8236, 4505, 42706, 295, 341, 11206, 11, 5574, 1451, 11, 264, 2697, 517, 3774, 13, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11288960774739583, "compression_ratio": 1.4861111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.7208229199233704e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 131154, "start": 1319.34, "end": 1324.32, "text": " Because up to this point, reading Fliction's work induced a bit of conceptual whiplash.", "tokens": [50755, 1436, 493, 281, 341, 935, 11, 3760, 3235, 4105, 311, 589, 33991, 257, 857, 295, 24106, 315, 34442, 1299, 13, 51004], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11288960774739583, "compression_ratio": 1.4861111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.7208229199233704e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 131154, "start": 1324.46, "end": 1329.6399999999999, "text": " Yeah, the transition from the first chapter to the second and third represents a massive shift in mathematical philosophy.", "tokens": [51011, 865, 11, 264, 6034, 490, 264, 700, 7187, 281, 264, 1150, 293, 2636, 8855, 257, 5994, 5513, 294, 18894, 10675, 13, 51270], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11288960774739583, "compression_ratio": 1.4861111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.7208229199233704e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 132964, "start": 1329.64, "end": 1332.6000000000001, "text": " Chapter one was entirely about the verbs of creation.", "tokens": [50365, 18874, 472, 390, 7696, 466, 264, 30051, 295, 8016, 13, 50513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253434075249566, "compression_ratio": 1.6589147286821706, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281887726428025e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 132964, "start": 1332.96, "end": 1342.3600000000001, "text": " It was about operators generating detail, pulling shakes into self-similar fractal attractors, taking a blank space, and growing a highly complex future.", "tokens": [50531, 467, 390, 466, 19077, 17746, 2607, 11, 8407, 37891, 666, 2698, 12, 30937, 2202, 17948, 304, 5049, 830, 11, 1940, 257, 8247, 1901, 11, 293, 4194, 257, 5405, 3997, 2027, 13, 51001], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253434075249566, "compression_ratio": 1.6589147286821706, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281887726428025e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 132964, "start": 1342.76, "end": 1346.0400000000002, "text": " And then chapters two and three were about the mathematics of destruction.", "tokens": [51021, 400, 550, 20013, 732, 293, 1045, 645, 466, 264, 18666, 295, 13563, 13, 51185], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253434075249566, "compression_ratio": 1.6589147286821706, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281887726428025e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 132964, "start": 1346.76, "end": 1355.76, "text": " They were about quotients, collapsing distinctions, forcing histories to merge, and calculating exactly how much information dies in the process.", "tokens": [51221, 814, 645, 466, 9641, 2448, 11, 45339, 1483, 49798, 11, 19030, 30631, 281, 22183, 11, 293, 28258, 2293, 577, 709, 1589, 2714, 294, 264, 1399, 13, 51671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253434075249566, "compression_ratio": 1.6589147286821706, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281887726428025e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 135576, "start": 1355.76, "end": 1360.0, "text": " It felt like trying to reconcile general relativity with quantum mechanics.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 2762, 411, 1382, 281, 41059, 2674, 45675, 365, 13018, 12939, 13, 50577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1372104230916725, "compression_ratio": 1.652027027027027, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014865436049907e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 135576, "start": 1360.3799999999999, "end": 1362.72, "text": " One builds the cosmos, the other breaks it down.", "tokens": [50596, 1485, 15182, 264, 41794, 11, 264, 661, 9857, 309, 760, 13, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1372104230916725, "compression_ratio": 1.652027027027027, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014865436049907e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 135576, "start": 1363.02, "end": 1364.6, "text": " It's a huge contradiction.", "tokens": [50728, 467, 311, 257, 2603, 34937, 13, 50807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1372104230916725, "compression_ratio": 1.652027027027027, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014865436049907e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 135576, "start": 1365.18, "end": 1373.42, "text": " How do you house a theory of infinite detail generation and a theory of merciless information compression under the exact same geometric roof?", "tokens": [50836, 1012, 360, 291, 1782, 257, 5261, 295, 13785, 2607, 5125, 293, 257, 5261, 295, 10811, 388, 442, 1589, 19355, 833, 264, 1900, 912, 33246, 8418, 30, 51248], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1372104230916725, "compression_ratio": 1.652027027027027, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014865436049907e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 135576, "start": 1373.74, "end": 1376.8, "text": " Well, Fliction solves this by revealing they are not opposites.", "tokens": [51264, 1042, 11, 3235, 4105, 39890, 341, 538, 23983, 436, 366, 406, 4665, 3324, 13, 51417], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1372104230916725, "compression_ratio": 1.652027027027027, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014865436049907e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 135576, "start": 1376.94, "end": 1381.5, "text": " They are the exact same mathematical object behaving differently based on a single parameter.", "tokens": [51424, 814, 366, 264, 1900, 912, 18894, 2657, 35263, 7614, 2361, 322, 257, 2167, 13075, 13, 51652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1372104230916725, "compression_ratio": 1.652027027027027, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014865436049907e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 135576, "start": 1382.3799999999999, "end": 1384.26, "text": " They are all continuation operators.", "tokens": [51696, 814, 366, 439, 29357, 19077, 13, 51790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1372104230916725, "compression_ratio": 1.652027027027027, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014865436049907e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 138426, "start": 1384.26, "end": 1387.76, "text": " Technically, they are Lipschitz maps acting on metric spaces.", "tokens": [50365, 42494, 11, 436, 366, 441, 2600, 339, 6862, 11317, 6577, 322, 20678, 7673, 13, 50540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07594382135491622, "compression_ratio": 1.7208480565371025, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614357680091007e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 138426, "start": 1388.3, "end": 1395.7, "text": " If we return to our magical map shrinking machine from the first chapter, the Lipschitz map is the formal mathematical generalization of that machine.", "tokens": [50567, 759, 321, 2736, 281, 527, 12066, 4471, 41684, 3479, 490, 264, 700, 7187, 11, 264, 441, 2600, 339, 6862, 4471, 307, 264, 9860, 18894, 2674, 2144, 295, 300, 3479, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07594382135491622, "compression_ratio": 1.7208480565371025, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614357680091007e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 138426, "start": 1395.92, "end": 1402.72, "text": " It's like a rule that transforms a space, but it comes with a built-in slider, a number called the Lipschitz constant, denoted by the letter L.", "tokens": [50948, 467, 311, 411, 257, 4978, 300, 35592, 257, 1901, 11, 457, 309, 1487, 365, 257, 3094, 12, 259, 26046, 11, 257, 1230, 1219, 264, 441, 2600, 339, 6862, 5754, 11, 1441, 23325, 538, 264, 5063, 441, 13, 51288], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07594382135491622, "compression_ratio": 1.7208480565371025, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614357680091007e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 138426, "start": 1403.28, "end": 1410.02, "text": " This constant dictates the maximum amount the operator is allowed to stretch or shrink the distances between points in that space.", "tokens": [51316, 639, 5754, 12569, 1024, 264, 6674, 2372, 264, 12973, 307, 4350, 281, 5985, 420, 23060, 264, 22182, 1296, 2793, 294, 300, 1901, 13, 51653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07594382135491622, "compression_ratio": 1.7208480565371025, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614357680091007e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 141002, "start": 1410.02, "end": 1416.72, "text": " And if you adjust the slider so that L is strictly less than 1, the machine acts as a contraction.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 498, 291, 4369, 264, 26046, 370, 300, 441, 307, 20792, 1570, 813, 502, 11, 264, 3479, 10672, 382, 257, 37372, 13, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13913879187210745, "compression_ratio": 1.6271929824561404, "no_speech_prob": 1.7148973213698682e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 141002, "start": 1417.46, "end": 1419.36, "text": " It relentlessly shrinks distances.", "tokens": [50737, 467, 34045, 12048, 9884, 16431, 22182, 13, 50832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13913879187210745, "compression_ratio": 1.6271929824561404, "no_speech_prob": 1.7148973213698682e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 141002, "start": 1419.94, "end": 1421.48, "text": " And that is the entirety of chapter 1.", "tokens": [50861, 400, 300, 307, 264, 31557, 295, 7187, 502, 13, 50938], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13913879187210745, "compression_ratio": 1.6271929824561404, "no_speech_prob": 1.7148973213698682e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 141002, "start": 1421.98, "end": 1431.52, "text": " When L is less than 1, the operator pulls everything together, relentlessly compressing the space until it generates that unique, infinitely detailed, self-similar fractal.", "tokens": [50963, 1133, 441, 307, 1570, 813, 502, 11, 264, 12973, 16982, 1203, 1214, 11, 34045, 12048, 14778, 278, 264, 1901, 1826, 309, 23815, 300, 3845, 11, 36227, 9942, 11, 2698, 12, 30937, 2202, 17948, 304, 13, 51440], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13913879187210745, "compression_ratio": 1.6271929824561404, "no_speech_prob": 1.7148973213698682e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 141002, "start": 1431.96, "end": 1433.32, "text": " It builds the cantor set.", "tokens": [51462, 467, 15182, 264, 11223, 284, 992, 13, 51530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13913879187210745, "compression_ratio": 1.6271929824561404, "no_speech_prob": 1.7148973213698682e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 143332, "start": 1433.32, "end": 1436.56, "text": " But the unification occurs when you slide L upwards.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 517, 3774, 11843, 562, 291, 4137, 441, 22167, 13, 50527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1367195068843781, "compression_ratio": 1.4456521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918370137660287e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 143332, "start": 1437.04, "end": 1441.08, "text": " What happens when the Lipschitz constant is exactly 1 or greater than 1?", "tokens": [50551, 708, 2314, 562, 264, 441, 2600, 339, 6862, 5754, 307, 2293, 502, 420, 5044, 813, 502, 30, 50753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1367195068843781, "compression_ratio": 1.4456521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918370137660287e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 143332, "start": 1441.28, "end": 1443.1399999999999, "text": " The operator stops shrinking things.", "tokens": [50763, 440, 12973, 10094, 41684, 721, 13, 50856], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1367195068843781, "compression_ratio": 1.4456521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918370137660287e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 143332, "start": 1443.28, "end": 1448.1, "text": " It might shuffle them around or preserve the distances or even stretch them, but the contraction stops.", "tokens": [50863, 467, 1062, 39426, 552, 926, 420, 15665, 264, 22182, 420, 754, 5985, 552, 11, 457, 264, 37372, 10094, 13, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1367195068843781, "compression_ratio": 1.4456521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918370137660287e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 144810, "start": 1448.1, "end": 1460.6, "text": " The draft proves that the operator we utilized in chapters 2 and 3, the operator that simply ticks the clock forward, advancing a state by one horizon to calculate its reachable future, is fundamentally a continuation operator.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 11206, 25019, 300, 264, 12973, 321, 28158, 294, 20013, 568, 293, 805, 11, 264, 12973, 300, 2935, 42475, 264, 7830, 2128, 11, 27267, 257, 1785, 538, 472, 18046, 281, 8873, 1080, 2524, 712, 2027, 11, 307, 17879, 257, 29357, 12973, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07597739579247646, "compression_ratio": 1.4635416666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552077854696922e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 144810, "start": 1461.06, "end": 1463.74, "text": " But its Lipschitz constant is typically 1 or greater.", "tokens": [51013, 583, 1080, 441, 2600, 339, 6862, 5754, 307, 5850, 502, 420, 5044, 13, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07597739579247646, "compression_ratio": 1.4635416666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552077854696922e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 146374, "start": 1463.74, "end": 1466.46, "text": " Because it isn't contracting to a single shape.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 309, 1943, 380, 36095, 281, 257, 2167, 3909, 13, 50501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10392982226151687, "compression_ratio": 1.643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 2.2894373029325177e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 146374, "start": 1466.84, "end": 1479.86, "text": " In a finite system like our four-phase traffic light, advancing the clock steps the state forward, inevitably reduces distinctions as things hit the confluence, merges the histories into quotients, and ultimately settles into a repeating periodic cycle.", "tokens": [50520, 682, 257, 19362, 1185, 411, 527, 1451, 12, 43331, 6419, 1442, 11, 27267, 264, 7830, 4439, 264, 1785, 2128, 11, 28171, 18081, 1483, 49798, 382, 721, 2045, 264, 1497, 40432, 11, 3551, 2880, 264, 30631, 666, 9641, 2448, 11, 293, 6284, 5584, 904, 666, 257, 18617, 27790, 6586, 13, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10392982226151687, "compression_ratio": 1.643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 2.2894373029325177e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 146374, "start": 1480.2, "end": 1482.92, "text": " The unification is breathtaking in its elegance.", "tokens": [51188, 440, 517, 3774, 307, 48393, 294, 1080, 14459, 719, 13, 51324], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10392982226151687, "compression_ratio": 1.643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 2.2894373029325177e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 146374, "start": 1483.7, "end": 1487.08, "text": " Generation and collapse are not warring theories of reality.", "tokens": [51363, 23898, 293, 15584, 366, 406, 1516, 2937, 13667, 295, 4103, 13, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10392982226151687, "compression_ratio": 1.643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 2.2894373029325177e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 146374, "start": 1487.6, "end": 1490.8, "text": " They are merely different regions of the exact same parameter space.", "tokens": [51558, 814, 366, 17003, 819, 10682, 295, 264, 1900, 912, 13075, 1901, 13, 51718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10392982226151687, "compression_ratio": 1.643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 2.2894373029325177e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 149080, "start": 1490.8, "end": 1499.3, "text": " The mathematics governing the creation of an infinite future, and the mathematics dictating the forgetting of an irrelevant past, are siblings.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 18666, 30054, 264, 8016, 295, 364, 13785, 2027, 11, 293, 264, 18666, 12569, 990, 264, 25428, 295, 364, 28682, 1791, 11, 366, 20571, 13, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14609740762149587, "compression_ratio": 1.7868217054263567, "no_speech_prob": 1.997089776537009e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 149080, "start": 1500.1, "end": 1502.78, "text": " It is a profound unification of mathematical verbs.", "tokens": [50830, 467, 307, 257, 14382, 517, 3774, 295, 18894, 30051, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14609740762149587, "compression_ratio": 1.7868217054263567, "no_speech_prob": 1.997089776537009e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 149080, "start": 1502.96, "end": 1505.72, "text": " I love how you phrase that, a unification of verbs.", "tokens": [50973, 286, 959, 577, 291, 9535, 300, 11, 257, 517, 3774, 295, 30051, 13, 51111], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14609740762149587, "compression_ratio": 1.7868217054263567, "no_speech_prob": 1.997089776537009e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 149080, "start": 1506.1, "end": 1512.6599999999999, "text": " The text actually points out that the earlier discussions about quotients, fibers, and house-earth distances were focused on nouns.", "tokens": [51130, 440, 2487, 767, 2793, 484, 300, 264, 3071, 11088, 466, 9641, 2448, 11, 25252, 11, 293, 1782, 12, 14881, 392, 22182, 645, 5178, 322, 48184, 13, 51458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14609740762149587, "compression_ratio": 1.7868217054263567, "no_speech_prob": 1.997089776537009e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 149080, "start": 1512.84, "end": 1514.18, "text": " They were the objects and measurements.", "tokens": [51467, 814, 645, 264, 6565, 293, 15383, 13, 51534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14609740762149587, "compression_ratio": 1.7868217054263567, "no_speech_prob": 1.997089776537009e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 149080, "start": 1514.8, "end": 1516.76, "text": " The continuation operators are the verbs.", "tokens": [51565, 440, 29357, 19077, 366, 264, 30051, 13, 51663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14609740762149587, "compression_ratio": 1.7868217054263567, "no_speech_prob": 1.997089776537009e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 151676, "start": 1516.76, "end": 1522.18, "text": " They do the actual work of moving reality forward, and it turns out there is only one verb.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 360, 264, 3539, 589, 295, 2684, 4103, 2128, 11, 293, 309, 4523, 484, 456, 307, 787, 472, 9595, 13, 50636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10142875503707718, "compression_ratio": 1.6346863468634687, "no_speech_prob": 1.728185953717154e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 151676, "start": 1522.7, "end": 1527.64, "text": " And to ensure this singular verb behaves properly when applied to complex, merging histories,", "tokens": [50662, 400, 281, 5586, 341, 20010, 9595, 36896, 6108, 562, 6456, 281, 3997, 11, 44559, 30631, 11, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10142875503707718, "compression_ratio": 1.6346863468634687, "no_speech_prob": 1.728185953717154e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 151676, "start": 1528.26, "end": 1532.22, "text": " Fliction introduces a vital mathematical safeguard called gamma compatibility.", "tokens": [50940, 3235, 4105, 31472, 257, 11707, 18894, 40153, 1219, 15546, 34237, 13, 51138], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10142875503707718, "compression_ratio": 1.6346863468634687, "no_speech_prob": 1.728185953717154e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 151676, "start": 1532.72, "end": 1538.76, "text": " When I first read about gamma compatibility, the notation was intimidating, but the concept is really just about keeping the math honest.", "tokens": [51163, 1133, 286, 700, 1401, 466, 15546, 34237, 11, 264, 24657, 390, 29714, 11, 457, 264, 3410, 307, 534, 445, 466, 5145, 264, 5221, 3245, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10142875503707718, "compression_ratio": 1.6346863468634687, "no_speech_prob": 1.728185953717154e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 151676, "start": 1539.14, "end": 1540.78, "text": " It prevents the operators from cheating.", "tokens": [51484, 467, 22367, 264, 19077, 490, 18309, 13, 51566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10142875503707718, "compression_ratio": 1.6346863468634687, "no_speech_prob": 1.728185953717154e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 154078, "start": 1540.78, "end": 1541.42, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1367248141247293, "compression_ratio": 1.6194331983805668, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047158377778374e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 154078, "start": 1541.94, "end": 1550.18, "text": " If you have an operator, a rule that takes action on a system's history, it must respect the equivalence classes established by the continuation quotient.", "tokens": [50423, 759, 291, 362, 364, 12973, 11, 257, 4978, 300, 2516, 3069, 322, 257, 1185, 311, 2503, 11, 309, 1633, 3104, 264, 9052, 655, 5359, 7545, 538, 264, 29357, 9641, 1196, 13, 50835], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1367248141247293, "compression_ratio": 1.6194331983805668, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047158377778374e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 154078, "start": 1550.44, "end": 1556.58, "text": " To put that in the context of our river analogy, if the two rivers have perfectly merged and a boat is floating downstream,", "tokens": [50848, 1407, 829, 300, 294, 264, 4319, 295, 527, 6810, 21663, 11, 498, 264, 732, 18361, 362, 6239, 36427, 293, 257, 6582, 307, 12607, 30621, 11, 51155], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1367248141247293, "compression_ratio": 1.6194331983805668, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047158377778374e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 154078, "start": 1556.98, "end": 1562.52, "text": " a gamma-compatible operator is a rule that governs the boat without secretly checking where the water came from.", "tokens": [51175, 257, 15546, 12, 1112, 11584, 964, 12973, 307, 257, 4978, 300, 1980, 82, 264, 6582, 1553, 22611, 8568, 689, 264, 1281, 1361, 490, 13, 51452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1367248141247293, "compression_ratio": 1.6194331983805668, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047158377778374e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 156252, "start": 1562.52, "end": 1570.3, "text": " Any action taken on a history cannot depend on information that the continuation quotient has already legally declared dead.", "tokens": [50365, 2639, 3069, 2726, 322, 257, 2503, 2644, 5672, 322, 1589, 300, 264, 29357, 9641, 1196, 575, 1217, 21106, 15489, 3116, 13, 50754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16245534203269266, "compression_ratio": 1.5569620253164558, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551335818738467e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 156252, "start": 1570.56, "end": 1570.78, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50767, 1779, 13, 50778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16245534203269266, "compression_ratio": 1.5569620253164558, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551335818738467e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 156252, "start": 1571.26, "end": 1573.5, "text": " Consider a rule that violates gamma compatibility.", "tokens": [50802, 17416, 257, 4978, 300, 3448, 1024, 15546, 34237, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16245534203269266, "compression_ratio": 1.5569620253164558, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551335818738467e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 156252, "start": 1574.44, "end": 1576.62, "text": " Imagine a time-traveling riverboat operator.", "tokens": [50961, 11739, 257, 565, 12, 17227, 779, 278, 6810, 31883, 12973, 13, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16245534203269266, "compression_ratio": 1.5569620253164558, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551335818738467e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 156252, "start": 1577.24, "end": 1577.92, "text": " The rule says,", "tokens": [51101, 440, 4978, 1619, 11, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16245534203269266, "compression_ratio": 1.5569620253164558, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551335818738467e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 156252, "start": 1578.46, "end": 1585.36, "text": " If the boat is at the confluence, turn left, but only if the water beneath the hull originally came from the northern glacier.", "tokens": [51162, 759, 264, 6582, 307, 412, 264, 1497, 40432, 11, 1261, 1411, 11, 457, 787, 498, 264, 1281, 17149, 264, 32335, 7993, 1361, 490, 264, 14197, 48021, 13, 51507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16245534203269266, "compression_ratio": 1.5569620253164558, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551335818738467e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 158536, "start": 1585.36, "end": 1592.78, "text": " It's sneaking into the mathematical trash can, pulling out the past history that we explicitly proved had no bearing on the future,", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 48525, 666, 264, 18894, 11321, 393, 11, 8407, 484, 264, 1791, 2503, 300, 321, 20803, 14617, 632, 572, 17350, 322, 264, 2027, 11, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1536305224309202, "compression_ratio": 1.7266881028938907, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612960143490673e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 158536, "start": 1593.1399999999999, "end": 1595.3999999999999, "text": " and using it to alter the trajectory of the boat.", "tokens": [50754, 293, 1228, 309, 281, 11337, 264, 21512, 295, 264, 6582, 13, 50867], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1536305224309202, "compression_ratio": 1.7266881028938907, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612960143490673e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 158536, "start": 1595.62, "end": 1596.9799999999998, "text": " It breaks the equivalence.", "tokens": [50878, 467, 9857, 264, 9052, 655, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1536305224309202, "compression_ratio": 1.7266881028938907, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612960143490673e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 158536, "start": 1597.4199999999998, "end": 1601.7199999999998, "text": " Gamma compatibility is the rigorous algebraic firewall that forbids that behavior.", "tokens": [50968, 24723, 1696, 34237, 307, 264, 29882, 21989, 299, 36109, 300, 16603, 3742, 300, 5223, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1536305224309202, "compression_ratio": 1.7266881028938907, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612960143490673e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 158536, "start": 1601.9199999999998, "end": 1602.1599999999999, "text": " Oh.", "tokens": [51193, 876, 13, 51205], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1536305224309202, "compression_ratio": 1.7266881028938907, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612960143490673e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 158536, "start": 1602.36, "end": 1607.9799999999998, "text": " It mathematically guarantees that if two histories have equivalent futures, the operator is blind to their differences.", "tokens": [51215, 467, 44003, 32567, 300, 498, 732, 30631, 362, 10344, 26071, 11, 264, 12973, 307, 6865, 281, 641, 7300, 13, 51496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1536305224309202, "compression_ratio": 1.7266881028938907, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612960143490673e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 158536, "start": 1608.6599999999999, "end": 1610.3999999999999, "text": " It ensures the verb respects the noun.", "tokens": [51530, 467, 28111, 264, 9595, 24126, 264, 23307, 13, 51617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1536305224309202, "compression_ratio": 1.7266881028938907, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612960143490673e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 158536, "start": 1610.6, "end": 1615.2199999999998, "text": " Armed with this unified, gamma-compatible machinery, we arrive at the fifth phase.", "tokens": [51627, 42024, 365, 341, 26787, 11, 15546, 12, 1112, 11584, 964, 27302, 11, 321, 8881, 412, 264, 9266, 5574, 13, 51858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1536305224309202, "compression_ratio": 1.7266881028938907, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612960143490673e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 161536, "start": 1615.6, "end": 1616.6799999999998, "text": " The unsolved mystery.", "tokens": [50377, 440, 2693, 29110, 11422, 13, 50431], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2389050693046756, "compression_ratio": 1.6099585062240664, "no_speech_prob": 2.2100155906701335e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 161536, "start": 1617.3999999999999, "end": 1622.34, "text": " Because Fliction builds this incredible mathematical engine, proves its internal consistency,", "tokens": [50467, 1436, 3235, 4105, 15182, 341, 4651, 18894, 2848, 11, 25019, 1080, 6920, 14416, 11, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2389050693046756, "compression_ratio": 1.6099585062240664, "no_speech_prob": 2.2100155906701335e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 161536, "start": 1622.78, "end": 1625.9399999999998, "text": " and then points it directly at a staggering unsolved question.", "tokens": [50736, 293, 550, 2793, 309, 3838, 412, 257, 42974, 2693, 29110, 1168, 13, 50894], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2389050693046756, "compression_ratio": 1.6099585062240664, "no_speech_prob": 2.2100155906701335e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 161536, "start": 1626.36, "end": 1629.1, "text": " They title this section Toward Universal Generation.", "tokens": [50915, 814, 4876, 341, 3541, 33814, 515, 22617, 23898, 13, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2389050693046756, "compression_ratio": 1.6099585062240664, "no_speech_prob": 2.2100155906701335e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 161536, "start": 1629.6399999999999, "end": 1634.9599999999998, "text": " This is the moment the draft transitions from establishing a foundation to gazing at the horizon of the field.", "tokens": [51079, 639, 307, 264, 1623, 264, 11206, 23767, 490, 22494, 257, 7030, 281, 290, 2118, 412, 264, 18046, 295, 264, 2519, 13, 51345], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2389050693046756, "compression_ratio": 1.6099585062240664, "no_speech_prob": 2.2100155906701335e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 161536, "start": 1635.56, "end": 1637.62, "text": " The central question is profoundly ambitious.", "tokens": [51375, 440, 5777, 1168, 307, 39954, 20239, 13, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2389050693046756, "compression_ratio": 1.6099585062240664, "no_speech_prob": 2.2100155906701335e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 163762, "start": 1637.62, "end": 1645.3, "text": " Can a small, fixed, finite set of these continuation operators generate any possible future geometry?", "tokens": [50365, 1664, 257, 1359, 11, 6806, 11, 19362, 992, 295, 613, 29357, 19077, 8460, 604, 1944, 2027, 18426, 30, 50749], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18785199483235676, "compression_ratio": 1.5497630331753554, "no_speech_prob": 1.655503750579157e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 163762, "start": 1645.3, "end": 1650.3799999999999, "text": " To grasp the magnitude of that question, consider how generative systems work in our daily lives.", "tokens": [50749, 1407, 21743, 264, 15668, 295, 300, 1168, 11, 1949, 577, 1337, 1166, 3652, 589, 294, 527, 5212, 2909, 13, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18785199483235676, "compression_ratio": 1.5497630331753554, "no_speech_prob": 1.655503750579157e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 163762, "start": 1650.76, "end": 1651.84, "text": " Take the English dictionary.", "tokens": [51022, 3664, 264, 3669, 25890, 13, 51076], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18785199483235676, "compression_ratio": 1.5497630331753554, "no_speech_prob": 1.655503750579157e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 163762, "start": 1652.4399999999998, "end": 1654.9199999999998, "text": " The English alphabet consists of 26 letters.", "tokens": [51106, 440, 3669, 23339, 14689, 295, 7551, 7825, 13, 51230], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18785199483235676, "compression_ratio": 1.5497630331753554, "no_speech_prob": 1.655503750579157e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 163762, "start": 1655.1999999999998, "end": 1657.6999999999998, "text": " That is a very small, rigidly first set of operators.", "tokens": [51244, 663, 307, 257, 588, 1359, 11, 22195, 356, 700, 992, 295, 19077, 13, 51369], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18785199483235676, "compression_ratio": 1.5497630331753554, "no_speech_prob": 1.655503750579157e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 165770, "start": 1657.7, "end": 1665.6200000000001, "text": " Yet, those 26 letters can generate every single word in the dictionary, every book ever written, and every word that hasn't even been invented yet.", "tokens": [50365, 10890, 11, 729, 7551, 7825, 393, 8460, 633, 2167, 1349, 294, 264, 25890, 11, 633, 1446, 1562, 3720, 11, 293, 633, 1349, 300, 6132, 380, 754, 668, 14479, 1939, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13570129510128137, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 2.9167588483369755e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 165770, "start": 1665.6200000000001, "end": 1667.74, "text": " Or consider the mechanics of chess.", "tokens": [50761, 1610, 1949, 264, 12939, 295, 24122, 13, 50867], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13570129510128137, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 2.9167588483369755e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 165770, "start": 1668.78, "end": 1673.98, "text": " You have a finite board of 64 squares and a very small set of allowed movements for the pieces.", "tokens": [50919, 509, 362, 257, 19362, 3150, 295, 12145, 19368, 293, 257, 588, 1359, 992, 295, 4350, 9981, 337, 264, 3755, 13, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13570129510128137, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 2.9167588483369755e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 165770, "start": 1674.7, "end": 1683.74, "text": " Yet, those rigidly fixed rules generate an effectively unbounded state space of possible games, far more games than there are atoms in the observable universe.", "tokens": [51215, 10890, 11, 729, 22195, 356, 6806, 4474, 8460, 364, 8659, 517, 18767, 292, 1785, 1901, 295, 1944, 2813, 11, 1400, 544, 2813, 813, 456, 366, 16871, 294, 264, 9951, 712, 6445, 13, 51667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13570129510128137, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 2.9167588483369755e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 168374, "start": 1683.74, "end": 1685.74, "text": " It is the ultimate generative trick.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 264, 9705, 1337, 1166, 4282, 13, 50465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10652689589667566, "compression_ratio": 1.596551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 2.3806100320211687e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 168374, "start": 1686.26, "end": 1690.78, "text": " You use a microscopic vocabulary to reach a practically infinite space of outcomes.", "tokens": [50491, 509, 764, 257, 47897, 19864, 281, 2524, 257, 15667, 13785, 1901, 295, 10070, 13, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10652689589667566, "compression_ratio": 1.596551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 2.3806100320211687e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 168374, "start": 1691.58, "end": 1692.58, "text": " Fliction is asking,", "tokens": [50757, 3235, 4105, 307, 3365, 11, 50807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10652689589667566, "compression_ratio": 1.596551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 2.3806100320211687e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 168374, "start": 1693.32, "end": 1695.96, "text": " Can we accomplish this for the geometry of time and choice?", "tokens": [50844, 1664, 321, 9021, 341, 337, 264, 18426, 295, 565, 293, 3922, 30, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10652689589667566, "compression_ratio": 1.596551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 2.3806100320211687e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 168374, "start": 1696.5, "end": 1703.36, "text": " Can we discover a core alphabet of mathematical rules that can build literally any future continuation space we could possibly imagine?", "tokens": [51003, 1664, 321, 4411, 257, 4965, 23339, 295, 18894, 4474, 300, 393, 1322, 3736, 604, 2027, 29357, 1901, 321, 727, 6264, 3811, 30, 51346], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10652689589667566, "compression_ratio": 1.596551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 2.3806100320211687e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 168374, "start": 1703.66, "end": 1710.68, "text": " To attack this monumental problem, the author deploys a highly specialized mathematical shortcut known as the collage theorem.", "tokens": [51361, 1407, 2690, 341, 43105, 1154, 11, 264, 3793, 368, 49522, 257, 5405, 19813, 18894, 24822, 2570, 382, 264, 1263, 609, 20904, 13, 51712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10652689589667566, "compression_ratio": 1.596551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 2.3806100320211687e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 171068, "start": 1710.68, "end": 1714.5, "text": " The name evokes art, but the mechanics are pure computational bypass.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1315, 1073, 8606, 1523, 11, 457, 264, 12939, 366, 6075, 28270, 24996, 13, 50556], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11606091611525592, "compression_ratio": 1.6157894736842104, "no_speech_prob": 2.3256984445912954e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 171068, "start": 1715.18, "end": 1721.48, "text": " Earlier, we established that a set of contracting rules eventually converges on a final shape the attractor at the absolute limit of infinity.", "tokens": [50590, 24552, 11, 321, 7545, 300, 257, 992, 295, 36095, 4474, 4728, 9652, 2880, 322, 257, 2572, 3909, 264, 5049, 284, 412, 264, 8236, 4948, 295, 13202, 13, 50905], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11606091611525592, "compression_ratio": 1.6157894736842104, "no_speech_prob": 2.3256984445912954e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 171068, "start": 1721.88, "end": 1727.2, "text": " But calculating the state of a system at the limit of infinity is computationally intractable.", "tokens": [50925, 583, 28258, 264, 1785, 295, 257, 1185, 412, 264, 4948, 295, 13202, 307, 24903, 379, 560, 1897, 712, 13, 51191], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11606091611525592, "compression_ratio": 1.6157894736842104, "no_speech_prob": 2.3256984445912954e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 172720, "start": 1727.2, "end": 1739.06, "text": " If you are an engineer or a mathematician trying to find a specific set of rules that will perfectly build a target shape, say, a specific highly desired future state for an economy,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 366, 364, 11403, 420, 257, 48281, 1382, 281, 915, 257, 2685, 992, 295, 4474, 300, 486, 6239, 1322, 257, 3779, 3909, 11, 584, 11, 257, 2685, 5405, 14721, 2027, 1785, 337, 364, 5010, 11, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09793467154869666, "compression_ratio": 1.5618556701030928, "no_speech_prob": 1.714741521517682e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 172720, "start": 1739.6200000000001, "end": 1745.76, "text": " you cannot afford to run millions of simulated rules out to infinity just to see if they eventually land on your target.", "tokens": [50986, 291, 2644, 6157, 281, 1190, 6803, 295, 41713, 4474, 484, 281, 13202, 445, 281, 536, 498, 436, 4728, 2117, 322, 428, 3779, 13, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09793467154869666, "compression_ratio": 1.5618556701030928, "no_speech_prob": 1.714741521517682e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 174576, "start": 1745.76, "end": 1748.06, "text": " It's an impossible inverse problem.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 364, 6243, 17340, 1154, 13, 50480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12139389514923096, "compression_ratio": 1.7735191637630663, "no_speech_prob": 1.4497492832957204e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 174576, "start": 1748.3799999999999, "end": 1750.12, "text": " The collage theorem provides the bypass.", "tokens": [50496, 440, 1263, 609, 20904, 6417, 264, 24996, 13, 50583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12139389514923096, "compression_ratio": 1.7735191637630663, "no_speech_prob": 1.4497492832957204e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 174576, "start": 1750.8, "end": 1754.28, "text": " It proves that you do not need to calculate the sequence all the way to infinity.", "tokens": [50617, 467, 25019, 300, 291, 360, 406, 643, 281, 8873, 264, 8310, 439, 264, 636, 281, 13202, 13, 50791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12139389514923096, "compression_ratio": 1.7735191637630663, "no_speech_prob": 1.4497492832957204e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 174576, "start": 1754.58, "end": 1761.5, "text": " You only need to check if one single application of the rules, a one-step collage, maps the space reasonably close to your target.", "tokens": [50806, 509, 787, 643, 281, 1520, 498, 472, 2167, 3861, 295, 264, 4474, 11, 257, 472, 12, 16792, 1263, 609, 11, 11317, 264, 1901, 23551, 1998, 281, 428, 3779, 13, 51152], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12139389514923096, "compression_ratio": 1.7735191637630663, "no_speech_prob": 1.4497492832957204e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 174576, "start": 1761.84, "end": 1762.12, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51169, 1779, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12139389514923096, "compression_ratio": 1.7735191637630663, "no_speech_prob": 1.4497492832957204e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 174576, "start": 1762.44, "end": 1767.32, "text": " If you apply the rules once, and the immediate output roughly covers the shape of your target,", "tokens": [51199, 759, 291, 3079, 264, 4474, 1564, 11, 293, 264, 11629, 5598, 9810, 10538, 264, 3909, 295, 428, 3779, 11, 51443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12139389514923096, "compression_ratio": 1.7735191637630663, "no_speech_prob": 1.4497492832957204e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 174576, "start": 1767.74, "end": 1772.72, "text": " the theorem guarantees that if you were to run those rules to infinity, they would permanently lock onto that target.", "tokens": [51464, 264, 20904, 32567, 300, 498, 291, 645, 281, 1190, 729, 4474, 281, 13202, 11, 436, 576, 24042, 4017, 3911, 300, 3779, 13, 51713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12139389514923096, "compression_ratio": 1.7735191637630663, "no_speech_prob": 1.4497492832957204e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 177272, "start": 1772.72, "end": 1779.34, "text": " It magically converts an intractable infinite limit problem into a highly manageable one-step geometric fitting problem.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 39763, 38874, 364, 560, 1897, 712, 13785, 4948, 1154, 666, 257, 5405, 38798, 472, 12, 16792, 33246, 15669, 1154, 13, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09051690382115982, "compression_ratio": 1.6654545454545455, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370830693320348e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 177272, "start": 1779.64, "end": 1783.1200000000001, "text": " So with the collage theorem acting as our bypass, do we have the answer?", "tokens": [50711, 407, 365, 264, 1263, 609, 20904, 6577, 382, 527, 24996, 11, 360, 321, 362, 264, 1867, 30, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09051690382115982, "compression_ratio": 1.6654545454545455, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370830693320348e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 177272, "start": 1783.38, "end": 1786.0, "text": " Do we have our universal alphabet for generating futures?", "tokens": [50898, 1144, 321, 362, 527, 11455, 23339, 337, 17746, 26071, 30, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09051690382115982, "compression_ratio": 1.6654545454545455, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370830693320348e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 177272, "start": 1786.64, "end": 1791.84, "text": " Well, Flitschian provides theorem 5.2, which delivers exactly half of the answer.", "tokens": [51061, 1042, 11, 3235, 1208, 339, 952, 6417, 20904, 1025, 13, 17, 11, 597, 24860, 2293, 1922, 295, 264, 1867, 13, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09051690382115982, "compression_ratio": 1.6654545454545455, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370830693320348e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 177272, "start": 1792.3, "end": 1799.98, "text": " The theorem proves that, yes, every compact target, every reasonable bounded future geometry can absolutely be approximated.", "tokens": [51344, 440, 20904, 25019, 300, 11, 2086, 11, 633, 14679, 3779, 11, 633, 10585, 37498, 2027, 18426, 393, 3122, 312, 8542, 770, 13, 51728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09051690382115982, "compression_ratio": 1.6654545454545455, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370830693320348e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 179998, "start": 1799.98, "end": 1803.04, "text": " A set of rules to build it definitively exists.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 992, 295, 4474, 281, 1322, 309, 28152, 356, 8198, 13, 50518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10942195653915406, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428710826298486e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 179998, "start": 1803.28, "end": 1804.88, "text": " But the caveat is devastating.", "tokens": [50530, 583, 264, 43012, 307, 21280, 13, 50610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10942195653915406, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428710826298486e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 179998, "start": 1805.08, "end": 1807.04, "text": " It is a massive mathematical limitation.", "tokens": [50620, 467, 307, 257, 5994, 18894, 27432, 13, 50718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10942195653915406, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428710826298486e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 179998, "start": 1807.7, "end": 1815.28, "text": " The theorem guarantees the existence of the rules, but it requires you to custom build an entirely new set of rules for every single new target.", "tokens": [50751, 440, 20904, 32567, 264, 9123, 295, 264, 4474, 11, 457, 309, 7029, 291, 281, 2375, 1322, 364, 7696, 777, 992, 295, 4474, 337, 633, 2167, 777, 3779, 13, 51130], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10942195653915406, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428710826298486e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 179998, "start": 1815.46, "end": 1817.8600000000001, "text": " Which means we do not have a 26-letter alphabet.", "tokens": [51139, 3013, 1355, 321, 360, 406, 362, 257, 7551, 12, 21248, 23339, 13, 51259], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10942195653915406, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428710826298486e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 179998, "start": 1818.2, "end": 1818.34, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51276, 865, 13, 51283], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10942195653915406, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428710826298486e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 181834, "start": 1818.34, "end": 1826.0, "text": " We have a system where, if I want to write the word Apple, I am forced to invent five completely unique custom letters that can only spell Apple.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 362, 257, 1185, 689, 11, 498, 286, 528, 281, 2464, 264, 1349, 6373, 11, 286, 669, 7579, 281, 7962, 1732, 2584, 3845, 2375, 7825, 300, 393, 787, 9827, 6373, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11314866037079782, "compression_ratio": 1.7102040816326531, "no_speech_prob": 1.9652270262515703e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 181834, "start": 1826.3999999999999, "end": 1832.0, "text": " And if I want to write Banana, I have to throw the first set away and invent a completely different set of custom letters just for that word.", "tokens": [50768, 400, 498, 286, 528, 281, 2464, 39588, 11, 286, 362, 281, 3507, 264, 700, 992, 1314, 293, 7962, 257, 2584, 819, 992, 295, 2375, 7825, 445, 337, 300, 1349, 13, 51048], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11314866037079782, "compression_ratio": 1.7102040816326531, "no_speech_prob": 1.9652270262515703e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 181834, "start": 1832.06, "end": 1832.4399999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51051, 7587, 13, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11314866037079782, "compression_ratio": 1.7102040816326531, "no_speech_prob": 1.9652270262515703e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 181834, "start": 1832.74, "end": 1837.6599999999999, "text": " The existence theorem answers the question, can this specific destination be reached at all?", "tokens": [51085, 440, 9123, 20904, 6338, 264, 1168, 11, 393, 341, 2685, 12236, 312, 6488, 412, 439, 30, 51331], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11314866037079782, "compression_ratio": 1.7102040816326531, "no_speech_prob": 1.9652270262515703e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 181834, "start": 1838.06, "end": 1839.72, "text": " The answer is undeniably yes.", "tokens": [51351, 440, 1867, 307, 674, 15711, 1188, 2086, 13, 51434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11314866037079782, "compression_ratio": 1.7102040816326531, "no_speech_prob": 1.9652270262515703e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 183972, "start": 1839.72, "end": 1843.42, "text": " But the universal generation conjecture asks a much harder question.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 11455, 5125, 416, 1020, 540, 8962, 257, 709, 6081, 1168, 13, 50550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304248304252166, "compression_ratio": 1.5847457627118644, "no_speech_prob": 2.004407273839548e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 183972, "start": 1844.08, "end": 1848.16, "text": " Can every destination be reached using a single set of tools chosen in advance?", "tokens": [50583, 1664, 633, 12236, 312, 6488, 1228, 257, 2167, 992, 295, 3873, 8614, 294, 7295, 30, 50787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304248304252166, "compression_ratio": 1.5847457627118644, "no_speech_prob": 2.004407273839548e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 183972, "start": 1848.5, "end": 1851.92, "text": " And the instinct is to ask why this is so difficult to achieve.", "tokens": [50804, 400, 264, 16556, 307, 281, 1029, 983, 341, 307, 370, 2252, 281, 4584, 13, 50975], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304248304252166, "compression_ratio": 1.5847457627118644, "no_speech_prob": 2.004407273839548e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 183972, "start": 1852.48, "end": 1856.1200000000001, "text": " Artificial neural networks seemingly bypass this problem constantly.", "tokens": [51003, 5735, 10371, 18161, 9590, 18709, 24996, 341, 1154, 6460, 13, 51185], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304248304252166, "compression_ratio": 1.5847457627118644, "no_speech_prob": 2.004407273839548e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 183972, "start": 1856.8600000000001, "end": 1862.34, "text": " A large language model uses a fixed, pre-chosen architecture to generate virtually any text.", "tokens": [51222, 316, 2416, 2856, 2316, 4960, 257, 6806, 11, 659, 12, 339, 6441, 9482, 281, 8460, 14103, 604, 2487, 13, 51496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304248304252166, "compression_ratio": 1.5847457627118644, "no_speech_prob": 2.004407273839548e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 186234, "start": 1862.34, "end": 1871.28, "text": " In mathematics, the universal approximation theorem guarantees that a neural network with enough width or depth can approximate any continuous function.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 18666, 11, 264, 11455, 28023, 20904, 32567, 300, 257, 18161, 3209, 365, 1547, 11402, 420, 7161, 393, 30874, 604, 10957, 2445, 13, 50812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1308827231912052, "compression_ratio": 1.7975708502024292, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796942746948428e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 186234, "start": 1871.8, "end": 1876.06, "text": " Why does this geometric framework fail where neural networks succeed?", "tokens": [50838, 1545, 775, 341, 33246, 8388, 3061, 689, 18161, 9590, 7754, 30, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1308827231912052, "compression_ratio": 1.7975708502024292, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796942746948428e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 186234, "start": 1876.3799999999999, "end": 1880.78, "text": " That gap is the exact open conjecture fliction leaves unsolved.", "tokens": [51067, 663, 7417, 307, 264, 1900, 1269, 416, 1020, 540, 932, 4105, 5510, 2693, 29110, 13, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1308827231912052, "compression_ratio": 1.7975708502024292, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796942746948428e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 186234, "start": 1881.1399999999999, "end": 1884.1399999999999, "text": " It represents a genuine frontier in geometric mathematics.", "tokens": [51305, 467, 8855, 257, 16699, 35853, 294, 33246, 18666, 13, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1308827231912052, "compression_ratio": 1.7975708502024292, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796942746948428e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 186234, "start": 1884.6399999999999, "end": 1889.8799999999999, "text": " The reason neural networks achieve universal approximation is rooted in their compositional depth.", "tokens": [51480, 440, 1778, 18161, 9590, 4584, 11455, 28023, 307, 25277, 294, 641, 10199, 2628, 7161, 13, 51742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1308827231912052, "compression_ratio": 1.7975708502024292, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796942746948428e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 188988, "start": 1889.88, "end": 1896.66, "text": " They possess a layered structure that allows simple functions to combine in complex ways, guaranteeing coverage of the target space.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 17490, 257, 34666, 3877, 300, 4045, 2199, 6828, 281, 10432, 294, 3997, 2098, 11, 10815, 278, 9645, 295, 264, 3779, 1901, 13, 50704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293108732804007, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182081274603634e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 188988, "start": 1896.7800000000002, "end": 1898.3200000000002, "text": " It's similar to polynomials, right?", "tokens": [50710, 467, 311, 2531, 281, 22560, 12356, 11, 558, 30, 50787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293108732804007, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182081274603634e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 188988, "start": 1898.66, "end": 1902.64, "text": " We know polynomials can approximate any curve because of the Stone-Weir-Strauss theorem.", "tokens": [50804, 492, 458, 22560, 12356, 393, 30874, 604, 7605, 570, 295, 264, 15012, 12, 4360, 347, 12, 4520, 424, 2023, 20904, 13, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293108732804007, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182081274603634e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 188988, "start": 1902.8200000000002, "end": 1904.0400000000002, "text": " They have an algebraic closure.", "tokens": [51012, 814, 362, 364, 21989, 299, 24653, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293108732804007, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182081274603634e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 188988, "start": 1904.2, "end": 1907.0, "text": " You can multiply them together, add them up, and they behave smoothly.", "tokens": [51081, 509, 393, 12972, 552, 1214, 11, 909, 552, 493, 11, 293, 436, 15158, 19565, 13, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293108732804007, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182081274603634e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 188988, "start": 1907.4, "end": 1907.92, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51241, 48746, 736, 13, 51267], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293108732804007, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182081274603634e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 188988, "start": 1908.3000000000002, "end": 1911.94, "text": " Neural networks and polynomials possess proven structural closure.", "tokens": [51286, 1734, 1807, 9590, 293, 22560, 12356, 17490, 12785, 15067, 24653, 13, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293108732804007, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182081274603634e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 188988, "start": 1912.5600000000002, "end": 1914.6000000000001, "text": " Continuation geometries currently do not.", "tokens": [51499, 14674, 16073, 12956, 2244, 4362, 360, 406, 13, 51601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293108732804007, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182081274603634e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 191460, "start": 1914.6, "end": 1923.1799999999998, "text": " We know the destination exists on the map, but we lack the mathematical proof that a universal vehicle can be constructed to navigate there using a finite engine.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 458, 264, 12236, 8198, 322, 264, 4471, 11, 457, 321, 5011, 264, 18894, 8177, 300, 257, 11455, 5864, 393, 312, 17083, 281, 12350, 456, 1228, 257, 19362, 2848, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09039007249425669, "compression_ratio": 1.515625, "no_speech_prob": 2.380843135488253e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 191460, "start": 1923.9399999999998, "end": 1926.6599999999999, "text": " Fliction is remarkably transparent about this limitation.", "tokens": [50832, 3235, 4105, 307, 37381, 12737, 466, 341, 27432, 13, 50968], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09039007249425669, "compression_ratio": 1.515625, "no_speech_prob": 2.380843135488253e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 191460, "start": 1927.4599999999998, "end": 1930.8799999999999, "text": " Closing that structural gap is the next great challenge for the field.", "tokens": [51008, 2033, 6110, 300, 15067, 7417, 307, 264, 958, 869, 3430, 337, 264, 2519, 13, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09039007249425669, "compression_ratio": 1.515625, "no_speech_prob": 2.380843135488253e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 193088, "start": 1930.88, "end": 1939.64, "text": " There is something thrilling about reading a dense mathematical text that suddenly stops at the edge of the known map, plants a flag, and basically says,", "tokens": [50365, 821, 307, 746, 39347, 466, 3760, 257, 18011, 18894, 2487, 300, 5800, 10094, 412, 264, 4691, 295, 264, 2570, 4471, 11, 5972, 257, 7166, 11, 293, 1936, 1619, 11, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11322223778926965, "compression_ratio": 1.6014492753623188, "no_speech_prob": 2.2448134930769248e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 193088, "start": 1940.1000000000001, "end": 1941.6200000000001, "text": " Here be dragons, good luck.", "tokens": [50826, 1692, 312, 27240, 11, 665, 3668, 13, 50902], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11322223778926965, "compression_ratio": 1.6014492753623188, "no_speech_prob": 2.2448134930769248e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 193088, "start": 1942.0800000000002, "end": 1946.22, "text": " Which leads us perfectly into the final phase of our deep dive, the roadmap.", "tokens": [50925, 3013, 6689, 505, 6239, 666, 264, 2572, 5574, 295, 527, 2452, 9192, 11, 264, 35738, 13, 51132], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11322223778926965, "compression_ratio": 1.6014492753623188, "no_speech_prob": 2.2448134930769248e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 193088, "start": 1946.72, "end": 1953.18, "text": " The working draft deliberately pauses here, but Fliction includes an outline of the unfinished chapters they intend to write next.", "tokens": [51157, 440, 1364, 11206, 23506, 2502, 8355, 510, 11, 457, 3235, 4105, 5974, 364, 16387, 295, 264, 41037, 20013, 436, 19759, 281, 2464, 958, 13, 51480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11322223778926965, "compression_ratio": 1.6014492753623188, "no_speech_prob": 2.2448134930769248e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 193088, "start": 1953.5200000000002, "end": 1955.7800000000002, "text": " It reads like the private sketchbook of an inventor.", "tokens": [51497, 467, 15700, 411, 264, 4551, 12325, 2939, 295, 364, 41593, 13, 51610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11322223778926965, "compression_ratio": 1.6014492753623188, "no_speech_prob": 2.2448134930769248e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 195578, "start": 1955.78, "end": 1960.52, "text": " It offers a rare, unsiltered glimpse into the real-time process of mathematical philosophy.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 7736, 257, 5892, 11, 2693, 388, 40665, 25838, 666, 264, 957, 12, 3766, 1399, 295, 18894, 10675, 13, 50602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15162111583508944, "compression_ratio": 1.6754966887417218, "no_speech_prob": 1.642767736079187e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 195578, "start": 1961.04, "end": 1964.34, "text": " The author outlines the conceptual hurdles they are preparing to tackle.", "tokens": [50628, 440, 3793, 40125, 264, 24106, 48387, 436, 366, 10075, 281, 14896, 13, 50793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15162111583508944, "compression_ratio": 1.6754966887417218, "no_speech_prob": 1.642767736079187e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 195578, "start": 1964.5, "end": 1968.78, "text": " Let's examine the notes for the plan, Chapter 6, titled State Insufficiency Made Explicit.", "tokens": [50801, 961, 311, 17496, 264, 5570, 337, 264, 1393, 11, 18874, 1386, 11, 19841, 4533, 9442, 1245, 42081, 18330, 2111, 4770, 270, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15162111583508944, "compression_ratio": 1.6754966887417218, "no_speech_prob": 1.642767736079187e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 195578, "start": 1969.44, "end": 1972.22, "text": " The notes describe a sleep coma toy system.", "tokens": [51048, 440, 5570, 6786, 257, 2817, 35106, 12058, 1185, 13, 51187], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15162111583508944, "compression_ratio": 1.6754966887417218, "no_speech_prob": 1.642767736079187e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 195578, "start": 1972.62, "end": 1973.92, "text": " What is the conceptual goal there?", "tokens": [51207, 708, 307, 264, 24106, 3387, 456, 30, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15162111583508944, "compression_ratio": 1.6754966887417218, "no_speech_prob": 1.642767736079187e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 195578, "start": 1974.24, "end": 1979.74, "text": " The goal is to formally, mathematically prove a highly subtle philosophical point.", "tokens": [51288, 440, 3387, 307, 281, 25983, 11, 44003, 7081, 257, 5405, 13743, 25066, 935, 13, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15162111583508944, "compression_ratio": 1.6754966887417218, "no_speech_prob": 1.642767736079187e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 195578, "start": 1980.6399999999999, "end": 1985.16, "text": " Observable state is drastically insufficient to capture the true geometry of the future.", "tokens": [51608, 42547, 712, 1785, 307, 29673, 41709, 281, 7983, 264, 2074, 18426, 295, 264, 2027, 13, 51834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15162111583508944, "compression_ratio": 1.6754966887417218, "no_speech_prob": 1.642767736079187e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 198516, "start": 1985.16, "end": 1990.5800000000002, "text": " The author wants to demonstrate that two systems can look completely identical to an outside observer,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3793, 2738, 281, 11698, 300, 732, 3652, 393, 574, 2584, 14800, 281, 364, 2380, 27878, 11, 50636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16755362800929857, "compression_ratio": 1.7525083612040133, "no_speech_prob": 1.755558589125461e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 198516, "start": 1990.8600000000001, "end": 1994.24, "text": " yet possess mathematically distinct continuation spaces.", "tokens": [50650, 1939, 17490, 44003, 10644, 29357, 7673, 13, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16755362800929857, "compression_ratio": 1.7525083612040133, "no_speech_prob": 1.755558589125461e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 198516, "start": 1994.72, "end": 1996.42, "text": " Consider the medical reality of that.", "tokens": [50843, 17416, 264, 4625, 4103, 295, 300, 13, 50928], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16755362800929857, "compression_ratio": 1.7525083612040133, "no_speech_prob": 1.755558589125461e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 198516, "start": 1996.76, "end": 1998.76, "text": " Imagine two patients in a hospital ward.", "tokens": [50945, 11739, 732, 4209, 294, 257, 4530, 15234, 13, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16755362800929857, "compression_ratio": 1.7525083612040133, "no_speech_prob": 1.755558589125461e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 198516, "start": 1999.42, "end": 2001.8400000000001, "text": " One patient is in a deep, natural sleep.", "tokens": [51078, 1485, 4537, 307, 294, 257, 2452, 11, 3303, 2817, 13, 51199], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16755362800929857, "compression_ratio": 1.7525083612040133, "no_speech_prob": 1.755558589125461e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 198516, "start": 2002.3200000000002, "end": 2004.48, "text": " The other patient is in a medically induced coma.", "tokens": [51223, 440, 661, 4537, 307, 294, 257, 49230, 33991, 35106, 13, 51331], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16755362800929857, "compression_ratio": 1.7525083612040133, "no_speech_prob": 1.755558589125461e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 198516, "start": 2005.24, "end": 2009.38, "text": " If a doctor walks into the room and merely observes their current state, the data is identical.", "tokens": [51369, 759, 257, 4631, 12896, 666, 264, 1808, 293, 17003, 3181, 9054, 641, 2190, 1785, 11, 264, 1412, 307, 14800, 13, 51576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16755362800929857, "compression_ratio": 1.7525083612040133, "no_speech_prob": 1.755558589125461e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 198516, "start": 2009.98, "end": 2014.14, "text": " Both patients have their eyes closed, their breathing is steady, their heart rates are suppressed.", "tokens": [51606, 6767, 4209, 362, 641, 2575, 5395, 11, 641, 9570, 307, 13211, 11, 641, 1917, 6846, 366, 42645, 13, 51814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16755362800929857, "compression_ratio": 1.7525083612040133, "no_speech_prob": 1.755558589125461e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 201414, "start": 2014.14, "end": 2017.0600000000002, "text": " Their observable internal states are indistinguishable.", "tokens": [50365, 6710, 9951, 712, 6920, 4368, 366, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 712, 13, 50511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10688159404656826, "compression_ratio": 1.6711111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 3.104349459784328e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 201414, "start": 2017.26, "end": 2021.8400000000001, "text": " But their continuation spaces, their mathematically accessible futures are wildly divergent.", "tokens": [50521, 583, 641, 29357, 7673, 11, 641, 44003, 9515, 26071, 366, 34731, 18558, 6930, 13, 50750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10688159404656826, "compression_ratio": 1.6711111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 3.104349459784328e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 201414, "start": 2022.3600000000001, "end": 2028.24, "text": " The naturally sleeping person's one-step future includes the possibility of waking up immediately if a loud alarm sounds.", "tokens": [50776, 440, 8195, 8296, 954, 311, 472, 12, 16792, 2027, 5974, 264, 7959, 295, 20447, 493, 4258, 498, 257, 6588, 14183, 3263, 13, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10688159404656826, "compression_ratio": 1.6711111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 3.104349459784328e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 201414, "start": 2028.8400000000001, "end": 2034.3400000000001, "text": " The coma patient's one-step future absolutely does not include that possibility, regardless of the alarm.", "tokens": [51100, 440, 35106, 4537, 311, 472, 12, 16792, 2027, 3122, 775, 406, 4090, 300, 7959, 11, 10060, 295, 264, 14183, 13, 51375], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10688159404656826, "compression_ratio": 1.6711111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 3.104349459784328e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 203434, "start": 2034.34, "end": 2042.9599999999998, "text": " Fliction wants to build a rigorous geometric proof, demonstrating that if you rely solely on observable state, you will inevitably miscalculate the future.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 2738, 281, 1322, 257, 29882, 33246, 8177, 11, 29889, 300, 498, 291, 10687, 23309, 322, 9951, 712, 1785, 11, 291, 486, 28171, 3346, 9895, 2444, 473, 264, 2027, 13, 50796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11620301859719413, "compression_ratio": 1.4806629834254144, "no_speech_prob": 2.4275748512075923e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 203434, "start": 2043.6799999999998, "end": 2049.96, "text": " The underlying history, the hidden rules governing the continuation space, must be integrated into the geometry.", "tokens": [50832, 440, 14217, 2503, 11, 264, 7633, 4474, 30054, 264, 29357, 1901, 11, 1633, 312, 10919, 666, 264, 18426, 13, 51146], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11620301859719413, "compression_ratio": 1.4806629834254144, "no_speech_prob": 2.4275748512075923e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 204996, "start": 2049.96, "end": 2067.42, "text": " Fliction wants to utilize this entire geometric framework of attractors, quotients, and operators to define the concept of meaning itself.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 2738, 281, 16117, 341, 2302, 33246, 8388, 295, 5049, 830, 11, 9641, 2448, 11, 293, 19077, 281, 6964, 264, 3410, 295, 3620, 2564, 13, 51238], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20361329714457194, "compression_ratio": 1.2777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.2190140350208942e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 206742, "start": 2067.42, "end": 2075.6, "text": " It is perhaps the most ambitious note in the draft, defining meaning not as linguistic abstraction, but as an equivalence class of reachable futures.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 4317, 264, 881, 20239, 3637, 294, 264, 11206, 11, 17827, 3620, 406, 382, 43002, 37765, 11, 457, 382, 364, 9052, 655, 1508, 295, 2524, 712, 26071, 13, 50774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07961893081665039, "compression_ratio": 1.7713178294573644, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283440725632484e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 206742, "start": 2075.98, "end": 2085.4, "text": " If we follow that logic, two different sentences or two different political actions possess the exact same meaning if and only if they lead to the exact same set of reachable futures.", "tokens": [50793, 759, 321, 1524, 300, 9952, 11, 732, 819, 16579, 420, 732, 819, 3905, 5909, 17490, 264, 1900, 912, 3620, 498, 293, 787, 498, 436, 1477, 281, 264, 1900, 912, 992, 295, 2524, 712, 26071, 13, 51264], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07961893081665039, "compression_ratio": 1.7713178294573644, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283440725632484e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 206742, "start": 2086.02, "end": 2089.4, "text": " Meaning is no longer a floating concept debated by philosophers.", "tokens": [51295, 19948, 307, 572, 2854, 257, 12607, 3410, 42212, 538, 36839, 13, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07961893081665039, "compression_ratio": 1.7713178294573644, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283440725632484e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 206742, "start": 2089.7400000000002, "end": 2092.62, "text": " It is literally the measurable shape of what happens next.", "tokens": [51481, 467, 307, 3736, 264, 43615, 3909, 295, 437, 2314, 958, 13, 51625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07961893081665039, "compression_ratio": 1.7713178294573644, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283440725632484e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 209262, "start": 2092.62, "end": 2098.52, "text": " It echoes the pragmatist philosophy of William James or Charles Pierce, but grounded in hard geometry.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 47051, 264, 33394, 15677, 468, 10675, 295, 6740, 5678, 420, 10523, 45432, 11, 457, 23535, 294, 1152, 18426, 13, 50660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13445736317152387, "compression_ratio": 1.5574912891986064, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901851875889996e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 209262, "start": 2099.06, "end": 2102.96, "text": " However, Fliction's own notes reveal incredible restraint here.", "tokens": [50687, 2908, 11, 3235, 4105, 311, 1065, 5570, 10658, 4651, 49281, 510, 13, 50882], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13445736317152387, "compression_ratio": 1.5574912891986064, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901851875889996e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 209262, "start": 2103.68, "end": 2112.8399999999997, "text": " They explicitly caution themselves against inventing new mathematical symbols or jumping to grand conclusions before fully mapping the underlying structure.", "tokens": [50918, 814, 20803, 23585, 2969, 1970, 7962, 278, 777, 18894, 16944, 420, 11233, 281, 2697, 22865, 949, 4498, 18350, 264, 14217, 3877, 13, 51376], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13445736317152387, "compression_ratio": 1.5574912891986064, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901851875889996e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 209262, "start": 2113.1, "end": 2115.42, "text": " They ask themselves a critical question in the margins.", "tokens": [51389, 814, 1029, 2969, 257, 4924, 1168, 294, 264, 30317, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13445736317152387, "compression_ratio": 1.5574912891986064, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901851875889996e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 209262, "start": 2115.96, "end": 2119.7599999999998, "text": " Is meaning simply calculated using the standard Hausdorff distance?", "tokens": [51532, 1119, 3620, 2935, 15598, 1228, 264, 3832, 22725, 67, 284, 602, 4560, 30, 51722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13445736317152387, "compression_ratio": 1.5574912891986064, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901851875889996e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 211976, "start": 2119.76, "end": 2125.2400000000002, "text": " Or does it require a much more complex topological relationship like a homeomorphism?", "tokens": [50365, 1610, 775, 309, 3651, 257, 709, 544, 3997, 1192, 4383, 2480, 411, 257, 1280, 32702, 1434, 30, 50639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12094257451310943, "compression_ratio": 1.6008064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 2.0685434701933625e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 211976, "start": 2125.8, "end": 2128.1800000000003, "text": " It demonstrates the immense integrity of the author.", "tokens": [50667, 467, 31034, 264, 22920, 16000, 295, 264, 3793, 13, 50786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12094257451310943, "compression_ratio": 1.6008064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 2.0685434701933625e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 211976, "start": 2128.5, "end": 2135.32, "text": " They are actively telling themselves not to write the theorem until they rigorously understand what the equal sign actually represents in that context.", "tokens": [50802, 814, 366, 13022, 3585, 2969, 406, 281, 2464, 264, 20904, 1826, 436, 42191, 5098, 1223, 437, 264, 2681, 1465, 767, 8855, 294, 300, 4319, 13, 51143], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12094257451310943, "compression_ratio": 1.6008064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 2.0685434701933625e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 211976, "start": 2135.84, "end": 2141.0800000000004, "text": " They refuse to dress up a philosophical speculation in the authoritative clothing of a mathematical proof.", "tokens": [51169, 814, 16791, 281, 5231, 493, 257, 25066, 27696, 294, 264, 3793, 14275, 11502, 295, 257, 18894, 8177, 13, 51431], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12094257451310943, "compression_ratio": 1.6008064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 2.0685434701933625e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 214108, "start": 2141.08, "end": 2144.38, "text": " We have covered a massive amount of intellectual terrain today.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 362, 5343, 257, 5994, 2372, 295, 12576, 17674, 965, 13, 50530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0720746618636111, "compression_ratio": 1.6595744680851063, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047290650443417e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 214108, "start": 2144.7999999999997, "end": 2155.1, "text": " We started by dismantling the idea of the future as a dark room, replacing it with the mechanics of fractal generation tiny rules acting as contractions, pulling reality into self-similar attractors.", "tokens": [50551, 492, 1409, 538, 30506, 1688, 264, 1558, 295, 264, 2027, 382, 257, 2877, 1808, 11, 19139, 309, 365, 264, 12939, 295, 17948, 304, 5125, 5870, 4474, 6577, 382, 4364, 626, 11, 8407, 4103, 666, 2698, 12, 30937, 2202, 5049, 830, 13, 51066], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0720746618636111, "compression_ratio": 1.6595744680851063, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047290650443417e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 214108, "start": 2155.36, "end": 2165.9, "text": " We examined the destruction of history, watching different trajectories flow across the landscape and merge into perfect continuation quotients, where the past mathematically vanishes into the confluence.", "tokens": [51079, 492, 30972, 264, 13563, 295, 2503, 11, 1976, 819, 18257, 2083, 3095, 2108, 264, 9661, 293, 22183, 666, 2176, 29357, 9641, 2448, 11, 689, 264, 1791, 44003, 3161, 16423, 666, 264, 1497, 40432, 13, 51606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0720746618636111, "compression_ratio": 1.6595744680851063, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047290650443417e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 216590, "start": 2165.9, "end": 2175.4, "text": " We calculated the exact one-bit loss of forcing a merge too early and explored how systems naturally expire their own memories through periodic deadlines.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 15598, 264, 1900, 472, 12, 5260, 4470, 295, 19030, 257, 22183, 886, 2440, 293, 24016, 577, 3652, 8195, 45447, 641, 1065, 8495, 807, 27790, 37548, 13, 50840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0860863622728285, "compression_ratio": 1.643939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 2.4275863437506207e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 216590, "start": 2175.88, "end": 2183.46, "text": " We discovered the magic parameter, the Lipschitz constant, that mathematically unifies the act of creating the future with the act of forgetting the past.", "tokens": [50864, 492, 6941, 264, 5585, 13075, 11, 264, 441, 2600, 339, 6862, 5754, 11, 300, 44003, 517, 11221, 264, 605, 295, 4084, 264, 2027, 365, 264, 605, 295, 25428, 264, 1791, 13, 51243], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0860863622728285, "compression_ratio": 1.643939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 2.4275863437506207e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 216590, "start": 2183.62, "end": 2190.26, "text": " And we stood at the edge of the theoretical map, contemplating the unsolved mystery of a universal alphabet for time itself.", "tokens": [51251, 400, 321, 9371, 412, 264, 4691, 295, 264, 20864, 4471, 11, 19935, 990, 264, 2693, 29110, 11422, 295, 257, 11455, 23339, 337, 565, 2564, 13, 51583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0860863622728285, "compression_ratio": 1.643939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 2.4275863437506207e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 219026, "start": 2190.26, "end": 2200.4, "text": " The entire framework forces a radical reframing of how we conceptualize our trajectories, the weight of our choices, and the historical information we insist on carrying with us.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2302, 8388, 5874, 257, 12001, 1895, 2356, 278, 295, 577, 321, 24106, 1125, 527, 18257, 2083, 11, 264, 3364, 295, 527, 7994, 11, 293, 264, 8584, 1589, 321, 13466, 322, 9792, 365, 505, 13, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.103086921606171, "compression_ratio": 1.6213991769547325, "no_speech_prob": 2.3348053091593046e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 219026, "start": 2200.5200000000004, "end": 2204.3, "text": " Which leaves a final, deeply personal application for you to consider.", "tokens": [50878, 3013, 5510, 257, 2572, 11, 8760, 2973, 3861, 337, 291, 281, 1949, 13, 51067], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.103086921606171, "compression_ratio": 1.6213991769547325, "no_speech_prob": 2.3348053091593046e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 219026, "start": 2204.6600000000003, "end": 2210.36, "text": " We now understand that the future is a geometry we are actively generating, not a room we are walking into.", "tokens": [51085, 492, 586, 1223, 300, 264, 2027, 307, 257, 18426, 321, 366, 13022, 17746, 11, 406, 257, 1808, 321, 366, 4494, 666, 13, 51370], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.103086921606171, "compression_ratio": 1.6213991769547325, "no_speech_prob": 2.3348053091593046e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 219026, "start": 2210.96, "end": 2212.78, "text": " Look at the rivers in your own life.", "tokens": [51400, 2053, 412, 264, 18361, 294, 428, 1065, 993, 13, 51491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.103086921606171, "compression_ratio": 1.6213991769547325, "no_speech_prob": 2.3348053091593046e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 221278, "start": 2212.78, "end": 2219.2000000000003, "text": " Look at a choice you are currently agonizing over, a distinction you are spending massive amounts of cognitive energy to maintain.", "tokens": [50365, 2053, 412, 257, 3922, 291, 366, 4362, 623, 266, 3319, 670, 11, 257, 16844, 291, 366, 6434, 5994, 11663, 295, 15605, 2281, 281, 6909, 13, 50686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12367499243352831, "compression_ratio": 1.5993031358885017, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191839756664716e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 221278, "start": 2219.84, "end": 2223.1400000000003, "text": " Are those two paths actually generating different futures?", "tokens": [50718, 2014, 729, 732, 14518, 767, 17746, 819, 26071, 30, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12367499243352831, "compression_ratio": 1.5993031358885017, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191839756664716e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 221278, "start": 2223.82, "end": 2228.1800000000003, "text": " Or do they share the exact same continuation space just a few horizons away?", "tokens": [50917, 1610, 360, 436, 2073, 264, 1900, 912, 29357, 1901, 445, 257, 1326, 7937, 892, 1314, 30, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12367499243352831, "compression_ratio": 1.5993031358885017, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191839756664716e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 221278, "start": 2228.6200000000003, "end": 2235.98, "text": " Are you unnecessarily paying a daily one-bit loss in mental energy to preserve a difference that the universe has already merged?", "tokens": [51157, 2014, 291, 16799, 3289, 6229, 257, 5212, 472, 12, 5260, 4470, 294, 4973, 2281, 281, 15665, 257, 2649, 300, 264, 6445, 575, 1217, 36427, 30, 51525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12367499243352831, "compression_ratio": 1.5993031358885017, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191839756664716e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 221278, "start": 2236.2400000000002, "end": 2239.38, "text": " It is a geometric question with profound psychological weight.", "tokens": [51538, 467, 307, 257, 33246, 1168, 365, 14382, 14346, 3364, 13, 51695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12367499243352831, "compression_ratio": 1.5993031358885017, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191839756664716e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 223938, "start": 2239.38, "end": 2242.96, "text": " Thank you for joining us on this deep dive into the architecture of the future.", "tokens": [50365, 1044, 291, 337, 5549, 505, 322, 341, 2452, 9192, 666, 264, 9482, 295, 264, 2027, 13, 50544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12319381096783806, "compression_ratio": 1.2522522522522523, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427278796085856e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 223938, "start": 2243.42, "end": 2245.86, "text": " Keep generating your geometry, and we'll see you next time.", "tokens": [50567, 5527, 17746, 428, 18426, 11, 293, 321, 603, 536, 291, 958, 565, 13, 50689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12319381096783806, "compression_ratio": 1.2522522522522523, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427278796085856e-12}], "language": "en"}
