[substitution] ./Generating_the_future_with_continuation_geometry.srt
  L35: It really does. It's called generative continuation geometry by an author named Flixing.
  L123: But Fliction proposes that the room doesn't even exist until the specific rules of the system build it.
  L235: It never forms a coherent, self-similar structure. Fliction is mathematically strict about the spreading
  L415: So, armed with the Hausdorff distance to measure the space and contractions to shrink the space, Flixian invokes the Banach fixed point theorem.
  L731: And to formalize this merging, fliction defines an equivalence relation called a continuation quotient.
